('430cbb30-d300-48df-a918-a6b1092010ca', 'Easy Yoga Pose', 'Full Body', 'Bodyweight', '{"Full Body"}'::text[], '{}'::text[], 'The Easy Yoga Pose provides a deep stretch for your full body, ideal for recovery and mobility work. Regular stretching improves flexibility, reduces injury risk, and aids recovery.', '78341201', '78341201-Easy-Yoga-Pose-(female)_Stretching_.mp4', 'female', FALSE, '2025-12-03 23:26:33.298565+00', '1. Move into the stretch position for Easy Yoga Pose. 2. Ease into the stretch until you feel gentle tension (not pain). 3. Hold for 20-30 seconds, breathing deeply and relaxing into the stretch.', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 1, NULL, 1, 1, NULL, 3, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 1, 1, NULL, 1, NULL, TRUE, NULL, 'Stretch', 15, 2, 6, FALSE, TRUE, 'yoga', 'Easy Yoga Pose', 'stretch_hip, stretch_back, plank', FALSE, 'bodyweight', TRUE, 1, 30, 2, 70, 88, 95, 65),
('431754d2-ae2f-4ebe-9be2-de7d6c3d3ac5', 'L Sit Chin Up (Pull-Up Bar)', 'Back', 'Pull-Up Bar', '{"Lats"}'::text[], '{"Biceps","Upper Back"}'::text[], 'The L Sit Chin Up is a movement exercise that targets your latissimus dorsi for a wider back. Your biceps work as secondary movers, adding to the training stimulus. No equipment needed—your body provides all the resistance. A strong back improves posture, prevents injury, and balances pressing movements.', '69411201', '69411201-L-Sit-Chin-up-(male)_Back_.mp4', 'male', FALSE, '2025-12-03 23:26:27.67144+00', '1. Pull yourself up, focusing on bicep and lat engagement. 2. Raise until chin is over the bar, lower with full control. 3. Repeat for the prescribed number of repetitions. Maintain consistent tempo throughout the set.', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 5, NULL, 7, 7, NULL, 5, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 8, 12, NULL, 6, NULL, TRUE, NULL, 'Strength', 70, 7, 8, TRUE, TRUE, 'pull_up', 'L Sit Chin Up', 'lat_pulldown, bent_over_row, bicep_curl', FALSE, 'pull_up_bar', FALSE, 3, 90, 4, 70, 88, 95, 65),
('432682b1-37ba-4d19-9032-dd936114b1cc', 'Seated Neck Backward Stretch', 'Neck', 'Bodyweight', '{"Neck"}'::text[], '{"Traps"}'::text[], 'Use this stretch to open up your back area and enhance overall flexibility. You''ll also feel your shoulders working to support the movement. Being seated provides stability, allowing you to focus on the working muscles. Include this in your routine for better mobility and reduced muscle tension.', '89181201', '89181201-Seated-Neck-Backward-Stretch-(male)_Stretching_.mp4', 'male', FALSE, '2025-12-03 23:26:28.52454+00', '1. Sit with your back supported, core engaged, feet flat on the floor. 2. Move into the stretch position for Seated Neck Backward Stretch. 3. Ease into the stretch until you feel gentle tension (not pain). 4. Hold for 20-30 seconds, breathing deeply and relaxing into the stretch.', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 1, NULL, 1, 1, NULL, 3, 'Seated', NULL, NULL, NULL, 1, 1, NULL, 1, NULL, TRUE, NULL, 'Stretch', 42, 2, 6, FALSE, TRUE, 'stretch_general', 'Seated Neck Backward Stretch', 'stretch_hip, stretch_hamstring, stretch_shoulder', FALSE, 'bodyweight', TRUE, 1, 30, 2, 70, 88, 95, 65),
('43345fbc-b578-4994-8f39-0f338d30527c', 'Seated Side Crunch (Against Wall)', 'Core', 'Wall', '{"Obliques"}'::text[], '{"Hip Flexors","Abs"}'::text[], 'This crunching exercise engages your abs for improved core stability and strength. You''ll also feel your abs working to support the movement. The seated position helps isolate the target muscles by removing momentum. Building core stability helps with everything from heavy deadlifts to daily activities.', '6911201', '06911201-Seated-Side-Crunch-(Wall)_Waist_.mp4', 'male', FALSE, '2025-12-03 23:26:27.384461+00', '1. Position yourself at the appropriate distance from a wall. 2. Sit with your back supported, core engaged, feet flat on the floor. 3. Curl your shoulders off the floor by contracting your abs. 4. Don''t pull on your neck—focus on the abdominal contraction. 5. Lower with control, maintaining some tension. 6. Complete all reps with control before resting.', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 2, NULL, 5, 7, NULL, 6, 'Seated', NULL, NULL, NULL, 12, 20, NULL, 4, NULL, TRUE, NULL, 'Strength', 64, 5, 7, FALSE, TRUE, 'crunch', 'Seated Side Crunch', 'leg_raise, plank, russian_twist, v_up', TRUE, 'bodyweight', FALSE, 3, 60, 2, 70, 88, 95, 65),
('435112ae-56ae-4fb9-a2af-b7da619781ab', 'Bicep Curl - Lying on Bench (Cable)', 'Arms', 'Cables, Flat Bench', '{"Biceps"}'::text[], '{"Forearms"}'::text[], 'The Cable Lying Biceps Curl is a curling exercise that isolates your biceps. You''ll also feel your forearms working to support the movement. Performing this lying down removes momentum for stricter form. Cables provide constant tension throughout the full range of motion. Dedicated arm training builds both strength and muscular definition.', '30551201', '30551201-Cable-Lying-Bicep-Curl-(female)_Upper-Arms_.mp4', 'female', FALSE, '2025-12-03 23:26:31.931873+00', '1. Adjust the cable machine to the correct height and attachment for Cable Lying Biceps Curl. 2. Lie down in the appropriate position for Cable Lying Biceps Curl. 3. Keep your elbows in a fixed position throughout the movement. 4. Curl the weight up by contracting your biceps, squeezing at the top. 5. Lower with control, resisting the weight on the way down. 6. Repeat for the prescribed number of repetitions.', 'Curl', 'Pull', NULL, NULL, NULL, 2, NULL, 5, 7, NULL, 6, 'Lying', NULL, NULL, NULL, 12, 20, NULL, 4, NULL, FALSE, NULL, 'Strength', 90, 5, 7, FALSE, TRUE, 'bicep_curl', 'Lying Biceps Curl', 'hammer_curl, preacher_curl, cable_curl', FALSE, 'cable', FALSE, 3, 60, 2, 85, 88, 30, 92),
('435565eb-67cd-47f9-bf2a-313fa5805696', 'Seated Diagonal Side Stretch', 'Full Body', 'Bodyweight', '{"Full Body"}'::text[], '{}'::text[], 'This stretch specifically works on your full body, promoting flexibility and reducing muscle tightness. The seated position helps isolate the target muscles by removing momentum. Include this in your routine for better mobility and reduced muscle tension.', '61681201', '61681201-Sitting-Diagonal-Side-Stretch-(female)_Stretching_.mp4', 'female', FALSE, '2025-12-03 23:26:37.628647+00', '1. Sit with your back supported, core engaged, feet flat on the floor. 2. Move into the stretch position for Seated Diagonal Side Stretch. 3. Ease into the stretch until you feel gentle tension (not pain). 4. Hold for 20-30 seconds, breathing deeply and relaxing into the stretch. 5. Switch sides and repeat for equal time. Focus on maintaining proper breathing throughout.', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 1, NULL, 1, 1, NULL, 3, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 1, 1, NULL, 1, NULL, TRUE, NULL, 'Stretch', 40, 2, 6, FALSE, TRUE, 'lat_stretch', 'Seated Diagonal Side Stretch', 'stretch_hip, stretch_back, stretch_shoulder', FALSE, 'bodyweight', TRUE, 1, 30, 2, 70, 88, 95, 65),
('435ca1e0-eddf-451d-8549-03369f3cc932', 'W Pose (Against Wall)', 'Full Body', 'Wall', '{"Full Body"}'::text[], '{}'::text[], 'The W Pose Against Wall provides a deep stretch for your full body, ideal for recovery and mobility work. Flexibility work like this enhances performance and prevents stiffness.', '76961201', '76961201-W-Pose-against-Wall-(male)_Stretching_.mp4', 'male', FALSE, '2025-12-03 23:26:22.536005+00', '1. Position yourself at the appropriate distance from a wall. 2. Move into the stretch position for W Pose Against Wall. 3. Ease into the stretch until you feel gentle tension (not pain). 4. Hold for 20-30 seconds, breathing deeply and relaxing into the stretch.', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 1, NULL, 1, 1, NULL, 3, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 1, 1, NULL, 1, NULL, TRUE, NULL, 'Stretch', 42, 2, 6, FALSE, TRUE, 'general_exercise', 'W Pose Against Wall', 'stretch_hip, stretch_back, plank', FALSE, 'bodyweight', TRUE, 1, 30, 2, 70, 88, 95, 65),
('437d7da2-4e40-43c8-8ecc-867b8b2abd43', 'Seated Shoulder Press (Band)', 'Shoulders', 'Resistance Band', '{"Shoulders"}'::text[], '{"Side Delts","Triceps"}'::text[], 'This pressing exercise works your delts for improved shoulder strength and aesthetics. The triceps assist throughout the movement, making this a well-rounded exercise. The seated position helps isolate the target muscles by removing momentum. The band creates increasing tension as it stretches, challenging the lockout. Strong shoulders improve overhead strength and support nearly all upper body movements.', '68731201', '68731201-Band-Seated-Shoulder-Press_Shoulders_.mp4', 'male', FALSE, '2025-12-03 23:26:27.805708+00', '1. Secure the resistance band appropriately for Band Seated Shoulder Press. 2. Sit with your back supported, core engaged, feet flat on the floor. 3. Start with the weight at shoulder level. 4. Press directly overhead until your arms are fully extended. 5. Lower back to shoulder level with control. 6. Complete all reps with control before resting.', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 3, NULL, 7, 7, NULL, 5, 'Seated', NULL, NULL, NULL, 8, 12, NULL, 6, NULL, TRUE, NULL, 'Strength', 87, 7, 8, TRUE, TRUE, 'shoulder_press', 'Seated Shoulder Press', 'lateral_raise, front_raise, rear_delt', FALSE, 'band', FALSE, 3, 90, 4, 60, 85, 90, 50),
('43976eac-6e6a-49c0-834c-a278bbb51bd3', 'Slip Right Slip Left Left Hook Cross (combo)', 'Full Body', 'Bodyweight', '{"Full Body"}'::text[], '{"Shoulders","Core"}'::text[], 'Elevate your training with this movement exercise that develops speed, power, and coordination. Your shoulders, core work as secondary movers, adding to the training stimulus. A versatile bodyweight movement perfect for home or gym training. Develops fast-twitch muscle fibers for quicker, more powerful movements.', '104451201', '104451201-Slip-Right-Slip-Left-Left-Hook-Cross-(combo)_Boxing.mp4', 'male', FALSE, '2025-12-03 23:26:27.805708+00', '1. Set up in the starting position for Slip Right Slip Left Left Hook Cross. 2. Execute the movement with proper form, focusing on your full body. 3. Control both the lifting and lowering phases of the movement. 4. Complete all reps with control before resting.', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 2, NULL, 7, 7, NULL, 5, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 8, 12, NULL, 6, NULL, TRUE, NULL, 'Strength', 50, 7, 8, TRUE, TRUE, 'boxing', 'Slip Right Slip Left Left Hook Cross', 'core_exercise, shoulder_exercise, burpee', FALSE, 'bodyweight', FALSE, 3, 90, 4, 70, 88, 95, 65),
('4398707d-6187-4090-b7d0-295ab06d88d4', 'Standing Overhead Shoulder Stretch', 'Shoulders', 'Bodyweight', '{"Shoulders"}'::text[], '{"Traps"}'::text[], 'This stretching exercise works your delts for improved shoulder strength and aesthetics. The standing position engages your core for stability. No equipment needed—your body provides all the resistance. Strong shoulders improve overhead strength and support nearly all upper body movements.', '46511201', '46511201-Standing-Overhead-Shoulder-Stretch-(VERSION-2)_Shoulders.mp4', 'male', FALSE, '2025-12-03 23:26:29.242428+00', '1. Stand tall with your feet firmly planted. 2. Set up in the starting position for Standing Overhead Shoulder Stretch. 3. Execute the movement with proper form, focusing on your delts. 4. Control both the lifting and lowering phases of the movement. 5. Repeat for the prescribed number of repetitions.', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 1, NULL, 1, 1, NULL, 3, 'Standing', NULL, NULL, NULL, 1, 1, NULL, 1, NULL, TRUE, NULL, 'Stretch', 42, 2, 6, FALSE, TRUE, 'shoulder_stretch', 'Standing Overhead Shoulder Stretch', 'stretch_chest, stretch_tricep, stretch_lat', FALSE, 'bodyweight', TRUE, 1, 30, 2, 70, 88, 95, 65),
('43ba82cd-2931-4620-b14e-211280d30922', 'Dolphin Pose', 'Full Body', 'Bodyweight', '{"Full Body"}'::text[], '{}'::text[], 'Designed to lengthen your full body, the Dolphin Pose helps improve mobility and prevent stiffness. Include this in your routine for better mobility and reduced muscle tension.', '65191201', '65191201-Dolphin-Pose-(male)_Stretching_.mp4', 'male', FALSE, '2025-12-03 23:26:28.397686+00', '1. Move into the stretch position for Dolphin Pose. 2. Ease into the stretch until you feel gentle tension (not pain). 3. Hold for 20-30 seconds, breathing deeply and relaxing into the stretch. Exhale during the exertion phase of the movement.', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 1, NULL, 1, 1, NULL, 3, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 1, 1, NULL, 1, NULL, TRUE, NULL, 'Stretch', 50, 2, 6, FALSE, TRUE, 'general_exercise', 'Dolphin Pose', 'stretch_hip, stretch_back, plank', FALSE, 'bodyweight', TRUE, 1, 30, 2, 70, 88, 95, 65),
('43bdc466-55ad-4b60-aa93-711da9b4114e', 'Standing Around The World (Resistance Band)', 'Shoulders', 'Resistance Band', '{"Shoulders"}'::text[], '{"Traps"}'::text[], 'The Resistance Band Standing Around The World is a flexibility exercise that targets your delts, helping to release tension and improve range of motion. The chest assist throughout the movement, making this a well-rounded exercise. Performing this standing challenges your balance and core engagement. Bands are joint-friendly and portable, perfect for any training environment. Regular stretching improves flexibility, reduces injury risk, and aids recovery.', '73221201', '73221201-Resistance-Band-Standing-Around-the-World-(male)_S.mp4', 'male', FALSE, '2025-12-03 23:26:22.755209+00', '1. Secure the resistance band appropriately for Resistance Band Standing Around The World. 2. Stand with feet about shoulder-width apart. 3. Move into the stretch position for Resistance Band Standing Around The World. 4. Ease into the stretch until you feel gentle tension (not pain). 5. Hold for 20-30 seconds, breathing deeply and relaxing into the stretch.', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 2, NULL, 7, 7, NULL, 5, 'Standing', NULL, NULL, NULL, 8, 12, NULL, 6, NULL, TRUE, NULL, 'Strength', 35, 7, 8, TRUE, TRUE, 'around_world', 'Standing Around The World', 'squat, bench_press, deadlift', FALSE, 'band', FALSE, 3, 90, 4, 60, 85, 90, 50),
('43de97c0-c69b-4e34-894f-98673e30ca1d', 'Bent Over Single Arm Kickback - Rope - Neutral Grip (Cable)', 'Arms', 'Cables', '{"Triceps"}'::text[], '{"Rear Delts"}'::text[], 'The Cable Bent Over Single Arm Neutral Grip Kickback With Rope Attachment targets your triceps through a kicking motion. The hamstrings assist throughout the movement, making this a well-rounded exercise. The bent over position requires core engagement to maintain a neutral spine. Cable resistance creates smooth, continuous muscle engagement. Arm strength supports grip, pulling, and pushing in compound movements.', '45671201', '45671201-Cable-Bent-Over-Single-Arm-Neutral-Grip-Kickback-with-Rope-Attachment_Upper-Arms_.mp4', 'male', FALSE, '2025-12-03 23:26:20.982555+00', '1. Adjust the cable machine to the correct height and attachment for Cable Bent Over Single Arm Neutral Grip Kickback With Rope Attachment. 2. Hinge at your hips, pushing them back while keeping your back flat. 3. Use a neutral grip with palms facing each other. 4. Keep your upper arm stationary and extend your forearm back. 5. Squeeze at full extension, then return with control. 6. Complete all reps on one side, then switch to the other side. 7. Repeat for the prescribed number of repetitions.', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 3, NULL, 5, 7, NULL, 6, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 12, 20, NULL, 4, NULL, FALSE, NULL, 'Strength', 37, 5, 7, FALSE, TRUE, 'tricep_kickback', 'Bent Over Single Arm Kickback - Neutral Grip', 'Bent Over Single Arm Kickback - Neutral Grip', FALSE, 'cable', FALSE, 3, 60, 2, 85, 88, 30, 92),
('43df2e82-0021-483b-adb6-fa13bc1b3eef', 'Sumo Stance Side Lunge', 'Legs', 'Bodyweight', '{"Quads"}'::text[], '{"Glutes","Inner Thighs"}'::text[], 'Target the front of your thighs with this lunging exercise for quad development. You''ll also feel your glutes, hamstrings working to support the movement. No equipment needed—your body provides all the resistance. Lower body strength improves everything from walking to heavy compound lifts.', '88621201', '88621201-Sumo-Stance-Side-Lunges-(female)_Thighs_.mp4', 'female', FALSE, '2025-12-03 23:26:39.340041+00', '1. Step to the side, bending that knee while keeping the other leg straight. 2. Push through your front/working leg to return to the starting position. 3. Complete all reps with control before resting. Maintain a neutral spine throughout. Ideal for quads strength and endurance.', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 2, NULL, 7, 7, NULL, 5, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 8, 12, NULL, 6, NULL, TRUE, NULL, 'Strength', 70, 7, 8, TRUE, TRUE, 'lunge', 'Sumo Stance Side Lunge', 'split_squat, step_up, squat', FALSE, 'bodyweight', FALSE, 3, 90, 4, 70, 88, 95, 65),
('43e02998-e762-4e2c-8ff9-bd1fd63390e4', 'Kneeling Hold To Stand (Kettlebell)', 'Core', 'Kettlebell', '{"Abs"}'::text[], '{"Hip Flexors"}'::text[], 'The Kettlebell Kneeling Hold To Stand is a lower body movement exercise that targets your core. The kneeling position adds a core stability challenge. The kettlebell grip position adds a unique training stimulus. Leg training boosts metabolism and builds functional, real-world strength.', '65201201', '65201201-Kettlebell-Kneeling-Hold-to-Stand_Thighs_.mp4', 'male', FALSE, '2025-12-03 23:26:22.938497+00', '1. Select an appropriately weighted kettlebell for Kettlebell Kneeling Hold To Stand. 2. Kneel on the floor (use a pad for comfort if needed). 3. Hold the position for the prescribed time, maintaining tension.', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 2, NULL, 7, 7, NULL, 5, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 8, 12, NULL, 6, NULL, TRUE, NULL, 'Strength', 53, 7, 8, TRUE, TRUE, 'kneeling_hold', 'Kneeling Hold To Stand', 'squat, leg_extension, lunge', FALSE, 'kettlebell', TRUE, 3, 90, 4, 75, 88, 88, 78),
('43e33e5f-2c9e-4f11-8546-1c12b3b02c0b', 'Calf Raise And Front Squat', 'Legs', 'Bodyweight', '{"Quads"}'::text[], '{"Glutes","Core"}'::text[], 'This squatting movement focuses on your gastrocnemius and soleus. Your glutes, hamstrings work as secondary movers, adding to the training stimulus. A versatile bodyweight movement perfect for home or gym training. Lower body strength improves everything from walking to heavy compound lifts.', '104481201', '104481201-Bodyweight-Calf-Raise-and-Front-Squat-(male)_Thig.mp4', 'male', FALSE, '2025-12-03 23:26:24.577164+00', '1. Push your hips back and bend your knees to lower your body. 2. Keep your chest up and knees tracking over your toes. 3. Drive through your heels to stand back up, squeezing your glutes at the top. 4. Complete all reps with control before resting. Keep the movement smooth and controlled. Include this in your legs training.', 'Squat', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 4, NULL, 5, 7, NULL, 6, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 12, 20, NULL, 4, NULL, TRUE, NULL, 'Strength', 100, 5, 7, FALSE, TRUE, 'front_squat', 'Calf Raise And Front Squat', 'squat, leg_press, leg_extension, goblet_squat', FALSE, 'bodyweight', FALSE, 3, 60, 2, 70, 88, 95, 65),
('43f0b6b7-44cd-4e86-8628-8a8c527343ce', 'Incline Pushdown (Cable)', 'Arms', 'Cables', '{"Triceps"}'::text[], '{"Chest","Shoulders"}'::text[], 'Build a stronger back with this pushing movement targeting your triceps. Using an incline changes the angle of resistance for varied muscle recruitment. The cable setup allows you to adjust the angle of resistance. Back development is crucial for pulling strength and overall upper body function.', '30511201', '30511201-Cable-Incline-Pushdown-(female)_Back_.mp4', 'female', FALSE, '2025-12-03 23:26:31.931873+00', '1. Adjust the cable machine to the correct height and attachment for Cable Incline Pushdown. 2. Set up in the starting position for Cable Incline Pushdown. 3. Execute the movement with proper form, focusing on your triceps. 4. Control both the lifting and lowering phases of the movement. 5. Continue for your target rep count, maintaining good form throughout.', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 2, NULL, 5, 7, NULL, 6, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 12, 20, NULL, 4, NULL, FALSE, NULL, 'Strength', 63, 5, 7, FALSE, TRUE, 'tricep_pushdown', 'Incline Pushdown', 'tricep_extension, close_grip_bench, dip', FALSE, 'cable', FALSE, 3, 60, 2, 85, 88, 30, 92),
('43fbbfce-6e65-4510-9b8e-27b56f909774', 'Hip Extension (Machine)', 'Legs', 'Machine', '{"Glutes"}'::text[], '{"Hamstrings"}'::text[], 'Build stronger glutes with this extension movement focused on hip extension. Secondary activation of your hamstrings provides additional muscle engagement. The machine guides your movement path for safer, more controlled repetitions. Leg training boosts metabolism and builds functional, real-world strength.', '22861201', '22861201-Lever-Hip-Extension-(VERSION-2)_Hips_.mp4', 'male', FALSE, '2025-12-03 23:26:24.203368+00', '1. Adjust the machine settings (seat height, weight, pads) to fit your body for Lever Hip Extension. 2. Extend through the target joint(s) for Lever Hip Extension. 3. Complete all reps with control before resting. Focus on maintaining proper breathing throughout.', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 1, NULL, 5, 7, NULL, 6, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 10, 15, NULL, 4, NULL, FALSE, NULL, 'Strength', 78, 5, 7, FALSE, TRUE, 'glute_kickback', 'Lever Hip Extension', 'hip_thrust, lunge, squat', FALSE, 'machine', FALSE, 3, 60, 2, 80, 75, 20, 88),
('441746bc-01d3-48d2-ba05-33b9bb7b660a', 'Shoulder Transverse Flexion', 'Shoulders', 'Bodyweight', '{"Shoulders"}'::text[], '{"Traps"}'::text[], 'The Shoulder Transverse Flexion is a flexion exercise that targets your delts for shoulder development. This bodyweight exercise requires no equipment and can be done anywhere. Strong shoulders improve overhead strength and support nearly all upper body movements.', '106911201', '106911201-Shoulder---Transverse-Flexion-(female)_.mp4', 'female', FALSE, '2025-12-03 23:26:36.985772+00', '1. Set up in the starting position for Shoulder Transverse Flexion. 2. Execute the movement with proper form, focusing on your delts. 3. Control both the lifting and lowering phases of the movement. 4. Repeat for the prescribed number of repetitions.', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 2, NULL, 7, 7, NULL, 5, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 8, 12, NULL, 6, NULL, TRUE, NULL, 'Strength', 50, 7, 8, TRUE, TRUE, 'shoulder_exercise', 'Shoulder Transverse Flexion', 'lateral_raise, shoulder_press, front_raise', FALSE, 'bodyweight', FALSE, 3, 90, 4, 70, 88, 95, 65),
('441fa386-7a80-4e8f-9024-51cbefbe8bb3', 'Decline Push Up (Gymnastic Rings)', 'Chest', 'Gymnastic Rings', '{"Chest","Lower Chest"}'::text[], '{"Front Delts","Triceps"}'::text[], 'The Ring Decline Push Up is a pushing exercise that targets your chest muscles. You''ll also feel your triceps, front delts working to support the movement. The decline position targets the lower portion of the muscles more intensely. A well-developed chest contributes to upper body strength and aesthetics.', '78741201', '78741201-Ring-Decline-Push-up_Chest_.mp4', 'male', FALSE, '2025-12-03 23:26:26.678791+00', '1. Keep your body in a straight line from head to heels throughout. 2. Lower your chest toward the floor by bending your elbows. 3. Push through your palms to return to the starting position. 4. Complete all reps with control before resting. Ensure full range of motion on each rep. This exercise is excellent for chest development. Variation: Ring Decline Push Up.', 'Push Up', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 3, NULL, 7, 7, NULL, 5, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 8, 12, NULL, 6, NULL, TRUE, NULL, 'Strength', 61, 7, 8, TRUE, TRUE, 'push_up', 'Ring Decline Push Up', 'bench_press, chest_fly, dip', TRUE, 'gymnastic_rings', FALSE, 3, 90, 4, 68, 85, 85, 70),
('442126d6-8679-453e-b774-c346441b4c0f', 'Roll Thoracic Spine Lying On Floor', 'Core', 'Bodyweight', '{"Abs"}'::text[], '{"Hip Flexors"}'::text[], 'The Roll Thoracic Spine Lying On Floor is a movement exercise that develops back strength and muscle. The lying position provides back support and helps isolate the target muscles. A versatile bodyweight movement perfect for home or gym training. Back development is crucial for pulling strength and overall upper body function.', '54231201', '54231201-Roll-Thoracic-Spine-Lying-on-Floor-(female)_Back_.mp4', 'female', FALSE, '2025-12-03 23:26:36.38616+00', '1. Position yourself on the floor for Roll Thoracic Spine Lying On Floor. 2. Lie down in the appropriate position for Roll Thoracic Spine Lying On Floor. 3. Repeat for the prescribed number of repetitions.', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 2, NULL, 7, 7, NULL, 5, 'Lying', NULL, NULL, NULL, 8, 12, NULL, 6, NULL, TRUE, NULL, 'Strength', 45, 7, 8, TRUE, TRUE, 'spinal_stretch', 'Roll Thoracic Spine Lying On Floor', 'running, elliptical, rowing_cardio', FALSE, 'bodyweight', FALSE, 3, 90, 4, 70, 88, 95, 65),
('442bc2d7-b17f-4e6b-9ced-96c6d691ed45', 'Seated Chest Fly (Cable)', 'Chest', 'Cables', '{"Chest"}'::text[], '{"Front Delts"}'::text[], 'Target your chest with the Cable Seated Chest Fly, an effective flying movement for upper body strength. Your front delts work as secondary movers, adding to the training stimulus. The seated position helps isolate the target muscles by removing momentum. Cable resistance creates smooth, continuous muscle engagement. A well-developed chest contributes to upper body strength and aesthetics.', '38691201', '38691201-Cable-Seated-Chest-Fly_Chest_.mp4', 'male', FALSE, '2025-12-03 23:26:24.831811+00', '1. Adjust the cable machine to the correct height and attachment for Cable Seated Chest Fly. 2. Sit with your back supported, core engaged, feet flat on the floor. 3. With a slight bend in your elbows, move the weight in a wide arc. 4. Squeeze your chest muscles at the center/top of the movement. 5. Return with control, feeling the stretch at the bottom. 6. Continue for your target rep count, maintaining good form throughout.', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 1, NULL, 5, 7, NULL, 6, 'Seated', NULL, NULL, NULL, 12, 20, NULL, 4, NULL, FALSE, NULL, 'Strength', 92, 5, 7, FALSE, TRUE, 'chest_fly', 'Seated Chest Fly', 'bench_press, incline_press, push_up', FALSE, 'cable', FALSE, 3, 60, 2, 85, 88, 30, 92),
('443033f5-2fee-425c-9445-e29af3743cb3', 'Side Squat', 'Legs', 'Bodyweight', '{"Quads"}'::text[], '{"Glutes","Hamstrings"}'::text[], 'Target the front of your thighs with this squatting exercise for quad development. You''ll also feel your glutes, hamstrings working to support the movement. No equipment needed—your body provides all the resistance. Strong legs are the foundation for athletic performance and functional fitness.', '47891201', '47891201-Side-Squat_Thighs_.mp4', 'male', FALSE, '2025-12-03 23:26:29.971345+00', '1. Push your hips back and bend your knees to lower your body. 2. Keep your chest up and knees tracking over your toes. 3. Drive through your heels to stand back up, squeezing your glutes at the top. 4. Continue for your target rep count, maintaining good form throughout. Keep the movement smooth and controlled. Include this in your legs training.', 'Squat', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 3, NULL, 7, 7, NULL, 5, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 8, 12, NULL, 6, NULL, TRUE, NULL, 'Strength', 85, 7, 8, TRUE, TRUE, 'squat', 'Side Squat', 'leg_press, front_squat, goblet_squat, lunge, leg_extension', FALSE, 'bodyweight', FALSE, 3, 90, 4, 70, 88, 95, 65),
('4433dd1a-1240-4896-9965-5947c39fe88c', 'Over Bench Single Arm Wrist Curl (Dumbbell)', 'Arms', 'Dumbbells', '{"Forearms"}'::text[], '{}'::text[], 'The Dumbbell Over Bench One Arm Wrist Curl strengthens your forearms and grip through a curling motion. The forearms assist throughout the movement, making this a well-rounded exercise. Dumbbells allow each arm to work independently, helping correct imbalances. Dedicated arm training builds both strength and muscular definition.', '3671201', '03671201-Dumbbell-Over-Bench-One-Arm-Wrist-Curl_Forearms_.mp4', 'male', FALSE, '2025-12-03 23:26:21.995567+00', '1. Select an appropriate weight dumbbell and hold it in one hand. 2. Keep your elbows in a fixed position throughout the movement. 3. Curl the weight up by contracting your biceps, squeezing at the top. 4. Lower with control, resisting the weight on the way down. 5. Complete all reps on one side, then switch to the other side. 6. Repeat for the prescribed number of repetitions. Don''t rush—quality over quantity.', 'Curl', 'Pull', NULL, NULL, NULL, 3, NULL, 5, 7, NULL, 6, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 12, 20, NULL, 4, NULL, TRUE, NULL, 'Strength', 77, 5, 7, FALSE, TRUE, 'wrist_curl', 'Over Bench Single Arm Wrist Curl', 'tricep_pushdown, tricep_extension, hammer_curl, preacher_curl', TRUE, 'dumbbell', FALSE, 3, 60, 2, 92, 90, 92, 90),
('444b2972-ad10-4396-a3b9-88d2922a73df', 'Seated Side Bend (Chair)', 'Core', 'Chair', '{"Obliques"}'::text[], '{"Abs"}'::text[], 'Strengthen your midsection with this movement movement that works your abs. Your abs work as secondary movers, adding to the training stimulus. Being seated provides stability, allowing you to focus on the working muscles. A strong core improves posture, protects your spine, and enhances all other lifts.', '91611201', '91611201-Sitting-Side-Bend-on-a-Chair-(female)_Waist_.mp4', 'female', FALSE, '2025-12-03 23:26:37.877283+00', '1. Position yourself with a sturdy chair for support or as part of the movement. 2. Sit with your back supported, core engaged, feet flat on the floor. 3. Complete all reps with control before resting. Engage your stabilizer muscles for better control. Works well for abs activation.', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 2, NULL, 7, 7, NULL, 5, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 8, 12, NULL, 6, NULL, TRUE, NULL, 'Strength', 35, 7, 8, TRUE, TRUE, 'side_bend', 'Seated Side Bend On A Chair', 'russian_twist, woodchop, oblique_crunch', FALSE, 'bodyweight', FALSE, 3, 90, 4, 70, 88, 95, 65),
('444ea37b-1fd4-45c0-b0ba-349654496425', 'Standing Toe Down Hamstring Stretch (Gymnastic Rings)', 'Legs', 'Gymnastic Rings', '{"Hamstrings"}'::text[], '{"Glutes"}'::text[], 'Strengthen the back of your thighs with this stretching exercise. The standing position engages your core for stability. Strong legs are the foundation for athletic performance and functional fitness.', '19081201', '19081201-Standing-Toe-Down-Hamstring-Stretch_Thighs_.mp4', 'male', FALSE, '2025-12-03 23:26:23.288245+00', '1. Stand tall with your feet firmly planted. 2. Set up in the starting position for Standing Toe Down Hamstring Stretch. 3. Execute the movement with proper form, focusing on your hamstrings. 4. Control both the lifting and lowering phases of the movement. 5. Repeat for the prescribed number of repetitions.', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 1, NULL, 1, 1, NULL, 3, 'Standing', NULL, NULL, NULL, 1, 1, NULL, 1, NULL, TRUE, NULL, 'Stretch', 30, 2, 6, FALSE, TRUE, 'hamstring_stretch', 'Standing Toe Down Hamstring Stretch', 'stretch_hip, stretch_calf, stretch_back', FALSE, 'gymnastic_rings', TRUE, 1, 30, 2, 68, 85, 85, 70),
('4456b8d9-15a9-4435-afc6-f5e7637bc8d1', 'Back Kick Overhead Press', 'Shoulders', 'Bodyweight', '{"Front Delts"}'::text[], '{"Side Delts","Triceps"}'::text[], 'The Back Kick Overhead Press is an explosive exercise that combines cardiovascular training with dynamic pressing movements. The triceps assist throughout the movement, making this a well-rounded exercise. This bodyweight exercise requires no equipment and can be done anywhere. Great for improving athletic performance, burning calories, and building conditioning.', '60961201', '60961201-Back-Kick-Overhead-Press-(female)_Plyometrics_.mp4', 'female', FALSE, '2025-12-03 23:26:30.685158+00', '1. Start with the weight at shoulder level. 2. Press directly overhead until your arms are fully extended. 3. Lower back to shoulder level with control. 4. Complete all reps with control before resting. Keep your shoulders relaxed and away from your ears.', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 3, NULL, 7, 7, NULL, 5, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 8, 12, NULL, 6, NULL, TRUE, NULL, 'Strength', 85, 7, 8, TRUE, TRUE, 'shoulder_press', 'Back Kick Overhead Press', 'lateral_raise, front_raise, rear_delt', FALSE, 'bodyweight', FALSE, 3, 90, 4, 70, 88, 95, 65),
('4458e20e-29c8-4c97-a2dc-e0fd9c0a38f7', 'Sumo Squat', 'Legs', 'Bodyweight', '{"Quads"}'::text[], '{"Glutes","Inner Thighs","Hamstrings"}'::text[], 'This squatting movement emphasizes your quadriceps for stronger, more powerful legs. Secondary activation of your glutes, hamstrings provides additional muscle engagement. A versatile bodyweight movement perfect for home or gym training. Strong legs are the foundation for athletic performance and functional fitness.', '8021201', '08021201-Sumo-Squat_Thighs.mp4', 'female', FALSE, '2025-12-03 23:26:39.340041+00', '1. Push your hips back and bend your knees to lower your body. 2. Keep your chest up and knees tracking over your toes. 3. Drive through your heels to stand back up, squeezing your glutes at the top. 4. Continue for your target rep count, maintaining good form throughout. Start with lighter weight to perfect your form. Ideal for quads strength and endurance. Variation: Sumo Squat.', 'Squat', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 2, NULL, 7, 7, NULL, 5, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 8, 12, NULL, 6, NULL, TRUE, NULL, 'Strength', 85, 7, 8, TRUE, TRUE, 'squat', 'Sumo Squat', 'leg_press, front_squat, goblet_squat, lunge, leg_extension', FALSE, 'bodyweight', FALSE, 3, 90, 4, 70, 88, 95, 65),
('44731918-6ac4-435c-833d-900ef45471a5', 'Abdominal Leg Raise (Machine)', 'Core', 'Machine', '{"Lower Abs"}'::text[], '{"Hip Flexors"}'::text[], 'Build a stronger core with the Lever Abdominal Leg Raise, focusing on your abs. The hip flexors assist throughout the movement, making this a well-rounded exercise. Machine exercises are great for isolating muscles and training to failure safely. Building core stability helps with everything from heavy deadlifts to daily activities.', '65081201', '65081201-Lever-Abdominal-Leg-Raise-(male)_Waist_.mp4', 'male', FALSE, '2025-12-03 23:26:24.831811+00', '1. Adjust the machine settings (seat height, weight, pads) to fit your body for Lever Abdominal Leg Raise. 2. Keeping legs mostly straight, raise them toward the ceiling. 3. Lower with control, stopping just before touching down. 4. Continue for your target rep count, maintaining good form throughout.', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 1, NULL, 5, 7, NULL, 6, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 12, 20, NULL, 4, NULL, FALSE, NULL, 'Strength', 78, 5, 7, FALSE, TRUE, 'leg_raise', 'Lever Abdominal Leg Raise', 'crunch, plank, v_up', FALSE, 'machine', FALSE, 3, 60, 2, 80, 75, 20, 88),
('4477035a-f10d-456a-9fb4-905615740ca5', 'Ring Inverted Row (Gymnastic Rings)', 'Back', 'Gymnastic Rings', '{"Upper Back"}'::text[], '{"Lats","Biceps","Rear Delts"}'::text[], 'The Ring Inverted Row is a rowing exercise that builds thickness in your upper back. Secondary activation of your biceps provides additional muscle engagement. Back development is crucial for pulling strength and overall upper body function.', '74541201', '74541201-Ring-Inverted-Row-(female)_Back_.mp4', 'female', FALSE, '2025-12-03 23:26:36.38616+00', '1. Pull the weight toward your torso, leading with your elbow(s). 2. Squeeze your shoulder blades together at the peak contraction. 3. Extend back out with control, feeling the stretch in your back. 4. Repeat for the prescribed number of repetitions. Focus on maintaining proper breathing throughout.', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 3, NULL, 7, 7, NULL, 5, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 8, 12, NULL, 6, NULL, TRUE, NULL, 'Strength', 58, 7, 8, TRUE, TRUE, 'general_exercise', 'Ring Inverted Row', 'lat_pulldown, bent_over_row, pull_up', FALSE, 'gymnastic_rings', FALSE, 3, 90, 4, 68, 85, 85, 70),
('447c1ebb-c587-4d71-968c-a4b05b4318a7', 'Side Press (Dumbbell) - Alternating', 'Shoulders', 'Dumbbells', '{"Front Delts"}'::text[], '{"Side Delts","Triceps"}'::text[], 'The Dumbbell Alternate Side Press is a pressing exercise that targets your delts for shoulder development. The dumbbell variation provides freedom of movement and greater range of motion. Shoulder development enhances both performance and upper body aesthetics.', '25921201', '25921201-Dumbbell-Alternate-Side-Press-(female)_Shoulders_.mp4', 'female', FALSE, '2025-12-03 23:26:32.624497+00', '1. Select a pair of dumbbells at an appropriate weight for Dumbbell Alternate Side Press. 2. Start with the weight at shoulder level. 3. Press directly overhead until your arms are fully extended. 4. Lower back to shoulder level with control. 5. Alternate between sides/arms/legs with each repetition. 6. Repeat for the prescribed number of repetitions.', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 2, NULL, 7, 8, NULL, 5, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 8, 12, NULL, 6, NULL, TRUE, NULL, 'Strength', 82, 7, 8, TRUE, TRUE, 'general_exercise', 'Side Press - Alternating', 'squat, bench_press, deadlift', TRUE, 'dumbbell', FALSE, 3, 90, 4, 92, 90, 92, 90),
('44868de0-cca5-41bb-acc5-0cf239a13877', 'Overhead Leg Lift Tap', 'Full Body', 'Bodyweight', '{"Full Body"}'::text[], '{}'::text[], 'Build power and athleticism with this high-intensity movement exercise that challenges your entire body. A versatile bodyweight movement perfect for home or gym training. Great for improving athletic performance, burning calories, and building conditioning. Maintain proper breathing - exhale during the effort phase.', '81791201', '81791201-Overhead-Leg-Lift-Tap-(male)_Plyometrics_.mp4', 'male', FALSE, '2025-12-03 23:26:29.242428+00', '1. Set up in the starting position for Overhead Leg Lift Tap. 2. Execute the movement with proper form, focusing on your full body. 3. Control both the lifting and lowering phases of the movement. 4. Repeat for the prescribed number of repetitions.', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 2, NULL, 7, 7, NULL, 5, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 8, 12, NULL, 6, NULL, TRUE, NULL, 'Strength', 50, 7, 8, TRUE, TRUE, 'leg_exercise', 'Overhead Leg Lift Tap', 'crunch, plank, russian_twist, hanging_knee_raise', FALSE, 'bodyweight', FALSE, 3, 90, 4, 70, 88, 95, 65),
('4488783c-5cb7-4a7b-8f3f-6d6926443add', 'Gobelt Curtsey Lunge (Dumbbell)', 'Legs', 'Dumbbells', '{"Quads"}'::text[], '{"Glutes","Hamstrings"}'::text[], 'This lunging movement emphasizes your quadriceps for stronger, more powerful legs. The glutes, hamstrings assist throughout the movement, making this a well-rounded exercise. The dumbbell variation provides freedom of movement and greater range of motion. Lower body strength improves everything from walking to heavy compound lifts.', '57311201', '57311201-Dumbbell-Gobelt-Curtsey-Lunge-(female)_Thighs_.mp4', 'female', FALSE, '2025-12-03 23:26:32.735372+00', '1. Select a pair of dumbbells at an appropriate weight for Dumbbell Gobelt Curtsey Lunge. 2. Step forward into a lunge until both knees are at about 90 degrees. 3. Push through your front/working leg to return to the starting position. 4. Complete all reps with control before resting.', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 3, NULL, 7, 8, NULL, 5, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 8, 12, NULL, 6, NULL, TRUE, NULL, 'Strength', 82, 7, 8, TRUE, TRUE, 'lunge', 'Gobelt Curtsey Lunge', 'split_squat, step_up, squat', TRUE, 'dumbbell', FALSE, 3, 90, 4, 92, 90, 92, 90),
('44917f50-05ab-41a4-990a-84ada3346a7a', 'Pushdown - Reverse Grip (Cable)', 'Arms', 'Cables', '{"Triceps"}'::text[], '{"Chest","Shoulders"}'::text[], 'The Cable Reverse Grip Pushdown targets your triceps through a pushing motion. Cable resistance creates smooth, continuous muscle engagement. Dedicated arm training builds both strength and muscular definition.', '25201201', '25201201-Cable-Reverse-grip-Pushdown-(female)_Upper-Arms_.mp4', 'female', FALSE, '2025-12-03 23:26:32.054831+00', '1. Adjust the cable machine to the correct height and attachment for Cable Reverse Grip Pushdown. 2. Use a reverse grip (opposite of the standard grip for this exercise). 3. Repeat for the prescribed number of repetitions.', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 2, NULL, 5, 7, NULL, 6, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 12, 20, NULL, 4, NULL, FALSE, NULL, 'Strength', 60, 5, 7, FALSE, TRUE, 'tricep_pushdown', 'Pushdown - Reverse Grip', 'Pushdown - Reverse Grip', FALSE, 'cable', FALSE, 3, 60, 2, 85, 88, 30, 92),
('44a2963f-fab0-49e7-96f0-57bdbc1ac16b', 'Kneeling Shoulder Bottom Up Hold (Kettlebell)', 'Core', 'Kettlebell', '{"Abs"}'::text[], '{"Hip Flexors"}'::text[], 'Build stronger shoulders with this movement movement focusing on your core. The kneeling position adds a core stability challenge. Kettlebells are excellent for building functional, real-world strength. Strong shoulders improve overhead strength and support nearly all upper body movements.', '65831201', '65831201-Kettlebell-Kneeling-Shoulder-Bottom-Up-Hold_Should.mp4', 'male', FALSE, '2025-12-03 23:26:23.172397+00', '1. Select an appropriately weighted kettlebell for Kettlebell Kneeling Shoulder Bottom Up Hold. 2. Kneel on the floor (use a pad for comfort if needed). 3. Hold the position for the prescribed time, maintaining tension.', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 2, NULL, 7, 7, NULL, 5, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 8, 12, NULL, 6, NULL, TRUE, NULL, 'Strength', 53, 7, 8, TRUE, TRUE, 'shoulder_exercise', 'Kneeling Shoulder Bottom Up Hold', 'squat, leg_extension, lunge', FALSE, 'kettlebell', TRUE, 3, 90, 4, 75, 88, 88, 78),
('44a2c02e-b765-4444-93ae-8b10f9129b04', 'Mid Back Elbow Squeeze', 'Back', 'Bodyweight', '{"Upper Back"}'::text[], '{"Rear Delts"}'::text[], 'This movement exercise strengthens the muscles between your shoulder blades. Your rear delts work as secondary movers, adding to the training stimulus. A versatile bodyweight movement perfect for home or gym training. Back development is crucial for pulling strength and overall upper body function.', '85851201', '85851201-Mid-Back-Elbow-Squeez-(female)_Back_.mp4', 'female', FALSE, '2025-12-03 23:26:35.532804+00', '1. Set up in the starting position for Mid Back Elbow Squeeze. 2. Execute the movement with proper form, focusing on your upper back. 3. Control both the lifting and lowering phases of the movement. 4. Complete all reps with control before resting.', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 2, NULL, 7, 7, NULL, 5, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 8, 12, NULL, 6, NULL, TRUE, NULL, 'Strength', 50, 7, 8, TRUE, TRUE, 'back_exercise', 'Mid Back Elbow Squeeze', 'lat_pulldown, bent_over_row, pull_up', FALSE, 'bodyweight', FALSE, 3, 90, 4, 70, 88, 95, 65),
('44b67b6a-5b1b-44b9-a73c-75cf6d24dae8', 'Chest Press - Neutral Grip (Cable)', 'Chest', 'Cables', '{"Chest"}'::text[], '{"Triceps","Front Delts"}'::text[], 'Target your chest with the Cable Neutral Grip Chest Press, an effective pressing movement for upper body strength. Your triceps, front delts work as secondary movers, adding to the training stimulus. Cables provide constant tension throughout the full range of motion. A well-developed chest contributes to upper body strength and aesthetics.', '64961201', '64961201-Cable-Neutral-grip-Chest-Press_Chest_.mp4', 'male', FALSE, '2025-12-03 23:26:24.099303+00', '1. Adjust the cable machine to the correct height and attachment for Cable Neutral Grip Chest Press. 2. Use a neutral grip with palms facing each other. 3. Lower the weight toward your chest with control. 4. Press the weight up until your arms are extended (don''t lock elbows). 5. Complete all reps with control before resting.', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 3, NULL, 7, 8, NULL, 5, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 8, 12, NULL, 6, NULL, FALSE, NULL, 'Strength', 80, 7, 8, TRUE, TRUE, 'bench_press', 'Chest Press - Neutral Grip', 'Chest Press - Neutral Grip', FALSE, 'cable', FALSE, 3, 90, 4, 85, 88, 30, 92),
('44b84594-1358-42eb-9711-608ace469dd0', 'Squat Twist (Band)', 'Legs', 'Resistance Band', '{"Quads"}'::text[], '{"Glutes","Hamstrings"}'::text[], 'Build rotational power and define your waistline with the Band Squat Twist. Your abs work as secondary movers, adding to the training stimulus. Bands are joint-friendly and portable, perfect for any training environment. Core strength is foundational for athletic performance and injury prevention.', '41371201', '41371201-Band-Squat-Twist_Waist_.mp4', 'male', FALSE, '2025-12-03 23:26:24.698781+00', '1. Secure the resistance band appropriately for Band Squat Twist. 2. Push your hips back and bend your knees to lower your body. 3. Keep your chest up and knees tracking over your toes. 4. Drive through your heels to stand back up, squeezing your glutes at the top. 5. Continue for your target rep count, maintaining good form throughout.', 'Squat', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 3, NULL, 5, 7, NULL, 6, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 10, 15, NULL, 4, NULL, TRUE, NULL, 'Strength', 90, 5, 7, FALSE, TRUE, 'squat', 'Squat Twist', 'leg_press, front_squat, goblet_squat, lunge, leg_extension', FALSE, 'band', FALSE, 3, 60, 2, 60, 85, 90, 50),
('44b96390-e9a2-4dab-bd44-c9ab2d7f362b', 'Pull Through (Band)', 'Legs', 'Resistance Band, Anchor Point', '{"Quads"}'::text[], '{"Glutes","Hamstrings"}'::text[], 'The Band Pull Through is a hip-dominant pulling exercise that targets your glutes. Secondary activation of your hamstrings provides additional muscle engagement. The band creates increasing tension as it stretches, challenging the lockout. Lower body strength improves everything from walking to heavy compound lifts.', '9911201', '09911201-Band-pull-through_Hips.mp4', 'male', FALSE, '2025-12-03 23:26:20.982555+00', '1. Secure the resistance band appropriately for Band Pull Through. 2. Set up in the starting position for Band Pull Through. 3. Execute the movement with proper form, focusing on your glutes. 4. Control both the lifting and lowering phases of the movement. 5. Repeat for the prescribed number of repetitions.', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 2, NULL, 7, 7, NULL, 5, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 8, 12, NULL, 6, NULL, TRUE, NULL, 'Strength', 55, 7, 8, TRUE, TRUE, 'pull_through', 'Pull Through', 'lat_pulldown, bent_over_row, pull_up', FALSE, 'band', FALSE, 3, 90, 4, 60, 85, 90, 50),
('44bef00d-259b-4b51-946f-f8895f12557b', 'Seated Double Jab (Chair)', 'Full Body', 'Chair', '{"Shoulders"}'::text[], '{"Biceps","Triceps","Core"}'::text[], 'Elevate your training with this movement exercise that develops speed, power, and coordination. You''ll also feel your shoulders, core working to support the movement. The seated position helps isolate the target muscles by removing momentum. Plyometric training builds explosive power that transfers to sports and daily activities.', '104881201', '104881201-Seated-Double-Jab-on-Chair-(male)_Chest_.mp4', 'male', FALSE, '2025-12-03 23:26:24.831811+00', '1. Position yourself with a sturdy chair for support or as part of the movement. 2. Sit with your back supported, core engaged, feet flat on the floor. 3. Complete all reps with control before resting. Keep your shoulders relaxed and away from your ears.', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 2, NULL, 7, 7, NULL, 5, 'Seated', NULL, NULL, NULL, 8, 12, NULL, 6, NULL, TRUE, NULL, 'Strength', 37, 7, 8, TRUE, TRUE, 'boxing', 'Seated Double Jab On Chair', 'core_exercise, shoulder_exercise, burpee', FALSE, 'bodyweight', FALSE, 3, 90, 4, 70, 88, 95, 65),
('44c2df45-ef16-4414-8322-07ba960c20da', 'Plank Scapular Push Up', 'Chest', 'Bodyweight', '{"Chest"}'::text[], '{"Triceps","Front Delts"}'::text[], 'Build a stronger back with this pushing movement targeting your chest. Your triceps, front delts work as secondary movers, adding to the training stimulus. This bodyweight exercise requires no equipment and can be done anywhere. Back development is crucial for pulling strength and overall upper body function.', '81381201', '81381201-Plank-Scapular-Push-up-(male)_Back_.mp4', 'male', FALSE, '2025-12-03 23:26:28.968567+00', '1. Keep your body in a straight line from head to heels throughout. 2. Lower your chest toward the floor by bending your elbows. 3. Push through your palms to return to the starting position. 4. Continue for your target rep count, maintaining good form throughout. Ensure full range of motion on each rep. This variation specifically emphasizes the chest.', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 2, NULL, 7, 7, NULL, 5, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 8, 12, NULL, 6, NULL, TRUE, NULL, 'Strength', 70, 7, 8, TRUE, TRUE, 'push_up', 'Plank Scapular Push Up', 'bench_press, chest_fly, dip', TRUE, 'bodyweight', FALSE, 3, 90, 4, 70, 88, 95, 65),
('44cb54d0-92d4-416f-9477-4dca950941c2', 'Clean Grip Front Squat (Barbell)', 'Legs', 'Barbell', '{"Quads","Glutes","Core"}'::text[], '{}'::text[], 'Target the front of your thighs with this squatting exercise for quad development. The glutes, hamstrings assist throughout the movement, making this a well-rounded exercise. Using a barbell provides stability for progressive overload. Lower body strength improves everything from walking to heavy compound lifts. Perfect for including in both strength and hypertrophy programs.', '57161201', '57161201-Barbell-Clean-grip-Front-Squat-(female)_Thighs_.mp4', 'female', FALSE, '2025-12-03 23:26:31.013316+00', '1. Set up a barbell in a rack at the appropriate height for Barbell Clean Grip Front Squat. 2. Push your hips back and bend your knees to lower your body. 3. Keep your chest up and knees tracking over your toes. 4. Drive through your heels to stand back up, squeezing your glutes at the top. 5. Complete all reps with control before resting.', 'Squat', 'Push', 'Compound', 'Bilateral', NULL, 4, NULL, 10, 10, NULL, 4, 'Standing', NULL, 'Overhand (Pronated)', 'Standard (Just outside shoulders)', 3, 6, NULL, 9, NULL, TRUE, NULL, 'Strength', 97, 7, 9, TRUE, FALSE, 'front_squat', 'Clean Grip Front Squat', 'squat, leg_press, leg_extension, goblet_squat', TRUE, 'barbell', FALSE, 4, 120, 6, 95, 80, 65, 95);
INSERT INTO _exercise_staging (id, name, category, equipment, primary_muscles, secondary_muscles, description, video_code, video_filename, gender, is_custom, created_at, steps_to_perform, movement_pattern, force_type, movement_type, laterality, plane_of_motion, difficulty_level, complexity_score, strength_rating, hypertrophy_rating, power_rating, endurance_rating, body_position, bench_angle, grip_type, grip_width, optimal_rep_range_min, optimal_rep_range_max, placement_in_workout, fatigability, popularity_score, home_gym_friendly, instructions, workout_type, practicality_score, fat_loss_rating, general_fitness_rating, is_compound, supersetable, exercise_family, base_exercise_name, complementary_families, is_equipment_primary, equipment_category, duration_based, recommended_sets, rest_seconds, muscles_worked_count, priority_build_muscle, priority_get_lean, priority_home, priority_gym) VALUES
('44de55a9-6df8-4df0-9920-5602fdd69148', 'Overhead Triceps Stretch', 'Arms', 'Bodyweight', '{"Triceps"}'::text[], '{"Shoulders"}'::text[], 'This stretching movement isolates your triceps for improved arm development. This bodyweight exercise requires no equipment and can be done anywhere. Dedicated arm training builds both strength and muscular definition.', '6431201', '06431201-Overhead-Triceps-Stretch_Upper-Arms-FIX_.mp4', 'male', FALSE, '2025-12-03 23:26:21.249384+00', '1. Set up in the starting position for Overhead Triceps Stretch. 2. Execute the movement with proper form, focusing on your triceps. 3. Control both the lifting and lowering phases of the movement. 4. Complete all reps with control before resting. Maintain a neutral spine throughout.', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 1, NULL, 1, 1, NULL, 3, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 1, 1, NULL, 1, NULL, TRUE, NULL, 'Stretch', 40, 2, 6, FALSE, TRUE, 'tricep_stretch', 'Overhead Triceps Stretch', 'bicep_curl, dip', FALSE, 'bodyweight', TRUE, 1, 30, 2, 70, 88, 95, 65),
('4508d252-0d03-41b4-9d0c-5dab19f7587e', 'Oblique Crunch Floor', 'Core', 'Bodyweight', '{"Obliques"}'::text[], '{"Abs"}'::text[], 'Strengthen your midsection with this crunching movement that works your abs. Secondary activation of your abs provides additional muscle engagement. This bodyweight exercise requires no equipment and can be done anywhere. Building core stability helps with everything from heavy deadlifts to daily activities.', '6351201', '06351201-Oblique-Crunches-Floor_Waist-FIX_.mp4', 'male', FALSE, '2025-12-03 23:26:27.145158+00', '1. Position yourself on the floor for Oblique Crunches Floor. 2. Curl your shoulders off the floor by contracting your abs. 3. Don''t pull on your neck—focus on the abdominal contraction. 4. Lower with control, maintaining some tension. 5. Repeat for the prescribed number of repetitions.', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 2, NULL, 5, 7, NULL, 6, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 12, 20, NULL, 4, NULL, TRUE, NULL, 'Strength', 65, 5, 7, FALSE, TRUE, 'crunch', 'Oblique Crunch Floor', 'leg_raise, plank, russian_twist, v_up', TRUE, 'bodyweight', FALSE, 3, 60, 2, 70, 88, 95, 65),
('451bfd52-7396-4eed-8f2c-d7033ed17861', 'Standing Wide Good Morning', 'Back', 'Bodyweight', '{"Lower Back"}'::text[], '{"Hamstrings","Glutes"}'::text[], 'Use this stretch to open up your full body area and enhance overall flexibility. The glutes, lower back assist throughout the movement, making this a well-rounded exercise. The standing position engages your core for stability. Include this in your routine for better mobility and reduced muscle tension.', '87741201', '87741201-Standing-Wide-Good-Morning-(female)_Stretching_.mp4', 'female', FALSE, '2025-12-03 23:26:38.992671+00', '1. Stand tall with your feet firmly planted. 2. Move into the stretch position for Standing Wide Good Morning. 3. Ease into the stretch until you feel gentle tension (not pain). 4. Hold for 20-30 seconds, breathing deeply and relaxing into the stretch.', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 3, NULL, 7, 7, NULL, 5, 'Standing', NULL, NULL, NULL, 8, 12, NULL, 6, NULL, TRUE, NULL, 'Strength', 52, 7, 8, TRUE, TRUE, 'back_extension', 'Standing Wide Good Morning', 'romanian_deadlift, back_extension, hip_thrust', FALSE, 'bodyweight', FALSE, 3, 90, 4, 70, 88, 95, 65),
('451e77ff-ac6e-4833-993f-93c70306f95f', 'Seated Legs Circle Over Bench', 'Core', 'Bodyweight', '{"Abs"}'::text[], '{"Hip Flexors"}'::text[], 'Build a stronger core with the Seated Legs Circle Over Bench, focusing on your abs. The seated position helps isolate the target muscles by removing momentum. Building core stability helps with everything from heavy deadlifts to daily activities.', '78041201', '78041201-Seated-Legs-Circle-over-Bench_Waist_.mp4', 'male', FALSE, '2025-12-03 23:26:26.39056+00', '1. Sit with your back supported, core engaged, feet flat on the floor. 2. Set up in the starting position for Seated Legs Circle Over Bench. 3. Execute the movement with proper form, focusing on your abs. 4. Control both the lifting and lowering phases of the movement. 5. Complete all reps with control before resting.', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 2, NULL, 7, 7, NULL, 5, 'Seated', NULL, NULL, NULL, 8, 12, NULL, 6, NULL, TRUE, NULL, 'Strength', 52, 7, 8, TRUE, TRUE, 'leg_exercise', 'Seated Legs Circle Over Bench', 'squat, lunge, leg_press', FALSE, 'bodyweight', FALSE, 3, 90, 4, 70, 88, 95, 65),
('4528fe92-0774-46d3-bdf8-70b0a0bad331', 'Bench Hip Extension', 'Legs', 'Bodyweight', '{"Glutes"}'::text[], '{"Hamstrings"}'::text[], 'The Bench Hip Extension is a hip-dominant extension exercise that targets your glutes. The hamstrings assist throughout the movement, making this a well-rounded exercise. Leg training boosts metabolism and builds functional, real-world strength.', '1301201', '01301201-Bench-Hip-Extension_Hips_.mp4', 'male', FALSE, '2025-12-03 23:26:26.808474+00', '1. Extend through the target joint(s) for Bench Hip Extension. 2. Set up in the starting position for Bench Hip Extension. 3. Execute the movement with proper form, focusing on your glutes. 4. Control both the lifting and lowering phases of the movement. 5. Repeat for the prescribed number of repetitions.', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 2, NULL, 5, 7, NULL, 6, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 10, 15, NULL, 4, NULL, TRUE, NULL, 'Strength', 70, 5, 7, FALSE, TRUE, 'glute_kickback', 'Bench Hip Extension', 'hip_thrust, lunge, squat', FALSE, 'bodyweight', FALSE, 3, 60, 2, 70, 88, 95, 65),
('452d1621-0773-428b-80c3-b2cc236d1f08', 'Russian Twist', 'Core', 'Bodyweight', '{"Obliques"}'::text[], '{"Abs"}'::text[], 'Build rotational power and define your waistline with the Russian Twist. You''ll also feel your abs working to support the movement. No equipment needed—your body provides all the resistance. Building core stability helps with everything from heavy deadlifts to daily activities.', '25381201', '25381201-Russian-Twist-(female)_waist.mp4', 'female', FALSE, '2025-12-03 23:26:36.581585+00', '1. Rotate your torso through the movement pattern for Russian Twist. 2. Control the rotation in both directions—avoid using momentum. 3. Continue for your target rep count, maintaining good form throughout.', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 2, NULL, 5, 7, NULL, 6, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 10, 15, NULL, 4, NULL, TRUE, NULL, 'Strength', 50, 5, 7, FALSE, TRUE, 'russian_twist', 'Russian Twist', 'crunch, plank, leg_raise, wood_chop', FALSE, 'bodyweight', FALSE, 3, 60, 2, 70, 88, 95, 65),
('4531a2e7-119a-41ae-ad9f-b265a8f80424', 'Bent Over Rear Delt Fly (Machine)', 'Shoulders', 'Machine', '{"Rear Delts"}'::text[], '{"Upper Back","Traps"}'::text[], 'The Lever Seated Bent Over Rear Delt Fly is a flying exercise that targets your rear delts for shoulder development. Your upper back work as secondary movers, adding to the training stimulus. The seated position helps isolate the target muscles by removing momentum. Machine exercises are great for isolating muscles and training to failure safely. Strong shoulders improve overhead strength and support nearly all upper body movements.', '55271201', '55271201-Lever-Seated-Bent-Over-Rear-Delt-Fly_Shoulders_.mp4', 'male', FALSE, '2025-12-03 23:26:24.577164+00', '1. Adjust the machine settings (seat height, weight, pads) to fit your body for Lever Seated Bent Over Rear Delt Fly. 2. Sit with your back supported, core engaged, feet flat on the floor. 3. With a slight bend in your elbows, move the weight in a wide arc. 4. Squeeze your chest muscles at the center/top of the movement. 5. Return with control, feeling the stretch at the bottom. 6. Repeat for the prescribed number of repetitions.', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 1, NULL, 5, 7, NULL, 6, 'Seated', NULL, NULL, NULL, 10, 15, NULL, 4, NULL, FALSE, NULL, 'Strength', 80, 5, 7, FALSE, TRUE, 'rear_delt', 'Lever Seated Bent Over Rear Delt Fly', 'bench_press, incline_bench_press, push_up', FALSE, 'machine', FALSE, 3, 60, 2, 80, 75, 20, 88),
('453e8583-ed96-4ee5-97f3-a2a7833534bd', 'Roll Triceps Side Lying On Floor', 'Arms', 'Bodyweight', '{"Triceps"}'::text[], '{"Chest","Shoulders"}'::text[], 'The Roll Triceps Side Lying On Floor is an arm movement exercise targeting your core. The lying position provides back support and helps isolate the target muscles. This bodyweight exercise requires no equipment and can be done anywhere. Arm strength supports grip, pulling, and pushing in compound movements.', '54141201', '54141201-Roll-Triceps-Side-Lying-on-Floor-(female)_Upper-Ar.mp4', 'female', FALSE, '2025-12-03 23:26:36.38616+00', '1. Position yourself on the floor for Roll Triceps Side Lying On Floor. 2. Lie on your side with your body aligned. 3. Repeat for the prescribed number of repetitions.', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 2, NULL, 7, 7, NULL, 5, 'Lying', NULL, NULL, NULL, 8, 12, NULL, 6, NULL, TRUE, NULL, 'Strength', 45, 7, 8, TRUE, TRUE, 'arm_exercise', 'Roll Triceps Side Lying On Floor', 'bicep_curl, tricep_pushdown, skull_crusher, dip', FALSE, 'bodyweight', FALSE, 3, 90, 4, 70, 88, 95, 65),
('45484579-ba71-4437-9cb8-b93e674e4b4a', 'Standing Preacher Curl (Dumbbell)', 'Arms', 'Dumbbells, Preacher Bench', '{"Biceps"}'::text[], '{"Forearms"}'::text[], 'This curling exercise focuses on your biceps for improved arm size and strength. You''ll also feel your forearms working to support the movement. The standing position engages your core for stability. Dumbbells allow each arm to work independently, helping correct imbalances. Arm strength supports grip, pulling, and pushing in compound movements.', '4281201', '04281201-Dumbbell-Standing-Preacher-Curl_Upper-Arms.mp4', 'male', FALSE, '2025-12-03 23:26:29.837118+00', '1. Select a pair of dumbbells at an appropriate weight for Dumbbell Standing Preacher Curl. 2. Begin in a standing position with good posture. 3. Keep your elbows in a fixed position throughout the movement. 4. Curl the weight up by contracting your biceps, squeezing at the top. 5. Lower with control, resisting the weight on the way down. 6. Complete all reps with control before resting.', 'Curl', 'Pull', NULL, NULL, NULL, 2, NULL, 5, 7, NULL, 6, 'Standing', NULL, NULL, NULL, 10, 15, NULL, 4, NULL, TRUE, NULL, 'Strength', 94, 5, 7, FALSE, TRUE, 'preacher_curl', 'Standing Preacher Curl', 'tricep_pushdown, tricep_extension, bicep_curl, hammer_curl', TRUE, 'dumbbell', FALSE, 3, 60, 2, 92, 90, 92, 90),
('454c4f69-d093-4e8c-83b9-4c4b374463eb', 'Poliquin Step From Stepbox (Step Platform)', 'Legs', 'Step Platform', '{"Quads"}'::text[], '{"Glutes","Hamstrings"}'::text[], 'Build leg strength with this stepping movement focusing on your full body. Your quads work as secondary movers, adding to the training stimulus. Strong legs are the foundation for athletic performance and functional fitness. Can be modified for beginners or progressed for advanced athletes.', '96041201', '96041201-Bodyweight-Poliquin-Step-from-StepBox-(female)_Thi.mp4', 'female', FALSE, '2025-12-03 23:26:31.475486+00', '1. Set up a box or step platform at the appropriate height. 2. Set up in the starting position for Bodyweight Poliquin Step From Stepbox. 3. Execute the movement with proper form, focusing on your full body. 4. Control both the lifting and lowering phases of the movement. 5. Continue for your target rep count, maintaining good form throughout.', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 2, NULL, 7, 7, NULL, 5, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 8, 12, NULL, 6, NULL, TRUE, NULL, 'Strength', 50, 7, 8, TRUE, TRUE, 'general_exercise', 'Poliquin Step From Stepbox', 'squat, bench_press, deadlift', FALSE, 'bodyweight', FALSE, 3, 90, 4, 70, 88, 95, 65),
('45627255-f6a6-4e3a-a9e5-b6755738dcba', 'Pullover Dead Bug (Kettlebell)', 'Core', 'Kettlebell, Flat Bench', '{"Abs"}'::text[], '{"Hip Flexors"}'::text[], 'The Kettlebell Pullover Dead Bug is a core pulling exercise that primarily targets your abs. Secondary activation of your hip flexors provides additional muscle engagement. The kettlebell grip position adds a unique training stimulus. Building core stability helps with everything from heavy deadlifts to daily activities.', '95181201', '95181201-Kettlebell-Pullover-Dead-Bug-(male)_Waist_.mp4', 'male', FALSE, '2025-12-03 23:26:23.288245+00', '1. Select an appropriately weighted kettlebell for Kettlebell Pullover Dead Bug. 2. With arms slightly bent, lower the weight behind your head in an arc. 3. Pull the weight back over your chest, squeezing your lats and chest. 4. Complete all reps with control before resting.', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 3, NULL, 7, 7, NULL, 5, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 8, 12, NULL, 6, NULL, TRUE, NULL, 'Strength', 58, 7, 8, TRUE, TRUE, 'pullover', 'Pullover Dead Bug', 'bicep_curl, face_pull, lat_pulldown', FALSE, 'kettlebell', FALSE, 3, 90, 4, 75, 88, 88, 78),
('4567dcce-99d6-4cfa-bc96-bfef13d2cc10', 'Monster Walk', 'Legs', 'Bodyweight', '{"Quads"}'::text[], '{"Glutes","Hamstrings"}'::text[], 'The Monster Walk is a lower body stepping exercise that targets your full body. A versatile bodyweight movement perfect for home or gym training. Lower body strength improves everything from walking to heavy compound lifts.', '6281201', '06281201-Monster-Walk_Hips_.mp4', 'male', FALSE, '2025-12-03 23:26:24.422129+00', '1. Set up in the starting position for Monster Walk. 2. Execute the movement with proper form, focusing on your full body. 3. Control both the lifting and lowering phases of the movement. 4. Repeat for the prescribed number of repetitions.', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 2, NULL, 7, 7, NULL, 5, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 8, 12, NULL, 6, NULL, TRUE, NULL, 'Strength', 50, 7, 8, TRUE, TRUE, 'walking', 'Monster Walk', 'squat, bench_press, deadlift', FALSE, 'bodyweight', FALSE, 3, 90, 4, 70, 88, 95, 65),
('45753a6f-8271-4a7b-9429-f8eccc4f5074', 'Leg Front Kick', 'Core', 'Bodyweight', '{"Abs"}'::text[], '{"Hip Flexors"}'::text[], 'This kicking exercise engages your abs for improved core stability and strength. This bodyweight exercise requires no equipment and can be done anywhere. Core strength is foundational for athletic performance and injury prevention.', '46161201', '46161201-Leg-Front-Kick_Waist.mp4', 'male', FALSE, '2025-12-03 23:26:23.056255+00', '1. Set up in the starting position for Leg Front Kick. 2. Execute the movement with proper form, focusing on your abs. 3. Control both the lifting and lowering phases of the movement. 4. Continue for your target rep count, maintaining good form throughout.', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 2, NULL, 7, 7, NULL, 5, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 8, 12, NULL, 6, NULL, TRUE, NULL, 'Strength', 50, 7, 8, TRUE, TRUE, 'leg_exercise', 'Leg Front Kick', 'hip_flexor, lunge, dynamic_warmup', FALSE, 'bodyweight', FALSE, 3, 90, 4, 70, 88, 95, 65),
('45868195-e059-4c7f-9a55-1782d8d30efa', 'Burpee Side Tap Step Jack', 'Full Body', 'Bodyweight', '{"Full Body"}'::text[], '{"Chest","Quads","Core"}'::text[], 'The Burpee Side Tap Step Jack is an explosive exercise that combines cardiovascular training with dynamic stepping movements. The chest, quads assist throughout the movement, making this a well-rounded exercise. Great for improving athletic performance, burning calories, and building conditioning.', '89021201', '89021201-Burpee-Side-Tap-Step-Jack-(male)_Plyometrics_.mp4', 'male', FALSE, '2025-12-03 23:26:20.392006+00', '1. Set up a box or step platform at the appropriate height. 2. Squat down and place hands on the floor, jump feet back to plank. 3. Jump feet back toward hands, then explosively jump up with arms overhead. 4. Land softly and immediately begin the next rep. 5. Repeat for the prescribed number of repetitions.', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 2, NULL, 5, 4, NULL, 8, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 8, 12, NULL, 7, NULL, TRUE, NULL, 'Plyometrics', 50, 9, 8, TRUE, TRUE, 'burpee', 'Burpee Side Tap Step Jack', 'mountain_climber, box_jump, jumping_jack', TRUE, 'bodyweight', FALSE, 3, 60, 4, 70, 88, 95, 65),
('4587ee7b-b245-4dce-a762-4b303b7df484', 'Lying Extension - Across Face (Dumbbell)', 'Arms', 'Dumbbells, Flat Bench', '{"Triceps"}'::text[], '{"Chest","Shoulders"}'::text[], 'Build power and athleticism with this high-intensity extension exercise that challenges your entire body. The shoulders, core assist throughout the movement, making this a well-rounded exercise. Performing this lying down removes momentum for stricter form. Using dumbbells requires more stabilization than barbell variations. Develops fast-twitch muscle fibers for quicker, more powerful movements.', '3371201', '03371201-Dumbbell-Lying-Extension-(across-face)_Upper-Arms.mp4', 'male', FALSE, '2025-12-03 23:26:28.260518+00', '1. Select a pair of dumbbells at an appropriate weight for Dumbbell Lying Extension. 2. Lie down in the appropriate position for Dumbbell Lying Extension. 3. Extend through the target joint(s) for Dumbbell Lying Extension. 4. Repeat for the prescribed number of repetitions.', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 2, NULL, 5, 7, NULL, 6, 'Lying', NULL, NULL, NULL, 10, 15, NULL, 4, NULL, TRUE, NULL, 'Strength', 74, 5, 7, FALSE, TRUE, 'boxing', 'Lying Extension', 'squat, bench_press, deadlift', TRUE, 'dumbbell', FALSE, 3, 60, 2, 92, 90, 92, 90),
('458a734f-ee74-4d58-acaa-3c2746001d4b', 'Sumo Squat Front Raise (Dumbbell)', 'Legs', 'Dumbbells', '{"Quads","Glutes"}'::text[], '{"Chest"}'::text[], 'This squatting movement emphasizes your quadriceps for stronger, more powerful legs. You''ll also feel your glutes, hamstrings working to support the movement. Dumbbells allow each arm to work independently, helping correct imbalances. Leg training boosts metabolism and builds functional, real-world strength.', '72671201', '72671201-Dumbbell-Sumo-Squat-Front-Raise-(male)_Thighs_.mp4', 'male', FALSE, '2025-12-03 23:26:21.732034+00', '1. Select a pair of dumbbells at an appropriate weight for Dumbbell Sumo Squat Front Raise. 2. Raise the weight in front of you to shoulder height. 3. Lower with control, maintaining tension throughout. 4. Complete all reps with control before resting.', 'Squat', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 2, NULL, 10, 10, NULL, 4, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 5, 8, NULL, 9, NULL, TRUE, NULL, 'Strength', 97, 7, 9, TRUE, FALSE, 'front_raise', 'Sumo Squat Front Raise', 'shoulder_press, lateral_raise, rear_delt_fly', TRUE, 'dumbbell', FALSE, 4, 120, 5, 92, 90, 92, 90),
('458e8759-6745-4a08-8f6c-fbb053ec4e7c', 'Step Knee Thrust', 'Legs', 'Bodyweight', '{"Quads"}'::text[], '{"Glutes","Hamstrings"}'::text[], 'A challenging plyometric exercise, the Step Knee Thrust builds reactive power and improves conditioning. You''ll also feel your quads working to support the movement. Develops fast-twitch muscle fibers for quicker, more powerful movements.', '66881201', '66881201-Step-Knee-Thrust-(female)_Plyometrics_.mp4', 'female', FALSE, '2025-12-03 23:26:39.21093+00', '1. Set up a box or step platform at the appropriate height. 2. Drive through your heels to lift your hips toward the ceiling. 3. Squeeze your glutes hard at the top of the movement. 4. Lower your hips back down with control. 5. Continue for your target rep count, maintaining good form throughout. Start with lighter weight to perfect your form.', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 2, NULL, 7, 7, NULL, 5, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 8, 12, NULL, 6, NULL, TRUE, NULL, 'Strength', 50, 7, 8, TRUE, TRUE, 'knee_drive', 'Step Knee Thrust', 'butt_kicks, jumping_jack, mountain_climber', FALSE, 'bodyweight', FALSE, 3, 90, 4, 70, 88, 95, 65),
('458fae5a-3d4b-46cd-b94e-ae84b027bfc9', 'Table Top Bridge Pulse', 'Legs', 'Bodyweight', '{"Glutes"}'::text[], '{"Hamstrings"}'::text[], 'Build stronger glutes with this bridging movement focused on hip extension. The hamstrings assist throughout the movement, making this a well-rounded exercise. This bodyweight exercise requires no equipment and can be done anywhere. Lower body strength improves everything from walking to heavy compound lifts.', '84961201', '84961201-Table-Top-Bridge-Pulse-(female)_Hips_.mp4', 'female', FALSE, '2025-12-03 23:26:39.623429+00', '1. Drive through your heels to lift your hips toward the ceiling. 2. Squeeze your glutes hard at the top of the movement. 3. Lower your hips back down with control. 4. At the bottom or top, pulse up and down in small movements before completing the rep. 5. Repeat for the prescribed number of repetitions. Keep your core engaged for stability.', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 2, NULL, 7, 7, NULL, 5, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 8, 12, NULL, 6, NULL, TRUE, NULL, 'Strength', 50, 7, 8, TRUE, TRUE, 'glute_bridge', 'Table Top Bridge Pulse', 'hip_thrust, romanian_deadlift', TRUE, 'bodyweight', FALSE, 3, 90, 4, 70, 88, 95, 65),
('459c7e6f-3118-4ec6-a01b-14e671bb2cb8', 'Single Leg Sit (Against Wall) - Alternating', 'Legs', 'Wall', '{"Quads"}'::text[], '{"Glutes","Hamstrings"}'::text[], 'Target the front of your thighs with this movement exercise for quad development. Leg training boosts metabolism and builds functional, real-world strength.', '75411201', '75411201-Alternate-Single-Leg-Sit-Wall-(male)_Thighs_.mp4', 'male', FALSE, '2025-12-03 23:26:28.52454+00', '1. Position yourself at the appropriate distance from a wall. 2. Alternate between sides/arms/legs with each repetition. 3. Complete all reps with control before resting. Focus on the mind-muscle connection.', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 3, NULL, 7, 7, NULL, 5, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 8, 12, NULL, 6, NULL, TRUE, NULL, 'Strength', 37, 7, 8, TRUE, TRUE, 'leg_exercise', 'Single Leg Sit Wall - Alternating', 'squat, lunge, leg_press', FALSE, 'bodyweight', FALSE, 3, 90, 4, 70, 88, 95, 65),
('45a994ab-4562-4914-9419-46b06f2513e9', 'Air Pillow Balance Counterbalanced Skater Squat (Balance Pad)', 'Legs', 'Balance Pad', '{"Quads"}'::text[], '{"Glutes","Hamstrings"}'::text[], 'Build stronger quads with this squatting movement that develops leg drive and power. The glutes, hamstrings assist throughout the movement, making this a well-rounded exercise. A versatile bodyweight movement perfect for home or gym training. Leg training boosts metabolism and builds functional, real-world strength. Excellent for pre-exhausting the target muscle before compound lifts.', '84801201', '84801201-Air-Pillow-Balance-Counterbalanced-Skater-Squat-(m.mp4', 'male', FALSE, '2025-12-03 23:26:20.982555+00', '1. Push your hips back and bend your knees to lower your body. 2. Keep your chest up and knees tracking over your toes. 3. Drive through your heels to stand back up, squeezing your glutes at the top. 4. Repeat for the prescribed number of repetitions. Keep the movement smooth and controlled.', 'Squat', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 3, NULL, 5, 4, NULL, 8, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 8, 12, NULL, 7, NULL, TRUE, NULL, 'Plyometrics', 10, 9, 8, TRUE, TRUE, 'balance', 'Air Pillow Balance Counterbalanced Skater Squat', 'leg_press, leg_extension, leg_curl, lunge, front_squat, hack_squat', FALSE, 'bodyweight', FALSE, 3, 60, 4, 70, 88, 95, 65),
('45ac54e6-0b93-44cc-a882-8ee1baf8cf0b', 'Lying Heel To Heel Dragback', 'Core', 'Bodyweight', '{"Abs"}'::text[], '{"Hip Flexors"}'::text[], 'The Lying Heel To Heel Dragback is a lower body movement exercise that targets your core. Performing this lying down removes momentum for stricter form. This bodyweight exercise requires no equipment and can be done anywhere. Lower body strength improves everything from walking to heavy compound lifts.', '89321201', '89321201-Lying-Heel-to-Heel-Dragback-(female)_Hips_.mp4', 'female', FALSE, '2025-12-03 23:26:35.133808+00', '1. Lie down in the appropriate position for Lying Heel To Heel Dragback. 2. Set up in the starting position for Lying Heel To Heel Dragback. 3. Execute the movement with proper form, focusing on your core. 4. Control both the lifting and lowering phases of the movement. 5. Repeat for the prescribed number of repetitions.', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 2, NULL, 7, 7, NULL, 5, 'Lying', NULL, NULL, NULL, 8, 12, NULL, 6, NULL, TRUE, NULL, 'Strength', 50, 7, 8, TRUE, TRUE, 'back_exercise', 'Lying Heel To Heel Dragback', 'lat_pulldown, bent_over_row, pull_up', FALSE, 'bodyweight', FALSE, 3, 90, 4, 70, 88, 95, 65),
('45b93fef-5faa-468f-9654-e0679a268b2e', 'Seated Bench Extension (Dumbbell)', 'Arms', 'Dumbbells, Flat Bench', '{"Triceps"}'::text[], '{"Chest","Shoulders"}'::text[], 'This extension movement isolates your triceps for improved arm development. The seated position helps isolate the target muscles by removing momentum. The dumbbell variation provides freedom of movement and greater range of motion. Arm strength supports grip, pulling, and pushing in compound movements.', '3891201', '03891201-Dumbbell-Seated-Bench-Extension_Upper-Arms_.mp4', 'male', FALSE, '2025-12-03 23:26:23.689343+00', '1. Select a pair of dumbbells at an appropriate weight for Dumbbell Seated Bench Extension. 2. Sit with your back supported, core engaged, feet flat on the floor. 3. Extend through the target joint(s) for Dumbbell Seated Bench Extension. 4. Complete all reps with control before resting.', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 2, NULL, 5, 7, NULL, 6, 'Seated', NULL, NULL, NULL, 10, 15, NULL, 4, NULL, TRUE, NULL, 'Strength', 84, 5, 7, FALSE, TRUE, 'general_exercise', 'Seated Bench Extension', 'bench_press, chest_fly, push_up', TRUE, 'dumbbell', FALSE, 3, 60, 2, 92, 90, 92, 90),
('45c602e6-da9b-4d5a-9a5d-7eef75a5662c', 'Seated Russian Twist (Chair)', 'Core', 'Chair', '{"Obliques"}'::text[], '{"Abs"}'::text[], 'The Seated Russian Twist On A Chair is a lower body twisting exercise that targets your obliques. Secondary activation of your abs provides additional muscle engagement. Being seated provides stability, allowing you to focus on the working muscles. Leg training boosts metabolism and builds functional, real-world strength.', '76331201', '76331201-Sitting-Russian-Twist-on-a-Chair-(female)_Hips_.mp4', 'female', FALSE, '2025-12-03 23:26:37.877283+00', '1. Position yourself with a sturdy chair for support or as part of the movement. 2. Sit with your back supported, core engaged, feet flat on the floor. 3. Rotate your torso through the movement pattern for Seated Russian Twist On A Chair. 4. Control the rotation in both directions—avoid using momentum. 5. Repeat for the prescribed number of repetitions. Keep your shoulders relaxed and away from your ears.', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 2, NULL, 5, 7, NULL, 6, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 10, 15, NULL, 4, NULL, TRUE, NULL, 'Strength', 35, 5, 7, FALSE, TRUE, 'russian_twist', 'Seated Russian Twist On A Chair', 'crunch, plank, leg_raise, wood_chop', FALSE, 'bodyweight', FALSE, 3, 60, 2, 70, 88, 95, 65),
('45c90ded-1840-4bc5-9d3c-0338e77aa733', 'Calf Raise From Deficit Supported (Step Platform)', 'Legs', 'Step Platform, Chair', '{"Calves"}'::text[], '{}'::text[], 'Build stronger calves with this targeted raising exercise. Leg training boosts metabolism and builds functional, real-world strength. This variation is excellent for building mind-muscle connection.', '70741201', '70741201-Calf-Raise-from-Deficit-with-Chair-Supported-(fema.mp4', 'female', FALSE, '2025-12-03 23:26:32.166461+00', '1. Position yourself with a sturdy chair for support or as part of the movement. 2. Lower your heels below the platform to get a full stretch. 3. Rise up onto your toes as high as possible, squeezing your calves. 4. Lower with control and repeat. 5. Continue for your target rep count, maintaining good form throughout.', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 4, NULL, 5, 7, NULL, 6, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 12, 20, NULL, 4, NULL, TRUE, NULL, 'Strength', 65, 5, 7, FALSE, TRUE, 'calf_raise', 'Calf Raise From Deficit With Chair Supported', 'standing_calf_raise, seated_calf_raise, tibialis_raise', FALSE, 'bodyweight', FALSE, 3, 60, 2, 70, 88, 95, 65),
('45d2ee0d-ad6a-43b2-83da-69297e76a9cf', 'Single Arm Lateral Raise (Dumbbell)', 'Shoulders', 'Dumbbells', '{"Side Delts"}'::text[], '{"Traps"}'::text[], 'Build stronger shoulders with this raising movement focusing on your lateral delts. Dumbbells allow each arm to work independently, helping correct imbalances. Shoulder development enhances both performance and upper body aesthetics.', '3551201', '03551201-Dumbbell-One-Arm-Lateral-Raise_Shoulder.mp4', 'male', FALSE, '2025-12-03 23:26:25.737494+00', '1. Select an appropriate weight dumbbell and hold it in one hand. 2. Raise your arms out to the sides until parallel to the floor. 3. Lower with control, maintaining tension throughout. 4. Complete all reps on one side, then switch to the other side. 5. Complete all reps with control before resting.', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 3, NULL, 5, 7, NULL, 6, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 10, 15, NULL, 4, NULL, TRUE, NULL, 'Strength', 87, 5, 7, FALSE, TRUE, 'lateral_raise', 'Single Arm Lateral Raise', 'shoulder_press, front_raise, rear_delt', TRUE, 'dumbbell', FALSE, 3, 60, 2, 92, 90, 92, 90),
('45d493ba-7f82-4194-a1cc-2aa6eff7b099', 'Burpee Two Star Jumps', 'Full Body', 'Bodyweight', '{"Full Body"}'::text[], '{"Chest","Quads","Core"}'::text[], 'A challenging plyometric exercise, the Burpee Two Star Jumps builds reactive power and improves conditioning. The chest, quads assist throughout the movement, making this a well-rounded exercise. A versatile bodyweight movement perfect for home or gym training. Plyometric training builds explosive power that transfers to sports and daily activities.', '76721201', '76721201-Burpee-Two-Star-Jumps-(male)_Plyometrics_.mp4', 'male', FALSE, '2025-12-03 23:26:26.808474+00', '1. Squat down and place hands on the floor, jump feet back to plank. 2. Jump feet back toward hands, then explosively jump up with arms overhead. 3. Land softly and immediately begin the next rep. 4. Continue for your target rep count, maintaining good form throughout. Focus on the mind-muscle connection.', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 2, NULL, 5, 4, NULL, 8, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 8, 12, NULL, 7, NULL, TRUE, NULL, 'Plyometrics', 50, 9, 8, TRUE, TRUE, 'burpee', 'Burpee Two Star Jumps', 'mountain_climber, box_jump, jumping_jack', TRUE, 'bodyweight', FALSE, 3, 60, 4, 70, 88, 95, 65),
('45e11e44-d0fc-4121-b0a0-45bdd8cfc00e', 'Deep Push Up Hold', 'Chest', 'Bodyweight', '{"Chest"}'::text[], '{"Triceps","Front Delts"}'::text[], 'The Deep Push Up Hold is a pushing exercise that targets your chest muscles. You''ll also feel your triceps, front delts working to support the movement. A versatile bodyweight movement perfect for home or gym training. A well-developed chest contributes to upper body strength and aesthetics.', '83511201', '83511201-Deep-Push-Up-Hold-(male)_Chest_.mp4', 'male', FALSE, '2025-12-03 23:26:25.123298+00', '1. Keep your body in a straight line from head to heels throughout. 2. Lower your chest toward the floor by bending your elbows. 3. Push through your palms to return to the starting position. 4. Hold the position for the prescribed time, maintaining tension. Ensure full range of motion on each rep.', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 2, NULL, 7, 7, NULL, 5, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 8, 12, NULL, 6, NULL, TRUE, NULL, 'Strength', 65, 7, 8, TRUE, TRUE, 'push_up', 'Deep Push Up Hold', 'bench_press, chest_fly, dip', TRUE, 'bodyweight', FALSE, 3, 90, 4, 70, 88, 95, 65),
('45efe324-cb0e-4cfb-8a53-8699c402e347', 'Faber Test', 'Full Body', 'Bodyweight', '{"Full Body"}'::text[], '{}'::text[], 'Target your full body with this movement stretch that helps restore range of motion. Regular stretching improves flexibility, reduces injury risk, and aids recovery. Can be modified for beginners or progressed for advanced athletes.', '67861201', '67861201-Faber-test-(female)_Stretching_.mp4', 'female', FALSE, '2025-12-03 23:26:33.505723+00', '1. Move into the stretch position for Faber Test. 2. Ease into the stretch until you feel gentle tension (not pain). 3. Hold for 20-30 seconds, breathing deeply and relaxing into the stretch.', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 2, NULL, 7, 7, NULL, 5, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 8, 12, NULL, 6, NULL, TRUE, NULL, 'Strength', 50, 7, 8, TRUE, TRUE, 'general_exercise', 'Faber Test', 'plank, crunch, leg_raise', FALSE, 'bodyweight', FALSE, 3, 90, 4, 70, 88, 95, 65),
('45f5a77d-94f2-4bb9-807e-a7a89fc239ec', 'Dynamic Leg Swing', 'Full Body', 'Bodyweight', '{"Full Body"}'::text[], '{}'::text[], 'The Dynamic Leg Swing is a flexibility exercise that targets your full body, helping to release tension and improve range of motion. Regular stretching improves flexibility, reduces injury risk, and aids recovery.', '56921201', '56921201-Dynamic-Leg-Swing-(female)_Hips_.mp4', 'female', FALSE, '2025-12-03 23:26:33.298565+00', '1. Hinge at your hips, letting the weight swing back between your legs. 2. Explosively drive hips forward, propelling the weight forward/up. 3. Let gravity bring it back as you hinge for the next rep. Don''t rush—quality over quantity.', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 2, NULL, 7, 7, NULL, 5, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 8, 12, NULL, 6, NULL, TRUE, NULL, 'Strength', 50, 7, 8, TRUE, TRUE, 'leg_exercise', 'Dynamic Leg Swing', 'high_knees, butt_kicks, jumping_jack', FALSE, 'bodyweight', FALSE, 3, 90, 4, 70, 88, 95, 65),
('45fa6c9b-3d22-44b7-b490-57f03d767a5d', 'Side Split', 'Full Body', 'Bodyweight', '{"Full Body"}'::text[], '{}'::text[], 'Designed to lengthen your full body, the Side Split helps improve mobility and prevent stiffness. Regular stretching improves flexibility, reduces injury risk, and aids recovery.', '61551201', '61551201-Side-Split-(female)_Stretching_.mp4', 'female', FALSE, '2025-12-03 23:26:37.179953+00', '1. Move into the stretch position for Side Split. 2. Ease into the stretch until you feel gentle tension (not pain). 3. Hold for 20-30 seconds, breathing deeply and relaxing into the stretch. 4. Switch sides and repeat for equal time.', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 2, NULL, 7, 7, NULL, 5, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 8, 12, NULL, 6, NULL, TRUE, NULL, 'Strength', 50, 7, 8, TRUE, TRUE, 'general_exercise', 'Side Split', 'squat, bench_press, deadlift', FALSE, 'bodyweight', FALSE, 3, 90, 4, 70, 88, 95, 65),
('460dc0b8-5f3c-484f-b3eb-be914584bf2c', 'Extra Decline Sit Up (Decline Bench)', 'Core', 'Decline Bench', '{"Abs"}'::text[], '{"Hip Flexors"}'::text[], 'The Extra Decline Sit Up is a core movement exercise that primarily targets your abs. Secondary activation of your hip flexors provides additional muscle engagement. Declining shifts the emphasis to hit the muscles from a different angle. A strong core improves posture, protects your spine, and enhances all other lifts.', '18641201', '18641201-Extra-Decline-Sit-Up_Waist_.mp4', 'male', FALSE, '2025-12-03 23:26:29.242428+00', '1. Set up in the starting position for Extra Decline Sit Up. 2. Execute the movement with proper form, focusing on your abs. 3. Control both the lifting and lowering phases of the movement. 4. Repeat for the prescribed number of repetitions.', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 2, NULL, 5, 7, NULL, 6, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 10, 15, NULL, 4, NULL, TRUE, NULL, 'Strength', 73, 5, 7, FALSE, TRUE, 'crunch', 'Extra Decline Sit Up', 'leg_raise, plank, russian_twist, v_up', FALSE, 'bodyweight', FALSE, 3, 60, 2, 70, 88, 95, 65),
('4620e85c-cb90-464d-9f77-e519a6b6d364', 'Weighted V Up Passes With Pad', 'Core', 'Bodyweight', '{"Abs"}'::text[], '{"Hip Flexors"}'::text[], 'The Weighted V Up Passes With Pad is a core movement exercise that primarily targets your abs. Secondary activation of your hip flexors provides additional muscle engagement. No equipment needed—your body provides all the resistance. A strong core improves posture, protects your spine, and enhances all other lifts.', '64291201', '64291201-Weighted-V-up-Passes-with-Pad-(female)_Waist_.mp4', 'female', FALSE, '2025-12-03 23:26:40.037451+00', '1. Set up in the starting position for Weighted V Up Passes With Pad. 2. Execute the movement with proper form, focusing on your abs. 3. Control both the lifting and lowering phases of the movement. 4. Repeat for the prescribed number of repetitions. Keep your shoulders relaxed and away from your ears.', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 3, NULL, 7, 7, NULL, 5, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 8, 12, NULL, 6, NULL, TRUE, NULL, 'Strength', 50, 7, 8, TRUE, TRUE, 'v_up', 'Weighted V Up Passes With Pad', 'squat, bench_press, deadlift', FALSE, 'bodyweight', FALSE, 3, 90, 4, 70, 88, 95, 65),
('4632172a-0756-4ed4-a2ca-10952f6d7287', 'Hanging Garhammer Raise (Pull-Up Bar)', 'Core', 'Pull-Up Bar', '{"Lower Abs"}'::text[], '{"Hip Flexors","Forearms"}'::text[], 'Strengthen your midsection with this raising movement that works your abs. Your hip flexors, grip work as secondary movers, adding to the training stimulus. The hanging position challenges your grip while targeting the primary muscles. No equipment needed—your body provides all the resistance. Building core stability helps with everything from heavy deadlifts to daily activities.', '106061201', '106061201-Hanging-Garhammer-Raise-(male)_Waist_.mp4', 'male', FALSE, '2025-12-03 23:26:23.288245+00', '1. Grip the bar and hang with arms fully extended, engaging your shoulders. 2. Use a hammer/neutral grip with palms facing each other throughout. 3. Raise the weight in the prescribed direction for Hanging Garhammer Raise. 4. Lower with control, maintaining tension throughout. 5. Repeat for the prescribed number of repetitions.', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 2, NULL, 5, 7, NULL, 6, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 10, 15, NULL, 4, NULL, TRUE, NULL, 'Strength', 70, 5, 7, FALSE, TRUE, 'general_exercise', 'Hanging Garhammer Raise', 'pull_up, lat_pulldown, grip_training', FALSE, 'pull_up_bar', FALSE, 3, 60, 2, 70, 88, 95, 65),
('463a4639-eafa-4982-8ac0-619e826c3e09', 'Body Extension (backward Reach)', 'Back', 'Bodyweight', '{"Lower Back"}'::text[], '{"Glutes"}'::text[], 'Build leg strength with this extension movement focusing on your lower back. Your glutes work as secondary movers, adding to the training stimulus. A versatile bodyweight movement perfect for home or gym training. Strong legs are the foundation for athletic performance and functional fitness.', '45601201', '45601201-Body-Extension-(Backward-Reach)_Thighs_.mp4', 'male', FALSE, '2025-12-03 23:26:24.099303+00', '1. Raise your torso by extending at the lower back/hips. 2. Lower with control, maintaining tension. 3. Complete all reps with control before resting. Control the movement—avoid using momentum.', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 2, NULL, 5, 7, NULL, 6, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 10, 15, NULL, 4, NULL, TRUE, NULL, 'Strength', 70, 5, 7, FALSE, TRUE, 'back_exercise', 'Body Extension', 'lat_pulldown, bent_over_row, pull_up', FALSE, 'bodyweight', FALSE, 3, 60, 2, 70, 88, 95, 65),
('4641e324-3592-4835-b515-336450ff0383', 'Standing Shoulder External Rotation At 90 (Dumbbell)', 'Shoulders', 'Dumbbells', '{"Rotator Cuff"}'::text[], '{"Shoulders"}'::text[], 'Target your rotator cuff with the Dumbbell Standing Shoulder External Rotation At 90, an effective shoulder rotation exercise. Performing this standing challenges your balance and core engagement. Using dumbbells requires more stabilization than barbell variations. Strong shoulders improve overhead strength and support nearly all upper body movements.', '91821201', '91821201-Dumbbell-Standing-Shoulder-External-Rotation-at-90.mp4', 'female', FALSE, '2025-12-03 23:26:33.168801+00', '1. Select a pair of dumbbells at an appropriate weight for Dumbbell Standing Shoulder External Rotation At 90. 2. Begin in a standing position with good posture. 3. Rotate your torso through the movement pattern for Dumbbell Standing Shoulder External Rotation At 90. 4. Control the rotation in both directions—avoid using momentum. 5. Continue for your target rep count, maintaining good form throughout.', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 2, NULL, 7, 8, NULL, 5, 'Standing', NULL, NULL, NULL, 8, 12, NULL, 6, NULL, TRUE, NULL, 'Strength', 54, 7, 8, TRUE, TRUE, 'external_rotation', 'Standing Shoulder External Rotation At 90', 'squat, bench_press, deadlift', TRUE, 'dumbbell', FALSE, 3, 90, 4, 92, 90, 92, 90),
('464a3512-fb0c-43ad-99ab-dcd7268b2eec', 'Incline Bicep Curl - Inner (Dumbbell)', 'Arms', 'Dumbbells, Incline Bench', '{"Biceps"}'::text[], '{"Forearms"}'::text[], 'This curling exercise focuses on your biceps for improved arm size and strength. Secondary activation of your forearms provides additional muscle engagement. Using an incline changes the angle of resistance for varied muscle recruitment. The dumbbell variation provides freedom of movement and greater range of motion. Arm strength supports grip, pulling, and pushing in compound movements.', '97441201', '97441201-Dumbbell-Incline-Inner-Biceps-Curl-(female)_Upper-.mp4', 'female', FALSE, '2025-12-03 23:26:32.914483+00', '1. Select a pair of dumbbells at an appropriate weight for Dumbbell Incline Inner Biceps Curl. 2. Keep your elbows in a fixed position throughout the movement. 3. Curl the weight up by contracting your biceps, squeezing at the top. 4. Lower with control, resisting the weight on the way down. 5. Complete all reps with control before resting.', 'Curl', 'Pull', NULL, NULL, NULL, 2, NULL, 5, 7, NULL, 6, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 10, 15, NULL, 4, NULL, TRUE, NULL, 'Strength', 95, 5, 7, FALSE, TRUE, 'bicep_curl', 'Incline Inner Biceps Curl', 'hammer_curl, preacher_curl, cable_curl', TRUE, 'dumbbell', FALSE, 3, 60, 2, 92, 90, 92, 90),
('464fdf5b-8bed-4ef1-95c7-db859a2632b7', 'Squat (Barbell)', 'Legs', 'Barbell', '{"Quads"}'::text[], '{"Glutes","Hamstrings"}'::text[], 'This squatting movement emphasizes your quadriceps for stronger, more powerful legs. Secondary activation of your glutes, hamstrings provides additional muscle engagement. Barbells enable bilateral loading for building raw strength. Lower body strength improves everything from walking to heavy compound lifts.', '35931201', '35931201-Barbell-Squat-(female)_Thighs.mp4', 'female', FALSE, '2025-12-03 23:26:31.133197+00', '1. Set up a barbell in a rack at the appropriate height for Barbell Squat. 2. Push your hips back and bend your knees to lower your body. 3. Keep your chest up and knees tracking over your toes. 4. Drive through your heels to stand back up, squeezing your glutes at the top. 5. Continue for your target rep count, maintaining good form throughout.', 'Squat', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 3, NULL, 10, 10, NULL, 4, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 5, 8, NULL, 9, NULL, TRUE, NULL, 'Strength', 97, 7, 9, TRUE, FALSE, 'squat', 'Squat', 'leg_press, front_squat, goblet_squat, lunge, leg_extension', TRUE, 'barbell', FALSE, 4, 120, 5, 95, 80, 65, 95),
('46550f15-277c-44a4-bd68-01e5c996c00e', 'Narrow Row (Smith Machine)', 'Back', 'Smith Machine', '{"Upper Back"}'::text[], '{"Lats","Biceps","Rear Delts"}'::text[], 'This rowing exercise strengthens the muscles between your shoulder blades. The biceps, rear delts assist throughout the movement, making this a well-rounded exercise. The fixed path allows you to focus purely on muscular effort. A strong back improves posture, prevents injury, and balances pressing movements.', '7611201', '07611201-Smith-Narrow-Row_Back.mp4', 'male', FALSE, '2025-12-03 23:26:24.941834+00', '1. Set the Smith machine bar to the appropriate starting height for Smith Narrow Row. 2. Use a close/narrow grip (hands closer than shoulder-width). 3. Pull the weight toward your torso, leading with your elbow(s). 4. Squeeze your shoulder blades together at the peak contraction. 5. Extend back out with control, feeling the stretch in your back. 6. Complete all reps with control before resting.', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 2, NULL, 10, 10, NULL, 4, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 5, 8, NULL, 8, NULL, FALSE, NULL, 'Strength', 78, 7, 9, TRUE, FALSE, 'general_exercise', 'Smith Narrow Row', 'Narrow Row', FALSE, 'smith_machine', FALSE, 4, 120, 4, 80, 75, 20, 88),
('46551143-2be1-49fa-a328-149f5e6aacf0', 'Single Leg Squat With Support', 'Legs', 'Bodyweight', '{"Quads"}'::text[], '{"Glutes","Hamstrings"}'::text[], 'Build stronger quads with this squatting movement that develops leg drive and power. You''ll also feel your glutes, hamstrings working to support the movement. This bodyweight exercise requires no equipment and can be done anywhere. Lower body strength improves everything from walking to heavy compound lifts. Progress gradually by increasing resistance over time.', '75611201', '75611201-Bodyweight-Single-Leg-Squat-with-Support-(male)_Th.mp4', 'male', FALSE, '2025-12-03 23:26:27.805708+00', '1. Push your hips back and bend your knees to lower your body. 2. Keep your chest up and knees tracking over your toes. 3. Drive through your heels to stand back up, squeezing your glutes at the top. 4. Complete all reps on one side, then switch to the other side. 5. Repeat for the prescribed number of repetitions. Start with lighter weight to perfect your form.', 'Squat', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 4, NULL, 7, 7, NULL, 5, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 8, 12, NULL, 6, NULL, TRUE, NULL, 'Strength', 80, 7, 8, TRUE, TRUE, 'pistol_squat', 'Single Leg Squat With Support', 'squat, bench_press, deadlift', TRUE, 'bodyweight', FALSE, 3, 90, 4, 70, 88, 95, 65),
('4661f207-91c3-49c4-a150-029a952606c9', 'Mountain Climber And Dynamic Plank', 'Core', 'Bodyweight', '{"Abs"}'::text[], '{"Shoulders","Lower Back"}'::text[], 'A challenging plyometric exercise, the Mountain Climber And Dynamic Plank builds reactive power and improves conditioning. You''ll also feel your hip flexors, shoulders working to support the movement. This bodyweight exercise requires no equipment and can be done anywhere. Great for improving athletic performance, burning calories, and building conditioning.', '72501201', '72501201-Mountain-Climber-and-Dynamic-Plank-(male)_Plyometr.mp4', 'male', FALSE, '2025-12-03 23:26:28.851102+00', '1. Hold your body in a straight line from head to heels. 2. Don''t let your hips sag or pike up—engage your core and glutes. 3. Breathe steadily while maintaining the position. 4. Continue for your target rep count, maintaining good form throughout. Keep your core engaged for stability. A solid choice for plyometrics day.', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 2, NULL, 5, 4, NULL, 8, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 8, 12, NULL, 7, NULL, TRUE, NULL, 'Plyometrics', 70, 9, 8, TRUE, TRUE, 'mountain_climber', 'Mountain Climber And Dynamic Plank', 'crunch, leg_raise, russian_twist, dead_bug', TRUE, 'bodyweight', TRUE, 3, 60, 4, 70, 88, 95, 65),
('466c4214-f643-4679-99b7-e0724ae0a249', 'Step Up With Knee Raise (Dumbbell)', 'Legs', 'Dumbbells, Step Platform', '{"Quads"}'::text[], '{"Glutes","Hamstrings"}'::text[], 'The Dumbbell Step Up With Knee Raise is a raising exercise that primarily loads your quadriceps. The hip flexors assist throughout the movement, making this a well-rounded exercise. Using dumbbells requires more stabilization than barbell variations. Leg training boosts metabolism and builds functional, real-world strength.', '45651201', '45651201-Dumbbell-Step-up-with-Knee-Raise_Hips_.mp4', 'male', FALSE, '2025-12-03 23:26:26.271124+00', '1. Select a pair of dumbbells at an appropriate weight for Dumbbell Step Up With Knee Raise. 2. Set up a box or step platform at the appropriate height. 3. Raise the weight in the prescribed direction for Dumbbell Step Up With Knee Raise. 4. Lower with control, maintaining tension throughout. 5. Complete all reps with control before resting.', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 2, NULL, 7, 8, NULL, 5, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 8, 12, NULL, 6, NULL, TRUE, NULL, 'Strength', 82, 7, 8, TRUE, TRUE, 'leg_raise', 'Step Up With Knee Raise', 'crunch, plank, v_up', TRUE, 'dumbbell', FALSE, 3, 90, 4, 92, 90, 92, 90),
('4678ccf6-8ab4-4c53-ae58-72642e990643', 'Lying Rollover Pilates', 'Back', 'Bodyweight', '{"Lats"}'::text[], '{"Shoulders"}'::text[], 'The Lying Rollover Pilates is a flexibility exercise that targets your lats, helping to release tension and improve range of motion. Your shoulders work as secondary movers, adding to the training stimulus. Performing this lying down removes momentum for stricter form. Regular stretching improves flexibility, reduces injury risk, and aids recovery.', '86971201', '86971201-Lying-Rollover-Pilates-(female)_Stretching_.mp4', 'female', FALSE, '2025-12-03 23:26:35.250398+00', '1. Lie down in the appropriate position for Lying Rollover Pilates. 2. Move into the stretch position for Lying Rollover Pilates. 3. Ease into the stretch until you feel gentle tension (not pain). 4. Hold for 20-30 seconds, breathing deeply and relaxing into the stretch.', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 2, NULL, 7, 7, NULL, 5, 'Lying', NULL, NULL, NULL, 8, 12, NULL, 6, NULL, TRUE, NULL, 'Strength', 50, 7, 8, TRUE, TRUE, 'back_exercise', 'Lying Rollover Pilates', 'lat_pulldown, bent_over_row, pull_up', FALSE, 'bodyweight', FALSE, 3, 90, 4, 70, 88, 95, 65),
('468dc841-1759-4ecd-bef5-f9e63f312684', 'Hip Thrust (Plate Loaded Machine)', 'Legs', 'Machine', '{"Glutes"}'::text[], '{"Hamstrings","Core"}'::text[], 'This thrusting exercise isolates your glutes for improved hip strength and power. Secondary activation of your hamstrings provides additional muscle engagement. The fixed path allows you to focus purely on muscular effort. Leg training boosts metabolism and builds functional, real-world strength.', '35491201', '35491201-Lever-Hip-Thrust-(plate-loaded)-(female)_Hips_.mp4', 'female', FALSE, '2025-12-03 23:26:34.724336+00', '1. Adjust the machine settings (seat height, weight, pads) to fit your body for Lever Hip Thrust. 2. Drive through your heels to lift your hips toward the ceiling. 3. Squeeze your glutes hard at the top of the movement. 4. Lower your hips back down with control. 5. Continue for your target rep count, maintaining good form throughout.', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 1, NULL, 7, 7, NULL, 5, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 8, 12, NULL, 6, NULL, FALSE, NULL, 'Strength', 78, 7, 8, TRUE, TRUE, 'hip_thrust', 'Lever Hip Thrust', 'glute_bridge, romanian_deadlift, leg_curl', FALSE, 'machine', FALSE, 3, 90, 4, 80, 75, 20, 88),
('468f1e03-7875-4b19-8fc0-b3d779934242', 'Cross Arms Leg Lift - Alternating', 'Full Body', 'Bodyweight', '{"Full Body"}'::text[], '{}'::text[], 'The Cross Arms Alternate Leg Lift is an explosive exercise that combines cardiovascular training with dynamic movement movements. No equipment needed—your body provides all the resistance. Plyometric training builds explosive power that transfers to sports and daily activities.', '81711201', '81711201-Cross-Arms-Alternate-Leg-Lift-(female)_Plyometrics.mp4', 'female', FALSE, '2025-12-03 23:26:32.501166+00', '1. Alternate between sides/arms/legs with each repetition. 2. Set up in the starting position for Cross Arms Alternate Leg Lift. 3. Execute the movement with proper form, focusing on your full body. 4. Control both the lifting and lowering phases of the movement. 5. Repeat for the prescribed number of repetitions.', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 2, NULL, 7, 7, NULL, 5, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 8, 12, NULL, 6, NULL, TRUE, NULL, 'Strength', 50, 7, 8, TRUE, TRUE, 'boxing', 'Cross Arms Leg Lift - Alternating', 'crunch, plank, russian_twist, hanging_knee_raise', FALSE, 'bodyweight', FALSE, 3, 90, 4, 70, 88, 95, 65),
('469281cd-2121-4943-93da-ec45bdcaf7df', 'Incline Fly (Stability Ball, Dumbbell)', 'Chest', 'Dumbbells, Stability Ball, Incline Bench', '{"Chest"}'::text[], '{"Front Delts"}'::text[], 'This flying exercise focuses on your pectorals for improved chest strength and development. You''ll also feel your front delts working to support the movement. Using an incline changes the angle of resistance for varied muscle recruitment. Dumbbells allow each arm to work independently, helping correct imbalances. Chest strength improves pushing power for sports, daily tasks, and other lifts.', '26261201', '26261201-Dumbbell-Incline-Fly-on-Exercise-Ball-(female)_Chest.mp4', 'female', FALSE, '2025-12-03 23:26:32.914483+00', '1. Select a pair of dumbbells at an appropriate weight for Dumbbell Incline Fly. 2. With a slight bend in your elbows, move the weight in a wide arc. 3. Squeeze your chest muscles at the center/top of the movement. 4. Return with control, feeling the stretch at the bottom. 5. Continue for your target rep count, maintaining good form throughout. Exhale during the exertion phase of the movement.', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 2, NULL, 5, 7, NULL, 6, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 12, 20, NULL, 4, NULL, TRUE, NULL, 'Strength', 69, 5, 7, FALSE, TRUE, 'chest_fly', 'Incline Fly', 'bench_press, incline_press, push_up', TRUE, 'dumbbell', FALSE, 3, 60, 2, 92, 90, 92, 90),
('469bdb70-1790-4bba-81b2-343f981dd46d', 'Twisting Crunch (arms Straight)', 'Core', 'Bodyweight', '{"Abs"}'::text[], '{}'::text[], 'Work your side abdominals with this crunching exercise that strengthens your obliques. The hip flexors assist throughout the movement, making this a well-rounded exercise. No equipment needed—your body provides all the resistance. Building core stability helps with everything from heavy deadlifts to daily activities.', '8231201', '08231201-Twisting-Crunch-(arms-straight)_Waist.mp4', 'female', FALSE, '2025-12-03 23:26:39.79101+00', '1. Curl your shoulders off the floor by contracting your abs. 2. Don''t pull on your neck—focus on the abdominal contraction. 3. Lower with control, maintaining some tension. 4. Complete all reps with control before resting. Ensure full range of motion on each rep. This variation specifically emphasizes the obliques.', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 2, NULL, 5, 7, NULL, 6, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 12, 20, NULL, 4, NULL, TRUE, NULL, 'Strength', 62, 5, 7, FALSE, TRUE, 'crunch', 'Twisting Crunch', 'leg_raise, plank, russian_twist, v_up', TRUE, 'bodyweight', FALSE, 3, 60, 2, 70, 88, 95, 65),
('46c96882-bccd-4d7d-b29c-1ce523335808', 'Seated Chest Push (Chair)', 'Chest', 'Chair', '{"Chest"}'::text[], '{}'::text[], 'Target your chest with the Seated Chest Push On A Chair, an effective pushing movement for upper body strength. Being seated provides stability, allowing you to focus on the working muscles. Chest strength improves pushing power for sports, daily tasks, and other lifts.', '91131201', '91131201-Sitting-Chest-Push-on-a-Chair-(female)_Chest_.mp4', 'female', FALSE, '2025-12-03 23:26:37.628647+00', '1. Position yourself with a sturdy chair for support or as part of the movement. 2. Sit with your back supported, core engaged, feet flat on the floor. 3. Continue for your target rep count, maintaining good form throughout. Focus on maintaining proper breathing throughout. This variation specifically emphasizes the chest.', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 2, NULL, 7, 7, NULL, 5, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 8, 12, NULL, 6, NULL, TRUE, NULL, 'Strength', 35, 7, 8, TRUE, TRUE, 'chest_exercise', 'Seated Chest Push On A Chair', 'bench_press, chest_fly, push_up', FALSE, 'bodyweight', FALSE, 3, 90, 4, 70, 88, 95, 65),
('46cf8be3-9b26-4df2-b968-f4fa74c85456', 'Standing Hamstring Stretch (Gymnastic Rings)', 'Legs', 'Gymnastic Rings', '{"Hamstrings"}'::text[], '{"Glutes"}'::text[], 'This stretching movement works your hamstrings for balanced leg development. The standing position engages your core for stability. Leg training boosts metabolism and builds functional, real-world strength.', '7891201', '07891201-Standing-Hamstring-Stretch-(female)_Thighs_.mp4', 'female', FALSE, '2025-12-03 23:26:38.7451+00', '1. Begin in a standing position with good posture. 2. Set up in the starting position for Standing Hamstring Stretch. 3. Execute the movement with proper form, focusing on your hamstrings. 4. Control both the lifting and lowering phases of the movement. 5. Complete all reps with control before resting.', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 1, NULL, 1, 1, NULL, 3, 'Standing', NULL, NULL, NULL, 1, 1, NULL, 1, NULL, TRUE, NULL, 'Stretch', 30, 2, 6, FALSE, TRUE, 'hamstring_stretch', 'Standing Hamstring Stretch', 'stretch_hip, stretch_calf, stretch_back', FALSE, 'gymnastic_rings', TRUE, 1, 30, 2, 68, 85, 85, 70),
('46d0da9d-3b15-4176-9521-849bf448186a', 'Side Swing Skater Stepback', 'Legs', 'Bodyweight', '{"Glutes"}'::text[], '{"Quads","Hip Abductors"}'::text[], 'The Side Swing Skater Stepback is an explosive exercise that combines cardiovascular training with dynamic swinging movements. You''ll also feel your quads working to support the movement. Great for improving athletic performance, burning calories, and building conditioning.', '83901201', '83901201-Side-Swing-Skater-Stepback-(male)_Plyometrics_.mp4', 'male', FALSE, '2025-12-03 23:26:26.39056+00', '1. Set up a box or step platform at the appropriate height. 2. Hinge at your hips, letting the weight swing back between your legs. 3. Explosively drive hips forward, propelling the weight forward/up. 4. Let gravity bring it back as you hinge for the next rep. 5. Complete all reps with control before resting. Keep tension on the target muscles throughout.', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 2, NULL, 5, 4, NULL, 8, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 8, 12, NULL, 7, NULL, TRUE, NULL, 'Plyometrics', 50, 9, 8, TRUE, TRUE, 'kettlebell_swing', 'Side Swing Skater Stepback', 'squat, bench_press, deadlift', FALSE, 'bodyweight', FALSE, 3, 60, 4, 70, 88, 95, 65),
('46f8cdf0-d50e-44a3-82c8-5048378c8127', 'Landmine Front Squat (Landmine)', 'Legs', 'Landmine Attachment, Barbell', '{"Quads"}'::text[], '{"Glutes","Core"}'::text[], 'Build stronger quads with this squatting movement that develops leg drive and power. Your glutes, hamstrings work as secondary movers, adding to the training stimulus. Strong legs are the foundation for athletic performance and functional fitness. Control the negative portion for maximum muscle engagement.', '42461201', '42461201-Landmine-Front-Squat_Thighs_.mp4', 'male', FALSE, '2025-12-03 23:26:21.249384+00', '1. Push your hips back and bend your knees to lower your body. 2. Keep your chest up and knees tracking over your toes. 3. Drive through your heels to stand back up, squeezing your glutes at the top. 4. Repeat for the prescribed number of repetitions. Keep your core engaged for stability. This exercise is excellent for quads development.', 'Squat', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 4, NULL, 10, 10, NULL, 4, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 5, 8, NULL, 9, NULL, TRUE, NULL, 'Strength', 85, 7, 9, TRUE, FALSE, 'front_squat', 'Landmine Front Squat', 'squat, leg_press, leg_extension, goblet_squat', TRUE, 'barbell', FALSE, 4, 120, 5, 95, 80, 65, 95),
('46fe3eba-5936-4b20-8927-737703e6df72', 'Butt Kicks', 'Legs', 'Bodyweight', '{"Glutes","Hamstrings"}'::text[], '{"Calves"}'::text[], 'This cardio exercise keeps your heart rate elevated for improved cardiovascular fitness. The hamstrings assist throughout the movement, making this a well-rounded exercise. Cardiovascular exercise improves heart health, endurance, and helps manage weight.', '1461201', '01461201-Butt-Kicks-(female)_Cardio.mp4', 'female', FALSE, '2025-12-03 23:26:31.723232+00', '1. Set up in the starting position for Butt Kicks. 2. Execute the movement with proper form, focusing on your cardio. 3. Control both the lifting and lowering phases of the movement. 4. Complete all reps with control before resting.', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 2, NULL, 7, 7, NULL, 5, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 8, 12, NULL, 6, NULL, TRUE, NULL, 'Strength', 50, 7, 8, TRUE, TRUE, 'glute_kickback', 'Butt Kicks', 'high_knees, jumping_jack, running', FALSE, 'bodyweight', FALSE, 3, 90, 4, 70, 88, 95, 65),
('4701cf20-4cd3-40f6-9960-61bc29b9676a', 'Lat Stretch (Stick)', 'Back', 'Bodyweight', '{"Lats"}'::text[], '{"Lower Back"}'::text[], 'This stretching exercise emphasizes your lats for improved back development. This bodyweight exercise requires no equipment and can be done anywhere. A strong back improves posture, prevents injury, and balances pressing movements.', '54001201', '54001201-Stick-Lat-Stretch-(female)_Back_.mp4', 'female', FALSE, '2025-12-03 23:26:39.21093+00', '1. Set up in the starting position for Stick Lat Stretch. 2. Execute the movement with proper form, focusing on your lats. 3. Control both the lifting and lowering phases of the movement. 4. Complete all reps with control before resting.', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 1, NULL, 1, 1, NULL, 3, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 1, 1, NULL, 1, NULL, TRUE, NULL, 'Stretch', 40, 2, 6, FALSE, TRUE, 'lat_stretch', 'Stick Lat Stretch', 'stretch_hip, stretch_back', FALSE, 'bodyweight', TRUE, 1, 30, 2, 70, 88, 95, 65),
('470208b7-69d3-4ae4-9c17-51be18d369d9', 'Bent Over Row - Reverse Grip (Cable)', 'Back', 'Cables', '{"Upper Back"}'::text[], '{"Lats","Biceps","Rear Delts"}'::text[], 'The Cable Bent Over Reverse Grip Row is a rowing exercise that builds thickness in your upper back. Your biceps, rear delts work as secondary movers, adding to the training stimulus. Bending over allows gravity to provide resistance in a different plane. The cable setup allows you to adjust the angle of resistance. A strong back improves posture, prevents injury, and balances pressing movements.', '43671201', '43671201-Cable-Bent-Over-Reverse-Grip-Row_Back_.mp4', 'male', FALSE, '2025-12-03 23:26:24.422129+00', '1. Adjust the cable machine to the correct height and attachment for Cable Bent Over Reverse Grip Row. 2. Hinge at your hips, pushing them back while keeping your back flat. 3. Use a reverse grip (opposite of the standard grip for this exercise). 4. Pull the weight toward your torso, leading with your elbow(s). 5. Squeeze your shoulder blades together at the peak contraction. 6. Extend back out with control, feeling the stretch in your back. 7. Repeat for the prescribed number of repetitions.', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 3, NULL, 7, 8, NULL, 5, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 8, 12, NULL, 6, NULL, FALSE, NULL, 'Strength', 80, 7, 8, TRUE, TRUE, 'general_exercise', 'Bent Over Row - Reverse Grip', 'Bent Over Row - Reverse Grip', FALSE, 'cable', FALSE, 3, 90, 4, 85, 88, 30, 92),
('470c459c-b9b7-43dc-b0fb-e7ab74135c37', 'Lateral Shuffle Crunch', 'Core', 'Bodyweight', '{"Abs"}'::text[], '{"Hip Flexors"}'::text[], 'A challenging plyometric exercise, the Lateral Shuffle Crunches builds reactive power and improves conditioning. The hip flexors assist throughout the movement, making this a well-rounded exercise. This bodyweight exercise requires no equipment and can be done anywhere. Develops fast-twitch muscle fibers for quicker, more powerful movements.', '59621201', '59621201-Lateral-Shuffle-Crunches-(female)_Plyometrics_.mp4', 'female', FALSE, '2025-12-03 23:26:34.603963+00', '1. Curl your shoulders off the floor by contracting your abs. 2. Don''t pull on your neck—focus on the abdominal contraction. 3. Lower with control, maintaining some tension. 4. Continue for your target rep count, maintaining good form throughout. Maintain a neutral spine throughout. Great for building strength in your abs.', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 2, NULL, 5, 4, NULL, 8, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 8, 12, NULL, 7, NULL, TRUE, NULL, 'Plyometrics', 70, 9, 8, TRUE, TRUE, 'shuffle', 'Lateral Shuffle Crunch', 'plank, leg_raise, russian_twist, sit_up', TRUE, 'bodyweight', FALSE, 3, 60, 4, 70, 88, 95, 65),
('470e4cd3-c6f0-44a8-be06-2ff81222a70f', 'Seated Lotus Pose Hand Behind Side Bend', 'Core', 'Bodyweight', '{"Obliques"}'::text[], '{"Abs"}'::text[], 'Work your side abdominals with this movement exercise that strengthens your obliques. The abs assist throughout the movement, making this a well-rounded exercise. Being seated provides stability, allowing you to focus on the working muscles. A strong core improves posture, protects your spine, and enhances all other lifts.', '88561201', '88561201-Sitting-Lotus-Pose-Hand-Behind-Side-Bend-(male)_Wa.mp4', 'male', FALSE, '2025-12-03 23:26:22.417605+00', '1. Sit with your back supported, core engaged, feet flat on the floor. 2. Set up in the starting position for Seated Lotus Pose Hand Behind Side Bend. 3. Execute the movement with proper form, focusing on your obliques. 4. Control both the lifting and lowering phases of the movement. 5. Repeat for the prescribed number of repetitions.', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 1, NULL, 1, 1, NULL, 3, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 1, 1, NULL, 1, NULL, TRUE, NULL, 'Stretch', 15, 2, 6, FALSE, TRUE, 'side_bend', 'Seated Lotus Pose Hand Behind Side Bend', 'stretch_hip, stretch_back, plank', FALSE, 'bodyweight', TRUE, 1, 30, 2, 70, 88, 95, 65),
('470fe50c-1896-4840-9051-a9878dc0ddb9', 'Aztec Push Up', 'Chest', 'Bodyweight', '{"Chest"}'::text[], '{"Triceps","Front Delts"}'::text[], 'This pushing exercise engages your abs for improved core stability and strength. You''ll also feel your triceps, front delts working to support the movement. No equipment needed—your body provides all the resistance. Core strength is foundational for athletic performance and injury prevention. Keep your core engaged throughout the exercise.', '74641201', '74641201-Aztec-Push-up-(male)_Waist_.mp4', 'male', FALSE, '2025-12-03 23:26:25.737494+00', '1. Keep your body in a straight line from head to heels throughout. 2. Lower your chest toward the floor by bending your elbows. 3. Push through your palms to return to the starting position. 4. Continue for your target rep count, maintaining good form throughout. Maintain consistent tempo throughout the set. Include this in your core training.', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 2, NULL, 7, 7, NULL, 5, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 8, 12, NULL, 6, NULL, TRUE, NULL, 'Strength', 70, 7, 8, TRUE, TRUE, 'push_up', 'Aztec Push Up', 'bench_press, chest_fly, dip', TRUE, 'bodyweight', FALSE, 3, 90, 4, 70, 88, 95, 65),
('471ec267-2cb3-4a52-9f9c-63047b38964b', 'Elevated Heel Squat (Barbell)', 'Legs', 'Barbell, Step Platform', '{"Quads"}'::text[], '{"Glutes","Hamstrings"}'::text[], 'Build stronger quads with this squatting movement that develops leg drive and power. You''ll also feel your glutes, hamstrings working to support the movement. Barbells enable bilateral loading for building raw strength. Leg training boosts metabolism and builds functional, real-world strength.', '41781201', '41781201-Barbell-Elevated-Heel-Squat_Thighs_.mp4', 'male', FALSE, '2025-12-03 23:26:29.971345+00', '1. Set up a barbell in a rack at the appropriate height for Barbell Elevated Heel Squat. 2. Push your hips back and bend your knees to lower your body. 3. Keep your chest up and knees tracking over your toes. 4. Drive through your heels to stand back up, squeezing your glutes at the top. 5. Complete all reps with control before resting.', 'Squat', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 3, NULL, 10, 10, NULL, 4, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 5, 8, NULL, 9, NULL, TRUE, NULL, 'Strength', 97, 7, 9, TRUE, FALSE, 'squat', 'Elevated Heel Squat', 'leg_press, front_squat, goblet_squat, lunge, leg_extension', TRUE, 'barbell', FALSE, 4, 120, 5, 95, 80, 65, 95),
('472491b2-8c37-4f09-a5dd-5c283296dd60', 'Single Leg Squat (Hack Squat Machine)', 'Legs', 'Machine', '{"Quads"}'::text[], '{"Glutes","Hamstrings"}'::text[], 'Build stronger quads with this squatting movement that develops leg drive and power. Your glutes work as secondary movers, adding to the training stimulus. The fixed path allows you to focus purely on muscular effort. Strong legs are the foundation for athletic performance and functional fitness.', '99291201', '99291201-Lever-Single-Leg-Squat-on-Hack-Squat-Machine-(fema.mp4', 'female', FALSE, '2025-12-03 23:26:34.855778+00', '1. Adjust the machine settings (seat height, weight, pads) to fit your body for Lever Single Leg Squat On Hack Squat Machine. 2. Push your hips back and bend your knees to lower your body. 3. Keep your chest up and knees tracking over your toes. 4. Drive through your heels to stand back up, squeezing your glutes at the top. 5. Complete all reps on one side, then switch to the other side. 6. Repeat for the prescribed number of repetitions.', 'Squat', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 1, NULL, 10, 10, NULL, 4, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 5, 8, NULL, 9, NULL, FALSE, NULL, 'Strength', 88, 7, 9, TRUE, FALSE, 'pistol_squat', 'Lever Single Leg Squat On Hack Squat', 'leg_press, squat, leg_extension', TRUE, 'machine', FALSE, 4, 120, 5, 80, 75, 20, 88),
('473523cd-f5a5-40ff-9a91-c1269bfec3e1', 'Kneeling Sissy Squat', 'Legs', 'Bodyweight', '{"Quads"}'::text[], '{"Glutes"}'::text[], 'The Bodyweight Kneeling Sissy Squat is a squatting exercise that primarily loads your quadriceps. Your glutes, hamstrings work as secondary movers, adding to the training stimulus. The kneeling position adds a core stability challenge. No equipment needed—your body provides all the resistance. Lower body strength improves everything from walking to heavy compound lifts.', '70581201', '70581201-Bodyweight-Kneeling-Sissy-Squat-(female)_Thighs_.mp4', 'female', FALSE, '2025-12-03 23:26:31.347577+00', '1. Kneel on the floor (use a pad for comfort if needed). 2. Push your hips back and bend your knees to lower your body. 3. Keep your chest up and knees tracking over your toes. 4. Drive through your heels to stand back up, squeezing your glutes at the top. 5. Repeat for the prescribed number of repetitions. Keep tension on the target muscles throughout.', 'Squat', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 4, NULL, 7, 7, NULL, 5, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 8, 12, NULL, 6, NULL, TRUE, NULL, 'Strength', 85, 7, 8, TRUE, TRUE, 'squat', 'Kneeling Sissy Squat', 'leg_press, front_squat, goblet_squat, lunge, leg_extension', FALSE, 'bodyweight', FALSE, 3, 90, 4, 70, 88, 95, 65),
('4742d70b-88ed-4db0-a67e-dec126c035f8', 'Roll Glute Twist Lying On Floor', 'Legs', 'Bodyweight', '{"Glutes"}'::text[], '{"Hamstrings"}'::text[], 'Develop your posterior chain with this twisting movement that emphasizes the glutes. Your abs work as secondary movers, adding to the training stimulus. The lying position provides back support and helps isolate the target muscles. No equipment needed—your body provides all the resistance. Leg training boosts metabolism and builds functional, real-world strength.', '54291201', '54291201-Roll-Glute-Twist-Lying-on-Floor-(female)_Hips_.mp4', 'female', FALSE, '2025-12-03 23:26:36.38616+00', '1. Position yourself on the floor for Roll Glute Twist Lying On Floor. 2. Lie down in the appropriate position for Roll Glute Twist Lying On Floor. 3. Rotate your torso through the movement pattern for Roll Glute Twist Lying On Floor. 4. Control the rotation in both directions—avoid using momentum. 5. Continue for your target rep count, maintaining good form throughout.', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 2, NULL, 5, 7, NULL, 6, 'Lying', NULL, NULL, NULL, 10, 15, NULL, 4, NULL, TRUE, NULL, 'Strength', 45, 5, 7, FALSE, TRUE, 'russian_twist', 'Roll Glute Twist Lying On Floor', 'hip_thrust, glute_bridge, leg_curl', FALSE, 'bodyweight', FALSE, 3, 60, 2, 70, 88, 95, 65),
('475a1880-efab-4520-bd5b-e48fc1c7c8cc', 'Plyo Squat (Dumbbell)', 'Legs', 'Dumbbells', '{"Quads"}'::text[], '{"Glutes","Hamstrings"}'::text[], 'Target the front of your thighs with this squatting exercise for quad development. Your glutes, hamstrings work as secondary movers, adding to the training stimulus. Using dumbbells requires more stabilization than barbell variations. Lower body strength improves everything from walking to heavy compound lifts. Keep your core engaged throughout the exercise.', '69991201', '69991201-Dumbbell-Plyo-Squat-(female)_Thighs_.mp4', 'female', FALSE, '2025-12-03 23:26:33.034396+00', '1. Select a pair of dumbbells at an appropriate weight for Dumbbell Plyo Squat. 2. Push your hips back and bend your knees to lower your body. 3. Keep your chest up and knees tracking over your toes. 4. Drive through your heels to stand back up, squeezing your glutes at the top. 5. Continue for your target rep count, maintaining good form throughout.', 'Squat', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 4, NULL, 5, 4, NULL, 8, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 8, 12, NULL, 7, NULL, TRUE, NULL, 'Plyometrics', 97, 9, 8, TRUE, TRUE, 'squat', 'Plyo Squat', 'leg_press, front_squat, goblet_squat, lunge, leg_extension', FALSE, 'dumbbell', FALSE, 3, 60, 4, 92, 90, 92, 90),
('475c7463-fc76-4273-ab1b-7f205746a9e5', 'Standing Shoulder External Rotation (Cable)', 'Shoulders', 'Cables', '{"Rotator Cuff"}'::text[], '{"Shoulders"}'::text[], 'The Cable Standing Shoulder External Rotation is a rotation exercise that develops back strength and muscle. The standing position engages your core for stability. The cable setup allows you to adjust the angle of resistance. A strong back improves posture, prevents injury, and balances pressing movements.', '2351201', '02351201-Cable-Standing-Shoulder-External-Rotation_Back-FIX.mp4', 'male', FALSE, '2025-12-03 23:26:22.247914+00', '1. Adjust the cable machine to the correct height and attachment for Cable Standing Shoulder External Rotation. 2. Begin in a standing position with good posture. 3. Rotate your torso through the movement pattern for Cable Standing Shoulder External Rotation. 4. Control the rotation in both directions—avoid using momentum. 5. Repeat for the prescribed number of repetitions.', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 2, NULL, 7, 8, NULL, 5, 'Standing', NULL, NULL, NULL, 8, 12, NULL, 6, NULL, FALSE, NULL, 'Strength', 62, 7, 8, TRUE, TRUE, 'external_rotation', 'Standing Shoulder External Rotation', 'squat, bench_press, deadlift', FALSE, 'cable', FALSE, 3, 90, 4, 85, 88, 30, 92),
('47656b75-478b-47a4-9a28-16f041ba6d06', 'Seated Twist (Straight Arm)', 'Core', 'Bodyweight', '{"Obliques"}'::text[], '{"Abs"}'::text[], 'Build rotational power and define your waistline with the Seated Twist (straight Arm). Secondary activation of your abs provides additional muscle engagement. Being seated provides stability, allowing you to focus on the working muscles. Core strength is foundational for athletic performance and injury prevention.', '43071201', '43071201-Seated-Twist-(Straight-Arm)-(male)_Waist.mp4', 'male', FALSE, '2025-12-03 23:26:29.837118+00', '1. Sit with your back supported, core engaged, feet flat on the floor. 2. Rotate your torso through the movement pattern for Seated Twist. 3. Control the rotation in both directions—avoid using momentum. 4. Complete all reps with control before resting.', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 2, NULL, 5, 7, NULL, 6, 'Seated', NULL, NULL, NULL, 10, 15, NULL, 4, NULL, TRUE, NULL, 'Strength', 52, 5, 7, FALSE, TRUE, 'russian_twist', 'Seated Twist', 'bicep_curl, tricep_extension, hammer_curl', FALSE, 'bodyweight', FALSE, 3, 60, 2, 70, 88, 95, 65),
('476945cb-8338-4c98-b68c-b245d2ee5f7c', 'Hanging Straight Twisting Leg Hip Raise (Pull-Up Bar)', 'Core', 'Pull-Up Bar', '{"Obliques"}'::text[], '{"Abs"}'::text[], 'This raising movement focuses on your obliques for a complete core workout. Secondary activation of your hip flexors, grip provides additional muscle engagement. Hanging adds a grip and core stability component to the exercise. A versatile bodyweight movement perfect for home or gym training. A strong core improves posture, protects your spine, and enhances all other lifts.', '4761201', '04761201-Hanging-Straight-Twisting-Leg-Hip-Raise_Waist_.mp4', 'male', FALSE, '2025-12-03 23:26:26.39056+00', '1. Grip the bar and hang with arms fully extended, engaging your shoulders. 2. Rotate your torso through the movement pattern for Hanging Straight Twisting Leg Hip Raise. 3. Control the rotation in both directions—avoid using momentum. 4. Complete all reps with control before resting.', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 2, NULL, 5, 7, NULL, 6, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 10, 15, NULL, 4, NULL, TRUE, NULL, 'Strength', 62, 5, 7, FALSE, TRUE, 'russian_twist', 'Hanging Straight Twisting Leg Hip Raise', 'leg_raise, crunch, plank', FALSE, 'pull_up_bar', FALSE, 3, 60, 2, 70, 88, 95, 65),
('4769b913-159e-41cb-a9f2-41fef06ea280', 'Side Step Shuffles', 'Legs', 'Bodyweight', '{"Quads"}'::text[], '{"Glutes","Hamstrings"}'::text[], 'Elevate your training with this stepping exercise that develops speed, power, and coordination. You''ll also feel your quads working to support the movement. Develops fast-twitch muscle fibers for quicker, more powerful movements.', '57631201', '57631201-Side-Step-Shuffles_Plyometrics_.mp4', 'male', FALSE, '2025-12-03 23:26:20.982555+00', '1. Set up a box or step platform at the appropriate height. 2. Set up in the starting position for Side Step Shuffles. 3. Execute the movement with proper form, focusing on your full body. 4. Control both the lifting and lowering phases of the movement. 5. Complete all reps with control before resting.', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 2, NULL, 5, 4, NULL, 8, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 8, 12, NULL, 7, NULL, TRUE, NULL, 'Plyometrics', 50, 9, 8, TRUE, TRUE, 'shuffle', 'Side Step Shuffles', 'squat, bench_press, deadlift', FALSE, 'bodyweight', FALSE, 3, 60, 4, 70, 88, 95, 65),
('477208bd-1884-415f-921c-b64f7259f2ce', 'Standing Hands Behind Chest Stretch', 'Chest', 'Bodyweight', '{"Chest"}'::text[], '{"Front Delts"}'::text[], 'The Standing Hands Behind Chest Stretch provides a deep stretch for your chest, ideal for recovery and mobility work. The shoulders assist throughout the movement, making this a well-rounded exercise. The standing position engages your core for stability. Regular stretching improves flexibility, reduces injury risk, and aids recovery.', '96821201', '96821201-Standing-Hands-Behind-Chest-Stretch-(male)_Stretch.mp4', 'male', FALSE, '2025-12-03 23:26:21.109351+00', '1. Begin in a standing position with good posture. 2. Move into the stretch position for Standing Hands Behind Chest Stretch. 3. Ease into the stretch until you feel gentle tension (not pain). 4. Hold for 20-30 seconds, breathing deeply and relaxing into the stretch.', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 1, NULL, 1, 1, NULL, 3, 'Standing', NULL, NULL, NULL, 1, 1, NULL, 1, NULL, TRUE, NULL, 'Stretch', 42, 2, 6, FALSE, TRUE, 'chest_stretch', 'Standing Hands Behind Chest Stretch', 'stretch_shoulder, stretch_back', FALSE, 'bodyweight', TRUE, 1, 30, 2, 70, 88, 95, 65),
('477b9dbf-e31c-4847-84a9-edec1eaeb6b4', 'Lying Frog Kick - Alternating', 'Core', 'Bodyweight', '{"Abs"}'::text[], '{"Hip Flexors"}'::text[], 'The Lying Alternate Frog Kick is a lower body kicking exercise that targets your core. Performing this lying down removes momentum for stricter form. No equipment needed—your body provides all the resistance. Strong legs are the foundation for athletic performance and functional fitness.', '60221201', '60221201-Lying-Alternate-Frog-Kick-(female)_Hips_.mp4', 'female', FALSE, '2025-12-03 23:26:35.010404+00', '1. Lie down in the appropriate position for Lying Alternate Frog Kick. 2. Alternate between sides/arms/legs with each repetition. 3. Complete all reps with control before resting.', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 2, NULL, 7, 7, NULL, 5, 'Lying', NULL, NULL, NULL, 8, 12, NULL, 6, NULL, TRUE, NULL, 'Strength', 50, 7, 8, TRUE, TRUE, 'general_exercise', 'Lying Frog Kick - Alternating', 'hip_flexor, lunge, dynamic_warmup', FALSE, 'bodyweight', FALSE, 3, 90, 4, 70, 88, 95, 65),
('478ee29d-20ff-4d1b-992d-9f3c4dca0ad2', 'Seated Row (Chair)', 'Back', 'Chair', '{"Upper Back"}'::text[], '{"Lats","Biceps","Rear Delts"}'::text[], 'Target your rhomboids and mid-traps with this rowing movement. Secondary activation of your biceps, lats provides additional muscle engagement. The seated position helps isolate the target muscles by removing momentum. A strong back improves posture, prevents injury, and balances pressing movements.', '104751201', '104751201-Seated-Row-on-a-Chair-(male)_Back_.mp4', 'male', FALSE, '2025-12-03 23:26:22.755209+00', '1. Position yourself with a sturdy chair for support or as part of the movement. 2. Sit with your back supported, core engaged, feet flat on the floor. 3. Pull the weight toward your torso, leading with your elbow(s). 4. Squeeze your shoulder blades together at the peak contraction. 5. Extend back out with control, feeling the stretch in your back. 6. Continue for your target rep count, maintaining good form throughout. Keep tension on the target muscles throughout.', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 2, NULL, 7, 7, NULL, 5, 'Seated', NULL, NULL, NULL, 8, 12, NULL, 6, NULL, TRUE, NULL, 'Strength', 67, 7, 8, TRUE, TRUE, 'cable_row', 'Seated Row On A Chair', 'lat_pulldown, bent_over_row, pull_up', FALSE, 'bodyweight', FALSE, 3, 90, 4, 70, 88, 95, 65),
('4794285e-058a-4a17-bed8-d4fdd57722e7', 'Twist Turn Chop', 'Full Body', 'Bodyweight', '{"Full Body"}'::text[], '{"Abs"}'::text[], 'Elevate your training with this twisting exercise that develops speed, power, and coordination. Secondary activation of your abs provides additional muscle engagement. No equipment needed—your body provides all the resistance. Great for improving athletic performance, burning calories, and building conditioning.', '73401201', '73401201-Twist-Turn-Chop-(male)_Plyometrics_.mp4', 'male', FALSE, '2025-12-03 23:26:20.392006+00', '1. Rotate your torso through the movement pattern for Twist Turn Chop. 2. Control the rotation in both directions—avoid using momentum. 3. Complete all reps with control before resting.', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 2, NULL, 5, 4, NULL, 8, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 8, 12, NULL, 7, NULL, TRUE, NULL, 'Plyometrics', 50, 9, 8, TRUE, TRUE, 'russian_twist', 'Twist Turn Chop', 'squat, bench_press, deadlift', FALSE, 'bodyweight', FALSE, 3, 60, 4, 70, 88, 95, 65),
('4795c408-ac4c-4f01-a569-f281a328500a', 'Arm Curl (TRX)', 'Arms', 'TRX', '{"Biceps"}'::text[], '{"Forearms"}'::text[], 'The Suspender Arm Curl is a curling exercise that isolates your biceps. You''ll also feel your forearms working to support the movement. Suspension training adds instability, increasing core activation throughout. Arm strength supports grip, pulling, and pushing in compound movements.', '10701201', '10701201-Suspender-Arm-Curl-(female)_Upper-Arms_.mp4', 'female', FALSE, '2025-12-03 23:26:39.340041+00', '1. Adjust the TRX/suspension straps to the appropriate length for Suspender Arm Curl. 2. Keep your elbows in a fixed position throughout the movement. 3. Curl the weight up by contracting your biceps, squeezing at the top. 4. Lower with control, resisting the weight on the way down. 5. Repeat for the prescribed number of repetitions. Control the movement—avoid using momentum.', 'Curl', 'Pull', NULL, NULL, NULL, 2, NULL, 5, 7, NULL, 6, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 10, 15, NULL, 4, NULL, TRUE, NULL, 'Strength', 60, 5, 7, FALSE, TRUE, 'bicep_curl', 'Suspender Arm Curl', 'hammer_curl, preacher_curl, cable_curl', FALSE, 'trx', FALSE, 3, 60, 2, 68, 85, 85, 70),
('47b7c842-8a3a-4648-a285-c5507015f55c', 'Standing Left Over Right Hand Slant', 'Full Body', 'Bodyweight', '{"Full Body"}'::text[], '{}'::text[], 'Target your full body with this movement stretch that helps restore range of motion. The standing position engages your core for stability. Include this in your routine for better mobility and reduced muscle tension.', '95341201', '95341201-Standing-Left-Over-Right-Hand-Slant-(female)_Stret.mp4', 'female', FALSE, '2025-12-03 23:26:38.7451+00', '1. Begin in a standing position with good posture. 2. Move into the stretch position for Standing Left Over Right Hand Slant. 3. Ease into the stretch until you feel gentle tension (not pain). 4. Hold for 20-30 seconds, breathing deeply and relaxing into the stretch. 5. Switch sides and repeat for equal time.', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 2, NULL, 7, 7, NULL, 5, 'Standing', NULL, NULL, NULL, 8, 12, NULL, 6, NULL, TRUE, NULL, 'Strength', 52, 7, 8, TRUE, TRUE, 'general_exercise', 'Standing Left Over Right Hand Slant', 'squat, bench_press, deadlift', FALSE, 'bodyweight', FALSE, 3, 90, 4, 70, 88, 95, 65),
('47b9d20b-5ea9-4ea4-832b-e847ab4f8650', 'Decline Bench Press (Barbell)', 'Chest', 'Barbell, Decline Bench', '{"Chest","Lower Chest"}'::text[], '{"Front Delts","Triceps"}'::text[], 'The Barbell Decline Bench Press is a pressing exercise that targets your chest muscles. The triceps, front delts assist throughout the movement, making this a well-rounded exercise. The decline position targets the lower portion of the muscles more intensely. The barbell allows you to handle heavier loads for maximum strength gains. Chest strength improves pushing power for sports, daily tasks, and other lifts.', '24531201', '24531201-Barbell-Decline-Bench-Press-(female)_Chest.mp4', 'female', FALSE, '2025-12-03 23:26:31.013316+00', '1. Load a barbell and set it on a bench rack at the appropriate height. 2. Lower the weight toward your chest with control. 3. Press the weight up until your arms are extended (don''t lock elbows). 4. Repeat for the prescribed number of repetitions. Exhale during the exertion phase of the movement.', 'Press', 'Push', 'Compound', 'Bilateral', NULL, 3, NULL, 10, 10, NULL, 4, 'Lying (Decline)', NULL, 'Overhand (pronated)', 'Slightly wider than shoulder-width', 5, 8, NULL, 8, NULL, FALSE, NULL, 'Strength', 100, 7, 9, TRUE, FALSE, 'decline_press', 'Decline Bench Press', 'bench_press, incline_bench_press, chest_fly, dip', TRUE, 'barbell', FALSE, 4, 120, 4, 95, 80, 65, 95),
('47d2073a-aaab-4f0c-bb36-736fa15f58f2', 'Twisting Jack Knife (TRX)', 'Core', 'TRX', '{"Obliques"}'::text[], '{"Abs"}'::text[], 'This twisting movement focuses on your obliques for a complete core workout. You''ll also feel your abs working to support the movement. Suspension training adds instability, increasing core activation throughout. Building core stability helps with everything from heavy deadlifts to daily activities.', '11061201', '11061201-Suspender-Twisting-Jack-knife-(female)_Waist_.mp4', 'female', FALSE, '2025-12-03 23:26:39.623429+00', '1. Adjust the TRX/suspension straps to the appropriate length for Suspender Twisting Jack Knife. 2. Rotate your torso through the movement pattern for Suspender Twisting Jack Knife. 3. Control the rotation in both directions—avoid using momentum. 4. Continue for your target rep count, maintaining good form throughout.', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 2, NULL, 5, 4, NULL, 8, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 8, 12, NULL, 7, NULL, TRUE, NULL, 'Plyometrics', 32, 9, 8, TRUE, TRUE, 'russian_twist', 'Suspender Twisting Jack Knife', 'squat, bench_press, deadlift', FALSE, 'trx', FALSE, 3, 60, 4, 68, 85, 85, 70),
('47dcb7c5-4809-46ec-8f61-6c2b01189ba1', 'Jumping Jack High Knee', 'Legs', 'Bodyweight', '{"Hip Flexors"}'::text[], '{"Quads","Calves"}'::text[], 'A challenging plyometric exercise, the Jumping Jack High Knee builds reactive power and improves conditioning. You''ll also feel your shoulders, calves working to support the movement. A versatile bodyweight movement perfect for home or gym training. Develops fast-twitch muscle fibers for quicker, more powerful movements.', '75551201', '75551201-Jumping-Jack-High-Knee-(male)_Plyometrics_.mp4', 'male', FALSE, '2025-12-03 23:26:25.233728+00', '1. Set up in the starting position for Jumping Jack High Knee. 2. Execute the movement with proper form, focusing on your full body. 3. Control both the lifting and lowering phases of the movement. 4. Continue for your target rep count, maintaining good form throughout.', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 2, NULL, 5, 4, NULL, 8, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 8, 12, NULL, 7, NULL, TRUE, NULL, 'Plyometrics', 50, 9, 8, TRUE, TRUE, 'jumping_jack', 'Jumping Jack High Knee', 'butt_kicks, jumping_jack, mountain_climber', FALSE, 'bodyweight', FALSE, 3, 60, 4, 70, 88, 95, 65),
('47e0ec08-eed4-4f10-a67f-9b68ed3267a1', 'Stiff Legged Deadlift (Barbell)', 'Legs', 'Barbell', '{"Hamstrings"}'::text[], '{"Glutes","Lower Back"}'::text[], 'Build leg strength with this hip hinge movement focusing on your hamstrings/glutes. The glutes, lower back assist throughout the movement, making this a well-rounded exercise. Using a barbell provides stability for progressive overload. Leg training boosts metabolism and builds functional, real-world strength. A staple exercise that belongs in most training programs.', '57211201', '57211201-Barbell-Stiff-Legged-Deadlift-(female)_Hips_.mp4', 'female', FALSE, '2025-12-03 23:26:31.133197+00', '1. Grip a barbell with hands at the appropriate width for Barbell Stiff Legged Deadlift. 2. Push your hips back, lowering the weight along your legs with a flat back. 3. Lower until you feel a stretch in your hamstrings. 4. Drive hips forward to stand, squeezing glutes at the top. 5. Continue for your target rep count, maintaining good form throughout.', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 3, NULL, 10, 10, NULL, 4, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 3, 6, NULL, 10, NULL, TRUE, NULL, 'Strength', 97, 7, 9, TRUE, FALSE, 'romanian_deadlift', 'Stiff Legged Deadlift', 'deadlift, leg_curl, hip_thrust', TRUE, 'barbell', FALSE, 4, 120, 6, 95, 80, 65, 95),
('47f3e8b2-2681-4a38-84d7-d868bf34d950', 'Bridge Yoga Pose Setu Bandha Sarvangasana', 'Legs', 'Bodyweight', '{"Glutes"}'::text[], '{"Hamstrings"}'::text[], 'Designed to lengthen your glutes, the Bridge Yoga Pose Setu Bandha Sarvangasana helps improve mobility and prevent stiffness. The hamstrings assist throughout the movement, making this a well-rounded exercise. The band creates increasing tension as it stretches, challenging the lockout. Flexibility work like this enhances performance and prevents stiffness.', '80131201', '80131201-Bridge-Yoga-Pose-Setu-Bandha-Sarvangasana-(male)_S.mp4', 'male', FALSE, '2025-12-03 23:26:25.123298+00', '1. Secure the resistance band appropriately for Bridge Yoga Pose Setu Bandha Sarvangasana. 2. Drive through your heels to lift your hips toward the ceiling. 3. Squeeze your glutes hard at the top of the movement. 4. Lower your hips back down with control.', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 1, NULL, 1, 1, NULL, 3, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 1, 1, NULL, 1, NULL, TRUE, NULL, 'Stretch', 15, 2, 6, FALSE, TRUE, 'yoga', 'Bridge Yoga Pose Setu Bandha Sarvangasana', 'stretch_hip, stretch_back, plank', FALSE, 'bodyweight', TRUE, 1, 30, 2, 60, 85, 90, 50),
('47f8b5db-3f85-4afe-b8a6-493b014e4fd5', 'Side Hip Rollout (Barbell)', 'Core', 'Barbell', '{"Abs"}'::text[], '{"Hip Flexors"}'::text[], 'Build leg strength with this movement movement focusing on your abs. You''ll also feel your lats, shoulders working to support the movement. Using a barbell provides stability for progressive overload. Strong legs are the foundation for athletic performance and functional fitness.', '103711201', '103711201-Barbell-Side-Hip-Rollout_Hips_.mp4', 'male', FALSE, '2025-12-03 23:26:22.644637+00', '1. Grip a barbell with hands at the appropriate width for Barbell Side Hip Rollout. 2. Set up in the starting position for Barbell Side Hip Rollout. 3. Execute the movement with proper form, focusing on your abs. 4. Control both the lifting and lowering phases of the movement. 5. Complete all reps with control before resting.', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 3, NULL, 7, 8, NULL, 5, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 8, 12, NULL, 6, NULL, TRUE, NULL, 'Strength', 62, 7, 8, TRUE, TRUE, 'ab_rollout', 'Side Hip Rollout', 'plank, crunch, dead_bug', FALSE, 'barbell', FALSE, 3, 90, 4, 95, 80, 65, 95),
('48094d48-6960-45df-9c47-d40cd70dcec9', 'Sumo Deadlift (Barbell)', 'Legs', 'Barbell', '{"Glutes"}'::text[], '{"Quads","Lower Back","Inner Thighs"}'::text[], 'Build leg strength with this hip hinge movement focusing on your hamstrings/glutes. Secondary activation of your glutes, lower back provides additional muscle engagement. The barbell allows you to handle heavier loads for maximum strength gains. Leg training boosts metabolism and builds functional, real-world strength.', '25171201', '25171201-Barbell-Sumo-Deadlift-(female)_Hips_.mp4', 'female', FALSE, '2025-12-03 23:26:31.133197+00', '1. Grip a barbell with hands at the appropriate width for Barbell Sumo Deadlift. 2. Hinge at hips and bend knees to grip the weight. 3. Drive through your heels, extending hips and knees to stand. 4. Lower by reversing the movement with control. 5. Continue for your target rep count, maintaining good form throughout.', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 4, NULL, 10, 10, NULL, 4, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 3, 6, NULL, 10, NULL, TRUE, NULL, 'Strength', 97, 7, 9, TRUE, FALSE, 'deadlift', 'Sumo Deadlift', 'romanian_deadlift, hip_thrust, leg_curl', TRUE, 'barbell', FALSE, 4, 120, 6, 95, 80, 65, 95),
('48212ba4-e9f1-4278-bbad-c2a0873230c0', 'Empty Can Exercise (Dumbbell)', 'Shoulders', 'Dumbbells', '{"Shoulders"}'::text[], '{"Traps"}'::text[], 'Target your delts with the Dumbbell Empty Can Exercise, an effective shoulder movement exercise. The dumbbell variation provides freedom of movement and greater range of motion. Strong shoulders improve overhead strength and support nearly all upper body movements.', '58191201', '58191201-Dumbbell-Empty-Can-Exercise-(male)_Shoulders_.mp4', 'male', FALSE, '2025-12-03 23:26:21.890719+00', '1. Select a pair of dumbbells at an appropriate weight for Dumbbell Empty Can Exercise. 2. Set up in the starting position for Dumbbell Empty Can Exercise. 3. Execute the movement with proper form, focusing on your delts. 4. Control both the lifting and lowering phases of the movement. 5. Continue for your target rep count, maintaining good form throughout.', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 2, NULL, 7, 8, NULL, 5, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 8, 12, NULL, 6, NULL, TRUE, NULL, 'Strength', 62, 7, 8, TRUE, TRUE, 'general_exercise', 'Empty Can Exercise', 'squat, bench_press, deadlift', TRUE, 'dumbbell', FALSE, 3, 90, 4, 92, 90, 92, 90),
('48254ce4-790c-4c26-a104-b99a3a9fce08', 'Overhead Clap March', 'Legs', 'Bodyweight', '{"Quads"}'::text[], '{"Glutes","Hamstrings"}'::text[], 'This dynamic movement movement gets your heart rate up while developing explosive strength. The hip flexors assist throughout the movement, making this a well-rounded exercise. This bodyweight exercise requires no equipment and can be done anywhere. Develops fast-twitch muscle fibers for quicker, more powerful movements.', '84641201', '84641201-Overhead-Clap-March-(female)_Plyometrics_.mp4', 'female', FALSE, '2025-12-03 23:26:35.667316+00', '1. Set up in the starting position for Overhead Clap March. 2. Execute the movement with proper form, focusing on your full body. 3. Control both the lifting and lowering phases of the movement. 4. Continue for your target rep count, maintaining good form throughout.', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 2, NULL, 7, 7, NULL, 5, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 8, 12, NULL, 6, NULL, TRUE, NULL, 'Strength', 50, 7, 8, TRUE, TRUE, 'marching', 'Overhead Clap March', 'high_knees, butt_kicks, jumping_jack', FALSE, 'bodyweight', FALSE, 3, 90, 4, 70, 88, 95, 65),
('482b9592-ecb4-4ed6-a174-06f949e2df15', 'Cocoons', 'Core', 'Bodyweight', '{"Abs"}'::text[], '{"Hip Flexors"}'::text[], 'Strengthen your midsection with this movement movement that works your abs. No equipment needed—your body provides all the resistance. Core strength is foundational for athletic performance and injury prevention.', '25821201', '25821201-Cocoons-(female)_waist.mp4', 'female', FALSE, '2025-12-03 23:26:32.374165+00', '1. Set up in the starting position for Cocoons. 2. Execute the movement with proper form, focusing on your abs. 3. Control both the lifting and lowering phases of the movement. 4. Repeat for the prescribed number of repetitions.', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 2, NULL, 7, 7, NULL, 5, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 8, 12, NULL, 6, NULL, TRUE, NULL, 'Strength', 50, 7, 8, TRUE, TRUE, 'general_exercise', 'Cocoons', 'squat, bench_press, deadlift', FALSE, 'bodyweight', FALSE, 3, 90, 4, 70, 88, 95, 65),
('4844a02c-1e3c-443c-8120-700b401bf8db', 'Split Squat (Barbell)', 'Legs', 'Barbell', '{"Quads"}'::text[], '{"Glutes","Hamstrings"}'::text[], 'The Barbell Split Squat is a squatting exercise that primarily loads your quadriceps. The glutes, hamstrings assist throughout the movement, making this a well-rounded exercise. Barbells enable bilateral loading for building raw strength. Lower body strength improves everything from walking to heavy compound lifts.', '23701201', '23701201-Barbell-Split-Squat-(female)_Thighs.mp4', 'female', FALSE, '2025-12-03 23:26:31.133197+00', '1. Set up a barbell in a rack at the appropriate height for Barbell Split Squat. 2. Push your hips back and bend your knees to lower your body. 3. Keep your chest up and knees tracking over your toes. 4. Drive through your heels to stand back up, squeezing your glutes at the top. 5. Complete all reps with control before resting.', 'Squat', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 3, NULL, 10, 10, NULL, 4, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 5, 8, NULL, 9, NULL, TRUE, NULL, 'Strength', 97, 7, 9, TRUE, FALSE, 'split_squat', 'Split Squat', 'lunge, bulgarian_split_squat, squat', FALSE, 'barbell', FALSE, 4, 120, 5, 95, 80, 65, 95),
('4844eae8-82cf-4733-8814-35ad3ab6670c', 'Incline Single Arm Fly (Dumbbell)', 'Chest', 'Dumbbells, Incline Bench', '{"Chest"}'::text[], '{"Front Delts"}'::text[], 'This flying exercise focuses on your pectorals for improved chest strength and development. Your front delts work as secondary movers, adding to the training stimulus. The incline angle shifts emphasis toward the upper portion of the target muscles. Using dumbbells requires more stabilization than barbell variations. A well-developed chest contributes to upper body strength and aesthetics.', '12791201', '12791201-Dumbbell-Incline-One-Arm-Fly_Chest_.mp4', 'male', FALSE, '2025-12-03 23:26:30.099411+00', '1. Select an appropriate weight dumbbell and hold it in one hand. 2. With a slight bend in your elbows, move the weight in a wide arc. 3. Squeeze your chest muscles at the center/top of the movement. 4. Return with control, feeling the stretch at the bottom. 5. Complete all reps on one side, then switch to the other side. 6. Complete all reps with control before resting. Keep your core engaged for stability.', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 3, NULL, 5, 7, NULL, 6, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 10, 15, NULL, 4, NULL, TRUE, NULL, 'Strength', 80, 5, 7, FALSE, TRUE, 'chest_fly', 'Incline Single Arm Fly', 'bench_press, incline_press, push_up', TRUE, 'dumbbell', FALSE, 3, 60, 2, 92, 90, 92, 90),
('4848f2d3-0814-48d2-b8b8-9e7cdfff89f1', 'Double Triceps Kickback', 'Arms', 'Bodyweight', '{"Triceps"}'::text[], '{"Rear Delts"}'::text[], 'The Bodyweight Double Triceps Kickback is an arm kicking exercise targeting your glutes. Secondary activation of your hamstrings provides additional muscle engagement. This bodyweight exercise requires no equipment and can be done anywhere. Arm strength supports grip, pulling, and pushing in compound movements.', '63761201', '63761201-Bodyweight-Double-Triceps-Kickback-(female)_Upper-.mp4', 'female', FALSE, '2025-12-03 23:26:31.347577+00', '1. Keep your upper arm stationary and extend your forearm back. 2. Squeeze at full extension, then return with control. 3. Continue for your target rep count, maintaining good form throughout. Maintain consistent tempo throughout the set.', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 2, NULL, 5, 7, NULL, 6, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 10, 15, NULL, 4, NULL, TRUE, NULL, 'Strength', 50, 5, 7, FALSE, TRUE, 'tricep_kickback', 'Double Triceps Kickback', 'tricep_pushdown, tricep_extension', FALSE, 'bodyweight', FALSE, 3, 60, 2, 70, 88, 95, 65),
('485808b4-afdd-4691-85bf-67dc1741142e', 'Single Arm Scapula Push Up', 'Chest', 'Bodyweight', '{"Chest"}'::text[], '{"Triceps","Front Delts"}'::text[], 'The Single Arm Scapula Push Up is a pushing exercise that develops back strength and muscle. Your triceps, front delts work as secondary movers, adding to the training stimulus. This bodyweight exercise requires no equipment and can be done anywhere. Back development is crucial for pulling strength and overall upper body function.', '29461201', '29461201-Single-Arm-Scapula-Push-up_Back_.mp4', 'male', FALSE, '2025-12-03 23:26:26.93819+00', '1. Keep your body in a straight line from head to heels throughout. 2. Lower your chest toward the floor by bending your elbows. 3. Push through your palms to return to the starting position. 4. Complete all reps on one side, then switch to the other side. 5. Repeat for the prescribed number of repetitions.', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 3, NULL, 7, 7, NULL, 5, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 8, 12, NULL, 6, NULL, TRUE, NULL, 'Strength', 65, 7, 8, TRUE, TRUE, 'push_up', 'Single Arm Scapula Push Up', 'bench_press, chest_fly, dip', TRUE, 'bodyweight', FALSE, 3, 90, 4, 70, 88, 95, 65),
('4868069a-e597-4447-bebd-8c6d660c09a8', 'Standing Chest and Biceps Stretch (Against Wall)', 'Arms', 'Wall', '{"Biceps","Chest"}'::text[], '{"Forearms"}'::text[], 'Designed to lengthen your chest, the Standing Chest And Biceps Stretch Against Wall helps improve mobility and prevent stiffness. Your shoulders work as secondary movers, adding to the training stimulus. Performing this standing challenges your balance and core engagement. Regular stretching improves flexibility, reduces injury risk, and aids recovery.', '82411201', '82411201-Standing-Chest-and-Biceps-Stretch-agains-Wall-(fem.mp4', 'female', FALSE, '2025-12-03 23:26:38.570929+00', '1. Position yourself at the appropriate distance from a wall. 2. Stand tall with your feet firmly planted. 3. Move into the stretch position for Standing Chest And Biceps Stretch Against Wall. 4. Ease into the stretch until you feel gentle tension (not pain). 5. Hold for 20-30 seconds, breathing deeply and relaxing into the stretch.', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 1, NULL, 1, 1, NULL, 3, 'Standing', NULL, NULL, NULL, 1, 1, NULL, 1, NULL, TRUE, NULL, 'Stretch', 34, 2, 6, FALSE, TRUE, 'stretch_general', 'Standing Chest And Biceps Stretch Against Wall', 'stretch_shoulder, stretch_back', FALSE, 'bodyweight', TRUE, 1, 30, 2, 70, 88, 95, 65),
('4870d86b-5a1b-42b9-92bc-cd4f7ec04d3e', 'Inverted Row On Floor - Wide Grip (TRX)', 'Back', 'TRX', '{"Upper Back"}'::text[], '{"Lats","Biceps","Rear Delts"}'::text[], 'This rowing exercise strengthens the muscles between your shoulder blades. Secondary activation of your biceps provides additional muscle engagement. The TRX allows you to adjust difficulty by changing your body angle. Back development is crucial for pulling strength and overall upper body function.', '44511201', '44511201-Suspender-Wide-Grip-Inverted-Row-on-floor-(female)_Back.mp4', 'female', FALSE, '2025-12-03 23:26:39.623429+00', '1. Adjust the TRX/suspension straps to the appropriate length for Suspender Wide Grip Inverted Row On Floor. 2. Position yourself on the floor for Suspender Wide Grip Inverted Row On Floor. 3. Use a wide grip (wider than shoulder-width) for this variation. 4. Pull the weight toward your torso, leading with your elbow(s). 5. Squeeze your shoulder blades together at the peak contraction. 6. Extend back out with control, feeling the stretch in your back. 7. Complete all reps with control before resting.', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 2, NULL, 7, 7, NULL, 5, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 8, 12, NULL, 6, NULL, TRUE, NULL, 'Strength', 55, 7, 8, TRUE, TRUE, 'general_exercise', 'Suspender Inverted Row On Floor - Wide Grip', 'Suspender Inverted Row On Floor - Wide Grip', FALSE, 'trx', FALSE, 3, 90, 4, 68, 85, 85, 70),
('48756763-8eca-435e-8cee-c7c4d8522ec2', 'Prone Cobra Hands Interlocked', 'Back', 'Bodyweight', '{"Lower Back"}'::text[], '{"Glutes"}'::text[], 'Build leg strength with this movement movement focusing on your lower back. Secondary activation of your glutes provides additional muscle engagement. Performing this lying down removes momentum for stricter form. A versatile bodyweight movement perfect for home or gym training. Lower body strength improves everything from walking to heavy compound lifts.', '32101201', '32101201-Prone-Cobra-Hands-Interlocked-(female)_Hips_.mp4', 'female', FALSE, '2025-12-03 23:26:35.801913+00', '1. Lie face down (prone position) for Prone Cobra Hands Interlocked. 2. Set up in the starting position for Prone Cobra Hands Interlocked. 3. Execute the movement with proper form, focusing on your lower back. 4. Control both the lifting and lowering phases of the movement. 5. Continue for your target rep count, maintaining good form throughout.', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 1, NULL, 1, 1, NULL, 3, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 1, 1, NULL, 1, NULL, TRUE, NULL, 'Stretch', 35, 2, 6, FALSE, TRUE, 'back_stretch', 'Prone Cobra Hands Interlocked', 'stretch_hip, stretch_back, plank', FALSE, 'bodyweight', TRUE, 1, 30, 2, 70, 88, 95, 65),
('4892225e-96db-45b1-b5b5-035c005d72c7', 'Lateral Pulldown (Plate Loaded Machine)', 'Back', 'Machine', '{"Lats"}'::text[], '{"Biceps","Upper Back"}'::text[], 'This pulling exercise emphasizes your lats for improved back development. Secondary activation of your biceps, upper back provides additional muscle engagement. Machine exercises are great for isolating muscles and training to failure safely. A strong back improves posture, prevents injury, and balances pressing movements.', '18701201', '18701201-Lever-Lateral-Pulldown-(plate-loaded)_Back-FIX_.mp4', 'male', FALSE, '2025-12-03 23:26:23.987963+00', '1. Adjust the machine settings (seat height, weight, pads) to fit your body for Lever Lateral Pulldown. 2. Pull the bar/handle down toward your upper chest. 3. Drive your elbows down and back, squeezing your lats. 4. Control the weight back up without letting it yank your arms. 5. Complete all reps with control before resting.', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 1, NULL, 7, 7, NULL, 5, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 8, 12, NULL, 6, NULL, FALSE, NULL, 'Strength', 58, 7, 8, TRUE, TRUE, 'lat_pulldown', 'Lever Lateral Pulldown', 'pull_up, bent_over_row, cable_row, face_pull', FALSE, 'machine', FALSE, 3, 90, 4, 80, 75, 20, 88),
('48989778-ad6d-41b2-8e25-2c97b248e36b', 'Supported Split', 'Full Body', 'Bodyweight', '{"Full Body"}'::text[], '{}'::text[], 'Use this stretch to open up your full body area and enhance overall flexibility. Regular stretching improves flexibility, reduces injury risk, and aids recovery. Focus on controlled form throughout each repetition. Consistency with this movement will yield noticeable results.', '97671201', '97671201-Supported-Split-(female)_Stretching_.mp4', 'female', FALSE, '2025-12-03 23:26:39.340041+00', '1. Move into the stretch position for Supported Split. 2. Ease into the stretch until you feel gentle tension (not pain). 3. Hold for 20-30 seconds, breathing deeply and relaxing into the stretch.', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 2, NULL, 7, 7, NULL, 5, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 8, 12, NULL, 6, NULL, TRUE, NULL, 'Strength', 50, 7, 8, TRUE, TRUE, 'general_exercise', 'Supported Split', 'squat, bench_press, deadlift', FALSE, 'bodyweight', FALSE, 3, 90, 4, 70, 88, 95, 65),
('489d1edb-1516-48b3-a582-2def1fafc4bf', 'Elevated Single Leg Bridge', 'Legs', 'Bodyweight', '{"Glutes"}'::text[], '{"Hamstrings"}'::text[], 'The Elevanted Single Leg Bridge is a hip-dominant bridging exercise that targets your glutes. You''ll also feel your hamstrings working to support the movement. A versatile bodyweight movement perfect for home or gym training. Strong legs are the foundation for athletic performance and functional fitness.', '105491201', '105491201-Elevanted-Single-Leg-Bridge-(male)_Hips_.mp4', 'male', FALSE, '2025-12-03 23:26:21.732034+00', '1. Drive through your heels to lift your hips toward the ceiling. 2. Squeeze your glutes hard at the top of the movement. 3. Lower your hips back down with control. 4. Complete all reps on one side, then switch to the other side. 5. Repeat for the prescribed number of repetitions. Ensure full range of motion on each rep.', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 3, NULL, 7, 7, NULL, 5, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 8, 12, NULL, 6, NULL, TRUE, NULL, 'Strength', 45, 7, 8, TRUE, TRUE, 'glute_bridge', 'Elevanted Single Leg Bridge', 'hip_thrust, romanian_deadlift', TRUE, 'bodyweight', FALSE, 3, 90, 4, 70, 88, 95, 65),
('48a2c454-465a-433a-8f59-ba5ff6ef7100', 'Sit To Stand (Chair)', 'Legs', 'Chair', '{"Quads"}'::text[], '{"Glutes","Hamstrings"}'::text[], 'Target the front of your thighs with this movement exercise for quad development. You''ll also feel your glutes working to support the movement. Leg training boosts metabolism and builds functional, real-world strength.', '84171201', '84171201-Sit-to-Stand-on-a-Chair-(male)_Thighs_.mp4', 'male', FALSE, '2025-12-03 23:26:29.837118+00', '1. Position yourself with a sturdy chair for support or as part of the movement. 2. Set up in the starting position for Sit To Stand On A Chair. 3. Execute the movement with proper form, focusing on your quads. 4. Control both the lifting and lowering phases of the movement. 5. Complete all reps with control before resting.', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 2, NULL, 7, 7, NULL, 5, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 8, 12, NULL, 6, NULL, TRUE, NULL, 'Strength', 35, 7, 8, TRUE, TRUE, 'general_exercise', 'Sit To Stand On A Chair', 'squat, bench_press, deadlift', FALSE, 'bodyweight', FALSE, 3, 90, 4, 70, 88, 95, 65),
('48a6281e-75a0-4226-8449-73ea9da93d19', 'Side Step Grab', 'Legs', 'Bodyweight', '{"Quads"}'::text[], '{"Glutes","Hamstrings"}'::text[], 'The Side Step Grab is an explosive exercise that combines cardiovascular training with dynamic stepping movements. Secondary activation of your quads provides additional muscle engagement. Great for improving athletic performance, burning calories, and building conditioning.', '57681201', '57681201-Side-Step-Grab-(female)_Plyometrics_.mp4', 'female', FALSE, '2025-12-03 23:26:37.303932+00', '1. Set up a box or step platform at the appropriate height. 2. Set up in the starting position for Side Step Grab. 3. Execute the movement with proper form, focusing on your full body. 4. Control both the lifting and lowering phases of the movement. 5. Repeat for the prescribed number of repetitions.', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 2, NULL, 7, 7, NULL, 5, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 8, 12, NULL, 6, NULL, TRUE, NULL, 'Strength', 50, 7, 8, TRUE, TRUE, 'general_exercise', 'Side Step Grab', 'plank, crunch, leg_raise', FALSE, 'bodyweight', FALSE, 3, 90, 4, 70, 88, 95, 65),
('48a8599c-984b-48ae-928a-be8f9ae19040', 'Armless Prayer Stretch', 'Full Body', 'Bodyweight', '{"Full Body"}'::text[], '{}'::text[], 'Designed to lengthen your full body, the Armless Prayer Stretch helps improve mobility and prevent stiffness. Flexibility work like this enhances performance and prevents stiffness.', '65391201', '65391201-Armless-Prayer-Stretch-(male)_Stretching_.mp4', 'male', FALSE, '2025-12-03 23:26:29.483269+00', '1. Move into the stretch position for Armless Prayer Stretch. 2. Ease into the stretch until you feel gentle tension (not pain). 3. Hold for 20-30 seconds, breathing deeply and relaxing into the stretch.', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 1, NULL, 1, 1, NULL, 3, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 1, 1, NULL, 1, NULL, TRUE, NULL, 'Stretch', 25, 2, 6, FALSE, TRUE, 'back_stretch', 'Armless Prayer Stretch', 'stretch_hip, stretch_back, stretch_shoulder', FALSE, 'bodyweight', TRUE, 1, 30, 2, 70, 88, 95, 65),
('48b4ea25-66ce-4118-8cef-45fbd5f0d26a', 'Pulsing Donkey Kickback', 'Legs', 'Bodyweight', '{"Glutes","Hamstrings"}'::text[], '{}'::text[], 'This kicking exercise isolates your glutes for improved hip strength and power. Your hamstrings work as secondary movers, adding to the training stimulus. No equipment needed—your body provides all the resistance. Lower body strength improves everything from walking to heavy compound lifts.', '63151201', '63151201-Pulsing-Donkey-Kickback-(female)_Hips_.mp4', 'female', FALSE, '2025-12-03 23:26:35.801913+00', '1. Keep your upper arm stationary and extend your forearm back. 2. Squeeze at full extension, then return with control. 3. Continue for your target rep count, maintaining good form throughout. Ensure full range of motion on each rep.', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 2, NULL, 5, 7, NULL, 6, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 10, 15, NULL, 4, NULL, TRUE, NULL, 'Strength', 50, 5, 7, FALSE, TRUE, 'glute_kickback', 'Pulsing Donkey Kickback', 'hip_thrust, glute_bridge, leg_curl', FALSE, 'bodyweight', FALSE, 3, 60, 2, 70, 88, 95, 65),
('48b652c7-1498-483c-94f2-5b93df62a84c', 'Incline Palm In Press (Band)', 'Chest', 'Resistance Band, Incline Bench', '{"Chest"}'::text[], '{}'::text[], 'The Band Incline Palm In Press is a pressing exercise that targets your chest muscles. Using an incline changes the angle of resistance for varied muscle recruitment. Resistance bands provide accommodating resistance that increases through the range of motion. Chest strength improves pushing power for sports, daily tasks, and other lifts.', '68721201', '68721201-Band-Incline-Palm-in-Press_Chest_.mp4', 'male', FALSE, '2025-12-03 23:26:27.263406+00', '1. Secure the resistance band appropriately for Band Incline Palm In Press. 2. Lower the weight toward your chest with control. 3. Press the weight up until your arms are extended (don''t lock elbows). 4. Repeat for the prescribed number of repetitions.', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 3, NULL, 7, 7, NULL, 5, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 8, 12, NULL, 6, NULL, TRUE, NULL, 'Strength', 78, 7, 8, TRUE, TRUE, 'shoulder_press', 'Incline Palm In Press', 'lateral_raise, front_raise, rear_delt', FALSE, 'band', FALSE, 3, 90, 4, 60, 85, 90, 50),
('48b8e8a4-b61e-4b00-b985-eba61ea7f5d2', 'Sumo Pull Through (Dumbbell)', 'Legs', 'Dumbbells', '{"Quads"}'::text[], '{"Glutes","Hamstrings"}'::text[], 'The Dumbbell Sumo Pull Through is a hip-dominant pulling exercise that targets your glutes. The hamstrings assist throughout the movement, making this a well-rounded exercise. The dumbbell variation provides freedom of movement and greater range of motion. Leg training boosts metabolism and builds functional, real-world strength.', '28081201', '28081201-Dumbbell-Sumo-Pull-Through-(female)_Hips.mp4', 'female', FALSE, '2025-12-03 23:26:33.298565+00', '1. Select a pair of dumbbells at an appropriate weight for Dumbbell Sumo Pull Through. 2. Set up in the starting position for Dumbbell Sumo Pull Through. 3. Execute the movement with proper form, focusing on your glutes. 4. Control both the lifting and lowering phases of the movement. 5. Complete all reps with control before resting.', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 2, NULL, 7, 8, NULL, 5, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 8, 12, NULL, 6, NULL, TRUE, NULL, 'Strength', 62, 7, 8, TRUE, TRUE, 'pull_through', 'Sumo Pull Through', 'lat_pulldown, bent_over_row, pull_up', TRUE, 'dumbbell', FALSE, 3, 90, 4, 92, 90, 92, 90),
('48c4bc0e-9d46-4329-a1d7-25d41330c7cc', 'Row Door Handle (Door Frame)', 'Back', 'Door Frame', '{"Upper Back"}'::text[], '{"Lats","Biceps","Rear Delts"}'::text[], 'The Bodyweight Row Door Handle is a rowing exercise that builds thickness in your upper back. Your biceps, rear delts work as secondary movers, adding to the training stimulus. A versatile bodyweight movement perfect for home or gym training. A strong back improves posture, prevents injury, and balances pressing movements.', '79881201', '79881201-Bodyweight-Row-Door-Handle-(female)_Back_.mp4', 'female', FALSE, '2025-12-03 23:26:31.475486+00', '1. Pull the weight toward your torso, leading with your elbow(s). 2. Squeeze your shoulder blades together at the peak contraction. 3. Extend back out with control, feeling the stretch in your back. 4. Repeat for the prescribed number of repetitions. Maintain a neutral spine throughout. This variation specifically emphasizes the upper back.', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 2, NULL, 7, 7, NULL, 5, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 8, 12, NULL, 6, NULL, TRUE, NULL, 'Strength', 70, 7, 8, TRUE, TRUE, 'general_exercise', 'Row Door Handle', 'lat_pulldown, bent_over_row, pull_up', FALSE, 'bodyweight', FALSE, 3, 90, 4, 70, 88, 95, 65),
('48d9f904-9bf4-4b2b-9f40-9145ae5b592d', 'Front Raise - Neutral Grip (Resistance Band)', 'Shoulders', 'Resistance Band', '{"Front Delts"}'::text[], '{"Chest"}'::text[], 'Target your front delts with the Resistance Band Neutral Grip Front Raise, an effective shoulder raising exercise. The band creates increasing tension as it stretches, challenging the lockout. Shoulder development enhances both performance and upper body aesthetics.', '101461201', '101461201-Resistance-Band-Neutral-grip-Front-Raise-(female).mp4', 'female', FALSE, '2025-12-03 23:26:36.128549+00', '1. Secure the resistance band appropriately for Resistance Band Neutral Grip Front Raise. 2. Use a neutral grip with palms facing each other. 3. Raise the weight in front of you to shoulder height. 4. Lower with control, maintaining tension throughout. 5. Continue for your target rep count, maintaining good form throughout.', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 2, NULL, 5, 7, NULL, 6, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 10, 15, NULL, 4, NULL, TRUE, NULL, 'Strength', 75, 5, 7, FALSE, TRUE, 'front_raise', 'Front Raise - Neutral Grip', 'Front Raise - Neutral Grip', FALSE, 'band', FALSE, 3, 60, 2, 60, 85, 90, 50),
('48e493b9-e028-4b85-8d90-6c3a88dc84fa', 'Lunge Pass Through (Kettlebell)', 'Legs', 'Kettlebell', '{"Quads"}'::text[], '{"Glutes","Hamstrings"}'::text[], 'This lunging movement emphasizes your quadriceps for stronger, more powerful legs. Your glutes, hamstrings work as secondary movers, adding to the training stimulus. The kettlebell grip position adds a unique training stimulus. Lower body strength improves everything from walking to heavy compound lifts.', '5361201', '05361201-Kettlebell-Lunge-Pass-Through_Thighs_.mp4', 'male', FALSE, '2025-12-03 23:26:27.67144+00', '1. Select an appropriately weighted kettlebell for Kettlebell Lunge Pass Through. 2. Step forward into a lunge until both knees are at about 90 degrees. 3. Push through your front/working leg to return to the starting position. 4. Continue for your target rep count, maintaining good form throughout.', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 3, NULL, 7, 7, NULL, 5, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 8, 12, NULL, 6, NULL, TRUE, NULL, 'Strength', 78, 7, 8, TRUE, TRUE, 'pass_through', 'Lunge Pass Through', 'squat, split_squat, step_up, leg_press', FALSE, 'kettlebell', FALSE, 3, 90, 4, 75, 88, 88, 78);
INSERT INTO _exercise_staging (id, name, category, equipment, primary_muscles, secondary_muscles, description, video_code, video_filename, gender, is_custom, created_at, steps_to_perform, movement_pattern, force_type, movement_type, laterality, plane_of_motion, difficulty_level, complexity_score, strength_rating, hypertrophy_rating, power_rating, endurance_rating, body_position, bench_angle, grip_type, grip_width, optimal_rep_range_min, optimal_rep_range_max, placement_in_workout, fatigability, popularity_score, home_gym_friendly, instructions, workout_type, practicality_score, fat_loss_rating, general_fitness_rating, is_compound, supersetable, exercise_family, base_exercise_name, complementary_families, is_equipment_primary, equipment_category, duration_based, recommended_sets, rest_seconds, muscles_worked_count, priority_build_muscle, priority_get_lean, priority_home, priority_gym) VALUES
('48e88343-3eca-45d5-bd44-aa5c75099b98', 'Roll Recumbent Hip External Rotator And Hip Extens', 'Legs', 'Bodyweight', '{"Quads"}'::text[], '{"Glutes","Hamstrings"}'::text[], 'Build stronger glutes with this movement movement focused on hip extension. This bodyweight exercise requires no equipment and can be done anywhere. Strong legs are the foundation for athletic performance and functional fitness.', '51831201', '51831201-Roll-Recumbent-Hip-External-Rotator-and-Hip-Extens.mp4', 'female', FALSE, '2025-12-03 23:26:36.38616+00', '1. Set up in the starting position for Roll Recumbent Hip External Rotator And Hip Extens. 2. Execute the movement with proper form, focusing on your glutes. 3. Control both the lifting and lowering phases of the movement. 4. Complete all reps with control before resting.', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 2, NULL, 7, 7, NULL, 5, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 8, 12, NULL, 6, NULL, TRUE, NULL, 'Strength', 50, 7, 8, TRUE, TRUE, 'external_rotation', 'Roll Recumbent Hip External Rotator And Hip Extens', 'hip_thrust, lunge, squat', FALSE, 'bodyweight', FALSE, 3, 90, 4, 70, 88, 95, 65),
('48f9f44a-4b8e-48e0-9293-15828f1e834d', 'Standing Hip Circle', 'Shoulders', 'Bodyweight', '{"Shoulders"}'::text[], '{"Traps"}'::text[], 'The Standing Hip Circle is a lower body movement exercise that targets your delts. The standing position engages your core for stability. No equipment needed—your body provides all the resistance. Lower body strength improves everything from walking to heavy compound lifts.', '81321201', '81321201-Standing-Hip-Circle-(female)_Hips_.mp4', 'female', FALSE, '2025-12-03 23:26:38.7451+00', '1. Stand with feet about shoulder-width apart. 2. Set up in the starting position for Standing Hip Circle. 3. Execute the movement with proper form, focusing on your delts. 4. Control both the lifting and lowering phases of the movement. 5. Complete all reps with control before resting.', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 2, NULL, 7, 7, NULL, 5, 'Standing', NULL, NULL, NULL, 8, 12, NULL, 6, NULL, TRUE, NULL, 'Strength', 52, 7, 8, TRUE, TRUE, 'hip_circle', 'Standing Hip Circle', 'hip_thrust, lunge, squat', FALSE, 'bodyweight', FALSE, 3, 90, 4, 70, 88, 95, 65),
('490ebce1-9ddb-4c5b-b573-0086bc9b8b8f', 'Bicep Table Row', 'Back', 'Bodyweight, Table', '{"Upper Back"}'::text[], '{"Lats","Biceps","Rear Delts"}'::text[], 'This rowing exercise focuses on your biceps for improved arm size and strength. The biceps, rear delts assist throughout the movement, making this a well-rounded exercise. This bodyweight exercise requires no equipment and can be done anywhere. Arm strength supports grip, pulling, and pushing in compound movements.', '90141201', '90141201-Biceps-Table-Row-(male)_Upper-Arms_.mp4', 'male', FALSE, '2025-12-03 23:26:24.941834+00', '1. Pull the weight toward your torso, leading with your elbow(s). 2. Squeeze your shoulder blades together at the peak contraction. 3. Extend back out with control, feeling the stretch in your back. 4. Complete all reps with control before resting. Engage your stabilizer muscles for better control. Works well for biceps activation.', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 2, NULL, 7, 7, NULL, 5, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 8, 12, NULL, 6, NULL, TRUE, NULL, 'Strength', 70, 7, 8, TRUE, TRUE, 'arm_exercise', 'Biceps Table Row', 'lat_pulldown, bent_over_row, pull_up', FALSE, 'bodyweight', FALSE, 3, 90, 4, 70, 88, 95, 65),
('49101649-73d1-434c-ab8d-9908bf9893bb', 'Seated Lotus Pose Woodchoper', 'Core', 'Bodyweight', '{"Obliques"}'::text[], '{"Abs"}'::text[], 'The Seated Lotus Pose Woodchoper targets your obliques through a movement motion, building rotational core strength. Being seated provides stability, allowing you to focus on the working muscles. Core strength is foundational for athletic performance and injury prevention.', '88541201', '88541201-Sitting-Lotus-Pose-Woodchoper-(male)_Waist_.mp4', 'male', FALSE, '2025-12-03 23:26:23.586683+00', '1. Sit with your back supported, core engaged, feet flat on the floor. 2. Set up in the starting position for Seated Lotus Pose Woodchoper. 3. Execute the movement with proper form, focusing on your obliques. 4. Control both the lifting and lowering phases of the movement. 5. Repeat for the prescribed number of repetitions.', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 1, NULL, 5, 4, NULL, 8, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 8, 12, NULL, 7, NULL, TRUE, NULL, 'Plyometrics', 15, 9, 8, TRUE, TRUE, 'woodchop', 'Seated Lotus Pose Woodchoper', 'stretch_hip, stretch_back, plank', FALSE, 'bodyweight', FALSE, 3, 60, 4, 70, 88, 95, 65),
('4910a548-cc5a-4b8e-bf8d-98266b776667', 'Lying Single Arm Rear Lateral Raise (Dumbbell)', 'Shoulders', 'Dumbbells, Flat Bench', '{"Side Delts"}'::text[], '{"Traps"}'::text[], 'Build stronger shoulders with this raising movement focusing on your rear delts. Performing this lying down removes momentum for stricter form. Dumbbells allow each arm to work independently, helping correct imbalances. Strong shoulders improve overhead strength and support nearly all upper body movements. Maintain proper breathing - exhale during the effort phase.', '3451201', '03451201-Dumbbell-Lying-One-Arm-Rear-Lateral-Raise_shoulder.mp4', 'male', FALSE, '2025-12-03 23:26:27.384461+00', '1. Select an appropriate weight dumbbell and hold it in one hand. 2. Lie down in the appropriate position for Dumbbell Lying One Arm Rear Lateral Raise. 3. Raise your arms out to the sides until parallel to the floor. 4. Lower with control, maintaining tension throughout. 5. Complete all reps on one side, then switch to the other side. 6. Repeat for the prescribed number of repetitions.', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 3, NULL, 5, 7, NULL, 6, 'Lying', NULL, NULL, NULL, 10, 15, NULL, 4, NULL, TRUE, NULL, 'Strength', 87, 5, 7, FALSE, TRUE, 'lateral_raise', 'Lying Single Arm Rear Lateral Raise', 'shoulder_press, front_raise, rear_delt', TRUE, 'dumbbell', FALSE, 3, 60, 2, 92, 90, 92, 90),
('4912e3f7-79d3-4715-b99d-b57d1f81c1c2', 'Cobra Push Up', 'Chest', 'Bodyweight', '{"Chest"}'::text[], '{"Triceps","Front Delts"}'::text[], 'The Cobra Push Up is a pushing exercise that targets your chest muscles. You''ll also feel your triceps, front delts working to support the movement. No equipment needed—your body provides all the resistance. Chest strength improves pushing power for sports, daily tasks, and other lifts.', '70301201', '70301201-Cobra-Push-up-(female)_Chest_.mp4', 'female', FALSE, '2025-12-03 23:26:32.374165+00', '1. Keep your body in a straight line from head to heels throughout. 2. Lower your chest toward the floor by bending your elbows. 3. Push through your palms to return to the starting position. 4. Repeat for the prescribed number of repetitions. Don''t rush—quality over quantity. This exercise is excellent for chest development.', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 1, NULL, 1, 1, NULL, 3, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 1, 1, NULL, 1, NULL, TRUE, NULL, 'Stretch', 70, 2, 6, FALSE, TRUE, 'push_up', 'Cobra Push Up', 'bench_press, chest_fly, dip', FALSE, 'bodyweight', TRUE, 1, 30, 2, 70, 88, 95, 65),
('491daa1a-a7a6-42f1-9bd4-0736ab566645', 'Chair Pose I Utkatasana I (Chair)', 'Full Body', 'Chair', '{"Quads"}'::text[], '{"Glutes","Hamstrings"}'::text[], 'The Chair Pose I Utkatasana I is a flexibility exercise that targets your full body, helping to release tension and improve range of motion. Include this in your routine for better mobility and reduced muscle tension.', '9441201', '09441201-Chair-Pose-I-Utkatasana-I-(female)_Stretching_.mp4', 'female', FALSE, '2025-12-03 23:26:32.166461+00', '1. Position yourself with a sturdy chair for support or as part of the movement. 2. Move into the stretch position for Chair Pose I Utkatasana I. 3. Ease into the stretch until you feel gentle tension (not pain). 4. Hold for 20-30 seconds, breathing deeply and relaxing into the stretch.', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 1, NULL, 1, 1, NULL, 3, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 1, 1, NULL, 1, NULL, TRUE, NULL, 'Stretch', 15, 2, 6, FALSE, TRUE, 'yoga', 'Chair Pose I Utkatasana I', 'stretch_hip, stretch_back, plank', FALSE, 'bodyweight', TRUE, 1, 30, 2, 70, 88, 95, 65),
('4939f54a-5b6a-43a0-b585-637ac7b25a0f', 'Standing Forward Leg Swing', 'Full Body', 'Bodyweight', '{"Full Body"}'::text[], '{}'::text[], 'The Back Forward Leg Swings is a flexibility exercise that targets your back, helping to release tension and improve range of motion. Flexibility work like this enhances performance and prevents stiffness.', '35021201', '35021201-Back-Forward-Leg-Swings-(male)_Hips_.mp4', 'male', FALSE, '2025-12-03 23:26:22.123147+00', '1. Hinge at your hips, letting the weight swing back between your legs. 2. Explosively drive hips forward, propelling the weight forward/up. 3. Let gravity bring it back as you hinge for the next rep. Focus on maintaining proper breathing throughout.', NULL, 'Static', NULL, 'Bilateral', NULL, 2, NULL, 7, 7, NULL, 5, 'Standing', NULL, NULL, NULL, 8, 12, NULL, 6, NULL, TRUE, NULL, 'Strength', 52, 7, 8, TRUE, TRUE, 'leg_exercise', 'Standing Forward Leg Swing', 'high_knees, butt_kicks, jumping_jack', FALSE, 'bodyweight', FALSE, 3, 90, 4, 70, 88, 95, 65),
('49408317-2f43-4d09-92ab-f821b9228900', 'Kneeling Shoulder Press (Resistance Band)', 'Shoulders', 'Resistance Band', '{"Shoulders"}'::text[], '{"Side Delts","Triceps"}'::text[], 'The Resistance Band Kneeling Shoulder Press is a pressing exercise that targets your delts for shoulder development. You''ll also feel your triceps working to support the movement. Kneeling helps eliminate lower body momentum from the movement. Bands are joint-friendly and portable, perfect for any training environment. Strong shoulders improve overhead strength and support nearly all upper body movements.', '85961201', '85961201-Resistance-Band-Kneeling-Shoulder-Press-(male)_Sho.mp4', 'male', FALSE, '2025-12-03 23:26:26.678791+00', '1. Secure the resistance band appropriately for Resistance Band Kneeling Shoulder Press. 2. Kneel on the floor (use a pad for comfort if needed). 3. Start with the weight at shoulder level. 4. Press directly overhead until your arms are fully extended. 5. Lower back to shoulder level with control. 6. Repeat for the prescribed number of repetitions.', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 2, NULL, 7, 7, NULL, 5, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 8, 12, NULL, 6, NULL, TRUE, NULL, 'Strength', 85, 7, 8, TRUE, TRUE, 'shoulder_press', 'Kneeling Shoulder Press', 'lateral_raise, front_raise, rear_delt', FALSE, 'band', FALSE, 3, 90, 4, 60, 85, 90, 50),
('4944cdbd-d390-46eb-ba33-dd8cc8869a93', 'Lying Single To Double Leg Raise', 'Core', 'Bodyweight', '{"Lower Abs"}'::text[], '{"Hip Flexors"}'::text[], 'Build a stronger core with the Lying Single To Double Leg Raise, focusing on your abs. Your hip flexors work as secondary movers, adding to the training stimulus. The lying position provides back support and helps isolate the target muscles. No equipment needed—your body provides all the resistance. A strong core improves posture, protects your spine, and enhances all other lifts.', '52581201', '52581201-Lying-Single-to-Double-Leg-Raise-(female)_Waist_.mp4', 'female', FALSE, '2025-12-03 23:26:35.38119+00', '1. Lie down in the appropriate position for Lying Single To Double Leg Raise. 2. Keeping legs mostly straight, raise them toward the ceiling. 3. Lower with control, stopping just before touching down. 4. Complete all reps with control before resting.', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 2, NULL, 5, 7, NULL, 6, 'Lying', NULL, NULL, NULL, 10, 15, NULL, 4, NULL, TRUE, NULL, 'Strength', 70, 5, 7, FALSE, TRUE, 'leg_raise', 'Lying Single To Double Leg Raise', 'crunch, plank, v_up', FALSE, 'bodyweight', FALSE, 3, 60, 2, 70, 88, 95, 65),
('49559647-3a72-4b20-abf6-0081874090f5', 'Hip Adduction (Machine)', 'Legs', 'Machine', '{"Inner Thighs"}'::text[], '{}'::text[], 'The Lever Seated Hip Adduction is a lower body movement exercise that targets your adductors. Being seated provides stability, allowing you to focus on the working muscles. The machine guides your movement path for safer, more controlled repetitions. Strong legs are the foundation for athletic performance and functional fitness.', '18671201', '18671201-Lever-Seated-Hip-Adduction-(Version-2)_Hips_.mp4', 'male', FALSE, '2025-12-03 23:26:26.93819+00', '1. Adjust the machine settings (seat height, weight, pads) to fit your body for Lever Seated Hip Adduction. 2. Sit with your back supported, core engaged, feet flat on the floor. 3. Repeat for the prescribed number of repetitions. Maintain consistent tempo throughout the set.', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 1, NULL, 7, 7, NULL, 5, 'Seated', NULL, NULL, NULL, 8, 12, NULL, 6, NULL, FALSE, NULL, 'Strength', 60, 7, 8, TRUE, TRUE, 'hip_adduction', 'Lever Seated Hip Adduction', 'hip_abduction, squat, lunge', TRUE, 'machine', FALSE, 3, 90, 4, 80, 75, 20, 88),
('496a0f3d-724a-41ea-874b-ac4b426588f1', 'Leg Extension (Machine)', 'Legs', 'Machine', '{"Quads"}'::text[], '{}'::text[], 'This extension movement emphasizes your quadriceps for stronger, more powerful legs. The machine guides your movement path for safer, more controlled repetitions. Lower body strength improves everything from walking to heavy compound lifts.', '5851201', '05851201-Lever-Leg-Extension_Thighs.mp4', 'male', FALSE, '2025-12-03 23:26:28.851102+00', '1. Adjust the machine settings (seat height, weight, pads) to fit your body for Lever Leg Extension. 2. Extend your legs until straight, squeezing your quads at the top. 3. Lower with control back to the starting position. 4. Continue for your target rep count, maintaining good form throughout. Maintain a neutral spine throughout.', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 1, NULL, 5, 7, NULL, 6, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 10, 15, NULL, 4, NULL, FALSE, NULL, 'Strength', 88, 5, 7, FALSE, TRUE, 'leg_extension', 'Lever Leg Extension', 'squat, leg_press, lunge', TRUE, 'machine', FALSE, 3, 60, 2, 80, 75, 20, 88),
('496a0f8f-5455-4a79-81d6-7824b66cba97', 'Jaw Stretch', 'Full Body', 'Bodyweight', '{"Full Body"}'::text[], '{}'::text[], 'Use this stretch to open up your neck area and enhance overall flexibility. Include this in your routine for better mobility and reduced muscle tension. Works well as both a primary exercise or accessory movement.', '86901201', '86901201-Jaw-Stretch_Face.mp4', 'male', FALSE, '2025-12-03 23:26:22.123147+00', '1. Move into the stretch position for Jaw Stretch. 2. Ease into the stretch until you feel gentle tension (not pain). 3. Hold for 20-30 seconds, breathing deeply and relaxing into the stretch.', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 1, NULL, 1, 1, NULL, 3, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 1, 1, NULL, 1, NULL, TRUE, NULL, 'Stretch', 40, 2, 6, FALSE, TRUE, 'stretch_general', 'Jaw Stretch', 'stretch_hip, stretch_back, stretch_shoulder', FALSE, 'bodyweight', TRUE, 1, 30, 2, 70, 88, 95, 65),
('497ff493-3557-491d-baf3-3ba271d7c369', 'High Knee Squat', 'Legs', 'Bodyweight', '{"Quads"}'::text[], '{"Glutes","Hamstrings"}'::text[], 'This cardio exercise keeps your heart rate elevated for improved cardiovascular fitness. Secondary activation of your hip flexors provides additional muscle engagement. Regular cardio training builds the aerobic base for better overall fitness.', '4781201', '04781201-High-Knee-Squat-(female)_Cardio-FIX_.mp4', 'female', FALSE, '2025-12-03 23:26:33.960339+00', '1. Push your hips back and bend your knees to lower your body. 2. Keep your chest up and knees tracking over your toes. 3. Drive through your heels to stand back up, squeezing your glutes at the top. 4. Continue for your target rep count, maintaining good form throughout. Keep tension on the target muscles throughout. This variation specifically emphasizes the cardio.', 'Squat', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 2, NULL, 5, 4, NULL, 8, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 8, 12, NULL, 7, NULL, TRUE, NULL, 'Plyometrics', 85, 9, 8, TRUE, TRUE, 'high_knees', 'High Knee Squat', 'butt_kicks, jumping_jack, mountain_climber', FALSE, 'bodyweight', FALSE, 3, 60, 4, 70, 88, 95, 65),
('498ba500-519d-4065-aeac-19fcc0c86b2b', 'Punches Side Lunge', 'Legs', 'Bodyweight', '{"Quads"}'::text[], '{"Glutes","Inner Thighs"}'::text[], 'Target the front of your thighs with this lunging exercise for quad development. Secondary activation of your glutes, hamstrings provides additional muscle engagement. A versatile bodyweight movement perfect for home or gym training. Strong legs are the foundation for athletic performance and functional fitness. Excellent for pre-exhausting the target muscle before compound lifts.', '56851201', '56851201-Punches-Side-Lunge-(female)_Thighs_.mp4', 'female', FALSE, '2025-12-03 23:26:35.801913+00', '1. Step to the side, bending that knee while keeping the other leg straight. 2. Push through your front/working leg to return to the starting position. 3. Continue for your target rep count, maintaining good form throughout. Keep the movement smooth and controlled.', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 2, NULL, 7, 7, NULL, 5, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 8, 12, NULL, 6, NULL, TRUE, NULL, 'Strength', 70, 7, 8, TRUE, TRUE, 'lunge', 'Punches Side Lunge', 'split_squat, step_up, squat', FALSE, 'bodyweight', FALSE, 3, 90, 4, 70, 88, 95, 65),
('498eb91b-91ff-4609-8737-c270619c5fee', 'Clap Push Up', 'Chest', 'Bodyweight', '{"Chest"}'::text[], '{"Triceps","Front Delts"}'::text[], 'Build power and athleticism with this high-intensity pushing exercise that challenges your entire body. You''ll also feel your triceps, front delts working to support the movement. No equipment needed—your body provides all the resistance. Great for improving athletic performance, burning calories, and building conditioning.', '70111201', '70111201-Clap-Push-Up-(female)_Plyometrics_.mp4', 'female', FALSE, '2025-12-03 23:26:32.374165+00', '1. Keep your body in a straight line from head to heels throughout. 2. Lower your chest toward the floor by bending your elbows. 3. Push through your palms to return to the starting position. 4. Repeat for the prescribed number of repetitions. Focus on the mind-muscle connection.', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 2, NULL, 7, 7, NULL, 5, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 8, 12, NULL, 6, NULL, TRUE, NULL, 'Strength', 70, 7, 8, TRUE, TRUE, 'push_up', 'Clap Push Up', 'bench_press, chest_fly, dip', TRUE, 'bodyweight', FALSE, 3, 90, 4, 70, 88, 95, 65),
('498f539f-d7b0-4fa6-99d9-d5111ae8c579', 'Standing Balance Hip Flexion Pulse', 'Full Body', 'Bodyweight', '{"Full Body"}'::text[], '{}'::text[], 'Build leg strength with this flexion movement focusing on your full body. Performing this standing challenges your balance and core engagement. No equipment needed—your body provides all the resistance. Strong legs are the foundation for athletic performance and functional fitness.', '81141201', '81141201-Standing-Balance-Hip-Flexion-Pulse-(female)_Hips_.mp4', 'female', FALSE, '2025-12-03 23:26:38.425788+00', '1. Stand tall with your feet firmly planted. 2. At the bottom or top, pulse up and down in small movements before completing the rep. 3. Continue for your target rep count, maintaining good form throughout.', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 2, NULL, 7, 7, NULL, 5, 'Standing', NULL, NULL, NULL, 8, 12, NULL, 6, NULL, TRUE, NULL, 'Strength', 52, 7, 8, TRUE, TRUE, 'balance', 'Standing Balance Hip Flexion Pulse', 'squat, bench_press, deadlift', FALSE, 'bodyweight', FALSE, 3, 90, 4, 70, 88, 95, 65),
('499986af-5422-4eaa-b7fd-74856658e8ab', 'Hip External Rotation Test', 'Shoulders', 'Bodyweight', '{"Rotator Cuff"}'::text[], '{"Shoulders"}'::text[], 'Target your hips with this rotation stretch that helps restore range of motion. Secondary activation of your glutes provides additional muscle engagement. Include this in your routine for better mobility and reduced muscle tension.', '67871201', '67871201-Hip-External-Rotation-Test-(female)_Stretching_.mp4', 'female', FALSE, '2025-12-03 23:26:34.073704+00', '1. Rotate your torso through the movement pattern for Hip External Rotation Test. 2. Control the rotation in both directions—avoid using momentum. 3. Move into the stretch position for Hip External Rotation Test. 4. Ease into the stretch until you feel gentle tension (not pain). 5. Hold for 20-30 seconds, breathing deeply and relaxing into the stretch.', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 2, NULL, 7, 7, NULL, 5, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 8, 12, NULL, 6, NULL, TRUE, NULL, 'Strength', 50, 7, 8, TRUE, TRUE, 'external_rotation', 'Hip External Rotation Test', 'squat, bench_press, deadlift', FALSE, 'bodyweight', FALSE, 3, 90, 4, 70, 88, 95, 65),
('49aec4fa-34ff-45f9-a136-6093e54b82a3', 'Lying Crunch (Machine)', 'Core', 'Machine', '{"Abs"}'::text[], '{"Hip Flexors"}'::text[], 'This crunching exercise engages your abs for improved core stability and strength. The hip flexors assist throughout the movement, making this a well-rounded exercise. The lying position provides back support and helps isolate the target muscles. Machine exercises are great for isolating muscles and training to failure safely. A strong core improves posture, protects your spine, and enhances all other lifts.', '23141201', '23141201-Lever-Lying-Crunch-(VERSION-2)-(female)_Waist.mp4', 'female', FALSE, '2025-12-03 23:26:34.724336+00', '1. Adjust the machine settings (seat height, weight, pads) to fit your body for Lever Lying Crunch. 2. Lie down in the appropriate position for Lever Lying Crunch. 3. Curl your shoulders off the floor by contracting your abs. 4. Don''t pull on your neck—focus on the abdominal contraction. 5. Lower with control, maintaining some tension. 6. Complete all reps with control before resting.', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 1, NULL, 5, 7, NULL, 6, 'Lying', NULL, NULL, NULL, 12, 20, NULL, 4, NULL, FALSE, NULL, 'Strength', 78, 5, 7, FALSE, TRUE, 'crunch', 'Lever Lying Crunch', 'leg_raise, plank, russian_twist, v_up', FALSE, 'machine', FALSE, 3, 60, 2, 80, 75, 20, 88),
('49b294f6-b3bd-49ab-a4ab-2af7e9450142', 'Kneeling Straight Leg Side Kick', 'Core', 'Bodyweight', '{"Abs"}'::text[], '{"Hip Flexors"}'::text[], 'Build leg strength with this kicking movement focusing on your core. Kneeling helps eliminate lower body momentum from the movement. This bodyweight exercise requires no equipment and can be done anywhere. Strong legs are the foundation for athletic performance and functional fitness.', '48961201', '48961201-Kneeling-Straight-Leg-Side-Kick-(female)_Hips_.mp4', 'female', FALSE, '2025-12-03 23:26:34.487002+00', '1. Kneel on the floor (use a pad for comfort if needed). 2. Set up in the starting position for Kneeling Straight Leg Side Kick. 3. Execute the movement with proper form, focusing on your core. 4. Control both the lifting and lowering phases of the movement. 5. Continue for your target rep count, maintaining good form throughout.', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 1, NULL, 7, 7, NULL, 5, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 8, 12, NULL, 6, NULL, TRUE, NULL, 'Strength', 50, 7, 8, TRUE, TRUE, 'romanian_deadlift', 'Kneeling Straight Leg Side Kick', 'deadlift, leg_curl, hip_thrust', FALSE, 'bodyweight', FALSE, 3, 90, 4, 70, 88, 95, 65),
('49b548a3-2734-48ff-bf99-90e8853326e1', 'Triceps Pushdown (Resistance Band)', 'Arms', 'Resistance Band, Anchor Point', '{"Triceps"}'::text[], '{"Chest","Shoulders"}'::text[], 'This pushing movement isolates your triceps for improved arm development. The band creates increasing tension as it stretches, challenging the lockout. Arm strength supports grip, pulling, and pushing in compound movements. Keep your core engaged throughout the exercise.', '46881201', '46881201-Resistance-Band-Triceps-Pushdown_Upper-Arms_.mp4', 'male', FALSE, '2025-12-03 23:26:20.667107+00', '1. Secure the resistance band appropriately for Resistance Band Triceps Pushdown. 2. Set up in the starting position for Resistance Band Triceps Pushdown. 3. Execute the movement with proper form, focusing on your triceps. 4. Control both the lifting and lowering phases of the movement. 5. Complete all reps with control before resting. Maintain a neutral spine throughout.', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 2, NULL, 5, 7, NULL, 6, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 10, 15, NULL, 4, NULL, TRUE, NULL, 'Strength', 55, 5, 7, FALSE, TRUE, 'tricep_pushdown', 'Triceps Pushdown', 'tricep_extension, close_grip_bench, dip', FALSE, 'band', FALSE, 3, 60, 2, 60, 85, 90, 50),
('49bc713a-d800-4d7b-9ac0-f4052d9a8240', 'Seated Front Raise (Chair)', 'Shoulders', 'Chair', '{"Front Delts"}'::text[], '{"Chest"}'::text[], 'Target your front delts with the Seated Front Raise On Chair, an effective shoulder raising exercise. The seated position helps isolate the target muscles by removing momentum. Shoulder development enhances both performance and upper body aesthetics.', '104831201', '104831201-Seated-Front-Raise-on-Chair-(male)_Shoulders_.mp4', 'male', FALSE, '2025-12-03 23:26:28.968567+00', '1. Position yourself with a sturdy chair for support or as part of the movement. 2. Sit with your back supported, core engaged, feet flat on the floor. 3. Raise the weight in front of you to shoulder height. 4. Lower with control, maintaining tension throughout. 5. Complete all reps with control before resting.', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 2, NULL, 5, 7, NULL, 6, 'Seated', NULL, NULL, NULL, 10, 15, NULL, 4, NULL, TRUE, NULL, 'Strength', 57, 5, 7, FALSE, TRUE, 'front_raise', 'Seated Front Raise On Chair', 'shoulder_press, lateral_raise, rear_delt_fly', FALSE, 'bodyweight', FALSE, 3, 60, 2, 70, 88, 95, 65),
('49bcccef-223a-4b56-b008-375b47a7fe2a', 'Lying Triceps Extension With Pillow', 'Arms', 'Bodyweight', '{"Triceps"}'::text[], '{"Chest","Shoulders"}'::text[], 'This extension movement isolates your triceps for improved arm development. The lying position provides back support and helps isolate the target muscles. A versatile bodyweight movement perfect for home or gym training. Arm strength supports grip, pulling, and pushing in compound movements.', '82311201', '82311201-Lying-Triceps-Extension-with-Pillow-(female)_Upper.mp4', 'female', FALSE, '2025-12-03 23:26:35.38119+00', '1. Lie down in the appropriate position for Lying Triceps Extension With Pillow. 2. Extend at the elbow until your arm is straight, squeezing the tricep. 3. Lower with control, keeping your upper arm stationary. 4. Complete all reps with control before resting.', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 3, NULL, 5, 7, NULL, 6, 'Lying', NULL, NULL, NULL, 10, 15, NULL, 4, NULL, TRUE, NULL, 'Strength', 10, 5, 7, FALSE, TRUE, 'tricep_extension', 'Lying Triceps Extension With Pillow', 'tricep_pushdown, close_grip_bench', FALSE, 'bodyweight', FALSE, 3, 60, 2, 70, 88, 95, 65),
('49cf74b9-8326-4ec3-a8f2-0e9dbc35b0ea', 'Forward Step Arm Swing - Alternating', 'Legs', 'Bodyweight', '{"Quads"}'::text[], '{"Glutes","Hamstrings"}'::text[], 'A challenging plyometric exercise, the Alternate Forward Step Arm Swing builds reactive power and improves conditioning. Your quads work as secondary movers, adding to the training stimulus. Develops fast-twitch muscle fibers for quicker, more powerful movements.', '86311201', '86311201-Alternate-Forward-Step-Arm-Swing-(male)_Plyometric.mp4', 'male', FALSE, '2025-12-03 23:26:20.667107+00', '1. Set up a box or step platform at the appropriate height. 2. Hinge at your hips, letting the weight swing back between your legs. 3. Explosively drive hips forward, propelling the weight forward/up. 4. Let gravity bring it back as you hinge for the next rep. 5. Alternate between sides/arms/legs with each repetition. 6. Continue for your target rep count, maintaining good form throughout.', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 2, NULL, 7, 7, NULL, 5, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 8, 12, NULL, 6, NULL, TRUE, NULL, 'Strength', 50, 7, 8, TRUE, TRUE, 'arm_exercise', 'Forward Step Arm Swing - Alternating', 'high_knees, butt_kicks, jumping_jack', FALSE, 'bodyweight', FALSE, 3, 90, 4, 70, 88, 95, 65),
('49cfa8ba-734f-43cf-b0d9-a4282cd9d42c', 'Inverted Row Under Table', 'Back', 'Bodyweight', '{"Upper Back"}'::text[], '{"Lats","Biceps","Rear Delts"}'::text[], 'This rowing exercise strengthens the muscles between your shoulder blades. Your biceps work as secondary movers, adding to the training stimulus. A versatile bodyweight movement perfect for home or gym training. A strong back improves posture, prevents injury, and balances pressing movements.', '83571201', '83571201-Inverted-Row-under-Table-(male)_Back_.mp4', 'male', FALSE, '2025-12-03 23:26:23.586683+00', '1. Pull the weight toward your torso, leading with your elbow(s). 2. Squeeze your shoulder blades together at the peak contraction. 3. Extend back out with control, feeling the stretch in your back. 4. Complete all reps with control before resting. Exhale during the exertion phase of the movement.', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 2, NULL, 7, 7, NULL, 5, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 8, 12, NULL, 6, NULL, TRUE, NULL, 'Strength', 70, 7, 8, TRUE, TRUE, 'general_exercise', 'Inverted Row Under Table', 'lat_pulldown, bent_over_row, pull_up', FALSE, 'bodyweight', FALSE, 3, 90, 4, 70, 88, 95, 65),
('49f6cdb5-f471-43d3-9e8c-0b6ad5486f55', 'Over The Bench Supination (Dumbbell)', 'Arms', 'Dumbbells', '{"Forearms"}'::text[], '{}'::text[], 'The Dumbbell Over The Bench Supination strengthens your forearms and grip through a movement motion. Dumbbells allow each arm to work independently, helping correct imbalances. Arm strength supports grip, pulling, and pushing in compound movements.', '67581201', '67581201-Dumbbell-Over-the-Bench-Supination_Forearms_.mp4', 'female', FALSE, '2025-12-03 23:26:33.034396+00', '1. Select a pair of dumbbells at an appropriate weight for Dumbbell Over The Bench Supination. 2. Set up in the starting position for Dumbbell Over The Bench Supination. 3. Execute the movement with proper form, focusing on your forearms. 4. Control both the lifting and lowering phases of the movement. 5. Complete all reps with control before resting.', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 2, NULL, 7, 8, NULL, 5, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 8, 12, NULL, 6, NULL, TRUE, NULL, 'Strength', 62, 7, 8, TRUE, TRUE, 'general_exercise', 'Over The Bench Supination', 'bench_press, chest_fly, push_up', TRUE, 'dumbbell', FALSE, 3, 90, 4, 92, 90, 92, 90),
('49f88ce8-8cb8-412b-bef4-869e44bd4af4', 'Dive Bomber Push Up', 'Chest', 'Bodyweight', '{"Chest"}'::text[], '{"Triceps","Front Delts"}'::text[], 'This dynamic pushing movement gets your heart rate up while developing explosive strength. Secondary activation of your triceps, front delts provides additional muscle engagement. This bodyweight exercise requires no equipment and can be done anywhere. Develops fast-twitch muscle fibers for quicker, more powerful movements.', '86261201', '86261201-Dive-Bomber-Push-up-(male)_Plyometrics_.mp4', 'male', FALSE, '2025-12-03 23:26:27.937212+00', '1. Keep your body in a straight line from head to heels throughout. 2. Lower your chest toward the floor by bending your elbows. 3. Push through your palms to return to the starting position. 4. Continue for your target rep count, maintaining good form throughout. Control the movement—avoid using momentum. Perfect for targeting your chest.', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 2, NULL, 7, 7, NULL, 5, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 8, 12, NULL, 6, NULL, TRUE, NULL, 'Strength', 70, 7, 8, TRUE, TRUE, 'push_up', 'Dive Bomber Push Up', 'bench_press, chest_fly, dip', TRUE, 'bodyweight', FALSE, 3, 90, 4, 70, 88, 95, 65),
('4a100f2a-30e9-4e45-a176-19166d2dae34', 'Cobra Yoga Pose', 'Core', 'Bodyweight', '{"Abs"}'::text[], '{"Hip Flexors"}'::text[], 'This movement exercise engages your abs for improved core stability and strength. This bodyweight exercise requires no equipment and can be done anywhere. Building core stability helps with everything from heavy deadlifts to daily activities. Maintain proper breathing - exhale during the effort phase.', '42671201', '42671201-Cobra-Yoga-Pose-(female)_Waist-FIX_.mp4', 'female', FALSE, '2025-12-03 23:26:32.374165+00', '1. Set up in the starting position for Cobra Yoga Pose. 2. Execute the movement with proper form, focusing on your abs. 3. Control both the lifting and lowering phases of the movement. 4. Continue for your target rep count, maintaining good form throughout.', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 1, NULL, 1, 1, NULL, 3, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 1, 1, NULL, 1, NULL, TRUE, NULL, 'Stretch', 15, 2, 6, FALSE, TRUE, 'back_stretch', 'Cobra Yoga Pose', 'stretch_hip, stretch_back, plank', FALSE, 'bodyweight', TRUE, 1, 30, 2, 70, 88, 95, 65),
('4a1b6d76-b972-4a15-a841-e845f00fbd58', 'Skater Hops', 'Legs', 'Bodyweight', '{"Glutes"}'::text[], '{"Quads","Hip Abductors"}'::text[], 'A challenging plyometric exercise, the Skater Hops builds reactive power and improves conditioning. No equipment needed—your body provides all the resistance. Plyometric training builds explosive power that transfers to sports and daily activities.', '33611201', '33611201-Skater-Hops-(male)_Plyometrics-FIX_.mp4', 'male', FALSE, '2025-12-03 23:26:29.083517+00', '1. Set up in the starting position for Skater Hops. 2. Execute the movement with proper form, focusing on your full body. 3. Control both the lifting and lowering phases of the movement. 4. Continue for your target rep count, maintaining good form throughout. Focus on maintaining proper breathing throughout.', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 2, NULL, 5, 4, NULL, 8, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 8, 12, NULL, 7, NULL, TRUE, NULL, 'Plyometrics', 50, 9, 8, TRUE, TRUE, 'skater', 'Skater Hops', 'squat, bench_press, deadlift', FALSE, 'bodyweight', FALSE, 3, 60, 4, 70, 88, 95, 65),
('4a2765a1-2a92-4f8e-8bd9-806d99d2b809', 'Side To Side Way', 'Full Body', 'Bodyweight', '{"Full Body"}'::text[], '{}'::text[], 'A challenging plyometric exercise, the Side To Side Way builds reactive power and improves conditioning. A versatile bodyweight movement perfect for home or gym training. Great for improving athletic performance, burning calories, and building conditioning.', '66401201', '66401201-Side-to-Side-Way-(female)_Plyometrics_.mp4', 'female', FALSE, '2025-12-03 23:26:37.429219+00', '1. Set up in the starting position for Side To Side Way. 2. Execute the movement with proper form, focusing on your full body. 3. Control both the lifting and lowering phases of the movement. 4. Continue for your target rep count, maintaining good form throughout.', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 2, NULL, 7, 7, NULL, 5, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 8, 12, NULL, 6, NULL, TRUE, NULL, 'Strength', 50, 7, 8, TRUE, TRUE, 'general_exercise', 'Side To Side Way', 'squat, bench_press, deadlift', FALSE, 'bodyweight', FALSE, 3, 90, 4, 70, 88, 95, 65),
('4a315a07-5dee-4821-a4ff-e2c0de79bdb7', 'Standing Yin Yang Circles', 'Shoulders', 'Bodyweight', '{"Shoulders"}'::text[], '{"Traps"}'::text[], 'This movement exercise works your delts for improved shoulder strength and aesthetics. Performing this standing challenges your balance and core engagement. A versatile bodyweight movement perfect for home or gym training. Shoulder development enhances both performance and upper body aesthetics. This is a great exercise for all fitness levels with proper scaling.', '64471201', '64471201-Standing-Yin-Yang-Circles-(femele)_Shoulders_.mp4', 'female', FALSE, '2025-12-03 23:26:39.21093+00', '1. Stand tall with your feet firmly planted. 2. Set up in the starting position for Standing Yin Yang Circles. 3. Execute the movement with proper form, focusing on your delts. 4. Control both the lifting and lowering phases of the movement. 5. Continue for your target rep count, maintaining good form throughout.', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 2, NULL, 7, 7, NULL, 5, 'Standing', NULL, NULL, NULL, 8, 12, NULL, 6, NULL, TRUE, NULL, 'Strength', 52, 7, 8, TRUE, TRUE, 'general_exercise', 'Standing Yin Yang Circles', 'squat, bench_press, deadlift', FALSE, 'bodyweight', FALSE, 3, 90, 4, 70, 88, 95, 65),
('4a4a98ce-95a3-4978-bc0d-73af36899dc6', 'Wipers (Straight Leg)', 'Core', 'Bodyweight', '{"Abs"}'::text[], '{"Hip Flexors"}'::text[], 'Build a stronger core with the Wipers (straight Leg), focusing on your abs. A versatile bodyweight movement perfect for home or gym training. Building core stability helps with everything from heavy deadlifts to daily activities.', '12491201', '12491201-Wipers-(straight-leg)_Waist-FIX_.mp4', 'male', FALSE, '2025-12-03 23:26:28.851102+00', '1. Set up in the starting position for Wipers. 2. Execute the movement with proper form, focusing on your abs. 3. Control both the lifting and lowering phases of the movement. 4. Continue for your target rep count, maintaining good form throughout. Keep tension on the target muscles throughout.', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 2, NULL, 7, 7, NULL, 5, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 8, 12, NULL, 6, NULL, TRUE, NULL, 'Strength', 50, 7, 8, TRUE, TRUE, 'romanian_deadlift', 'Wipers', 'deadlift, leg_curl, hip_thrust', FALSE, 'bodyweight', FALSE, 3, 90, 4, 70, 88, 95, 65),
('4a5dbb55-0cd4-41ff-84fb-c48b00482a02', 'Decline Bench Press (Plate)', 'Chest', 'Weight Plate, Decline Bench', '{"Chest","Lower Chest"}'::text[], '{"Front Delts","Triceps"}'::text[], 'Target your chest with the Weighted Plate Decline Chest Press, an effective pressing movement for upper body strength. The triceps, front delts assist throughout the movement, making this a well-rounded exercise. Declining shifts the emphasis to hit the muscles from a different angle. A well-developed chest contributes to upper body strength and aesthetics.', '66121201', '66121201-Weighted-Plate-Decline-Chest-Press-(male)_Chest_.mp4', 'male', FALSE, '2025-12-03 23:26:26.808474+00', '1. Lower the weight toward your chest with control. 2. Press the weight up until your arms are extended (don''t lock elbows). 3. Continue for your target rep count, maintaining good form throughout. Focus on the mind-muscle connection.', 'Press', 'Push', 'Compound', 'Bilateral', NULL, 4, NULL, 7, 7, NULL, 5, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 8, 12, NULL, 6, NULL, TRUE, NULL, 'Strength', 73, 7, 8, TRUE, TRUE, 'decline_press', 'Weighted Plate Decline Chest Press', 'bench_press, incline_bench_press, chest_fly, dip', FALSE, 'plate', FALSE, 3, 90, 4, 70, 88, 95, 65),
('4a5f0173-5a3e-4aee-a71f-179527378ff7', 'Chest Fly Plyo Squat', 'Legs', 'Bodyweight', '{"Quads","Glutes"}'::text[], '{"Front Delts"}'::text[], 'Build stronger quads with this squatting movement that develops leg drive and power. Your front delts work as secondary movers, adding to the training stimulus. A versatile bodyweight movement perfect for home or gym training. Strong legs are the foundation for athletic performance and functional fitness.', '60851201', '60851201-Chest-Fly-Plyo-Squat-(female)_Hips_.mp4', 'female', FALSE, '2025-12-03 23:26:32.166461+00', '1. With a slight bend in your elbows, move the weight in a wide arc. 2. Squeeze your chest muscles at the center/top of the movement. 3. Return with control, feeling the stretch at the bottom. 4. Repeat for the prescribed number of repetitions. Ensure full range of motion on each rep.', 'Squat', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 3, NULL, 5, 4, NULL, 8, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 8, 12, NULL, 7, NULL, TRUE, NULL, 'Plyometrics', 100, 9, 8, TRUE, TRUE, 'chest_fly', 'Chest Fly Plyo Squat', 'bench_press, incline_press, push_up', FALSE, 'bodyweight', FALSE, 3, 60, 4, 70, 88, 95, 65),
('4a74b14e-d4d9-48ff-8aed-cfeba361c50e', 'Triceps Kickback (TRX)', 'Arms', 'TRX', '{"Triceps"}'::text[], '{"Rear Delts"}'::text[], 'The Suspender Triceps Kickback targets your triceps through a kicking motion. You''ll also feel your hamstrings working to support the movement. Suspension training adds instability, increasing core activation throughout. Arm strength supports grip, pulling, and pushing in compound movements.', '11501201', '11501201-Suspender-Triceps-Kickback-(female)_Upper-arms_.mp4', 'female', FALSE, '2025-12-03 23:26:39.623429+00', '1. Adjust the TRX/suspension straps to the appropriate length for Suspender Triceps Kickback. 2. Keep your upper arm stationary and extend your forearm back. 3. Squeeze at full extension, then return with control. 4. Repeat for the prescribed number of repetitions.', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 2, NULL, 5, 7, NULL, 6, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 10, 15, NULL, 4, NULL, TRUE, NULL, 'Strength', 40, 5, 7, FALSE, TRUE, 'tricep_kickback', 'Suspender Triceps Kickback', 'tricep_pushdown, tricep_extension', FALSE, 'trx', FALSE, 3, 60, 2, 68, 85, 85, 70),
('4a7cce38-366e-419a-be4b-9d9b96161bce', 'Heel Tap Arm Curl', 'Arms', 'Bodyweight', '{"Biceps"}'::text[], '{"Forearms"}'::text[], 'Elevate your training with this curling exercise that develops speed, power, and coordination. The forearms assist throughout the movement, making this a well-rounded exercise. A versatile bodyweight movement perfect for home or gym training. Plyometric training builds explosive power that transfers to sports and daily activities.', '98521201', '98521201-Heel-Tap-Arm-Curl-(male)_Plyometrics_.mp4', 'male', FALSE, '2025-12-03 23:26:24.831811+00', '1. Keep your elbows in a fixed position throughout the movement. 2. Curl the weight up by contracting your biceps, squeezing at the top. 3. Lower with control, resisting the weight on the way down. 4. Complete all reps with control before resting. Engage your stabilizer muscles for better control.', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 2, NULL, 5, 7, NULL, 6, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 10, 15, NULL, 4, NULL, TRUE, NULL, 'Strength', 70, 5, 7, FALSE, TRUE, 'bicep_curl', 'Heel Tap Arm Curl', 'hammer_curl, preacher_curl, cable_curl', FALSE, 'bodyweight', FALSE, 3, 60, 2, 70, 88, 95, 65),
('4a80b66e-fd96-404a-86e9-1a8bec6c7f5a', 'Pushdown (Band)', 'Arms', 'Resistance Band, Anchor Point', '{"Triceps"}'::text[], '{"Chest","Shoulders"}'::text[], 'The Band Pushdown targets your triceps through a pushing motion. The band creates increasing tension as it stretches, challenging the lockout. Dedicated arm training builds both strength and muscular definition.', '9161201', '09161201-Band-pushdown-(female)_Upper-Arms.mp4', 'female', FALSE, '2025-12-03 23:26:30.887491+00', '1. Secure the resistance band appropriately for Band Pushdown. 2. Set up in the starting position for Band Pushdown. 3. Execute the movement with proper form, focusing on your triceps. 4. Control both the lifting and lowering phases of the movement. 5. Repeat for the prescribed number of repetitions.', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 2, NULL, 5, 7, NULL, 6, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 10, 15, NULL, 4, NULL, TRUE, NULL, 'Strength', 55, 5, 7, FALSE, TRUE, 'tricep_pushdown', 'Pushdown', 'tricep_extension, close_grip_bench, dip', FALSE, 'band', FALSE, 3, 60, 2, 60, 85, 90, 50),
('4a9673b2-6e03-4f3e-9ae6-cdc3214c4f3e', 'Planked Side Toe Tap', 'Core', 'Bodyweight', '{"Abs"}'::text[], '{"Shoulders"}'::text[], 'Strengthen your midsection with this stabilization movement that works your abs. The shoulders, lower back assist throughout the movement, making this a well-rounded exercise. This bodyweight exercise requires no equipment and can be done anywhere. Building core stability helps with everything from heavy deadlifts to daily activities.', '72191201', '72191201-Planked-Side-Toe-Tap-(male)_Waist_.mp4', 'male', FALSE, '2025-12-03 23:26:26.678791+00', '1. Hold your body in a straight line from head to heels. 2. Don''t let your hips sag or pike up—engage your core and glutes. 3. Breathe steadily while maintaining the position. 4. Complete all reps with control before resting. Ensure full range of motion on each rep.', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 2, NULL, 7, 7, NULL, 5, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 8, 12, NULL, 6, NULL, TRUE, NULL, 'Strength', 70, 7, 8, TRUE, TRUE, 'plank', 'Planked Side Toe Tap', 'side_plank, dead_bug, hollow_hold', FALSE, 'bodyweight', FALSE, 3, 90, 4, 70, 88, 95, 65),
('4aa538af-3d19-4783-b239-f1810b025b05', 'Side Hands Standing Crunch', 'Core', 'Bodyweight', '{"Abs"}'::text[], '{"Hip Flexors"}'::text[], 'The Side Hands Standing Crunch is an explosive exercise that combines cardiovascular training with dynamic crunching movements. Your hip flexors work as secondary movers, adding to the training stimulus. The standing position engages your core for stability. A versatile bodyweight movement perfect for home or gym training. Plyometric training builds explosive power that transfers to sports and daily activities.', '91551201', '91551201-Side-Hands-Standing-Crunch-(female)_Plyometrics_.mp4', 'female', FALSE, '2025-12-03 23:26:36.985772+00', '1. Begin in a standing position with good posture. 2. Curl your shoulders off the floor by contracting your abs. 3. Don''t pull on your neck—focus on the abdominal contraction. 4. Lower with control, maintaining some tension. 5. Repeat for the prescribed number of repetitions.', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 2, NULL, 5, 7, NULL, 6, 'Standing', NULL, NULL, NULL, 12, 20, NULL, 4, NULL, TRUE, NULL, 'Strength', 72, 5, 7, FALSE, TRUE, 'crunch', 'Side Hands Standing Crunch', 'leg_raise, plank, russian_twist, v_up', TRUE, 'bodyweight', FALSE, 3, 60, 2, 70, 88, 95, 65),
('4aa66d7e-d77d-438d-ae98-0369653c0f08', 'Lying Crossed Legs Twist', 'Full Body', 'Bodyweight', '{"Full Body"}'::text[], '{"Shoulders","Core"}'::text[], 'Build power and athleticism with this high-intensity twisting exercise that challenges your entire body. Secondary activation of your shoulders, core provides additional muscle engagement. Performing this lying down removes momentum for stricter form. No equipment needed—your body provides all the resistance. Develops fast-twitch muscle fibers for quicker, more powerful movements.', '96591201', '96591201-Lying-Crossed-Legs-Twist-(male)_Waist_.mp4', 'male', FALSE, '2025-12-03 23:26:21.109351+00', '1. Lie down in the appropriate position for Lying Crossed Legs Twist. 2. Rotate your torso through the movement pattern for Lying Crossed Legs Twist. 3. Control the rotation in both directions—avoid using momentum. 4. Repeat for the prescribed number of repetitions.', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 2, NULL, 5, 7, NULL, 6, 'Lying', NULL, NULL, NULL, 10, 15, NULL, 4, NULL, TRUE, NULL, 'Strength', 50, 5, 7, FALSE, TRUE, 'russian_twist', 'Lying Crossed Legs Twist', 'squat, lunge, leg_press', FALSE, 'bodyweight', FALSE, 3, 60, 2, 70, 88, 95, 65),
('4aab6110-dc3c-4174-8494-5f18ca75825c', 'Landmine Shoulders Press With Viking Press Attachm (Landmine)', 'Shoulders', 'Landmine Attachment, Barbell', '{"Front Delts"}'::text[], '{"Side Delts","Triceps"}'::text[], 'Build stronger shoulders with this pressing movement focusing on your delts. Shoulder development enhances both performance and upper body aesthetics.', '87141201', '87141201-Landmine-Shoulders-Press-with-Viking-Press-Attachm.mp4', 'male', FALSE, '2025-12-03 23:26:29.837118+00', '1. Start with the weight at shoulder level. 2. Press directly overhead until your arms are fully extended. 3. Lower back to shoulder level with control. 4. Complete all reps with control before resting. Don''t rush—quality over quantity.', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 3, NULL, 7, 8, NULL, 5, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 8, 12, NULL, 6, NULL, TRUE, NULL, 'Strength', 70, 7, 8, TRUE, TRUE, 'shoulder_exercise', 'Landmine Shoulders Press With Viking Press Attachm', 'lateral_raise, front_raise, rear_delt_fly, upright_row', TRUE, 'barbell', FALSE, 3, 90, 4, 95, 80, 65, 95),
('4aafdf39-7542-4b43-a793-d01aeabf2888', 'Seated Side To Side Hip Mobilization On Exercise', 'Legs', 'Bodyweight', '{"Quads"}'::text[], '{"Glutes","Hamstrings"}'::text[], 'Develop your posterior chain with this movement movement that emphasizes the glutes. The seated position helps isolate the target muscles by removing momentum. Strong legs are the foundation for athletic performance and functional fitness.', '98301201', '98301201-Sitting-Side-to-Side-Hip-Mobilization-on-Exercise-.mp4', 'male', FALSE, '2025-12-03 23:26:27.937212+00', '1. Sit with your back supported, core engaged, feet flat on the floor. 2. Set up in the starting position for Seated Side To Side Hip Mobilization On Exercise. 3. Execute the movement with proper form, focusing on your glutes. 4. Control both the lifting and lowering phases of the movement. 5. Continue for your target rep count, maintaining good form throughout.', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 2, NULL, 1, 1, NULL, 3, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 1, 1, NULL, 1, NULL, TRUE, NULL, 'Stretch', 38, 2, 6, FALSE, TRUE, 'mobility', 'Seated Side To Side Hip Mobilization On Exercise', 'hip_thrust, lunge, squat', FALSE, 'bodyweight', TRUE, 1, 30, 2, 70, 88, 95, 65),
('4ab85793-11de-468d-8b0d-e9683600f7fe', 'Pulsing Side Squat', 'Legs', 'Bodyweight', '{"Quads"}'::text[], '{"Glutes","Hamstrings"}'::text[], 'This squatting movement emphasizes your quadriceps for stronger, more powerful legs. Secondary activation of your glutes, hamstrings provides additional muscle engagement. No equipment needed—your body provides all the resistance. Strong legs are the foundation for athletic performance and functional fitness.', '94441201', '94441201-Pulsing-Side-Squat-(female)_Hips_.mp4', 'female', FALSE, '2025-12-03 23:26:35.801913+00', '1. Push your hips back and bend your knees to lower your body. 2. Keep your chest up and knees tracking over your toes. 3. Drive through your heels to stand back up, squeezing your glutes at the top. 4. Continue for your target rep count, maintaining good form throughout. Keep tension on the target muscles throughout. This variation specifically emphasizes the quads.', 'Squat', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 3, NULL, 7, 7, NULL, 5, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 8, 12, NULL, 6, NULL, TRUE, NULL, 'Strength', 85, 7, 8, TRUE, TRUE, 'pulse', 'Pulsing Side Squat', 'leg_press, leg_extension, leg_curl, lunge, front_squat, hack_squat', FALSE, 'bodyweight', FALSE, 3, 90, 4, 70, 88, 95, 65),
('4ac33ce4-32bc-4df5-a1d7-7c645e7a58ec', 'Lunge Stretch', 'Legs', 'Bodyweight', '{"Quads"}'::text[], '{"Glutes","Hamstrings"}'::text[], 'Build stronger quads with this lunging movement that develops leg drive and power. Your glutes, hamstrings work as secondary movers, adding to the training stimulus. A versatile bodyweight movement perfect for home or gym training. Strong legs are the foundation for athletic performance and functional fitness.', '55951201', '55951201-Lunge-Stretch-(male)_Thighs-FIX_.mp4', 'male', FALSE, '2025-12-03 23:26:27.145158+00', '1. Step forward into a lunge until both knees are at about 90 degrees. 2. Push through your front/working leg to return to the starting position. 3. Repeat for the prescribed number of repetitions. Focus on maintaining proper breathing throughout. Great for building strength in your quads.', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 1, NULL, 1, 1, NULL, 3, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 1, 1, NULL, 1, NULL, TRUE, NULL, 'Stretch', 60, 2, 6, FALSE, TRUE, 'hip_stretch', 'Lunge Stretch', 'squat, split_squat, step_up, leg_press', FALSE, 'bodyweight', TRUE, 1, 30, 2, 70, 88, 95, 65),
('4ac6ce6b-9dcd-4532-b2df-5d069ad18c0b', 'Upright Row - Wide Grip (Barbell)', 'Shoulders', 'Barbell', '{"Side Delts"}'::text[], '{"Traps","Front Delts"}'::text[], 'Build stronger shoulders with this rowing movement focusing on your delts. Secondary activation of your traps provides additional muscle engagement. Using a barbell provides stability for progressive overload. Shoulder development enhances both performance and upper body aesthetics.', '35951201', '35951201-Barbell-Wide-Grip-Upright-Row-(female)_Shoulders.mp4', 'female', FALSE, '2025-12-03 23:26:31.133197+00', '1. Grip a barbell with hands at the appropriate width for Barbell Wide Grip Upright Row. 2. Use a wide grip (wider than shoulder-width) for this variation. 3. Pull the weight straight up along your body, leading with your elbows. 4. Raise until elbows reach shoulder height, then lower with control. 5. Complete all reps with control before resting. Focus on squeezing the target muscle at peak contraction.', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 3, NULL, 10, 10, NULL, 4, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 5, 8, NULL, 8, NULL, TRUE, NULL, 'Strength', 82, 7, 9, TRUE, FALSE, 'upright_row', 'Upright Row - Wide Grip', 'Upright Row - Wide Grip', FALSE, 'barbell', FALSE, 4, 120, 4, 95, 80, 65, 95),
('4accf13c-ea85-4674-a6ab-13534a6ceece', 'Segmental Roll', 'Full Body', 'Bodyweight', '{"Full Body"}'::text[], '{}'::text[], 'This stretch specifically works on your full body, promoting flexibility and reducing muscle tightness. Regular stretching improves flexibility, reduces injury risk, and aids recovery. Control the negative portion for maximum muscle engagement. Consistency with this movement will yield noticeable results.', '79151201', '79151201-Segmental-Roll-(female)_Stretching_.mp4', 'female', FALSE, '2025-12-03 23:26:36.848698+00', '1. Move into the stretch position for Segmental Roll. 2. Ease into the stretch until you feel gentle tension (not pain). 3. Hold for 20-30 seconds, breathing deeply and relaxing into the stretch.', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 2, NULL, 7, 7, NULL, 5, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 8, 12, NULL, 6, NULL, TRUE, NULL, 'Strength', 50, 7, 8, TRUE, TRUE, 'general_exercise', 'Segmental Roll', 'squat, bench_press, deadlift', FALSE, 'bodyweight', FALSE, 3, 90, 4, 70, 88, 95, 65),
('4ad8a196-037b-4925-90e0-0b6d5d03fd57', 'Roll Hip Stretch', 'Legs', 'Bodyweight', '{"Hips"}'::text[], '{"Glutes","Hip Flexors"}'::text[], 'The Roll Hip Stretch provides a deep stretch for your hips, ideal for recovery and mobility work. Regular stretching improves flexibility, reduces injury risk, and aids recovery.', '54341201', '54341201-Roll-Hip-Stretch-(female)_Hips_.mp4', 'female', FALSE, '2025-12-03 23:26:36.38616+00', '1. Move into the stretch position for Roll Hip Stretch. 2. Ease into the stretch until you feel gentle tension (not pain). 3. Hold for 20-30 seconds, breathing deeply and relaxing into the stretch.', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 1, NULL, 1, 1, NULL, 3, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 1, 1, NULL, 1, NULL, TRUE, NULL, 'Stretch', 40, 2, 6, FALSE, TRUE, 'hip_stretch', 'Roll Hip Stretch', 'stretch_hamstring, stretch_glute, stretch_back', FALSE, 'bodyweight', TRUE, 1, 30, 2, 70, 88, 95, 65),
('4adafdc8-a515-4ecc-8267-2841e552a793', 'Lying Leg Hip Raise', 'Core', 'Bodyweight', '{"Abs"}'::text[], '{"Hip Flexors"}'::text[], 'Build a stronger core with the Lying Leg Hip Raise, focusing on your abs. Performing this lying down removes momentum for stricter form. A versatile bodyweight movement perfect for home or gym training. A strong core improves posture, protects your spine, and enhances all other lifts.', '8651201', '08651201-Lying-leg-hip-raise_Waist.mp4', 'male', FALSE, '2025-12-03 23:26:28.71819+00', '1. Lie down in the appropriate position for Lying Leg Hip Raise. 2. Set up in the starting position for Lying Leg Hip Raise. 3. Execute the movement with proper form, focusing on your abs. 4. Control both the lifting and lowering phases of the movement. 5. Complete all reps with control before resting. Don''t rush—quality over quantity.', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 2, NULL, 5, 7, NULL, 6, 'Lying', NULL, NULL, NULL, 10, 15, NULL, 4, NULL, TRUE, NULL, 'Strength', 70, 5, 7, FALSE, TRUE, 'leg_exercise', 'Lying Leg Hip Raise', 'squat, leg_curl, calf_raise', FALSE, 'bodyweight', FALSE, 3, 60, 2, 70, 88, 95, 65),
('4ae0d9b8-ca72-4904-819e-48af6aa67ac5', 'Lying Leg Raise (modified)', 'Core', 'Bodyweight', '{"Lower Abs"}'::text[], '{"Hip Flexors"}'::text[], 'Build leg strength with this raising movement focusing on your abs. Secondary activation of your hip flexors provides additional muscle engagement. Performing this lying down removes momentum for stricter form. No equipment needed—your body provides all the resistance. Strong legs are the foundation for athletic performance and functional fitness.', '44191201', '44191201-Lying-Leg-Raise-(Modified)_Hips.mp4', 'male', FALSE, '2025-12-03 23:26:23.586683+00', '1. Lie down in the appropriate position for Lying Leg Raise. 2. Keeping legs mostly straight, raise them toward the ceiling. 3. Lower with control, stopping just before touching down. 4. Continue for your target rep count, maintaining good form throughout. Maintain consistent tempo throughout the set.', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 2, NULL, 5, 7, NULL, 6, 'Lying', NULL, NULL, NULL, 10, 15, NULL, 4, NULL, TRUE, NULL, 'Strength', 70, 5, 7, FALSE, TRUE, 'leg_raise', 'Lying Leg Raise', 'crunch, plank, v_up', FALSE, 'bodyweight', FALSE, 3, 60, 2, 70, 88, 95, 65),
('4ae2ef56-4e34-4785-8437-9ff4db4b6d0d', 'Tip Toe Glute Bridge Pulse', 'Legs', 'Bodyweight', '{"Glutes"}'::text[], '{"Hamstrings"}'::text[], 'Build stronger glutes with this bridging movement focused on hip extension. Your hamstrings work as secondary movers, adding to the training stimulus. This bodyweight exercise requires no equipment and can be done anywhere. Strong legs are the foundation for athletic performance and functional fitness.', '94471201', '94471201-Tip-Toe-Glute-Bridge-Pulse-(female)_Hips_.mp4', 'female', FALSE, '2025-12-03 23:26:39.623429+00', '1. Drive through your heels to lift your hips toward the ceiling. 2. Squeeze your glutes hard at the top of the movement. 3. Lower your hips back down with control. 4. At the bottom or top, pulse up and down in small movements before completing the rep. 5. Repeat for the prescribed number of repetitions. Engage your stabilizer muscles for better control.', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 2, NULL, 7, 7, NULL, 5, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 8, 12, NULL, 6, NULL, TRUE, NULL, 'Strength', 70, 7, 8, TRUE, TRUE, 'glute_bridge', 'Tip Toe Glute Bridge Pulse', 'hip_thrust, romanian_deadlift', TRUE, 'bodyweight', FALSE, 3, 90, 4, 70, 88, 95, 65),
('4aeeb797-5df5-4456-af4d-214295c111df', 'Reverse Fly (Band)', 'Shoulders', 'Resistance Band, Anchor Point', '{"Rear Delts"}'::text[], '{"Upper Back","Traps"}'::text[], 'Target your rear delts with the Band Reverse Fly, an effective shoulder flying exercise. You''ll also feel your upper back working to support the movement. Resistance bands provide accommodating resistance that increases through the range of motion. Shoulder development enhances both performance and upper body aesthetics.', '68641201', '68641201-Band-Reverse-Fly_Shoulders_.mp4', 'male', FALSE, '2025-12-03 23:26:29.483269+00', '1. Secure the resistance band appropriately for Band Reverse Fly. 2. With a slight bend in your elbows, move the weight in a wide arc. 3. Squeeze your chest muscles at the center/top of the movement. 4. Return with control, feeling the stretch at the bottom. 5. Continue for your target rep count, maintaining good form throughout. Keep the movement smooth and controlled.', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 2, NULL, 5, 7, NULL, 6, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 10, 15, NULL, 4, NULL, TRUE, NULL, 'Strength', 75, 5, 7, FALSE, TRUE, 'rear_delt', 'Reverse Fly', 'bench_press, incline_bench_press, push_up', FALSE, 'band', FALSE, 3, 60, 2, 60, 85, 90, 50),
('4af0ef2d-8f84-4bf6-b406-1cb58964c744', 'Leg Stretched Open Toes Together Knees Together', 'Full Body', 'Bodyweight', '{"Full Body"}'::text[], '{}'::text[], 'The Leg Stretched Open Toes Together Knees Together is a flexibility exercise that targets your full body, helping to release tension and improve range of motion. Flexibility work like this enhances performance and prevents stiffness.', '84911201', '84911201-Leg-Stretched-Open-Toes-Together-Knees-Together-(f.mp4', 'female', FALSE, '2025-12-03 23:26:34.603963+00', '1. Move into the stretch position for Leg Stretched Open Toes Together Knees Together. 2. Ease into the stretch until you feel gentle tension (not pain). 3. Hold for 20-30 seconds, breathing deeply and relaxing into the stretch.', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 1, NULL, 1, 1, NULL, 3, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 1, 1, NULL, 1, NULL, TRUE, NULL, 'Stretch', 40, 2, 6, FALSE, TRUE, 'stretch_general', 'Leg Stretched Open Toes Together Knees Together', 'stretch_hip, stretch_back, stretch_shoulder', FALSE, 'bodyweight', TRUE, 1, 30, 2, 70, 88, 95, 65),
('4af84019-d9c5-4d47-998b-f805731fe184', 'Standing Single Leg Curl', 'Legs', 'Bodyweight', '{"Hamstrings"}'::text[], '{"Glutes"}'::text[], 'This curling movement works your hamstrings for balanced leg development. You''ll also feel your calves working to support the movement. The standing position engages your core for stability. This bodyweight exercise requires no equipment and can be done anywhere. Lower body strength improves everything from walking to heavy compound lifts.', '7951201', '07951201-Standing-Single-Leg-Curl_Thighs_.mp4', 'male', FALSE, '2025-12-03 23:26:21.995567+00', '1. Begin in a standing position with good posture. 2. Curl your heels toward your glutes by bending at the knees. 3. Squeeze your hamstrings at peak contraction. 4. Extend legs back out with control. 5. Complete all reps on one side, then switch to the other side. 6. Complete all reps with control before resting.', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 2, NULL, 7, 7, NULL, 5, 'Standing', NULL, NULL, NULL, 8, 12, NULL, 6, NULL, TRUE, NULL, 'Strength', 77, 7, 8, TRUE, TRUE, 'leg_curl', 'Standing Single Leg Curl', 'romanian_deadlift, hip_thrust', FALSE, 'bodyweight', FALSE, 3, 90, 4, 70, 88, 95, 65),
('4aff94db-b08f-42ea-9da8-4704985ff578', 'Standing Front Leg Lift Cross Toe Touches', 'Core', 'Bodyweight', '{"Abs"}'::text[], '{"Hip Flexors"}'::text[], 'Build a stronger core with the Standing Front Leg Lift Cross Toe Touches, focusing on your abs. Your hip flexors work as secondary movers, adding to the training stimulus. The standing position engages your core for stability. A versatile bodyweight movement perfect for home or gym training. Building core stability helps with everything from heavy deadlifts to daily activities.', '65661201', '65661201-Standing-Front-Leg-Lift-Cross-Toe-Touches-(female).mp4', 'female', FALSE, '2025-12-03 23:26:38.570929+00', '1. Stand tall with your feet firmly planted. 2. Set up in the starting position for Standing Front Leg Lift Cross Toe Touches. 3. Execute the movement with proper form, focusing on your abs. 4. Control both the lifting and lowering phases of the movement. 5. Repeat for the prescribed number of repetitions.', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 2, NULL, 7, 7, NULL, 5, 'Standing', NULL, NULL, NULL, 8, 12, NULL, 6, NULL, TRUE, NULL, 'Strength', 52, 7, 8, TRUE, TRUE, 'toe_touch', 'Standing Front Leg Lift Cross Toe Touches', 'high_knees, butt_kicks, jumping_jack', FALSE, 'bodyweight', FALSE, 3, 90, 4, 70, 88, 95, 65),
('4b0b3d6d-fb3b-4552-b106-17429d186585', 'Seated Single Leg Curl (Chair)', 'Legs', 'Chair', '{"Hamstrings"}'::text[], '{"Glutes"}'::text[], 'The Seated Single Leg Curl On Chair targets your hamstrings through a controlled curling motion. You''ll also feel your calves working to support the movement. The seated position helps isolate the target muscles by removing momentum. Lower body strength improves everything from walking to heavy compound lifts.', '105001201', '105001201-Seated-Single-Leg-Curl-on-Chair-(male)_Thighs_.mp4', 'male', FALSE, '2025-12-03 23:26:24.831811+00', '1. Position yourself with a sturdy chair for support or as part of the movement. 2. Sit with your back supported, core engaged, feet flat on the floor. 3. Curl your heels toward your glutes by bending at the knees. 4. Squeeze your hamstrings at peak contraction. 5. Extend legs back out with control. 6. Complete all reps on one side, then switch to the other side. 7. Repeat for the prescribed number of repetitions.', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 2, NULL, 7, 7, NULL, 5, 'Seated', NULL, NULL, NULL, 8, 12, NULL, 6, NULL, TRUE, NULL, 'Strength', 62, 7, 8, TRUE, TRUE, 'leg_curl', 'Seated Single Leg Curl On Chair', 'romanian_deadlift, hip_thrust', FALSE, 'bodyweight', FALSE, 3, 90, 4, 70, 88, 95, 65),
('4b0d7d0f-7f86-4a28-9422-6f43251f28db', 'Push Up Rear Lunge (Against Wall) - Alternating', 'Legs', 'Wall', '{"Quads","Glutes"}'::text[], '{"Triceps","Front Delts"}'::text[], 'Target your chest with the Push Up Alternate Rear Lunge Against Wall, an effective pushing movement for upper body strength. The triceps, front delts assist throughout the movement, making this a well-rounded exercise. Chest strength improves pushing power for sports, daily tasks, and other lifts.', '76791201', '76791201-Push-up-Alternate-Rear-Lunge-against-Wall-(male)_C.mp4', 'male', FALSE, '2025-12-03 23:26:22.755209+00', '1. Position yourself at the appropriate distance from a wall. 2. Keep your body in a straight line from head to heels throughout. 3. Lower your chest toward the floor by bending your elbows. 4. Push through your palms to return to the starting position. 5. Complete all reps with control before resting. Control the movement—avoid using momentum.', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 2, NULL, 7, 7, NULL, 5, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 8, 12, NULL, 6, NULL, TRUE, NULL, 'Strength', 62, 7, 8, TRUE, TRUE, 'push_up', 'Push Up Rear Lunge Against Wall - Alternating', 'bench_press, chest_fly, dip', TRUE, 'bodyweight', FALSE, 3, 90, 4, 70, 88, 95, 65),
('4b120ac4-652b-4bc0-bf36-fab0e9e9fcc7', 'Diagonal Claps Woodchopper', 'Core', 'Bodyweight', '{"Obliques"}'::text[], '{"Abs"}'::text[], 'This dynamic movement movement gets your heart rate up while developing explosive strength. A versatile bodyweight movement perfect for home or gym training. Plyometric training builds explosive power that transfers to sports and daily activities. Can be modified for beginners or progressed for advanced athletes.', '83941201', '83941201-Diagonal-Claps-Woodchopper-(male)_Plyometrics_.mp4', 'male', FALSE, '2025-12-03 23:26:27.145158+00', '1. Set up in the starting position for Diagonal Claps Woodchopper. 2. Execute the movement with proper form, focusing on your full body. 3. Control both the lifting and lowering phases of the movement. 4. Complete all reps with control before resting.', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 2, NULL, 5, 4, NULL, 8, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 8, 12, NULL, 7, NULL, TRUE, NULL, 'Plyometrics', 50, 9, 8, TRUE, TRUE, 'woodchop', 'Diagonal Claps Woodchopper', 'russian_twist, pallof_press, cable_crunch', FALSE, 'bodyweight', FALSE, 3, 60, 4, 70, 88, 95, 65),
('4b14837b-648c-4480-94e1-9e2f1ba3b287', 'Hack Squat - Single Leg (Machine)', 'Legs', 'Machine', '{"Quads"}'::text[], '{"Glutes","Hamstrings"}'::text[], 'Build stronger quads with this squatting movement that develops leg drive and power. Your glutes work as secondary movers, adding to the training stimulus. Lower body strength improves everything from walking to heavy compound lifts.', '74081201', '74081201-Sled-One-Leg-Hack-Squat-(female)_Thighs_.mp4', 'female', FALSE, '2025-12-03 23:26:37.99429+00', '1. Push your hips back and bend your knees to lower your body. 2. Keep your chest up and knees tracking over your toes. 3. Drive through your heels to stand back up, squeezing your glutes at the top. 4. Complete all reps on one side, then switch to the other side. 5. Repeat for the prescribed number of repetitions. Exhale during the exertion phase of the movement.', 'Squat', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 4, NULL, 10, 10, NULL, 4, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 5, 8, NULL, 9, NULL, FALSE, NULL, 'Strength', 80, 7, 9, TRUE, FALSE, 'hack_squat', 'Sled Single Leg Hack Squat', 'leg_press, squat, leg_extension', TRUE, 'machine', FALSE, 4, 120, 5, 80, 75, 20, 88),
('4b1f3ee9-3747-4787-a8a4-88980a443cb6', 'Cow Face Yoga Pose Gomukhasana', 'Back', 'Bodyweight', '{"Lats"}'::text[], '{"Lower Back"}'::text[], 'The Cow Face Yoga Pose Gomukhasana provides a deep stretch for your full body, ideal for recovery and mobility work. Regular stretching improves flexibility, reduces injury risk, and aids recovery.', '69021201', '69021201-Cow-Face-Yoga-Pose-Gomukhasana-(female)_Stretching.mp4', 'female', FALSE, '2025-12-03 23:26:32.374165+00', '1. Move into the stretch position for Cow Face Yoga Pose Gomukhasana. 2. Ease into the stretch until you feel gentle tension (not pain). 3. Hold for 20-30 seconds, breathing deeply and relaxing into the stretch.', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 1, NULL, 1, 1, NULL, 3, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 1, 1, NULL, 1, NULL, TRUE, NULL, 'Stretch', 15, 2, 6, FALSE, TRUE, 'yoga', 'Cow Face Yoga Pose Gomukhasana', 'stretch_hip, stretch_back, plank', FALSE, 'bodyweight', TRUE, 1, 30, 2, 70, 88, 95, 65),
('4b2f3a9e-bebc-4f35-bf40-35437a559d22', 'Preacher Curl (Cable)', 'Arms', 'Cables', '{"Biceps"}'::text[], '{"Forearms"}'::text[], 'The Cable Preacher Curl is a curling exercise that isolates your biceps. You''ll also feel your forearms working to support the movement. Cable resistance creates smooth, continuous muscle engagement. Dedicated arm training builds both strength and muscular definition.', '97411201', '97411201-Cable-Preacher-Curl-(female)_Upper-Arms_.mp4', 'female', FALSE, '2025-12-03 23:26:32.054831+00', '1. Adjust the cable machine to the correct height and attachment for Cable Preacher Curl. 2. Keep your elbows in a fixed position throughout the movement. 3. Curl the weight up by contracting your biceps, squeezing at the top. 4. Lower with control, resisting the weight on the way down. 5. Repeat for the prescribed number of repetitions. Keep your shoulders relaxed and away from your ears.', 'Curl', 'Pull', NULL, NULL, NULL, 2, NULL, 5, 7, NULL, 6, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 12, 20, NULL, 4, NULL, FALSE, NULL, 'Strength', 90, 5, 7, FALSE, TRUE, 'preacher_curl', 'Preacher Curl', 'tricep_pushdown, tricep_extension, bicep_curl, hammer_curl', FALSE, 'cable', FALSE, 3, 60, 2, 85, 88, 30, 92),
('4b32e012-daa8-4fd0-9847-e00ce323a297', 'Dumbbel Seated Arnold Press', 'Shoulders', 'Bodyweight', '{"Front Delts"}'::text[], '{"Side Delts","Triceps"}'::text[], 'This pressing exercise works your delts for improved shoulder strength and aesthetics. Secondary activation of your triceps provides additional muscle engagement. The seated position helps isolate the target muscles by removing momentum. Using dumbbells requires more stabilization than barbell variations. Shoulder development enhances both performance and upper body aesthetics.', '69931201', '69931201-Dumbbel-Seated-Arnold-Press-(female)_Shoulders_.mp4', 'female', FALSE, '2025-12-03 23:26:32.624497+00', '1. Sit with your back supported, core engaged, feet flat on the floor. 2. Start with the weight at shoulder level. 3. Press directly overhead until your arms are fully extended. 4. Lower back to shoulder level with control. 5. Continue for your target rep count, maintaining good form throughout.', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 2, NULL, 7, 7, NULL, 5, 'Seated', NULL, NULL, NULL, 8, 12, NULL, 6, NULL, TRUE, NULL, 'Strength', 72, 7, 8, TRUE, TRUE, 'shoulder_press', 'Dumbbel Seated Arnold Press', 'lateral_raise, front_raise, rear_delt', FALSE, 'bodyweight', FALSE, 3, 90, 4, 70, 88, 95, 65),
('4b341238-1b38-43ea-b78b-736c1f4963e7', 'Full Zercher Squat (Barbell)', 'Legs', 'Barbell', '{"Quads"}'::text[], '{"Glutes","Hamstrings"}'::text[], 'Target the front of your thighs with this squatting exercise for quad development. The glutes, hamstrings assist throughout the movement, making this a well-rounded exercise. Using a barbell provides stability for progressive overload. Lower body strength improves everything from walking to heavy compound lifts. Keep your core engaged throughout the exercise.', '57521201', '57521201-Barbell-full-Zercher-Squat-(female)_Thighs_.mp4', 'female', FALSE, '2025-12-03 23:26:31.013316+00', '1. Set up a barbell in a rack at the appropriate height for Barbell Full Zercher Squat. 2. Push your hips back and bend your knees to lower your body. 3. Keep your chest up and knees tracking over your toes. 4. Drive through your heels to stand back up, squeezing your glutes at the top. 5. Continue for your target rep count, maintaining good form throughout.', 'Squat', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 4, NULL, 10, 10, NULL, 4, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 5, 8, NULL, 9, NULL, TRUE, NULL, 'Strength', 35, 7, 9, TRUE, FALSE, 'squat', 'Full Zercher Squat', 'leg_press, front_squat, goblet_squat, lunge, leg_extension', FALSE, 'barbell', FALSE, 4, 120, 5, 95, 80, 65, 95),
