('4b630e3b-37a5-4243-8033-96dd49b64e2a', 'Seated Lower Trunk Lateral Flexor Stretch', 'Back', 'Bodyweight', '{"Lats"}'::text[], '{"Lower Back"}'::text[], 'Target your lats with this stretching stretch that helps restore range of motion. Secondary activation of your shoulders provides additional muscle engagement. The seated position helps isolate the target muscles by removing momentum. Flexibility work like this enhances performance and prevents stiffness.', '21141201', '21141201-Seated-Lower-Trunk-Lateral-Flexor-Stretch-(female).mp4', 'female', FALSE, '2025-12-03 23:26:36.717157+00', '1. Sit with your back supported, core engaged, feet flat on the floor. 2. Move into the stretch position for Seated Lower Trunk Lateral Flexor Stretch. 3. Ease into the stretch until you feel gentle tension (not pain). 4. Hold for 20-30 seconds, breathing deeply and relaxing into the stretch.', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 1, NULL, 1, 1, NULL, 3, 'Seated', NULL, NULL, NULL, 1, 1, NULL, 1, NULL, TRUE, NULL, 'Stretch', 42, 2, 6, FALSE, TRUE, 'stretch_general', 'Seated Lower Trunk Lateral Flexor Stretch', 'stretch_hip, stretch_back', FALSE, 'bodyweight', TRUE, 1, 30, 2, 70, 88, 95, 65),
('4b705b1c-f5ac-47ef-9ddf-0276221f07d9', 'Lying Leg Abduction', 'Legs', 'Bodyweight', '{"Quads"}'::text[], '{"Glutes","Hamstrings"}'::text[], 'Build leg strength with this movement movement focusing on your glute med/abductors. The lying position provides back support and helps isolate the target muscles. This bodyweight exercise requires no equipment and can be done anywhere. Strong legs are the foundation for athletic performance and functional fitness.', '65881201', '65881201-Lying-Leg-Abduction-(male)_Hips_.mp4', 'male', FALSE, '2025-12-03 23:26:21.109351+00', '1. Lie down in the appropriate position for Lying Leg Abduction. 2. Set up in the starting position for Lying Leg Abduction. 3. Execute the movement with proper form, focusing on your glute med/abductors. 4. Control both the lifting and lowering phases of the movement. 5. Continue for your target rep count, maintaining good form throughout. Exhale during the exertion phase of the movement.', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 2, NULL, 7, 7, NULL, 5, 'Lying', NULL, NULL, NULL, 8, 12, NULL, 6, NULL, TRUE, NULL, 'Strength', 50, 7, 8, TRUE, TRUE, 'hip_abduction', 'Lying Leg Abduction', 'squat, lunge, leg_press', FALSE, 'bodyweight', FALSE, 3, 90, 4, 70, 88, 95, 65),
('4b805ea2-96b5-4335-8174-6f95e7b4ade4', 'Forward Arms Plank', 'Core', 'Bodyweight', '{"Abs"}'::text[], '{"Shoulders","Lower Back"}'::text[], 'The Forward Arms Plank is a core stabilization exercise that primarily targets your abs. Your shoulders, lower back work as secondary movers, adding to the training stimulus. No equipment needed—your body provides all the resistance. Core strength is foundational for athletic performance and injury prevention.', '66601201', '66601201-Forward-Arms-Plank-(male)_Waist_.mp4', 'male', FALSE, '2025-12-03 23:26:23.056255+00', '1. Hold your body in a straight line from head to heels. 2. Don''t let your hips sag or pike up—engage your core and glutes. 3. Breathe steadily while maintaining the position. 4. Repeat for the prescribed number of repetitions. Engage your stabilizer muscles for better control.', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 2, NULL, 7, 7, NULL, 5, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 8, 12, NULL, 6, NULL, TRUE, NULL, 'Strength', 70, 7, 8, TRUE, TRUE, 'plank', 'Forward Arms Plank', 'side_plank, dead_bug, hollow_hold', TRUE, 'bodyweight', TRUE, 3, 90, 4, 70, 88, 95, 65),
('4b8d3e4d-6284-44ff-b461-b3de6f0b7c25', 'Linear Delt Row (Machine)', 'Back', 'Machine', '{"Upper Back"}'::text[], '{"Lats","Biceps","Rear Delts"}'::text[], 'This rowing exercise strengthens the muscles between your shoulder blades. You''ll also feel your biceps, rear delts working to support the movement. Machine exercises are great for isolating muscles and training to failure safely. A strong back improves posture, prevents injury, and balances pressing movements. Perfect for including in both strength and hypertrophy programs.', '96891201', '96891201-Lever-Linear-Delt-Row-(male)_Back_.mp4', 'male', FALSE, '2025-12-03 23:26:22.644637+00', '1. Adjust the machine settings (seat height, weight, pads) to fit your body for Lever Linear Delt Row. 2. Pull the weight toward your torso, leading with your elbow(s). 3. Squeeze your shoulder blades together at the peak contraction. 4. Extend back out with control, feeling the stretch in your back. 5. Complete all reps with control before resting.', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 1, NULL, 10, 10, NULL, 4, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 5, 8, NULL, 8, NULL, FALSE, NULL, 'Strength', 78, 7, 9, TRUE, FALSE, 'shoulder_exercise', 'Lever Linear Delt Row', 'squat, bench_press, deadlift', TRUE, 'machine', FALSE, 4, 120, 4, 80, 75, 20, 88),
('4b94735b-c17e-4364-abab-6ce593375a37', 'Leg Length Test', 'Full Body', 'Bodyweight', '{"Full Body"}'::text[], '{}'::text[], 'This stretch specifically works on your full body, promoting flexibility and reducing muscle tightness. Include this in your routine for better mobility and reduced muscle tension. Aim for full range of motion on every rep. Listen to your body and adjust intensity as needed.', '67891201', '67891201-Leg-Length-Test-(female)_Stretching_.mp4', 'female', FALSE, '2025-12-03 23:26:34.603963+00', '1. Move into the stretch position for Leg Length Test. 2. Ease into the stretch until you feel gentle tension (not pain). 3. Hold for 20-30 seconds, breathing deeply and relaxing into the stretch.', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 2, NULL, 7, 7, NULL, 5, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 8, 12, NULL, 6, NULL, TRUE, NULL, 'Strength', 50, 7, 8, TRUE, TRUE, 'leg_exercise', 'Leg Length Test', 'squat, lunge, leg_press', FALSE, 'bodyweight', FALSE, 3, 90, 4, 70, 88, 95, 65),
('4ba38b5c-0551-462f-a2fd-770f2503fd34', 'Clean And Press (Kettlebell)', 'Full Body', 'Kettlebell', '{"Full Body"}'::text[], '{"Shoulders","Quads","Hamstrings"}'::text[], 'Develop functional strength with the Kettlebell Clean And Press, a comprehensive pressing exercise. Secondary activation of your shoulders, legs provides additional muscle engagement. Kettlebells are excellent for building functional, real-world strength. Full body exercises are time-efficient and build functional, real-world strength.', '58551201', '58551201-Kettlebell-Clean-and-Press_Weightlifting_.mp4', 'male', FALSE, '2025-12-03 23:26:29.971345+00', '1. Select an appropriately weighted kettlebell for Kettlebell Clean And Press. 2. Execute the pressing motion for Kettlebell Clean And Press, extending through the target muscles. 3. Continue for your target rep count, maintaining good form throughout.', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 3, NULL, 7, 7, NULL, 5, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 8, 12, NULL, 6, NULL, TRUE, NULL, 'Strength', 78, 7, 8, TRUE, TRUE, 'clean', 'Clean And Press', 'squat, bench_press, deadlift', FALSE, 'kettlebell', FALSE, 3, 90, 4, 75, 88, 88, 78),
('4ba90dca-7a13-442f-8c90-89f2c54a8641', 'Negative Biceps Leg Concentration Curl', 'Arms', 'Bodyweight', '{"Biceps"}'::text[], '{"Forearms"}'::text[], 'The Negative Biceps Leg Concentration Curl is a curling exercise that isolates your biceps. You''ll also feel your forearms working to support the movement. This bodyweight exercise requires no equipment and can be done anywhere. Arm strength supports grip, pulling, and pushing in compound movements.', '80841201', '80841201-Negative-Biceps-Leg-Concentration-Curl-(female)_Up.mp4', 'female', FALSE, '2025-12-03 23:26:35.532804+00', '1. Curl your heels toward your glutes by bending at the knees. 2. Squeeze your hamstrings at peak contraction. 3. Extend legs back out with control. 4. Focus on a slow, controlled lowering phase (3-5 seconds). 5. Repeat for the prescribed number of repetitions.', 'Curl', 'Pull', NULL, NULL, NULL, 2, NULL, 5, 7, NULL, 6, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 10, 15, NULL, 4, NULL, TRUE, NULL, 'Strength', 80, 5, 7, FALSE, TRUE, 'concentration_curl', 'Negative Biceps Leg Concentration Curl', 'tricep_pushdown, tricep_extension, bicep_curl, hammer_curl', FALSE, 'bodyweight', FALSE, 3, 60, 2, 70, 88, 95, 65),
('4bb248fd-cfb1-4810-b741-ebe72e308168', 'Curl - Reverse Grip (EZ Bar)', 'Arms', 'EZ Bar', '{"Forearms"}'::text[], '{"Biceps"}'::text[], 'Build bigger biceps with this curling movement that targets the front of your arms. Your forearms work as secondary movers, adding to the training stimulus. The barbell allows you to handle heavier loads for maximum strength gains. Dedicated arm training builds both strength and muscular definition.', '4511201', '04511201-EZ-Barbell-Reverse-Grip-Curl_Forearms.mp4', 'male', FALSE, '2025-12-03 23:26:20.392006+00', '1. Grip a barbell with hands at the appropriate width for EZ Barbell Reverse Grip Curl. 2. Use a reverse grip (opposite of the standard grip for this exercise). 3. Keep your elbows in a fixed position throughout the movement. 4. Curl the weight up by contracting your biceps, squeezing at the top. 5. Lower with control, resisting the weight on the way down. 6. Continue for your target rep count, maintaining good form throughout. Keep your shoulders relaxed and away from your ears.', 'Curl', 'Pull', NULL, NULL, NULL, 3, NULL, 5, 7, NULL, 6, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 10, 15, NULL, 4, NULL, TRUE, NULL, 'Strength', 82, 5, 7, FALSE, TRUE, 'general_exercise', 'EZ Curl - Reverse Grip', 'EZ Curl - Reverse Grip', FALSE, 'ez_bar', FALSE, 3, 60, 2, 95, 80, 65, 95),
('4bbf5e4d-6a0e-4f61-904e-9802f64ada28', 'Incline Twisting Sit Up', 'Core', 'Bodyweight, Decline Bench', '{"Abs"}'::text[], '{}'::text[], 'The Incline Twisting Sit Up targets your obliques through a twisting motion, building rotational core strength. The hip flexors assist throughout the movement, making this a well-rounded exercise. Using an incline changes the angle of resistance for varied muscle recruitment. Building core stability helps with everything from heavy deadlifts to daily activities.', '11901201', '11901201-Incline-Twisting-Sit-up-(version-2)_Waist-FIX_.mp4', 'male', FALSE, '2025-12-03 23:26:25.87243+00', '1. Rotate your torso through the movement pattern for Incline Twisting Sit Up. 2. Control the rotation in both directions—avoid using momentum. 3. Complete all reps with control before resting.', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 2, NULL, 5, 7, NULL, 6, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 10, 15, NULL, 4, NULL, TRUE, NULL, 'Strength', 65, 5, 7, FALSE, TRUE, 'crunch', 'Incline Twisting Sit Up', 'leg_raise, plank, russian_twist, v_up', FALSE, 'bodyweight', FALSE, 3, 60, 2, 70, 88, 95, 65),
('4bc7f0d5-0e7e-4881-82f0-96e10553caff', 'Bird Dog Male', 'Core', 'Bodyweight', '{"Core"}'::text[], '{"Lower Back","Glutes"}'::text[], 'The Bird Dog Male is a movement exercise that develops back strength and muscle. You''ll also feel your glutes, abs working to support the movement. This bodyweight exercise requires no equipment and can be done anywhere. Back development is crucial for pulling strength and overall upper body function.', '12411201', '12411201-Bird-Dog-male_Back.mp4', 'male', FALSE, '2025-12-03 23:26:21.109351+00', '1. Set up in the starting position for Bird Dog Male. 2. Execute the movement with proper form, focusing on your lower back. 3. Control both the lifting and lowering phases of the movement. 4. Repeat for the prescribed number of repetitions.', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 2, NULL, 7, 7, NULL, 5, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 8, 12, NULL, 6, NULL, TRUE, NULL, 'Strength', 50, 7, 8, TRUE, TRUE, 'bird_dog', 'Bird Dog Male', 'dead_bug, plank, back_extension', TRUE, 'bodyweight', FALSE, 3, 90, 4, 70, 88, 95, 65),
('4bd2591a-0756-402f-8375-6e1db2d88073', 'Standing Hands On Shoulder Raise And Elbow Touch', 'Core', 'Bodyweight', '{"Abs"}'::text[], '{"Hip Flexors"}'::text[], 'This raising exercise engages your abs for improved core stability and strength. Secondary activation of your obliques provides additional muscle engagement. Performing this standing challenges your balance and core engagement. No equipment needed—your body provides all the resistance. Building core stability helps with everything from heavy deadlifts to daily activities.', '95571201', '95571201-Standing-Hands-On-Shoulder-Raise-And-Elbow-Touch-(.mp4', 'female', FALSE, '2025-12-03 23:26:38.7451+00', '1. Begin in a standing position with good posture. 2. Raise the weight in the prescribed direction for Standing Hands On Shoulder Raise And Elbow Touch (. 3. Lower with control, maintaining tension throughout. 4. Continue for your target rep count, maintaining good form throughout. Keep the movement smooth and controlled.', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 2, NULL, 5, 7, NULL, 6, 'Standing', NULL, NULL, NULL, 10, 15, NULL, 4, NULL, TRUE, NULL, 'Strength', 72, 5, 7, FALSE, TRUE, 'shoulder_exercise', 'Standing Hands On Shoulder Raise And Elbow Touch (', 'lateral_raise, shoulder_press, front_raise', FALSE, 'bodyweight', FALSE, 3, 60, 2, 70, 88, 95, 65),
('4bd2aa35-5caa-475c-939a-81b693e8a585', 'Forearms To Wall Push Up - Wide Grip (Wall)', 'Chest', 'Wall', '{"Chest"}'::text[], '{"Triceps","Front Delts"}'::text[], 'Build a stronger chest with this pushing movement that develops pressing power. Your triceps, front delts work as secondary movers, adding to the training stimulus. A well-developed chest contributes to upper body strength and aesthetics.', '69001201', '69001201-Forearms-to-Wide-Grip-Wall-Push-up-(male)_Chest_.mp4', 'male', FALSE, '2025-12-03 23:26:22.247914+00', '1. Position yourself at the appropriate distance from a wall. 2. Keep your body in a straight line from head to heels throughout. 3. Lower your chest toward the floor by bending your elbows. 4. Push through your palms to return to the starting position. 5. Complete all reps with control before resting. Keep the movement smooth and controlled.', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 1, NULL, 7, 7, NULL, 5, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 8, 12, NULL, 6, NULL, TRUE, NULL, 'Strength', 62, 7, 8, TRUE, TRUE, 'push_up', 'Forearms To Wall Push Up - Wide Grip', 'Forearms To Wall Push Up - Wide Grip', TRUE, 'bodyweight', FALSE, 3, 90, 4, 70, 88, 95, 65),
('4bdbc174-7146-4b92-9bbc-cb324a11271e', 'Walking Knee Raise On Spot', 'Core', 'Bodyweight', '{"Lower Abs"}'::text[], '{"Hip Flexors"}'::text[], 'Build power and athleticism with this high-intensity raising exercise that challenges your entire body. The hip flexors assist throughout the movement, making this a well-rounded exercise. This bodyweight exercise requires no equipment and can be done anywhere. Plyometric training builds explosive power that transfers to sports and daily activities.', '92511201', '92511201-Walking-Knee-Raise-On-Spot-(front-POV)-(female)_Pl.mp4', 'female', FALSE, '2025-12-03 23:26:39.91585+00', '1. Raise the weight in front of you to shoulder height. 2. Lower with control, maintaining tension throughout. 3. Repeat for the prescribed number of repetitions. Ensure full range of motion on each rep.', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 2, NULL, 5, 7, NULL, 6, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 10, 15, NULL, 4, NULL, TRUE, NULL, 'Cardio', 70, 5, 7, FALSE, TRUE, 'leg_raise', 'Walking Knee Raise On Spot', 'crunch, plank, v_up', FALSE, 'bodyweight', FALSE, 3, 60, 2, 70, 88, 95, 65),
('4bdc62cd-edcd-4685-befc-ce3fae64dab5', 'Double Swing (Kettlebell)', 'Full Body', 'Kettlebell', '{"Full Body"}'::text[], '{"Glutes","Core"}'::text[], 'Build leg strength with this swinging movement focusing on your full body. The glutes, core assist throughout the movement, making this a well-rounded exercise. The kettlebell grip position adds a unique training stimulus. Lower body strength improves everything from walking to heavy compound lifts.', '98461201', '98461201-Kettlebell-Double-Swing-(male)_Hips_.mp4', 'male', FALSE, '2025-12-03 23:26:28.52454+00', '1. Position two kettlebells for Kettlebell Double Swing. 2. Hinge at your hips, letting the weight swing back between your legs. 3. Explosively drive hips forward, propelling the weight forward/up. 4. Let gravity bring it back as you hinge for the next rep. 5. Complete all reps with control before resting.', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 3, NULL, 7, 7, NULL, 5, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 8, 12, NULL, 6, NULL, TRUE, NULL, 'Strength', 58, 7, 8, TRUE, TRUE, 'general_exercise', 'Double Swing', 'squat, bench_press, deadlift', FALSE, 'kettlebell', FALSE, 3, 90, 4, 75, 88, 88, 78),
('4be04d6e-9383-4535-9492-34d00519383e', 'Shuffle', 'Full Body', 'Bodyweight', '{"Full Body"}'::text[], '{}'::text[], 'This dynamic movement movement gets your heart rate up while developing explosive strength. No equipment needed—your body provides all the resistance. Great for improving athletic performance, burning calories, and building conditioning. Aim for full range of motion on every rep.', '42571201', '42571201-Shuffle_Plyometrics_.mp4', 'male', FALSE, '2025-12-03 23:26:23.987963+00', '1. Set up in the starting position for Shuffle. 2. Execute the movement with proper form, focusing on your full body. 3. Control both the lifting and lowering phases of the movement. 4. Continue for your target rep count, maintaining good form throughout.', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 2, NULL, 5, 4, NULL, 8, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 8, 12, NULL, 7, NULL, TRUE, NULL, 'Plyometrics', 50, 9, 8, TRUE, TRUE, 'shuffle', 'Shuffle', 'squat, bench_press, deadlift', FALSE, 'bodyweight', FALSE, 3, 60, 4, 70, 88, 95, 65),
('4be91df4-2015-404d-97da-2a1d6ecc0de2', 'L Sit (Chair)', 'Core', 'Chair', '{"Abs"}'::text[], '{"Hip Flexors"}'::text[], 'Strengthen your midsection with this movement movement that works your abs. A strong core improves posture, protects your spine, and enhances all other lifts. Perfect for including in both strength and hypertrophy programs.', '72611201', '72611201-L-Sit-on-Chair-(male)_Waist_.mp4', 'male', FALSE, '2025-12-03 23:26:23.689343+00', '1. Position yourself with a sturdy chair for support or as part of the movement. 2. Set up in the starting position for L Sit On Chair. 3. Execute the movement with proper form, focusing on your abs. 4. Control both the lifting and lowering phases of the movement. 5. Repeat for the prescribed number of repetitions.', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 3, NULL, 7, 7, NULL, 5, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 8, 12, NULL, 6, NULL, TRUE, NULL, 'Strength', 35, 7, 8, TRUE, TRUE, 'general_exercise', 'L Sit On Chair', 'squat, bench_press, deadlift', FALSE, 'bodyweight', FALSE, 3, 90, 4, 70, 88, 95, 65),
('4beb372f-3025-4c12-8dff-a2a75ac7cb76', 'Kneeling Forward Palm Nudges', 'Core', 'Bodyweight', '{"Abs"}'::text[], '{"Hip Flexors"}'::text[], 'The Kneeling Forward Palm Nudges is an arm movement exercise targeting your core. The kneeling position adds a core stability challenge. This bodyweight exercise requires no equipment and can be done anywhere. Dedicated arm training builds both strength and muscular definition.', '69741201', '69741201-Kneeling-Forward-Palm-Nudges-(male)_Forearms_.mp4', 'male', FALSE, '2025-12-03 23:26:25.233728+00', '1. Kneel on the floor (use a pad for comfort if needed). 2. Set up in the starting position for Kneeling Forward Palm Nudges. 3. Execute the movement with proper form, focusing on your core. 4. Control both the lifting and lowering phases of the movement. 5. Complete all reps with control before resting.', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 1, NULL, 7, 7, NULL, 5, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 8, 12, NULL, 6, NULL, TRUE, NULL, 'Strength', 50, 7, 8, TRUE, TRUE, 'general_exercise', 'Kneeling Forward Palm Nudges', 'squat, leg_extension, lunge', FALSE, 'bodyweight', FALSE, 3, 90, 4, 70, 88, 95, 65),
('4bf26fa4-9885-4b2f-97df-8842142bff90', 'Seated Hip Sway Cut (Chair)', 'Legs', 'Chair', '{"Quads"}'::text[], '{"Glutes","Hamstrings"}'::text[], 'Build power and athleticism with this high-intensity movement exercise that challenges your entire body. Being seated provides stability, allowing you to focus on the working muscles. Great for improving athletic performance, burning calories, and building conditioning.', '90831201', '90831201-Sitting-Hip-Sway-Cut-on-a-Chair-(female)_Plyometri.mp4', 'female', FALSE, '2025-12-03 23:26:37.756436+00', '1. Position yourself with a sturdy chair for support or as part of the movement. 2. Sit with your back supported, core engaged, feet flat on the floor. 3. Repeat for the prescribed number of repetitions. Exhale during the exertion phase of the movement. Works well for glutes activation.', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 2, NULL, 7, 7, NULL, 5, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 8, 12, NULL, 6, NULL, TRUE, NULL, 'Strength', 35, 7, 8, TRUE, TRUE, 'glute_exercise', 'Seated Hip Sway Cut On A Chair', 'hip_thrust, lunge, squat', FALSE, 'bodyweight', FALSE, 3, 90, 4, 70, 88, 95, 65),
('4bf9fb9a-54ec-4072-ac7e-641e16df7a44', 'Single Leg Calf Stretch', 'Legs', 'Bodyweight', '{"Quads"}'::text[], '{"Glutes","Hamstrings"}'::text[], 'The Single Leg Calve Stretch isolates your calf muscles through a stretching motion. This bodyweight exercise requires no equipment and can be done anywhere. Strong legs are the foundation for athletic performance and functional fitness.', '49311201', '49311201-Single-Leg-Calve-Stretch-(female)_Calves_.mp4', 'female', FALSE, '2025-12-03 23:26:37.429219+00', '1. Complete all reps on one side, then switch to the other side. 2. Set up in the starting position for Single Leg Calve Stretch. 3. Execute the movement with proper form, focusing on your calves. 4. Control both the lifting and lowering phases of the movement. 5. Repeat for the prescribed number of repetitions.', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 1, NULL, 1, 1, NULL, 3, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 1, 1, NULL, 1, NULL, TRUE, NULL, 'Stretch', 35, 2, 6, FALSE, TRUE, 'stretch_general', 'Single Leg Calf Stretch', 'stretch_hip, stretch_back, stretch_shoulder', FALSE, 'bodyweight', TRUE, 1, 30, 2, 70, 88, 95, 65),
('4c094e6b-8087-4ace-a946-4b676a688188', 'Incline Bicep Curl - (Dumbbell)', 'Arms', 'Dumbbells, Incline Bench', '{"Biceps"}'::text[], '{"Forearms"}'::text[], 'This curling exercise focuses on your biceps for improved arm size and strength. The forearms assist throughout the movement, making this a well-rounded exercise. Using an incline changes the angle of resistance for varied muscle recruitment. The dumbbell variation provides freedom of movement and greater range of motion. Arm strength supports grip, pulling, and pushing in compound movements.', '24931201', '24931201-Dumbbell-Incline-Biceps-Curl-(female)_Upper-Arms.mp4', 'female', FALSE, '2025-12-03 23:26:32.735372+00', '1. Select a pair of dumbbells at an appropriate weight for Dumbbell Incline Biceps Curl. 2. Keep your elbows in a fixed position throughout the movement. 3. Curl the weight up by contracting your biceps, squeezing at the top. 4. Lower with control, resisting the weight on the way down. 5. Complete all reps with control before resting. Start with lighter weight to perfect your form.', 'Curl', 'Pull', NULL, NULL, NULL, 2, NULL, 5, 7, NULL, 6, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 10, 15, NULL, 4, NULL, TRUE, NULL, 'Strength', 95, 5, 7, FALSE, TRUE, 'bicep_curl', 'Incline Biceps Curl', 'hammer_curl, preacher_curl, cable_curl', TRUE, 'dumbbell', FALSE, 3, 60, 2, 92, 90, 92, 90),
('4c0afee6-f8ee-43a1-83bb-426b0fac23fc', 'Half Plyo Forward To Top Arms Raise', 'Full Body', 'Bodyweight', '{"Full Body"}'::text[], '{"Quads","Hamstrings"}'::text[], 'This dynamic raising movement gets your heart rate up while developing explosive strength. You''ll also feel your shoulders working to support the movement. A versatile bodyweight movement perfect for home or gym training. Develops fast-twitch muscle fibers for quicker, more powerful movements.', '71871201', '71871201-Half-Plyo-Forward-To-Top-Arms-Raise-(female)_Plyom.mp4', 'female', FALSE, '2025-12-03 23:26:33.778367+00', '1. Raise the weight in the prescribed direction for Half Plyo Forward To Top Arms Raise. 2. Lower with control, maintaining tension throughout. 3. Continue for your target rep count, maintaining good form throughout.', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 3, NULL, 5, 4, NULL, 8, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 8, 12, NULL, 7, NULL, TRUE, NULL, 'Plyometrics', 70, 9, 8, TRUE, TRUE, 'arm_exercise', 'Half Plyo Forward To Top Arms Raise', 'shoulder_press, lateral_raise, front_raise', FALSE, 'bodyweight', FALSE, 3, 60, 4, 70, 88, 95, 65),
('4c260740-b6f4-4708-b48b-d959f605445c', 'Incline Breeding (Dumbbell)', 'Chest', 'Dumbbells', '{"Chest"}'::text[], '{}'::text[], 'This movement exercise focuses on your pectorals for improved chest strength and development. The incline angle shifts emphasis toward the upper portion of the target muscles. Dumbbells allow each arm to work independently, helping correct imbalances. Chest strength improves pushing power for sports, daily tasks, and other lifts.', '101701201', '101701201-Dumbbell-Incline-Breeding-(female)_Chest_.mp4', 'female', FALSE, '2025-12-03 23:26:32.914483+00', '1. Select a pair of dumbbells at an appropriate weight for Dumbbell Incline Breeding. 2. Set up in the starting position for Dumbbell Incline Breeding. 3. Execute the movement with proper form, focusing on your chest. 4. Control both the lifting and lowering phases of the movement. 5. Complete all reps with control before resting. Keep your core engaged for stability.', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 2, NULL, 7, 8, NULL, 5, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 8, 12, NULL, 6, NULL, TRUE, NULL, 'Strength', 65, 7, 8, TRUE, TRUE, 'general_exercise', 'Incline Breeding', 'squat, bench_press, deadlift', TRUE, 'dumbbell', FALSE, 3, 90, 4, 92, 90, 92, 90),
('4c2bbd88-994d-4f3a-9f68-6f541604bbbc', 'Single Leg Hip Extension Supported (Chair)', 'Legs', 'Chair', '{"Glutes"}'::text[], '{"Hamstrings"}'::text[], 'This extension exercise isolates your glutes for improved hip strength and power. Your hamstrings work as secondary movers, adding to the training stimulus. Leg training boosts metabolism and builds functional, real-world strength.', '104721201', '104721201-Single-Leg-Hip-Extension-with-Chair-Supported-(ma.mp4', 'male', FALSE, '2025-12-03 23:26:29.242428+00', '1. Position yourself with a sturdy chair for support or as part of the movement. 2. Extend your legs until straight, squeezing your quads at the top. 3. Lower with control back to the starting position. 4. Complete all reps on one side, then switch to the other side. 5. Continue for your target rep count, maintaining good form throughout.', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 2, NULL, 5, 7, NULL, 6, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 10, 15, NULL, 4, NULL, TRUE, NULL, 'Strength', 50, 5, 7, FALSE, TRUE, 'glute_kickback', 'Single Leg Hip Extension With Chair Supported', 'leg_curl, squat, leg_press, lunge', FALSE, 'bodyweight', FALSE, 3, 60, 2, 70, 88, 95, 65),
('4c326704-91d7-4dc3-b00a-58342417372d', 'Seated Neck Rotation Stretch', 'Neck', 'Bodyweight', '{"Neck"}'::text[], '{"Traps"}'::text[], 'Target your neck with this rotation stretch that helps restore range of motion. Being seated provides stability, allowing you to focus on the working muscles. Include this in your routine for better mobility and reduced muscle tension.', '100111201', '100111201-Sitting-Neck-Rotation-Stretch-(female)_Neck_.mp4', 'female', FALSE, '2025-12-03 23:26:37.756436+00', '1. Sit with your back supported, core engaged, feet flat on the floor. 2. Rotate your torso through the movement pattern for Seated Neck Rotation Stretch. 3. Control the rotation in both directions—avoid using momentum.', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 1, NULL, 1, 1, NULL, 3, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 1, 1, NULL, 1, NULL, TRUE, NULL, 'Stretch', 40, 2, 6, FALSE, TRUE, 'neck_stretch', 'Seated Neck Rotation Stretch', 'stretch_hip, stretch_back', FALSE, 'bodyweight', TRUE, 1, 30, 2, 70, 88, 95, 65),
('4c36ca20-7fa4-4b72-800e-2a4861c30e55', 'Criss Cross Arms Prayer Push', 'Chest', 'Bodyweight', '{"Chest"}'::text[], '{}'::text[], 'This pushing exercise focuses on your pectorals for improved chest strength and development. A versatile bodyweight movement perfect for home or gym training. A well-developed chest contributes to upper body strength and aesthetics. Excellent for pre-exhausting the target muscle before compound lifts.', '88131201', '88131201-Criss-Cross-Arms-Prayer-Push-(female)_Chest_.mp4', 'female', FALSE, '2025-12-03 23:26:32.374165+00', '1. Set up in the starting position for Criss Cross Arms Prayer Push. 2. Execute the movement with proper form, focusing on your chest. 3. Control both the lifting and lowering phases of the movement. 4. Continue for your target rep count, maintaining good form throughout.', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 2, NULL, 7, 7, NULL, 5, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 8, 12, NULL, 6, NULL, TRUE, NULL, 'Strength', 35, 7, 8, TRUE, TRUE, 'boxing', 'Criss Cross Arms Prayer Push', 'bicep_curl, tricep_extension, hammer_curl', FALSE, 'bodyweight', FALSE, 3, 90, 4, 70, 88, 95, 65),
('4c5e0b0c-818d-484a-ad73-33c5559d54e7', 'Celebratory Knee Drives - Alternating', 'Full Body', 'Bodyweight', '{"Full Body"}'::text[], '{}'::text[], 'A challenging plyometric exercise, the Alternating Celebratory Knee Drives builds reactive power and improves conditioning. The hip flexors assist throughout the movement, making this a well-rounded exercise. No equipment needed—your body provides all the resistance. Great for improving athletic performance, burning calories, and building conditioning.', '93741201', '93741201-Alternating-Celebratory-Knee-Drives-(female)_Plyom.mp4', 'female', FALSE, '2025-12-03 23:26:30.412523+00', '1. Alternate between sides/arms/legs with each repetition. 2. Set up in the starting position for Alternating Celebratory Knee Drives. 3. Execute the movement with proper form, focusing on your full body. 4. Control both the lifting and lowering phases of the movement. 5. Complete all reps with control before resting.', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 2, NULL, 7, 7, NULL, 5, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 8, 12, NULL, 6, NULL, TRUE, NULL, 'Strength', 50, 7, 8, TRUE, TRUE, 'knee_drive', 'Celebratory Knee Drives - Alternating', 'butt_kicks, jumping_jack, mountain_climber', FALSE, 'bodyweight', FALSE, 3, 90, 4, 70, 88, 95, 65),
('4c5ef365-a898-478e-a838-9cef0a225f0f', 'Bent Over Row (Band)', 'Back', 'Resistance Band, Anchor Point', '{"Back","Lats"}'::text[], '{"Biceps","Rear Delts"}'::text[], 'The Band Bent Over Row is a rowing exercise that builds thickness in your upper back. Your biceps, lats work as secondary movers, adding to the training stimulus. The bent over position requires core engagement to maintain a neutral spine. Bands are joint-friendly and portable, perfect for any training environment. Back development is crucial for pulling strength and overall upper body function.', '8921201', '08921201-Band-Bent-over-Row-(female)_Back.mp4', 'female', FALSE, '2025-12-03 23:26:30.685158+00', '1. Secure the resistance band appropriately for Band Bent Over Row. 2. Hinge at your hips, pushing them back while keeping your back flat. 3. Pull the weight toward your torso, leading with your elbow(s). 4. Squeeze your shoulder blades together at the peak contraction. 5. Extend back out with control, feeling the stretch in your back. 6. Repeat for the prescribed number of repetitions.', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 3, NULL, 7, 7, NULL, 5, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 8, 12, NULL, 6, NULL, TRUE, NULL, 'Strength', 75, 7, 8, TRUE, TRUE, 'bent_over_row', 'Bent Over Row', 'cable_row, dumbbell_row, t_bar_row, lat_pulldown', FALSE, 'band', FALSE, 3, 90, 4, 60, 85, 90, 50),
('4c5fe974-c622-4d71-bc70-62c896f00339', 'Side Shuffle High Knee', 'Legs', 'Bodyweight', '{"Hip Flexors"}'::text[], '{"Quads","Calves"}'::text[], 'This dynamic movement movement gets your heart rate up while developing explosive strength. Your hip flexors work as secondary movers, adding to the training stimulus. No equipment needed—your body provides all the resistance. Plyometric training builds explosive power that transfers to sports and daily activities.', '71541201', '71541201-Side-Shuffle-High-Knee-(male)_Plyometrics_.mp4', 'male', FALSE, '2025-12-03 23:26:27.384461+00', '1. Set up in the starting position for Side Shuffle High Knee. 2. Execute the movement with proper form, focusing on your full body. 3. Control both the lifting and lowering phases of the movement. 4. Continue for your target rep count, maintaining good form throughout.', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 2, NULL, 5, 4, NULL, 8, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 8, 12, NULL, 7, NULL, TRUE, NULL, 'Plyometrics', 50, 9, 8, TRUE, TRUE, 'high_knees', 'Side Shuffle High Knee', 'butt_kicks, jumping_jack, mountain_climber', FALSE, 'bodyweight', FALSE, 3, 60, 4, 70, 88, 95, 65),
('4c776bdc-fcb4-4c9a-8772-66e90e55152b', 'Duck And Forward Punches', 'Full Body', 'Bodyweight', '{"Full Body"}'::text[], '{"Shoulders"}'::text[], 'This dynamic movement movement gets your heart rate up while developing explosive strength. Your shoulders work as secondary movers, adding to the training stimulus. No equipment needed—your body provides all the resistance. Great for improving athletic performance, burning calories, and building conditioning.', '76431201', '76431201-Duck-and-Forward-Punches-(male)_Plyometrics_.mp4', 'male', FALSE, '2025-12-03 23:26:26.678791+00', '1. Set up in the starting position for Duck And Forward Punches. 2. Execute the movement with proper form, focusing on your full body. 3. Control both the lifting and lowering phases of the movement. 4. Continue for your target rep count, maintaining good form throughout.', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 2, NULL, 7, 7, NULL, 5, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 8, 12, NULL, 6, NULL, TRUE, NULL, 'Strength', 50, 7, 8, TRUE, TRUE, 'boxing', 'Duck And Forward Punches', 'core_exercise, shoulder_exercise, burpee', FALSE, 'bodyweight', FALSE, 3, 90, 4, 70, 88, 95, 65),
('4c7cb666-98ec-4934-b88b-9d49cf90a058', 'Face Pull (Band)', 'Shoulders', 'Resistance Band, Anchor Point', '{"Rear Delts"}'::text[], '{"Upper Back","Rotator Cuff"}'::text[], 'Build stronger shoulders with this pulling movement focusing on your delts. Your upper back, rotator cuff work as secondary movers, adding to the training stimulus. Resistance bands provide accommodating resistance that increases through the range of motion. Strong shoulders improve overhead strength and support nearly all upper body movements.', '8961201', '08961201-Band-face-pull_Shoulders.mp4', 'female', FALSE, '2025-12-03 23:26:30.685158+00', '1. Secure the resistance band appropriately for Band Face Pull. 2. Pull the rope toward your face, separating your hands as you pull. 3. Squeeze your rear delts and upper back at peak contraction. 4. Return with control, maintaining cable tension. 5. Repeat for the prescribed number of repetitions.', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 2, NULL, 7, 7, NULL, 5, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 8, 12, NULL, 6, NULL, TRUE, NULL, 'Strength', 85, 7, 8, TRUE, TRUE, 'face_pull', 'Face Pull', 'rear_delt_fly, bent_over_row, lateral_raise', FALSE, 'band', FALSE, 3, 90, 4, 60, 85, 90, 50),
('4c80d2b3-3449-4f5b-8b2d-bd6cda7d4ddd', 'Bent Over Reverse Raise - Skier (Dumbbell)', 'Shoulders', 'Dumbbells', '{"Shoulders"}'::text[], '{"Traps"}'::text[], 'The Dumbbell Bent Over Reverse Raise (skier) is a raising exercise that targets your delts for shoulder development. Bending over allows gravity to provide resistance in a different plane. Dumbbells allow each arm to work independently, helping correct imbalances. Strong shoulders improve overhead strength and support nearly all upper body movements.', '66111201', '66111201-Dumbbell-Bent-Over-Reverse-Raise-(skier)-(male)_Shoulders_.mp4', 'male', FALSE, '2025-12-03 23:26:24.099303+00', '1. Select a pair of dumbbells at an appropriate weight for Dumbbell Bent Over Reverse Raise. 2. Hinge at your hips, pushing them back while keeping your back flat. 3. Raise the weight in the prescribed direction for Dumbbell Bent Over Reverse Raise. 4. Lower with control, maintaining tension throughout. 5. Repeat for the prescribed number of repetitions.', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 2, NULL, 5, 7, NULL, 6, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 10, 15, NULL, 4, NULL, TRUE, NULL, 'Strength', 74, 5, 7, FALSE, TRUE, 'general_exercise', 'Bent Over Reverse Raise', 'squat, bench_press, deadlift', TRUE, 'dumbbell', FALSE, 3, 60, 2, 92, 90, 92, 90),
('4c8c357a-8aec-401a-968a-dbd0d11748c2', 'Reverse Crunch (TRX)', 'Core', 'TRX', '{"Abs"}'::text[], '{"Hip Flexors"}'::text[], 'This crunching exercise engages your abs for improved core stability and strength. Secondary activation of your hip flexors provides additional muscle engagement. Suspension training adds instability, increasing core activation throughout. Core strength is foundational for athletic performance and injury prevention.', '8071201', '08071201-Suspender-Reverse-Crunch_Waist_.mp4', 'male', FALSE, '2025-12-03 23:26:24.698781+00', '1. Adjust the TRX/suspension straps to the appropriate length for Suspender Reverse Crunch. 2. Lift your hips off the floor by contracting your lower abs. 3. Bring your knees toward your chest, then lower with control. 4. Complete all reps with control before resting.', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 2, NULL, 5, 7, NULL, 6, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 12, 20, NULL, 4, NULL, TRUE, NULL, 'Strength', 60, 5, 7, FALSE, TRUE, 'crunch', 'Suspender Reverse Crunch', 'leg_raise, plank, russian_twist, v_up', FALSE, 'trx', FALSE, 3, 60, 2, 68, 85, 85, 70),
('4c8d2c89-e049-47b3-bb73-6227a056a775', 'Hamstring Curl With Punches (Gymnastic Rings) - Alternating', 'Legs', 'Gymnastic Rings', '{"Hamstrings"}'::text[], '{"Glutes"}'::text[], 'Build power and athleticism with this high-intensity curling exercise that challenges your entire body. Secondary activation of your forearms provides additional muscle engagement. Plyometric training builds explosive power that transfers to sports and daily activities.', '54851201', '54851201-Alternating-Hamstring-Curl-with-Punche-(female)_Pl.mp4', 'female', FALSE, '2025-12-03 23:26:30.54809+00', '1. Keep your elbows in a fixed position throughout the movement. 2. Curl the weight up by contracting your biceps, squeezing at the top. 3. Lower with control, resisting the weight on the way down. 4. Continue for your target rep count, maintaining good form throughout. Keep your shoulders relaxed and away from your ears.', NULL, NULL, 'Compound', 'Bilateral (Alternating)', NULL, 2, NULL, 5, 7, NULL, 6, 'Standing', NULL, NULL, NULL, 10, 15, NULL, 4, NULL, TRUE, NULL, 'Strength', 58, 5, 7, FALSE, TRUE, 'leg_curl', 'Hamstring Curl With Punches - Alternating', 'romanian_deadlift, hip_thrust', FALSE, 'gymnastic_rings', FALSE, 3, 60, 2, 68, 85, 85, 70),
('4c95f1d3-b7cd-4cc8-bd9b-67feedf4a097', 'Run And Hop', 'Legs', 'Bodyweight', '{"Quads"}'::text[], '{"Glutes","Calves"}'::text[], 'Build your aerobic capacity with this steady-state cardio movement. Regular cardio training builds the aerobic base for better overall fitness. Can be modified for beginners or progressed for advanced athletes.', '32691201', '32691201-Run-and-Hop-(female)_Cardio.mp4', 'female', FALSE, '2025-12-03 23:26:36.581585+00', '1. Set up in the starting position for Run And Hop. 2. Execute the movement with proper form, focusing on your cardio. 3. Control both the lifting and lowering phases of the movement. 4. Repeat for the prescribed number of repetitions.', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 2, NULL, 5, 4, NULL, 8, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 8, 12, NULL, 7, NULL, TRUE, NULL, 'Plyometrics', 50, 9, 8, TRUE, TRUE, 'hop', 'Run And Hop', 'cycling, rowing_cardio, jump_rope', FALSE, 'bodyweight', FALSE, 3, 60, 4, 70, 88, 95, 65),
('4c9883c2-a645-4f53-8917-1d7b6c068f00', 'Quadruped Hip Extension To Abduction', 'Legs', 'Bodyweight', '{"Glutes"}'::text[], '{"Hamstrings"}'::text[], 'Build leg strength with this extension movement focusing on your glute med/abductors. Your hamstrings work as secondary movers, adding to the training stimulus. This bodyweight exercise requires no equipment and can be done anywhere. Leg training boosts metabolism and builds functional, real-world strength.', '82571201', '82571201-Quadruped-Hip-Extension-to-Abduction-(female)_Hips.mp4', 'female', FALSE, '2025-12-03 23:26:35.936279+00', '1. Extend through the target joint(s) for Quadruped Hip Extension To Abduction. 2. Set up in the starting position for Quadruped Hip Extension To Abduction. 3. Execute the movement with proper form, focusing on your glute med/abductors. 4. Control both the lifting and lowering phases of the movement. 5. Continue for your target rep count, maintaining good form throughout.', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 1, NULL, 5, 7, NULL, 6, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 12, 20, NULL, 4, NULL, TRUE, NULL, 'Strength', 70, 5, 7, FALSE, TRUE, 'glute_kickback', 'Quadruped Hip Extension To Abduction', 'leg_curl, squat, leg_press, lunge', FALSE, 'bodyweight', FALSE, 3, 60, 2, 70, 88, 95, 65),
('4c9aa347-b8ba-453d-9c61-44fc03ce5b9a', 'Standing Scapular External Rotation Hold', 'Shoulders', 'Bodyweight', '{"Rotator Cuff"}'::text[], '{"Shoulders"}'::text[], 'The Standing Scapular External Rotation Hold is a rotation exercise that targets your rotator cuff for shoulder development. Performing this standing challenges your balance and core engagement. This bodyweight exercise requires no equipment and can be done anywhere. Strong shoulders improve overhead strength and support nearly all upper body movements.', '77921201', '77921201-Standing-Scapular-External-Rotation-Hold-(female)_.mp4', 'female', FALSE, '2025-12-03 23:26:38.870314+00', '1. Stand with feet about shoulder-width apart. 2. Rotate your torso through the movement pattern for Standing Scapular External Rotation Hold. 3. Control the rotation in both directions—avoid using momentum. 4. Hold the position for the prescribed time, maintaining tension.', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 2, NULL, 7, 7, NULL, 5, 'Standing', NULL, NULL, NULL, 8, 12, NULL, 6, NULL, TRUE, NULL, 'Strength', 47, 7, 8, TRUE, TRUE, 'external_rotation', 'Standing Scapular External Rotation Hold', 'squat, bench_press, deadlift', FALSE, 'bodyweight', TRUE, 3, 90, 4, 70, 88, 95, 65),
('4c9f8918-3c9f-4fbc-97b6-0b95ab7eb631', 'Bent Over Row - Reverse Grip (Barbell)', 'Back', 'Barbell', '{"Back","Lats"}'::text[], '{"Biceps","Rear Delts"}'::text[], 'The Barbell Reverse Grip Bent Over Row is a rowing exercise that builds thickness in your upper back. Secondary activation of your biceps, lats provides additional muscle engagement. Bending over allows gravity to provide resistance in a different plane. Barbells enable bilateral loading for building raw strength. A strong back improves posture, prevents injury, and balances pressing movements.', '24671201', '24671201-Barbell-Reverse-Grip-Bent-Over-Row-(female)_Back.mp4', 'female', FALSE, '2025-12-03 23:26:31.133197+00', '1. Grip a barbell with hands at the appropriate width for Barbell Reverse Grip Bent Over Row. 2. Hinge at your hips, pushing them back while keeping your back flat. 3. Use a reverse grip (opposite of the standard grip for this exercise). 4. Pull the weight toward your torso, leading with your elbow(s). 5. Squeeze your shoulder blades together at the peak contraction. 6. Extend back out with control, feeling the stretch in your back. 7. Repeat for the prescribed number of repetitions.', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 3, NULL, 10, 10, NULL, 4, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 5, 8, NULL, 8, NULL, TRUE, NULL, 'Strength', 82, 7, 9, TRUE, FALSE, 'bent_over_row', 'Bent Over Row - Reverse Grip', 'Bent Over Row - Reverse Grip', TRUE, 'barbell', FALSE, 4, 120, 4, 95, 80, 65, 95);
INSERT INTO _exercise_staging (id, name, category, equipment, primary_muscles, secondary_muscles, description, video_code, video_filename, gender, is_custom, created_at, steps_to_perform, movement_pattern, force_type, movement_type, laterality, plane_of_motion, difficulty_level, complexity_score, strength_rating, hypertrophy_rating, power_rating, endurance_rating, body_position, bench_angle, grip_type, grip_width, optimal_rep_range_min, optimal_rep_range_max, placement_in_workout, fatigability, popularity_score, home_gym_friendly, instructions, workout_type, practicality_score, fat_loss_rating, general_fitness_rating, is_compound, supersetable, exercise_family, base_exercise_name, complementary_families, is_equipment_primary, equipment_category, duration_based, recommended_sets, rest_seconds, muscles_worked_count, priority_build_muscle, priority_get_lean, priority_home, priority_gym) VALUES
('4ca17588-acf8-485a-a9e3-dd8420f48925', 'Seated Knee Raise (Stability Ball)', 'Core', 'Stability Ball', '{"Lower Abs"}'::text[], '{"Hip Flexors"}'::text[], 'Build leg strength with this raising movement focusing on your abs. Your hip flexors work as secondary movers, adding to the training stimulus. The seated position helps isolate the target muscles by removing momentum. The stability ball adds an instability challenge that activates more stabilizer muscles. Leg training boosts metabolism and builds functional, real-world strength.', '92751201', '92751201-Sitting-Knee-Raise-on-a-Stability-Ball-(female)_Hi.mp4', 'female', FALSE, '2025-12-03 23:26:37.756436+00', '1. Position the stability ball as needed for Seated Knee Raise. 2. Sit with your back supported, core engaged, feet flat on the floor. 3. Raise the weight in the prescribed direction for Seated Knee Raise. 4. Lower with control, maintaining tension throughout. 5. Complete all reps with control before resting.', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 2, NULL, 5, 7, NULL, 6, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 12, 20, NULL, 4, NULL, TRUE, NULL, 'Strength', 62, 5, 7, FALSE, TRUE, 'leg_raise', 'Seated Knee Raise', 'crunch, plank, v_up', FALSE, 'stability_ball', FALSE, 3, 60, 2, 70, 88, 95, 65),
('4ca23705-e0c8-48f3-8057-611184dae5e9', 'Split Squat (Band)', 'Legs', 'Resistance Band', '{"Quads"}'::text[], '{"Glutes","Hamstrings"}'::text[], 'Build stronger quads with this squatting movement that develops leg drive and power. The glutes, hamstrings assist throughout the movement, making this a well-rounded exercise. Bands are joint-friendly and portable, perfect for any training environment. Leg training boosts metabolism and builds functional, real-world strength.', '70481201', '70481201-Band-Split-Squat-(female)_Thighs_.mp4', 'female', FALSE, '2025-12-03 23:26:30.887491+00', '1. Secure the resistance band appropriately for Band Split Squat. 2. Push your hips back and bend your knees to lower your body. 3. Keep your chest up and knees tracking over your toes. 4. Drive through your heels to stand back up, squeezing your glutes at the top. 5. Repeat for the prescribed number of repetitions.', 'Squat', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 2, NULL, 7, 7, NULL, 5, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 8, 12, NULL, 6, NULL, TRUE, NULL, 'Strength', 90, 7, 8, TRUE, TRUE, 'split_squat', 'Split Squat', 'lunge, bulgarian_split_squat, squat', FALSE, 'band', FALSE, 3, 90, 4, 60, 85, 90, 50),
('4cae41da-19dd-4b01-873a-8417c834cd9a', 'Internal And External Shoulder Rotation Against Wa', 'Shoulders', 'Bodyweight', '{"Rotator Cuff"}'::text[], '{"Shoulders"}'::text[], 'This rotation exercise works your rotator cuff for improved shoulder strength and aesthetics. This bodyweight exercise requires no equipment and can be done anywhere. Strong shoulders improve overhead strength and support nearly all upper body movements.', '73001201', '73001201-Internal-and-External-Shoulder-Rotation-against-Wa.mp4', 'female', FALSE, '2025-12-03 23:26:34.073704+00', '1. Rotate your torso through the movement pattern for Internal And External Shoulder Rotation Against Wa. 2. Control the rotation in both directions—avoid using momentum. 3. Continue for your target rep count, maintaining good form throughout.', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 2, NULL, 7, 7, NULL, 5, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 8, 12, NULL, 6, NULL, TRUE, NULL, 'Strength', 50, 7, 8, TRUE, TRUE, 'shoulder_exercise', 'Internal And External Shoulder Rotation Against Wa', 'squat, bench_press, deadlift', FALSE, 'bodyweight', FALSE, 3, 90, 4, 70, 88, 95, 65),
('4cb52ef7-8da3-4479-bbf2-446023f1e77e', 'Walking Front Kick Hand Shake', 'Legs', 'Bodyweight', '{"Quads"}'::text[], '{"Glutes","Hamstrings"}'::text[], 'A challenging plyometric exercise, the Walking Front Kick Hand Shake builds reactive power and improves conditioning. A versatile bodyweight movement perfect for home or gym training. Develops fast-twitch muscle fibers for quicker, more powerful movements.', '90581201', '90581201-Walking-Front-Kick-Hand-Shake-(female)_Plyometrics.mp4', 'female', FALSE, '2025-12-03 23:26:39.91585+00', '1. Set up in the starting position for Walking Front Kick Hand Shake. 2. Execute the movement with proper form, focusing on your full body. 3. Control both the lifting and lowering phases of the movement. 4. Complete all reps with control before resting.', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 2, NULL, 2, 2, NULL, 10, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 1, 1, NULL, 3, NULL, TRUE, NULL, 'Cardio', 50, 9, 8, FALSE, TRUE, 'walking', 'Walking Front Kick Hand Shake', 'hip_flexor, lunge, dynamic_warmup', FALSE, 'bodyweight', TRUE, 1, 60, 4, 70, 88, 95, 65),
('4cb73ec0-18f8-4f48-8cb9-dd1388c1da5b', 'Standing Around The World (Plate)', 'Shoulders', 'Weight Plate', '{"Shoulders"}'::text[], '{"Traps"}'::text[], 'Build stronger shoulders with this movement movement focusing on your delts. The chest assist throughout the movement, making this a well-rounded exercise. Performing this standing challenges your balance and core engagement. This bodyweight exercise requires no equipment and can be done anywhere. Shoulder development enhances both performance and upper body aesthetics.', '65491201', '65491201-Weighted-Plate-Standing-Around-the-World-(female)_.mp4', 'female', FALSE, '2025-12-03 23:26:40.037451+00', '1. Stand with feet about shoulder-width apart. 2. Set up in the starting position for Weighted Plate Standing Around The World. 3. Execute the movement with proper form, focusing on your delts. 4. Control both the lifting and lowering phases of the movement. 5. Repeat for the prescribed number of repetitions.', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 3, NULL, 7, 7, NULL, 5, 'Standing', NULL, NULL, NULL, 8, 12, NULL, 6, NULL, TRUE, NULL, 'Strength', 35, 7, 8, TRUE, TRUE, 'around_world', 'Weighted Plate Standing Around The World', 'lat_pulldown, bent_over_row, pull_up', FALSE, 'plate', FALSE, 3, 90, 4, 70, 88, 95, 65),
('4cb75285-729d-4079-b946-ae6f23361e19', 'Bent Over Row - Wide Grip (Machine)', 'Back', 'Machine', '{"Upper Back"}'::text[], '{"Lats","Biceps","Rear Delts"}'::text[], 'Target your rhomboids and mid-traps with this rowing movement. The biceps, rear delts assist throughout the movement, making this a well-rounded exercise. Bending over allows gravity to provide resistance in a different plane. Machine exercises are great for isolating muscles and training to failure safely. A strong back improves posture, prevents injury, and balances pressing movements.', '65161201', '65161201-Lever-Bent-Over-Wide-Grip-Row-(with-chest-support).mp4', 'male', FALSE, '2025-12-03 23:26:24.099303+00', '1. Adjust the machine settings (seat height, weight, pads) to fit your body for Lever Bent Over Wide Grip Row. 2. Hinge at your hips, pushing them back while keeping your back flat. 3. Use a wide grip (wider than shoulder-width) for this variation. 4. Pull the weight toward your torso, leading with your elbow(s). 5. Squeeze your shoulder blades together at the peak contraction. 6. Extend back out with control, feeling the stretch in your back. 7. Continue for your target rep count, maintaining good form throughout.', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 1, NULL, 10, 10, NULL, 4, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 5, 8, NULL, 8, NULL, FALSE, NULL, 'Strength', 78, 7, 9, TRUE, FALSE, 'cable_row', 'Lever Bent Over Row - Wide Grip', 'Lever Bent Over Row - Wide Grip', FALSE, 'machine', FALSE, 4, 120, 4, 80, 75, 20, 88),
('4cc8e0e9-73f1-4226-b8b1-905f0f352dba', 'Narrow Stance Squat (Barbell)', 'Legs', 'Barbell', '{"Quads","Glutes"}'::text[], '{"Lats","Biceps","Rear Delts"}'::text[], 'The Barbell Narrow Stance Squat is a rowing exercise that primarily loads your quadriceps. Secondary activation of your glutes, hamstrings provides additional muscle engagement. The barbell allows you to handle heavier loads for maximum strength gains. Leg training boosts metabolism and builds functional, real-world strength.', '23891201', '23891201-Barbell-Narrow-Stance-Squat-(female)_Thighs_.mp4', 'female', FALSE, '2025-12-03 23:26:31.013316+00', '1. Set up a barbell in a rack at the appropriate height for Barbell Narrow Stance Squat. 2. Use a close/narrow grip (hands closer than shoulder-width). 3. Pull the weight toward your torso, leading with your elbow(s). 4. Squeeze your shoulder blades together at the peak contraction. 5. Extend back out with control, feeling the stretch in your back. 6. Complete all reps with control before resting.', 'Squat', 'Push', 'Compound', 'Bilateral', NULL, 3, NULL, 10, 10, NULL, 4, 'Standing', NULL, 'Overhand (Pronated)', 'Standard', 5, 8, NULL, 9, NULL, FALSE, NULL, 'Strength', 97, 7, 9, TRUE, FALSE, 'squat', 'Narrow Stance Squat', 'leg_press, front_squat, goblet_squat, lunge, leg_extension', TRUE, 'barbell', FALSE, 4, 120, 5, 95, 80, 65, 95),
('4cc96f83-ad47-4f6d-a267-bea571eebcaa', 'Bent Over Reverse Fly (Resistance Band)', 'Shoulders', 'Resistance Band, Anchor Point', '{"Rear Delts"}'::text[], '{"Upper Back","Traps"}'::text[], 'Build balanced shoulders by working the posterior delts with this flying exercise. Secondary activation of your upper back provides additional muscle engagement. The bent over position requires core engagement to maintain a neutral spine. Resistance bands provide accommodating resistance that increases through the range of motion. A strong back improves posture, prevents injury, and balances pressing movements.', '91311201', '91311201-Resistance-Band-Bent-Over-Reverse-Fly-(female)_Sho.mp4', 'female', FALSE, '2025-12-03 23:26:35.936279+00', '1. Secure the resistance band appropriately for Resistance Band Bent Over Reverse Fly. 2. Hinge at your hips, pushing them back while keeping your back flat. 3. With a slight bend in your elbows, move the weight in a wide arc. 4. Squeeze your chest muscles at the center/top of the movement. 5. Return with control, feeling the stretch at the bottom. 6. Complete all reps with control before resting.', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 2, NULL, 5, 7, NULL, 6, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 10, 15, NULL, 4, NULL, TRUE, NULL, 'Strength', 75, 5, 7, FALSE, TRUE, 'rear_delt', 'Bent Over Reverse Fly', 'bench_press, incline_bench_press, push_up', FALSE, 'band', FALSE, 3, 60, 2, 60, 85, 90, 50),
('4cd10cbb-09a5-451c-adee-c524c78a8bfc', 'Twist - Down Up (Cable)', 'Core', 'Cables', '{"Obliques"}'::text[], '{"Abs"}'::text[], 'Build rotational power and define your waistline with the Cable Twist (down Up). Your abs work as secondary movers, adding to the training stimulus. Cable resistance creates smooth, continuous muscle engagement. Building core stability helps with everything from heavy deadlifts to daily activities.', '12071201', '12071201-Cable-twist-(down-up)_waist.mp4', 'female', FALSE, '2025-12-03 23:26:32.166461+00', '1. Adjust the cable machine to the correct height and attachment for Cable Twist. 2. Rotate your torso through the movement pattern for Cable Twist. 3. Control the rotation in both directions—avoid using momentum. 4. Complete all reps with control before resting.', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 2, NULL, 5, 7, NULL, 6, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 12, 20, NULL, 4, NULL, FALSE, NULL, 'Strength', 52, 5, 7, FALSE, TRUE, 'russian_twist', 'Twist', 'plank, crunch, leg_raise', FALSE, 'cable', FALSE, 3, 60, 2, 85, 88, 30, 92),
('4cdc6d7d-c0c2-45d1-af8b-a86f66021790', 'Chest Pull Back', 'Chest', 'Bodyweight', '{"Chest"}'::text[], '{"Triceps"}'::text[], 'The Chest Pull Back is a pulling exercise that develops back strength and muscle. The triceps assist throughout the movement, making this a well-rounded exercise. No equipment needed—your body provides all the resistance. A strong back improves posture, prevents injury, and balances pressing movements.', '53611201', '53611201-Chest-Pull-Back-(female)_Back_.mp4', 'female', FALSE, '2025-12-03 23:26:32.166461+00', '1. Set up in the starting position for Chest Pull Back. 2. Execute the movement with proper form, focusing on your chest. 3. Control both the lifting and lowering phases of the movement. 4. Repeat for the prescribed number of repetitions.', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 2, NULL, 7, 7, NULL, 5, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 8, 12, NULL, 6, NULL, TRUE, NULL, 'Strength', 50, 7, 8, TRUE, TRUE, 'chest_exercise', 'Chest Pull Back', 'bench_press, chest_fly, push_up', FALSE, 'bodyweight', FALSE, 3, 90, 4, 70, 88, 95, 65),
('4cde2c89-75f2-44e2-93c7-03ae3f59eda8', 'Seated Trapezius Stretch (Chair)', 'Full Body', 'Chair', '{"Full Body"}'::text[], '{}'::text[], 'Designed to lengthen your traps, the Seated Trapezius Stretch On A Chair helps improve mobility and prevent stiffness. Your neck work as secondary movers, adding to the training stimulus. The seated position helps isolate the target muscles by removing momentum. Regular stretching improves flexibility, reduces injury risk, and aids recovery.', '92651201', '92651201-Sitting-Trapezius-Stretch-on-a-Chair-(female)_Stre.mp4', 'female', FALSE, '2025-12-03 23:26:37.877283+00', '1. Position yourself with a sturdy chair for support or as part of the movement. 2. Sit with your back supported, core engaged, feet flat on the floor. 3. Move into the stretch position for Seated Trapezius Stretch On A Chair. 4. Ease into the stretch until you feel gentle tension (not pain). 5. Hold for 20-30 seconds, breathing deeply and relaxing into the stretch.', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 1, NULL, 1, 1, NULL, 3, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 1, 1, NULL, 1, NULL, TRUE, NULL, 'Stretch', 25, 2, 6, FALSE, TRUE, 'stretch_general', 'Seated Trapezius Stretch On A Chair', 'stretch_hip, stretch_back, stretch_shoulder', FALSE, 'bodyweight', TRUE, 1, 30, 2, 70, 88, 95, 65),
('4cf01495-3ef7-4ef0-8da4-89c45b837088', 'Chest Press To Rollout (TRX)', 'Chest', 'TRX', '{"Chest"}'::text[], '{"Triceps","Front Delts"}'::text[], 'Target your chest with the Suspender Chest Press To Rollout, an effective pressing movement for upper body strength. Secondary activation of your triceps, front delts provides additional muscle engagement. Suspension training adds instability, increasing core activation throughout. A well-developed chest contributes to upper body strength and aesthetics.', '86941201', '86941201-Suspender-Chest-Press-to-Rollout-(male)_Chest_.mp4', 'male', FALSE, '2025-12-03 23:26:21.109351+00', '1. Adjust the TRX/suspension straps to the appropriate length for Suspender Chest Press To Rollout. 2. Lower the weight toward your chest with control. 3. Press the weight up until your arms are extended (don''t lock elbows). 4. Complete all reps with control before resting.', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 3, NULL, 7, 7, NULL, 5, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 8, 12, NULL, 6, NULL, TRUE, NULL, 'Strength', 60, 7, 8, TRUE, TRUE, 'bench_press', 'Suspender Chest Press To Rollout', 'incline_press, decline_press, chest_fly, push_up, dip', FALSE, 'trx', FALSE, 3, 90, 4, 68, 85, 85, 70),
('4cf19234-1b6a-47f8-a339-1d4d82c99231', 'Plyo Jack', 'Full Body', 'Bodyweight', '{"Full Body"}'::text[], '{"Quads","Hamstrings"}'::text[], 'Enhance your stamina and burn calories with this effective cardio movement. Regular cardio training builds the aerobic base for better overall fitness.', '31081201', '31081201-Plyo-Jack-(male)_Cardio_.mp4', 'male', FALSE, '2025-12-03 23:26:22.644637+00', '1. Set up in the starting position for Plyo Jack. 2. Execute the movement with proper form, focusing on your cardio. 3. Control both the lifting and lowering phases of the movement. 4. Continue for your target rep count, maintaining good form throughout.', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 3, NULL, 5, 4, NULL, 8, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 8, 12, NULL, 7, NULL, TRUE, NULL, 'Plyometrics', 50, 9, 8, TRUE, TRUE, 'general_exercise', 'Plyo Jack', 'squat, bench_press, deadlift', FALSE, 'bodyweight', FALSE, 3, 60, 4, 70, 88, 95, 65),
('4cf5a493-2650-4d89-a3e4-41ed87f1b493', 'Standing Bicep Curl (with Leg)', 'Arms', 'Bodyweight', '{"Biceps"}'::text[], '{"Forearms"}'::text[], 'The Standing Biceps Curl (with Leg) is a curling exercise that isolates your biceps. Secondary activation of your forearms provides additional muscle engagement. The standing position engages your core for stability. A versatile bodyweight movement perfect for home or gym training. Dedicated arm training builds both strength and muscular definition.', '54461201', '54461201-Standing-Biceps-Curl-(with-leg)_Upper-Arms_.mp4', 'male', FALSE, '2025-12-03 23:26:25.233728+00', '1. Stand with feet about shoulder-width apart. 2. Curl your heels toward your glutes by bending at the knees. 3. Squeeze your hamstrings at peak contraction. 4. Extend legs back out with control. 5. Continue for your target rep count, maintaining good form throughout.', 'Curl', 'Pull', NULL, NULL, NULL, 2, NULL, 5, 7, NULL, 6, 'Standing', NULL, NULL, NULL, 10, 15, NULL, 4, NULL, TRUE, NULL, 'Strength', 82, 5, 7, FALSE, TRUE, 'bicep_curl', 'Standing Biceps Curl', 'hammer_curl, preacher_curl, cable_curl', FALSE, 'bodyweight', FALSE, 3, 60, 2, 70, 88, 95, 65),
('4cf87ac8-7642-4ad7-b973-4bcc8f9dd7b7', 'Knee Tap Sky Reach', 'Full Body', 'Bodyweight', '{"Full Body"}'::text[], '{}'::text[], 'This dynamic movement movement gets your heart rate up while developing explosive strength. No equipment needed—your body provides all the resistance. Develops fast-twitch muscle fibers for quicker, more powerful movements. Quality repetitions are more important than quantity.', '80381201', '80381201-Knee-Tap-Sky-Reach-(female)_Plyometrics_.mp4', 'female', FALSE, '2025-12-03 23:26:34.322534+00', '1. Set up in the starting position for Knee Tap Sky Reach. 2. Execute the movement with proper form, focusing on your full body. 3. Control both the lifting and lowering phases of the movement. 4. Continue for your target rep count, maintaining good form throughout.', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 2, NULL, 7, 7, NULL, 5, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 8, 12, NULL, 6, NULL, TRUE, NULL, 'Strength', 50, 7, 8, TRUE, TRUE, 'shoulder_stretch', 'Knee Tap Sky Reach', 'squat, leg_extension, lunge', FALSE, 'bodyweight', FALSE, 3, 90, 4, 70, 88, 95, 65),
('4cfdb40c-e308-4c44-9c1e-fa6af2adc9ad', 'Plank From Knees', 'Core', 'Bodyweight', '{"Abs"}'::text[], '{"Shoulders","Lower Back"}'::text[], 'The Plank From Knees is a core stabilization exercise that primarily targets your abs. Your shoulders, lower back work as secondary movers, adding to the training stimulus. A versatile bodyweight movement perfect for home or gym training. Core strength is foundational for athletic performance and injury prevention.', '95271201', '95271201-Plank-from-Knees-(female)_Waist_.mp4', 'female', FALSE, '2025-12-03 23:26:35.667316+00', '1. Hold your body in a straight line from head to heels. 2. Don''t let your hips sag or pike up—engage your core and glutes. 3. Breathe steadily while maintaining the position. 4. Repeat for the prescribed number of repetitions. Keep tension on the target muscles throughout. Beneficial for overall core development.', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 2, NULL, 7, 7, NULL, 5, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 8, 12, NULL, 6, NULL, TRUE, NULL, 'Strength', 70, 7, 8, TRUE, TRUE, 'plank', 'Plank From Knees', 'side_plank, dead_bug, hollow_hold', TRUE, 'bodyweight', TRUE, 3, 90, 4, 70, 88, 95, 65),
('4d020465-c0d1-4ac5-ad70-6b6ab4bb37b4', 'Assisted Dip (Machine)', 'Chest', 'Machine', '{"Lower Chest"}'::text[], '{"Triceps","Front Delts"}'::text[], 'The Lever Graviton Assisted Dip targets your triceps through a dipping motion. The triceps, front delts assist throughout the movement, making this a well-rounded exercise. The fixed path allows you to focus purely on muscular effort. Arm strength supports grip, pulling, and pushing in compound movements.', '106051201', '106051201-Lever-Graviton-Assisted-Dip-(male)_Upper-Arms_.mp4', 'male', FALSE, '2025-12-03 23:26:29.36063+00', '1. Adjust the machine settings (seat height, weight, pads) to fit your body for Lever Graviton Assisted Dip. 2. Lower your body by bending your elbows to about 90 degrees. 3. Push back up until your arms are fully extended. 4. Repeat for the prescribed number of repetitions.', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 1, NULL, 7, 7, NULL, 5, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 8, 12, NULL, 6, NULL, FALSE, NULL, 'Strength', 78, 7, 8, TRUE, TRUE, 'dip', 'Lever Graviton Assisted Dip', 'bench_press, tricep_pushdown, push_up', FALSE, 'machine', FALSE, 3, 90, 4, 80, 75, 20, 88),
('4d034d4d-ec89-4382-af0b-58f94b868ddd', 'Deadlift (Barbell)', 'Back', 'Barbell', '{"Lower Back"}'::text[], '{"Glutes","Hamstrings","Traps"}'::text[], 'Build leg strength with this hip hinge movement focusing on your hamstrings/glutes. The glutes, lower back assist throughout the movement, making this a well-rounded exercise. The barbell allows you to handle heavier loads for maximum strength gains. Strong legs are the foundation for athletic performance and functional fitness.', '22141201', '22141201-Barbell-Deadlift-(female)_Hips_.mp4', 'female', FALSE, '2025-12-03 23:26:31.013316+00', '1. Grip a barbell with hands at the appropriate width for Barbell Deadlift. 2. Hinge at hips and bend knees to grip the weight. 3. Drive through your heels, extending hips and knees to stand. 4. Lower by reversing the movement with control. 5. Continue for your target rep count, maintaining good form throughout. Control the movement—avoid using momentum.', 'Hip Hinge', 'Pull', 'Compound', 'Bilateral', NULL, 3, NULL, 10, 10, NULL, 4, 'Standing', NULL, 'Overhand (Pronated)', 'Standard', 3, 6, NULL, 10, NULL, FALSE, NULL, 'Strength', 97, 7, 9, TRUE, FALSE, 'deadlift', 'Deadlift', 'romanian_deadlift, hip_thrust, leg_curl', TRUE, 'barbell', FALSE, 4, 120, 6, 95, 80, 65, 95),
('4d0453ec-82f3-475a-ad7e-4bca1ccfc7c6', 'Side Plank Leg Raise', 'Core', 'Bodyweight', '{"Core","Abs"}'::text[], '{"Shoulders"}'::text[], 'The Side Plank Leg Raise is a lower body raising exercise that targets your abs. The hip flexors assist throughout the movement, making this a well-rounded exercise. This bodyweight exercise requires no equipment and can be done anywhere. Strong legs are the foundation for athletic performance and functional fitness.', '32641201', '32641201-Side-Plank-Leg-raise-(female)_Hips.mp4', 'female', FALSE, '2025-12-03 23:26:37.179953+00', '1. Hold your body in a straight line from head to heels. 2. Don''t let your hips sag or pike up—engage your core and glutes. 3. Breathe steadily while maintaining the position. 4. Repeat for the prescribed number of repetitions. Keep your shoulders relaxed and away from your ears. Perfect for targeting your abs.', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 2, NULL, 5, 7, NULL, 6, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 10, 15, NULL, 4, NULL, TRUE, NULL, 'Strength', 70, 5, 7, FALSE, TRUE, 'side_plank', 'Side Plank Leg Raise', 'shoulder_press, front_raise, rear_delt_fly, upright_row', FALSE, 'bodyweight', TRUE, 3, 60, 2, 70, 88, 95, 65),
('4d3b9cf8-49d1-4586-a36d-c01cb5fad7aa', 'Horizontal Bicep Curl (Band)', 'Arms', 'Resistance Band', '{"Biceps"}'::text[], '{"Forearms"}'::text[], 'The Band Horizontal Biceps Curl is a curling exercise that isolates your biceps. Secondary activation of your forearms provides additional muscle engagement. Bands are joint-friendly and portable, perfect for any training environment. Arm strength supports grip, pulling, and pushing in compound movements.', '70381201', '70381201-Band-Horizontal-Biceps-Curl-(female)_Upper-Arms_.mp4', 'female', FALSE, '2025-12-03 23:26:30.685158+00', '1. Secure the resistance band appropriately for Band Horizontal Biceps Curl. 2. Keep your elbows in a fixed position throughout the movement. 3. Curl the weight up by contracting your biceps, squeezing at the top. 4. Lower with control, resisting the weight on the way down. 5. Repeat for the prescribed number of repetitions.', 'Curl', 'Pull', NULL, NULL, NULL, 2, NULL, 5, 7, NULL, 6, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 10, 15, NULL, 4, NULL, TRUE, NULL, 'Strength', 85, 5, 7, FALSE, TRUE, 'bicep_curl', 'Horizontal Biceps Curl', 'hammer_curl, preacher_curl, cable_curl', FALSE, 'band', FALSE, 3, 60, 2, 60, 85, 90, 50),
('4d4e025f-7490-4ded-a1e3-24612d4c8500', 'Seated Knee Drives (Chair)', 'Core', 'Chair', '{"Abs"}'::text[], '{"Hip Flexors"}'::text[], 'This movement exercise engages your abs for improved core stability and strength. The seated position helps isolate the target muscles by removing momentum. Core strength is foundational for athletic performance and injury prevention. Start with lighter weight to master the movement pattern.', '91051201', '91051201-Sitting-Knee-Drives-on-a-Chair-(female)_Waist_.mp4', 'female', FALSE, '2025-12-03 23:26:37.756436+00', '1. Position yourself with a sturdy chair for support or as part of the movement. 2. Sit with your back supported, core engaged, feet flat on the floor. 3. Continue for your target rep count, maintaining good form throughout. Keep your shoulders relaxed and away from your ears. A solid choice for core day.', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 2, NULL, 7, 7, NULL, 5, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 8, 12, NULL, 6, NULL, TRUE, NULL, 'Strength', 35, 7, 8, TRUE, TRUE, 'knee_drive', 'Seated Knee Drives On A Chair', 'butt_kicks, jumping_jack, mountain_climber', FALSE, 'bodyweight', FALSE, 3, 90, 4, 70, 88, 95, 65),
('4d597366-992b-4690-bfbe-1fcb057b6825', 'Single Arm Zottman Preacher Curl (Dumbbell)', 'Arms', 'Dumbbells, Preacher Bench', '{"Biceps"}'::text[], '{"Forearms"}'::text[], 'The Dumbbell One Arm Zottman Preacher Curl is a curling exercise that isolates your biceps. You''ll also feel your forearms working to support the movement. Using dumbbells requires more stabilization than barbell variations. Dedicated arm training builds both strength and muscular definition.', '37631201', '37631201-Dumbbell-One-Arm-Zottman-Preacher-Curl-(female)_Upper-Arms.mp4', 'female', FALSE, '2025-12-03 23:26:33.034396+00', '1. Select an appropriate weight dumbbell and hold it in one hand. 2. Keep your elbows in a fixed position throughout the movement. 3. Curl the weight up by contracting your biceps, squeezing at the top. 4. Lower with control, resisting the weight on the way down. 5. Complete all reps on one side, then switch to the other side. 6. Repeat for the prescribed number of repetitions. Focus on squeezing the target muscle at peak contraction.', 'Curl', 'Pull', NULL, NULL, NULL, 3, NULL, 5, 7, NULL, 6, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 10, 15, NULL, 4, NULL, TRUE, NULL, 'Strength', 35, 5, 7, FALSE, TRUE, 'preacher_curl', 'Single Arm Zottman Preacher Curl', 'tricep_pushdown, tricep_extension, bicep_curl, hammer_curl', TRUE, 'dumbbell', FALSE, 3, 60, 2, 92, 90, 92, 90),
('4d70265e-70b6-4490-bdf8-94a708666f0c', 'Seated W Press (Dumbbell)', 'Shoulders', 'Dumbbells, Flat Bench', '{"Front Delts"}'::text[], '{"Side Delts","Triceps"}'::text[], 'This pressing exercise works your delts for improved shoulder strength and aesthetics. Being seated provides stability, allowing you to focus on the working muscles. Dumbbells allow each arm to work independently, helping correct imbalances. Shoulder development enhances both performance and upper body aesthetics.', '93891201', '93891201-Dumbbell-Seated-W-Press_Shoulders_.mp4', 'male', FALSE, '2025-12-03 23:26:22.755209+00', '1. Select a pair of dumbbells at an appropriate weight for Dumbbell Seated W Press. 2. Sit with your back supported, core engaged, feet flat on the floor. 3. Start with the weight at shoulder level. 4. Press directly overhead until your arms are fully extended. 5. Lower back to shoulder level with control. 6. Complete all reps with control before resting.', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 2, NULL, 7, 8, NULL, 5, 'Seated', NULL, NULL, NULL, 8, 12, NULL, 6, NULL, TRUE, NULL, 'Strength', 84, 7, 8, TRUE, TRUE, 'general_exercise', 'Seated W Press', 'squat, bench_press, deadlift', TRUE, 'dumbbell', FALSE, 3, 90, 4, 92, 90, 92, 90),
('4d7ef754-c668-44b6-b156-c43b8e90d70c', 'Hip Flexor Hamstring Stretch (Gymnastic Rings) - Alternating', 'Legs', 'Gymnastic Rings', '{"Hamstrings"}'::text[], '{"Lower Back"}'::text[], 'Designed to lengthen your hip flexors, the Alternating Hip Flexor Hamstring Stretch helps improve mobility and prevent stiffness. The quads assist throughout the movement, making this a well-rounded exercise. Include this in your routine for better mobility and reduced muscle tension.', '82631201', '82631201-Alternating-Hip-Flexor-Hamstring-Stretch-(female)_.mp4', 'female', FALSE, '2025-12-03 23:26:30.54809+00', '1. Move into the stretch position for Alternating Hip Flexor Hamstring Stretch. 2. Ease into the stretch until you feel gentle tension (not pain). 3. Hold for 20-30 seconds, breathing deeply and relaxing into the stretch. 4. Alternate between sides/arms/legs with each repetition.', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 1, NULL, 1, 1, NULL, 3, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 1, 1, NULL, 1, NULL, TRUE, NULL, 'Stretch', 28, 2, 6, FALSE, TRUE, 'hamstring_stretch', 'Hip Flexor Hamstring Stretch - Alternating', 'stretch_hip, stretch_calf, stretch_back', FALSE, 'gymnastic_rings', TRUE, 1, 30, 2, 68, 85, 85, 70),
('4daa12fe-2442-4933-b011-56f5bd2b65b5', 'Split Squat - Rear Foot Elevated (Plate Loaded Machine)', 'Legs', 'Machine', '{"Quads"}'::text[], '{"Glutes","Hamstrings"}'::text[], 'This squatting movement emphasizes your quadriceps for stronger, more powerful legs. The glutes, hamstrings assist throughout the movement, making this a well-rounded exercise. Machine exercises are great for isolating muscles and training to failure safely. Lower body strength improves everything from walking to heavy compound lifts.', '87111201', '87111201-Lever-Rear-Foot-Elevanted-Split-Squat-(plate-loade.mp4', 'male', FALSE, '2025-12-03 23:26:24.577164+00', '1. Adjust the machine settings (seat height, weight, pads) to fit your body for Lever Rear Foot Elevanted Split Squat (plate Loade. 2. Push your hips back and bend your knees to lower your body. 3. Keep your chest up and knees tracking over your toes. 4. Drive through your heels to stand back up, squeezing your glutes at the top. 5. Continue for your target rep count, maintaining good form throughout.', 'Squat', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 1, NULL, 10, 10, NULL, 4, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 5, 8, NULL, 9, NULL, FALSE, NULL, 'Strength', 93, 7, 9, TRUE, FALSE, 'split_squat', 'Lever Rear Foot Elevanted Split Squat (plate Loade', 'lunge, bulgarian_split_squat, squat', FALSE, 'machine', FALSE, 4, 120, 5, 80, 75, 20, 88),
('4daa8dfa-6b43-46bd-8ddb-ef5bd40fd7f1', 'Glute Bridge Walk', 'Legs', 'Bodyweight', '{"Glutes"}'::text[], '{"Hamstrings"}'::text[], 'This bridging exercise isolates your glutes for improved hip strength and power. The hamstrings assist throughout the movement, making this a well-rounded exercise. A versatile bodyweight movement perfect for home or gym training. Strong legs are the foundation for athletic performance and functional fitness. Control the negative portion for maximum muscle engagement.', '73191201', '73191201-Glute-Bridge-Walk-(male)_Hips_.mp4', 'male', FALSE, '2025-12-03 23:26:20.982555+00', '1. Drive through your heels to lift your hips toward the ceiling. 2. Squeeze your glutes hard at the top of the movement. 3. Lower your hips back down with control. 4. Complete all reps with control before resting. Engage your stabilizer muscles for better control.', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 2, NULL, 7, 7, NULL, 5, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 8, 12, NULL, 6, NULL, TRUE, NULL, 'Strength', 70, 7, 8, TRUE, TRUE, 'glute_bridge', 'Glute Bridge Walk', 'hip_thrust, romanian_deadlift', TRUE, 'bodyweight', FALSE, 3, 90, 4, 70, 88, 95, 65),
('4dc49ea7-9ede-410b-93ca-2a9196e12ced', 'Split Squat Heel Raise', 'Legs', 'Bodyweight', '{"Quads"}'::text[], '{"Glutes","Hamstrings"}'::text[], 'Build stronger quads with this squatting movement that develops leg drive and power. Your glutes, hamstrings work as secondary movers, adding to the training stimulus. No equipment needed—your body provides all the resistance. Lower body strength improves everything from walking to heavy compound lifts. Quality repetitions are more important than quantity.', '87551201', '87551201-Split-Squat-Heel-Raise-(female)_Thighs_.mp4', 'female', FALSE, '2025-12-03 23:26:38.153182+00', '1. Raise the weight in the prescribed direction for Split Squat Heel Raise. 2. Lower with control, maintaining tension throughout. 3. Complete all reps with control before resting.', 'Squat', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 2, NULL, 5, 7, NULL, 6, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 10, 15, NULL, 4, NULL, TRUE, NULL, 'Strength', 85, 5, 7, FALSE, TRUE, 'split_squat', 'Split Squat Heel Raise', 'lunge, bulgarian_split_squat, squat', FALSE, 'bodyweight', FALSE, 3, 60, 2, 70, 88, 95, 65),
('4dc775a5-6f20-4b2b-83e4-270bbf230d42', 'Standing Shoulder Press (Smith Machine)', 'Shoulders', 'Smith Machine', '{"Shoulders"}'::text[], '{"Side Delts","Triceps"}'::text[], 'Build stronger shoulders with this pressing movement focusing on your delts. You''ll also feel your triceps working to support the movement. The standing position engages your core for stability. Machine exercises are great for isolating muscles and training to failure safely. Strong shoulders improve overhead strength and support nearly all upper body movements.', '70071201', '70071201-Smith-Standing-Shoulder-Press-(female)_Shoulders_.mp4', 'female', FALSE, '2025-12-03 23:26:38.153182+00', '1. Set the Smith machine bar to the appropriate starting height for Smith Standing Shoulder Press. 2. Begin in a standing position with good posture. 3. Start with the weight at shoulder level. 4. Press directly overhead until your arms are fully extended. 5. Lower back to shoulder level with control. 6. Repeat for the prescribed number of repetitions.', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 3, NULL, 7, 7, NULL, 5, 'Standing', NULL, NULL, NULL, 8, 12, NULL, 6, NULL, FALSE, NULL, 'Strength', 90, 7, 8, TRUE, TRUE, 'shoulder_press', 'Smith Standing Shoulder Press', 'Standing Shoulder Press', FALSE, 'smith_machine', FALSE, 3, 90, 4, 80, 75, 20, 88),
('4dd54070-2482-4551-8b75-9599dd9872b1', 'Zercher Bulgarian Split Squat (Barbell)', 'Legs', 'Barbell', '{"Quads"}'::text[], '{"Glutes","Hamstrings"}'::text[], 'The Barbell Zercher Bulgarian Split Squat is a squatting exercise that primarily loads your quadriceps. Secondary activation of your glutes, hamstrings provides additional muscle engagement. Barbells enable bilateral loading for building raw strength. Lower body strength improves everything from walking to heavy compound lifts.', '75521201', '75521201-Barbell-Zercher-Bulgarian-Split-Squat-(male)_Thigh.mp4', 'male', FALSE, '2025-12-03 23:26:22.644637+00', '1. Set up a barbell in a rack at the appropriate height for Barbell Zercher Bulgarian Split Squat. 2. Push your hips back and bend your knees to lower your body. 3. Keep your chest up and knees tracking over your toes. 4. Drive through your heels to stand back up, squeezing your glutes at the top. 5. Repeat for the prescribed number of repetitions.', 'Squat', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 4, NULL, 10, 10, NULL, 4, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 5, 8, NULL, 9, NULL, TRUE, NULL, 'Strength', 35, 7, 9, TRUE, FALSE, 'split_squat', 'Zercher Bulgarian Split Squat', 'split_squat, lunge, leg_press', FALSE, 'barbell', FALSE, 4, 120, 5, 95, 80, 65, 95),
('4dd8f2cb-d997-4de6-9a44-7c86d61ce556', 'Weighted Lying Leg Raise', 'Core', 'Bodyweight', '{"Lower Abs"}'::text[], '{"Hip Flexors"}'::text[], 'Build a stronger core with the Weighted Lying Leg Raise, focusing on your abs. The hip flexors assist throughout the movement, making this a well-rounded exercise. The lying position provides back support and helps isolate the target muscles. This bodyweight exercise requires no equipment and can be done anywhere. Core strength is foundational for athletic performance and injury prevention.', '104301201', '104301201-Weighted-Lying-Leg-Raise_Waist_.mp4', 'male', FALSE, '2025-12-03 23:26:24.422129+00', '1. Lie down in the appropriate position for Weighted Lying Leg Raise. 2. Keeping legs mostly straight, raise them toward the ceiling. 3. Lower with control, stopping just before touching down. 4. Continue for your target rep count, maintaining good form throughout.', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 3, NULL, 5, 7, NULL, 6, 'Lying', NULL, NULL, NULL, 10, 15, NULL, 4, NULL, TRUE, NULL, 'Strength', 70, 5, 7, FALSE, TRUE, 'leg_raise', 'Weighted Lying Leg Raise', 'crunch, plank, v_up', FALSE, 'bodyweight', FALSE, 3, 60, 2, 70, 88, 95, 65),
('4de86056-3131-44fe-943d-67c41faa0a42', 'Standing Inner Biceps Curl (Dumbbell)', 'Arms', 'Dumbbells', '{"Biceps"}'::text[], '{"Forearms"}'::text[], 'The Dumbbell Standing Inner Biceps Curl is a curling exercise that isolates your biceps. Your forearms work as secondary movers, adding to the training stimulus. The standing position engages your core for stability. Using dumbbells requires more stabilization than barbell variations. Dedicated arm training builds both strength and muscular definition.', '12281201', '12281201-Dumbbell-Standing-Inner-Biceps-Curl_Upper-Arms_.mp4', 'male', FALSE, '2025-12-03 23:26:28.851102+00', '1. Select a pair of dumbbells at an appropriate weight for Dumbbell Standing Inner Biceps Curl. 2. Stand with feet about shoulder-width apart. 3. Keep your elbows in a fixed position throughout the movement. 4. Curl the weight up by contracting your biceps, squeezing at the top. 5. Lower with control, resisting the weight on the way down. 6. Repeat for the prescribed number of repetitions.', 'Curl', 'Pull', NULL, NULL, NULL, 2, NULL, 5, 7, NULL, 6, 'Standing', NULL, NULL, NULL, 10, 15, NULL, 4, NULL, TRUE, NULL, 'Strength', 94, 5, 7, FALSE, TRUE, 'bicep_curl', 'Standing Inner Biceps Curl', 'hammer_curl, preacher_curl, cable_curl', TRUE, 'dumbbell', FALSE, 3, 60, 2, 92, 90, 92, 90),
('4ded3539-11ba-4de9-8790-fa0cc4741005', 'Tire Flip', 'Full Body', 'Bodyweight', '{"Full Body"}'::text[], '{}'::text[], 'A challenging plyometric exercise, the Tire Flip builds reactive power and improves conditioning. A versatile bodyweight movement perfect for home or gym training. Great for improving athletic performance, burning calories, and building conditioning.', '24591201', '24591201-Tire-Flip_Plyometrics_.mp4', 'male', FALSE, '2025-12-03 23:26:25.123298+00', '1. Set up in the starting position for Tire Flip. 2. Execute the movement with proper form, focusing on your full body. 3. Control both the lifting and lowering phases of the movement. 4. Continue for your target rep count, maintaining good form throughout.', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 2, NULL, 7, 7, NULL, 5, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 8, 12, NULL, 6, NULL, TRUE, NULL, 'Strength', 50, 7, 8, TRUE, TRUE, 'general_exercise', 'Tire Flip', 'squat, bench_press, deadlift', FALSE, 'bodyweight', FALSE, 3, 90, 4, 70, 88, 95, 65),
('4df040b7-72ec-410a-934a-cf7000987d6c', 'Seated Reverse Shrug (Cable)', 'Back', 'Cables', '{"Traps"}'::text[], '{"Upper Back"}'::text[], 'The Cable Seated Reverse Shrug is a shrugging exercise that develops back strength and muscle. The seated position helps isolate the target muscles by removing momentum. The cable setup allows you to adjust the angle of resistance. Back development is crucial for pulling strength and overall upper body function.', '71551201', '71551201-Cable-Seated-Reverse-Shrug-(male)_Back_.mp4', 'male', FALSE, '2025-12-03 23:26:28.079801+00', '1. Adjust the cable machine to the correct height and attachment for Cable Seated Reverse Shrug. 2. Sit with your back supported, core engaged, feet flat on the floor. 3. Shrug your shoulders straight up toward your ears. 4. Hold briefly at the top, then lower with control. 5. Complete all reps with control before resting.', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 1, NULL, 5, 7, NULL, 6, 'Seated', NULL, NULL, NULL, 12, 20, NULL, 4, NULL, FALSE, NULL, 'Strength', 82, 5, 7, FALSE, TRUE, 'shrug', 'Seated Reverse Shrug', 'deadlift, bent_over_row, face_pull', FALSE, 'cable', FALSE, 3, 60, 2, 85, 88, 30, 92),
('4df35803-fb80-4f9f-923c-ba0cf5f6f5f1', 'Oblique V Up On Floor', 'Core', 'Bodyweight', '{"Obliques"}'::text[], '{"Abs"}'::text[], 'The Oblique V Up On Floor is a core movement exercise that primarily targets your abs. You''ll also feel your abs working to support the movement. This bodyweight exercise requires no equipment and can be done anywhere. A strong core improves posture, protects your spine, and enhances all other lifts.', '35151201', '35151201-Oblique-V-up-on-Floor_Waist_.mp4', 'male', FALSE, '2025-12-03 23:26:22.123147+00', '1. Position yourself on the floor for Oblique V Up On Floor. 2. Set up in the starting position for Oblique V Up On Floor. 3. Execute the movement with proper form, focusing on your abs. 4. Control both the lifting and lowering phases of the movement. 5. Repeat for the prescribed number of repetitions.', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 2, NULL, 7, 7, NULL, 5, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 8, 12, NULL, 6, NULL, TRUE, NULL, 'Strength', 45, 7, 8, TRUE, TRUE, 'v_up', 'Oblique V Up On Floor', 'squat, bench_press, deadlift', FALSE, 'bodyweight', FALSE, 3, 90, 4, 70, 88, 95, 65),
('4df55e5d-25b7-49f4-87d3-25ecf33996c0', 'Reverse Frog Crunch', 'Core', 'Bodyweight', '{"Abs"}'::text[], '{"Hip Flexors"}'::text[], 'The Reverse Frog Crunch is a lower body crunching exercise that targets your abs. Your hip flexors work as secondary movers, adding to the training stimulus. A versatile bodyweight movement perfect for home or gym training. Strong legs are the foundation for athletic performance and functional fitness.', '52601201', '52601201-Reverse-Frog-Crunch-(female)_Hips_.mp4', 'female', FALSE, '2025-12-03 23:26:36.266593+00', '1. Lift your hips off the floor by contracting your lower abs. 2. Bring your knees toward your chest, then lower with control. 3. Repeat for the prescribed number of repetitions. Ensure full range of motion on each rep. Works well for abs activation.', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 2, NULL, 5, 7, NULL, 6, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 12, 20, NULL, 4, NULL, TRUE, NULL, 'Strength', 70, 5, 7, FALSE, TRUE, 'crunch', 'Reverse Frog Crunch', 'leg_raise, plank, russian_twist, v_up', FALSE, 'bodyweight', FALSE, 3, 60, 2, 70, 88, 95, 65),
('4df9db24-3706-423b-913f-b21097346413', 'Pilates Machine Hundred (Pilates Machine)', 'Back', 'Pilates Machine', '{"Lats"}'::text[], '{"Shoulders"}'::text[], 'Designed to lengthen your lats, the Pilates Machine Hundred helps improve mobility and prevent stiffness. You''ll also feel your shoulders working to support the movement. The machine guides your movement path for safer, more controlled repetitions. Flexibility work like this enhances performance and prevents stiffness.', '106581201', '106581201-Pilates-Machine-Hundred-(female)_Stretching_.mp4', 'female', FALSE, '2025-12-03 23:26:35.667316+00', '1. Adjust the machine settings (seat height, weight, pads) to fit your body for Pilates Machine Hundred. 2. Move into the stretch position for Pilates Machine Hundred. 3. Ease into the stretch until you feel gentle tension (not pain). 4. Hold for 20-30 seconds, breathing deeply and relaxing into the stretch.', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 1, NULL, 7, 7, NULL, 5, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 8, 12, NULL, 6, NULL, FALSE, NULL, 'Strength', 58, 7, 8, TRUE, TRUE, 'back_exercise', 'Pilates Hundred', 'Pilates Hundred', FALSE, 'machine', FALSE, 3, 90, 4, 80, 75, 20, 88),
('4e18e2bd-5afd-41ae-bfd2-ebc33ce74fe1', 'Seated Abdominal Breathing', 'Core', 'Bodyweight', '{"Abs"}'::text[], '{"Hip Flexors"}'::text[], 'The Seated Abdominal Breathing is a core movement exercise that primarily targets your abs. The seated position helps isolate the target muscles by removing momentum. A strong core improves posture, protects your spine, and enhances all other lifts.', '99761201', '99761201-Sitting-Abdominal-Breathing-(female)_Waist_.mp4', 'female', FALSE, '2025-12-03 23:26:37.628647+00', '1. Sit with your back supported, core engaged, feet flat on the floor. 2. Set up in the starting position for Seated Abdominal Breathing. 3. Execute the movement with proper form, focusing on your abs. 4. Control both the lifting and lowering phases of the movement. 5. Repeat for the prescribed number of repetitions.', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 2, NULL, 7, 7, NULL, 5, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 8, 12, NULL, 6, NULL, TRUE, NULL, 'Strength', 50, 7, 8, TRUE, TRUE, 'breathing', 'Seated Abdominal Breathing', 'plank, crunch, leg_raise', FALSE, 'bodyweight', FALSE, 3, 90, 4, 70, 88, 95, 65),
('4e199539-7875-4171-84cd-71d47741d539', 'Wide Leg Sit Up', 'Core', 'Bodyweight', '{"Abs"}'::text[], '{"Hip Flexors"}'::text[], 'Build a stronger core with the Wide Leg Sit Up, focusing on your abs. Secondary activation of your hip flexors provides additional muscle engagement. No equipment needed—your body provides all the resistance. Building core stability helps with everything from heavy deadlifts to daily activities.', '52071201', '52071201-Wide-Leg-Sit-Up-(female)_Waist_.mp4', 'female', FALSE, '2025-12-03 23:26:40.037451+00', '1. Set up in the starting position for Wide Leg Sit Up. 2. Execute the movement with proper form, focusing on your abs. 3. Control both the lifting and lowering phases of the movement. 4. Complete all reps with control before resting.', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 2, NULL, 5, 7, NULL, 6, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 10, 15, NULL, 4, NULL, TRUE, NULL, 'Strength', 70, 5, 7, FALSE, TRUE, 'crunch', 'Wide Leg Sit Up', 'leg_raise, plank, russian_twist, v_up', FALSE, 'bodyweight', FALSE, 3, 60, 2, 70, 88, 95, 65),
('4e1bac28-a13c-4fbf-98af-28f45b2401e1', 'Chest Press - Single Arm (Machine)', 'Chest', 'Machine', '{"Chest"}'::text[], '{"Triceps","Front Delts"}'::text[], 'The Lever Stack Seated Single Arm Chest Press is a pressing exercise that targets your chest muscles. You''ll also feel your triceps, front delts working to support the movement. The seated position helps isolate the target muscles by removing momentum. The fixed path allows you to focus purely on muscular effort. A well-developed chest contributes to upper body strength and aesthetics.', '106721201', '106721201-Lever-Stack-Seated-Single-Arm-Chest-Press-(male)_.mp4', 'male', FALSE, '2025-12-03 23:26:29.61214+00', '1. Adjust the machine settings (seat height, weight, pads) to fit your body for Lever Stack Seated Single Arm Chest Press. 2. Sit with your back supported, core engaged, feet flat on the floor. 3. Lower the weight toward your chest with control. 4. Press the weight up until your arms are extended (don''t lock elbows). 5. Complete all reps on one side, then switch to the other side. 6. Repeat for the prescribed number of repetitions.', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 1, NULL, 7, 7, NULL, 5, 'Seated', NULL, NULL, NULL, 8, 12, NULL, 6, NULL, FALSE, NULL, 'Strength', 75, 7, 8, TRUE, TRUE, 'bench_press', 'Lever Stack Seated Single Arm Chest Press', 'incline_press, decline_press, chest_fly, push_up, dip', FALSE, 'machine', FALSE, 3, 90, 4, 80, 75, 20, 88),
('4e1bfbf5-eba7-4a5a-8751-af25cbf76597', 'Seated Incline Press Stepout (Chair)', 'Chest', 'Chair', '{"Upper Chest"}'::text[], '{"Front Delts","Triceps"}'::text[], 'This pressing exercise focuses on your pectorals for improved chest strength and development. The front delts, triceps assist throughout the movement, making this a well-rounded exercise. The seated position helps isolate the target muscles by removing momentum. A well-developed chest contributes to upper body strength and aesthetics.', '90851201', '90851201-Sitting-Incline-Press-StepOut-on-a-Chair-(female)_.mp4', 'female', FALSE, '2025-12-03 23:26:37.756436+00', '1. Position yourself with a sturdy chair for support or as part of the movement. 2. Set up a box or step platform at the appropriate height. 3. Sit with your back supported, core engaged, feet flat on the floor. 4. Lower the weight toward your chest with control. 5. Press the weight up until your arms are extended (don''t lock elbows). 6. Continue for your target rep count, maintaining good form throughout.', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 3, NULL, 7, 7, NULL, 5, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 8, 12, NULL, 6, NULL, TRUE, NULL, 'Strength', 58, 7, 8, TRUE, TRUE, 'incline_press', 'Seated Incline Press Stepout On A Chair', 'bench_press, shoulder_press, chest_fly', FALSE, 'bodyweight', FALSE, 3, 90, 4, 70, 88, 95, 65),
('4e7c1316-24df-4dc3-b8d1-9f46b113bed2', 'Kneeling Backward Hip Circles', 'Shoulders', 'Bodyweight', '{"Shoulders"}'::text[], '{"Traps"}'::text[], 'The Kneeling Backward Hip Circles is a lower body movement exercise that targets your delts. The kneeling position adds a core stability challenge. No equipment needed—your body provides all the resistance. Leg training boosts metabolism and builds functional, real-world strength.', '106801201', '106801201-Kneeling-Backward-Hip-Circles-(female)_Hips_.mp4', 'female', FALSE, '2025-12-03 23:26:34.322534+00', '1. Kneel on the floor (use a pad for comfort if needed). 2. Set up in the starting position for Kneeling Backward Hip Circles. 3. Execute the movement with proper form, focusing on your delts. 4. Control both the lifting and lowering phases of the movement. 5. Complete all reps with control before resting.', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 1, NULL, 7, 7, NULL, 5, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 8, 12, NULL, 6, NULL, TRUE, NULL, 'Strength', 50, 7, 8, TRUE, TRUE, 'hip_circle', 'Kneeling Backward Hip Circles', 'hip_thrust, lunge, squat', FALSE, 'bodyweight', FALSE, 3, 90, 4, 70, 88, 95, 65),
('4e7d8487-30dd-4993-9126-f7798dd96dd6', 'Sliding Floor Pulldown (Towel)', 'Back', 'Towel', '{"Lats"}'::text[], '{"Biceps","Upper Back"}'::text[], 'The Sliding Floor Pulldown On Towel is a pulling exercise that targets your latissimus dorsi for a wider back. The biceps, upper back assist throughout the movement, making this a well-rounded exercise. A strong back improves posture, prevents injury, and balances pressing movements.', '70931201', '70931201-Sliding-Floor-Pulldown-on-Towel-(female)_Back_.mp4', 'female', FALSE, '2025-12-03 23:26:37.99429+00', '1. Position yourself on the floor for Sliding Floor Pulldown On Towel. 2. Pull the bar/handle down toward your upper chest. 3. Drive your elbows down and back, squeezing your lats. 4. Control the weight back up without letting it yank your arms. 5. Repeat for the prescribed number of repetitions.', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 2, NULL, 7, 7, NULL, 5, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 8, 12, NULL, 6, NULL, TRUE, NULL, 'Strength', 45, 7, 8, TRUE, TRUE, 'lat_pulldown', 'Sliding Floor Pulldown On Towel', 'pull_up, bent_over_row, cable_row, face_pull', FALSE, 'bodyweight', FALSE, 3, 90, 4, 70, 88, 95, 65),
