('4ea84917-afe2-4bc4-80f8-86a86f46d445', 'Seated Concentration Curl - Close Grip (EZ Bar)', 'Arms', 'EZ Bar', '{"Biceps"}'::text[], '{"Forearms"}'::text[], 'This curling exercise focuses on your biceps for improved arm size and strength. The forearms assist throughout the movement, making this a well-rounded exercise. Being seated provides stability, allowing you to focus on the working muscles. Dedicated arm training builds both strength and muscular definition.', '70131201', '70131201-EZ-Bar-Seated-Close-Grip-Concentration-Curl-(femal.mp4', 'female', FALSE, '2025-12-03 23:26:33.505723+00', '1. Grip the EZ bar on the angled portions for a comfortable wrist position. 2. Sit with your back supported, core engaged, feet flat on the floor. 3. Use a close/narrow grip (hands closer than shoulder-width). 4. Keep your elbows in a fixed position throughout the movement. 5. Curl the weight up by contracting your biceps, squeezing at the top. 6. Lower with control, resisting the weight on the way down. 7. Complete all reps with control before resting.', 'Curl', 'Pull', NULL, NULL, NULL, 2, NULL, 5, 7, NULL, 6, 'Seated', NULL, NULL, NULL, 10, 15, NULL, 4, NULL, TRUE, NULL, 'Strength', 82, 5, 7, FALSE, TRUE, 'concentration_curl', 'EZ Bar Seated Concentration Curl - Close Grip', 'EZ Bar Seated Concentration Curl - Close Grip', FALSE, 'ez_bar', FALSE, 3, 60, 2, 95, 80, 65, 95),
('4ea907dd-963b-45b5-a4af-a90d39dc7aa4', 'Seated Leg Hold', 'Core', 'Bodyweight', '{"Abs"}'::text[], '{"Hip Flexors"}'::text[], 'Build a stronger core with the Seated Leg Hold, focusing on your abs. The seated position helps isolate the target muscles by removing momentum. A strong core improves posture, protects your spine, and enhances all other lifts.', '96651201', '96651201-Sitting-Leg-Hold-(male)_Waist_.mp4', 'male', FALSE, '2025-12-03 23:26:24.698781+00', '1. Sit with your back supported, core engaged, feet flat on the floor. 2. Hold the position for the prescribed time, maintaining tension. Focus on squeezing the target muscle at peak contraction.', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 2, NULL, 7, 7, NULL, 5, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 8, 12, NULL, 6, NULL, TRUE, NULL, 'Strength', 45, 7, 8, TRUE, TRUE, 'leg_exercise', 'Seated Leg Hold', 'squat, lunge, leg_press', FALSE, 'bodyweight', TRUE, 3, 90, 4, 70, 88, 95, 65),
('4ec36eb5-b409-4e82-9a29-dea1ba2166c5', 'Squat Thrust', 'Legs', 'Bodyweight', '{"Quads"}'::text[], '{"Glutes","Hamstrings"}'::text[], 'A challenging plyometric exercise, the Squat Thrust builds reactive power and improves conditioning. Your glutes, hamstrings work as secondary movers, adding to the training stimulus. No equipment needed—your body provides all the resistance. Plyometric training builds explosive power that transfers to sports and daily activities.', '49981201', '49981201-Squat-Thrust-(female)_Plyometrics_.mp4', 'female', FALSE, '2025-12-03 23:26:38.285955+00', '1. Push your hips back and bend your knees to lower your body. 2. Keep your chest up and knees tracking over your toes. 3. Drive through your heels to stand back up, squeezing your glutes at the top. 4. Continue for your target rep count, maintaining good form throughout. Control the movement—avoid using momentum. Perfect for targeting your quads. Variation: Squat Thrust.', 'Squat', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 3, NULL, 7, 7, NULL, 5, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 8, 12, NULL, 6, NULL, TRUE, NULL, 'Strength', 85, 7, 8, TRUE, TRUE, 'squat', 'Squat Thrust', 'leg_press, front_squat, goblet_squat, lunge, leg_extension', FALSE, 'bodyweight', FALSE, 3, 90, 4, 70, 88, 95, 65),
('4ecba5c4-405e-4129-8666-9b87537dc097', 'Push And Arms Crossover', 'Chest', 'Bodyweight', '{"Chest"}'::text[], '{"Front Delts"}'::text[], 'Target your chest with the Push And Arms Crossover, an effective pushing movement for upper body strength. The front delts assist throughout the movement, making this a well-rounded exercise. A versatile bodyweight movement perfect for home or gym training. Chest strength improves pushing power for sports, daily tasks, and other lifts.', '53661201', '53661201-Push-and-Arms-Crossover-(female)_Chest_.mp4', 'female', FALSE, '2025-12-03 23:26:35.801913+00', '1. Set up in the starting position for Push And Arms Crossover. 2. Execute the movement with proper form, focusing on your chest. 3. Control both the lifting and lowering phases of the movement. 4. Continue for your target rep count, maintaining good form throughout.', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 2, NULL, 7, 7, NULL, 5, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 8, 12, NULL, 6, NULL, TRUE, NULL, 'Strength', 50, 7, 8, TRUE, TRUE, 'chest_fly', 'Push And Arms Crossover', 'bench_press, incline_press, push_up', FALSE, 'bodyweight', FALSE, 3, 90, 4, 70, 88, 95, 65),
('4ed739cd-16c8-4fc5-b181-0a1d159b4f7d', 'Incline Fly (Cable)', 'Chest', 'Cables', '{"Chest"}'::text[], '{"Front Delts"}'::text[], 'Target your chest with the Cable Incline Fly, an effective flying movement for upper body strength. Your front delts work as secondary movers, adding to the training stimulus. Using an incline changes the angle of resistance for varied muscle recruitment. Cables provide constant tension throughout the full range of motion. Chest strength improves pushing power for sports, daily tasks, and other lifts.', '30501201', '30501201-Cable-Incline-Fly-(female)_Chest_.mp4', 'female', FALSE, '2025-12-03 23:26:31.931873+00', '1. Adjust the cable machine to the correct height and attachment for Cable Incline Fly. 2. With a slight bend in your elbows, move the weight in a wide arc. 3. Squeeze your chest muscles at the center/top of the movement. 4. Return with control, feeling the stretch at the bottom. 5. Continue for your target rep count, maintaining good form throughout.', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 2, NULL, 5, 7, NULL, 6, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 12, 20, NULL, 4, NULL, FALSE, NULL, 'Strength', 83, 5, 7, FALSE, TRUE, 'chest_fly', 'Incline Fly', 'bench_press, incline_press, push_up', FALSE, 'cable', FALSE, 3, 60, 2, 85, 88, 30, 92),
('4ee7c97e-407c-415f-be0e-c191c718edf6', 'Front Squat (Kettlebell)', 'Legs', 'Kettlebell', '{"Quads"}'::text[], '{"Glutes","Core"}'::text[], 'The Kettlebell Front Squat is a squatting exercise that primarily loads your quadriceps. You''ll also feel your glutes, hamstrings working to support the movement. The kettlebell grip position adds a unique training stimulus. Leg training boosts metabolism and builds functional, real-world strength.', '5331201', '05331201-Kettlebell-Front-Squat_Thighs_.mp4', 'male', FALSE, '2025-12-03 23:26:26.146796+00', '1. Select an appropriately weighted kettlebell for Kettlebell Front Squat. 2. Push your hips back and bend your knees to lower your body. 3. Keep your chest up and knees tracking over your toes. 4. Drive through your heels to stand back up, squeezing your glutes at the top. 5. Complete all reps with control before resting.', 'Squat', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 4, NULL, 7, 7, NULL, 5, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 8, 12, NULL, 6, NULL, TRUE, NULL, 'Strength', 93, 7, 8, TRUE, TRUE, 'front_squat', 'Front Squat', 'squat, leg_press, leg_extension, goblet_squat', FALSE, 'kettlebell', FALSE, 3, 90, 4, 75, 88, 88, 78),
('4ef68911-8f77-4829-a615-9e280bc8dd3a', 'Tree Yoga Pose Open Chest', 'Chest', 'Bodyweight', '{"Chest"}'::text[], '{"Front Delts"}'::text[], 'The Tree Yoga Pose Open Chest provides a deep stretch for your chest, ideal for recovery and mobility work. Your shoulders work as secondary movers, adding to the training stimulus. Flexibility work like this enhances performance and prevents stiffness.', '95301201', '95301201-Tree-Yoga-Pose-Open-Chest-(female)_Stretching_.mp4', 'female', FALSE, '2025-12-03 23:26:39.79101+00', '1. Move into the stretch position for Tree Yoga Pose Open Chest. 2. Ease into the stretch until you feel gentle tension (not pain). 3. Hold for 20-30 seconds, breathing deeply and relaxing into the stretch. Maintain consistent tempo throughout the set.', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 1, NULL, 1, 1, NULL, 3, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 1, 1, NULL, 1, NULL, TRUE, NULL, 'Stretch', 15, 2, 6, FALSE, TRUE, 'yoga', 'Tree Yoga Pose Open Chest', 'stretch_hip, stretch_back, plank', FALSE, 'bodyweight', TRUE, 1, 30, 2, 70, 88, 95, 65),
('4f0dfbe5-d1b3-4bbf-a271-c9292a4a871e', 'Single Leg Split Squat With The Ring (Kettlebell)', 'Legs', 'Kettlebell, Gymnastic Rings', '{"Quads"}'::text[], '{"Glutes","Hamstrings"}'::text[], 'Build stronger quads with this squatting movement that develops leg drive and power. Your glutes, hamstrings work as secondary movers, adding to the training stimulus. Kettlebells are excellent for building functional, real-world strength. Lower body strength improves everything from walking to heavy compound lifts.', '66801201', '66801201-Kettlebell-Single-Leg-Split-Squat-with-the-Ring_Thighs_.mp4', 'male', FALSE, '2025-12-03 23:26:21.995567+00', '1. Select an appropriately weighted kettlebell for Kettlebell Single Leg Split Squat With The Ring. 2. Push your hips back and bend your knees to lower your body. 3. Keep your chest up and knees tracking over your toes. 4. Drive through your heels to stand back up, squeezing your glutes at the top. 5. Complete all reps on one side, then switch to the other side. 6. Repeat for the prescribed number of repetitions.', 'Squat', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 5, NULL, 7, 7, NULL, 5, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 8, 12, NULL, 6, NULL, TRUE, NULL, 'Strength', 76, 7, 8, TRUE, TRUE, 'split_squat', 'Single Leg Split Squat With The Ring', 'lunge, bulgarian_split_squat, squat', FALSE, 'kettlebell', FALSE, 3, 90, 4, 75, 88, 88, 78),
('4f21f9e0-4f60-4cb7-8a43-3a8612ac8a9a', 'Single Arm Triceps Pushdown (Resistance Band)', 'Arms', 'Resistance Band, Anchor Point', '{"Triceps"}'::text[], '{"Chest","Shoulders"}'::text[], 'This pushing movement isolates your triceps for improved arm development. The band creates increasing tension as it stretches, challenging the lockout. Arm strength supports grip, pulling, and pushing in compound movements. Quality repetitions are more important than quantity.', '91361201', '91361201-Resistance-Band-Single-Arm-Triceps-Pushdown-(femal.mp4', 'female', FALSE, '2025-12-03 23:26:36.266593+00', '1. Secure the resistance band appropriately for Resistance Band Single Arm Triceps Pushdown. 2. Complete all reps on one side, then switch to the other side. 3. Complete all reps with control before resting.', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 3, NULL, 5, 7, NULL, 6, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 10, 15, NULL, 4, NULL, TRUE, NULL, 'Strength', 50, 5, 7, FALSE, TRUE, 'tricep_pushdown', 'Single Arm Triceps Pushdown', 'tricep_extension, close_grip_bench, dip', FALSE, 'band', FALSE, 3, 60, 2, 60, 85, 90, 50),
('4f22f354-455a-4310-8a15-3f1077faee1b', 'Twist And Turn', 'Full Body', 'Bodyweight', '{"Full Body"}'::text[], '{"Abs"}'::text[], 'This dynamic twisting movement gets your heart rate up while developing explosive strength. The abs assist throughout the movement, making this a well-rounded exercise. No equipment needed—your body provides all the resistance. Great for improving athletic performance, burning calories, and building conditioning.', '51371201', '51371201-Twist-and-Turn-(female)_Plyometrics_.mp4', 'female', FALSE, '2025-12-03 23:26:39.79101+00', '1. Rotate your torso through the movement pattern for Twist And Turn. 2. Control the rotation in both directions—avoid using momentum. 3. Continue for your target rep count, maintaining good form throughout.', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 2, NULL, 5, 7, NULL, 6, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 10, 15, NULL, 4, NULL, TRUE, NULL, 'Strength', 50, 5, 7, FALSE, TRUE, 'russian_twist', 'Twist And Turn', 'squat, bench_press, deadlift', FALSE, 'bodyweight', FALSE, 3, 60, 2, 70, 88, 95, 65),
('4f26fc15-835f-49c1-a79e-fc0867caa841', 'Lying Leg Extension - 90 Degrees (Machine) - Alternating', 'Legs', 'Machine', '{"Quads"}'::text[], '{}'::text[], 'The Lying 90 Degree Alternate Leg Extension is a extension exercise that primarily loads your quadriceps. Performing this lying down removes momentum for stricter form. A versatile bodyweight movement perfect for home or gym training. Lower body strength improves everything from walking to heavy compound lifts.', '82061201', '82061201-Lying-90-Degree-Alternate-Leg-Extension-(male)_Hip.mp4', 'male', FALSE, '2025-12-03 23:26:24.831811+00', '1. Lie down in the appropriate position for Lying 90 Degree Alternate Leg Extension. 2. Extend your legs until straight, squeezing your quads at the top. 3. Lower with control back to the starting position. 4. Alternate between sides/arms/legs with each repetition. 5. Repeat for the prescribed number of repetitions.', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 1, NULL, 5, 7, NULL, 6, 'Lying', NULL, NULL, NULL, 10, 15, NULL, 4, NULL, TRUE, NULL, 'Strength', 80, 5, 7, FALSE, TRUE, 'leg_extension', 'Lying 90 Degree Leg Extension - Alternating', 'squat, leg_press, lunge', TRUE, 'bodyweight', FALSE, 3, 60, 2, 80, 75, 20, 88),
('4f336d04-1c3f-4e26-aca8-32aa75ae82cc', 'Lying Lean Forward Pilates', 'Back', 'Bodyweight', '{"Lats"}'::text[], '{"Shoulders"}'::text[], 'The Lying Lean Forward Pilates provides a deep stretch for your lats, ideal for recovery and mobility work. You''ll also feel your shoulders working to support the movement. Performing this lying down removes momentum for stricter form. Flexibility work like this enhances performance and prevents stiffness.', '86951201', '86951201-Lying-Lean-Forward-Pilates-(female)_Stretching_.mp4', 'female', FALSE, '2025-12-03 23:26:35.250398+00', '1. Lie down in the appropriate position for Lying Lean Forward Pilates. 2. Move into the stretch position for Lying Lean Forward Pilates. 3. Ease into the stretch until you feel gentle tension (not pain). 4. Hold for 20-30 seconds, breathing deeply and relaxing into the stretch.', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 2, NULL, 7, 7, NULL, 5, 'Lying', NULL, NULL, NULL, 8, 12, NULL, 6, NULL, TRUE, NULL, 'Strength', 50, 7, 8, TRUE, TRUE, 'back_exercise', 'Lying Lean Forward Pilates', 'stretch_hip, dynamic_warmup, yoga_pose', FALSE, 'bodyweight', FALSE, 3, 90, 4, 70, 88, 95, 65),
('4f37ef06-21f3-4b89-823a-7fc250586590', 'Standing Obliques Rotation', 'Core', 'Bodyweight', '{"Obliques"}'::text[], '{"Abs"}'::text[], 'Build rotational power and define your waistline with the Standing Obliques Rotation. Your abs work as secondary movers, adding to the training stimulus. The standing position engages your core for stability. No equipment needed—your body provides all the resistance. A strong core improves posture, protects your spine, and enhances all other lifts.', '73881201', '73881201-Standing-Obliques-Rotation-(male)_Waist_.mp4', 'male', FALSE, '2025-12-03 23:26:25.233728+00', '1. Begin in a standing position with good posture. 2. Rotate your torso through the movement pattern for Standing Obliques Rotation. 3. Control the rotation in both directions—avoid using momentum. 4. Continue for your target rep count, maintaining good form throughout.', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 2, NULL, 7, 7, NULL, 5, 'Standing', NULL, NULL, NULL, 8, 12, NULL, 6, NULL, TRUE, NULL, 'Strength', 52, 7, 8, TRUE, TRUE, 'core_exercise', 'Standing Obliques Rotation', 'squat, bench_press, deadlift', FALSE, 'bodyweight', FALSE, 3, 90, 4, 70, 88, 95, 65),
('4f3da818-8e5c-4794-907f-2ac485c051db', 'Incline Shrug (Dumbbell)', 'Back', 'Dumbbells', '{"Traps"}'::text[], '{"Upper Back"}'::text[], 'Build a stronger back with this shrugging movement targeting your traps. Using an incline changes the angle of resistance for varied muscle recruitment. Dumbbells allow each arm to work independently, helping correct imbalances. Back development is crucial for pulling strength and overall upper body function.', '39381201', '39381201-Dumbbell-Incline-Shrug-(female)_Back.mp4', 'female', FALSE, '2025-12-03 23:26:32.914483+00', '1. Select a pair of dumbbells at an appropriate weight for Dumbbell Incline Shrug. 2. Shrug your shoulders straight up toward your ears. 3. Hold briefly at the top, then lower with control. 4. Complete all reps with control before resting. Maintain consistent tempo throughout the set.', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 2, NULL, 5, 7, NULL, 6, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 10, 15, NULL, 4, NULL, TRUE, NULL, 'Strength', 85, 5, 7, FALSE, TRUE, 'shrug', 'Incline Shrug', 'deadlift, bent_over_row, face_pull', TRUE, 'dumbbell', FALSE, 3, 60, 2, 92, 90, 92, 90),
('4f43e88d-e0fe-4896-8740-5f01da9ed0ea', 'Seated Press - Close Grip (Dumbbell)', 'Shoulders', 'Dumbbells, Flat Bench', '{"Front Delts"}'::text[], '{"Side Delts","Triceps"}'::text[], 'Target your delts with the Dumbbell Seated Close Grip Press, an effective shoulder pressing exercise. The chest assist throughout the movement, making this a well-rounded exercise. The seated position helps isolate the target muscles by removing momentum. Dumbbells allow each arm to work independently, helping correct imbalances. Shoulder development enhances both performance and upper body aesthetics.', '42371201', '42371201-Dumbbell-Seated-Close-Grip-Press_Shoulders_.mp4', 'male', FALSE, '2025-12-03 23:26:24.577164+00', '1. Select a pair of dumbbells at an appropriate weight for Dumbbell Seated Close Grip Press. 2. Sit with your back supported, core engaged, feet flat on the floor. 3. Use a close/narrow grip (hands closer than shoulder-width). 4. Start with the weight at shoulder level. 5. Press directly overhead until your arms are fully extended. 6. Lower back to shoulder level with control. 7. Complete all reps with control before resting.', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 2, NULL, 7, 8, NULL, 5, 'Seated', NULL, NULL, NULL, 8, 12, NULL, 6, NULL, TRUE, NULL, 'Strength', 84, 7, 8, TRUE, TRUE, 'general_exercise', 'Seated Press - Close Grip', 'Seated Press - Close Grip', TRUE, 'dumbbell', FALSE, 3, 90, 4, 92, 90, 92, 90),
('4f625774-4a65-42ef-a9e5-1d2b9de149a4', 'Squat Jacks', 'Legs', 'Bodyweight', '{"Quads"}'::text[], '{"Glutes","Hamstrings"}'::text[], 'This cardio exercise keeps your heart rate elevated for improved cardiovascular fitness. The glutes, hamstrings assist throughout the movement, making this a well-rounded exercise. Cardiovascular exercise improves heart health, endurance, and helps manage weight.', '7851201', '07851201-Squat-Jacks-(female)_Cardio_.mp4', 'female', FALSE, '2025-12-03 23:26:38.285955+00', '1. Push your hips back and bend your knees to lower your body. 2. Keep your chest up and knees tracking over your toes. 3. Drive through your heels to stand back up, squeezing your glutes at the top. 4. Complete all reps with control before resting. Focus on maintaining proper breathing throughout. Beneficial for overall cardio development.', 'Squat', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 3, NULL, 5, 4, NULL, 8, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 8, 12, NULL, 7, NULL, TRUE, NULL, 'Plyometrics', 85, 9, 8, TRUE, TRUE, 'squat', 'Squat Jacks', 'leg_press, front_squat, goblet_squat, lunge, leg_extension', FALSE, 'bodyweight', FALSE, 3, 60, 4, 70, 88, 95, 65),
('4f7de2c4-a72a-4c76-a509-fb0e849aeac2', 'Bent Over Y Raise (Dumbbell)', 'Shoulders', 'Dumbbells', '{"Rear Delts"}'::text[], '{"Upper Back","Rotator Cuff"}'::text[], 'Build stronger shoulders with this raising movement focusing on your delts. Your upper back work as secondary movers, adding to the training stimulus. The bent over position requires core engagement to maintain a neutral spine. Dumbbells allow each arm to work independently, helping correct imbalances. Shoulder development enhances both performance and upper body aesthetics.', '83551201', '83551201-Dumbbell-Bent-over-Y-Raise-(male)_Shoulders_.mp4', 'male', FALSE, '2025-12-03 23:26:24.203368+00', '1. Select a pair of dumbbells at an appropriate weight for Dumbbell Bent Over Y Raise. 2. Hinge at your hips, pushing them back while keeping your back flat. 3. Raise the weight in the prescribed direction for Dumbbell Bent Over Y Raise. 4. Lower with control, maintaining tension throughout. 5. Repeat for the prescribed number of repetitions. Maintain consistent tempo throughout the set.', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 2, NULL, 5, 7, NULL, 6, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 10, 15, NULL, 4, NULL, TRUE, NULL, 'Strength', 82, 5, 7, FALSE, TRUE, 'lateral_raise', 'Bent Over Y Raise', 'shoulder_press, front_raise, rear_delt', TRUE, 'dumbbell', FALSE, 3, 60, 2, 92, 90, 92, 90),
('4f7f8575-c63a-47e6-94f7-81afb235477f', 'Preacher Curl (Stability Ball, Dumbbell)', 'Arms', 'Dumbbells, Stability Ball, Preacher Bench', '{"Biceps"}'::text[], '{"Forearms"}'::text[], 'Build bigger biceps with this curling movement that targets the front of your arms. Secondary activation of your forearms provides additional muscle engagement. Dumbbells allow each arm to work independently, helping correct imbalances. Arm strength supports grip, pulling, and pushing in compound movements. Aim for full range of motion on every rep.', '37621201', '37621201-Dumbbell-Preacher-Curl-over-Exercise-Ball-(female)_Upper-Arms.mp4', 'female', FALSE, '2025-12-03 23:26:33.034396+00', '1. Select a pair of dumbbells at an appropriate weight for Dumbbell Preacher Curl. 2. Keep your elbows in a fixed position throughout the movement. 3. Curl the weight up by contracting your biceps, squeezing at the top. 4. Lower with control, resisting the weight on the way down. 5. Continue for your target rep count, maintaining good form throughout. Keep tension on the target muscles throughout.', 'Curl', 'Pull', NULL, NULL, NULL, 2, NULL, 5, 7, NULL, 6, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 12, 20, NULL, 4, NULL, TRUE, NULL, 'Strength', 76, 5, 7, FALSE, TRUE, 'preacher_curl', 'Preacher Curl', 'tricep_pushdown, tricep_extension, bicep_curl, hammer_curl', TRUE, 'dumbbell', FALSE, 3, 60, 2, 92, 90, 92, 90),
('4f81ca82-5e7a-44ea-9992-22395f618b75', 'Prone Incline Curl (Dumbbell)', 'Arms', 'Dumbbells, Incline Bench', '{"Biceps"}'::text[], '{"Forearms"}'::text[], 'The Dumbbell Prone Incline Curl is a curling exercise that isolates your biceps. You''ll also feel your forearms working to support the movement. The lying position provides back support and helps isolate the target muscles. Dumbbells allow each arm to work independently, helping correct imbalances. Dedicated arm training builds both strength and muscular definition.', '24961201', '24961201-Dumbbell-Prone-Incline-Curl-(female)_Upper-Arms.mp4', 'female', FALSE, '2025-12-03 23:26:33.034396+00', '1. Select a pair of dumbbells at an appropriate weight for Dumbbell Prone Incline Curl. 2. Lie face down (prone position) for Dumbbell Prone Incline Curl. 3. Keep your elbows in a fixed position throughout the movement. 4. Curl the weight up by contracting your biceps, squeezing at the top. 5. Lower with control, resisting the weight on the way down. 6. Repeat for the prescribed number of repetitions.', 'Curl', 'Pull', NULL, NULL, NULL, 2, NULL, 5, 7, NULL, 6, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 10, 15, NULL, 4, NULL, TRUE, NULL, 'Strength', 95, 5, 7, FALSE, TRUE, 'incline_curl', 'Prone Incline Curl', 'bicep_curl, hammer_curl, preacher_curl', TRUE, 'dumbbell', FALSE, 3, 60, 2, 92, 90, 92, 90),
('4f8a4cbd-8a42-492f-966e-c79a52ba6149', 'Knee Thrust', 'Full Body', 'Bodyweight', '{"Full Body"}'::text[], '{}'::text[], 'The Knee Thrust is an explosive exercise that combines cardiovascular training with dynamic thrusting movements. No equipment needed—your body provides all the resistance. Develops fast-twitch muscle fibers for quicker, more powerful movements.', '71671201', '71671201-Knee-Thrust-(female)_Plyometrics_.mp4', 'female', FALSE, '2025-12-03 23:26:34.322534+00', '1. Drive through your heels to lift your hips toward the ceiling. 2. Squeeze your glutes hard at the top of the movement. 3. Lower your hips back down with control. 4. Repeat for the prescribed number of repetitions. Focus on maintaining proper breathing throughout.', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 2, NULL, 7, 7, NULL, 5, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 8, 12, NULL, 6, NULL, TRUE, NULL, 'Strength', 50, 7, 8, TRUE, TRUE, 'knee_drive', 'Knee Thrust', 'butt_kicks, jumping_jack, mountain_climber', FALSE, 'bodyweight', FALSE, 3, 90, 4, 70, 88, 95, 65),
('4f95e16c-8815-4b5d-9b2b-25f6659ae081', 'Pullover On Floor (Dumbbell)', 'Chest', 'Dumbbells', '{"Chest"}'::text[], '{"Lats","Triceps"}'::text[], 'Build a stronger back with this pulling movement targeting your chest. The lats, triceps assist throughout the movement, making this a well-rounded exercise. Using dumbbells requires more stabilization than barbell variations. Back development is crucial for pulling strength and overall upper body function.', '43181201', '43181201-Dumbbell-Pullover-on-floor_Back.mp4', 'male', FALSE, '2025-12-03 23:26:25.233728+00', '1. Select a pair of dumbbells at an appropriate weight for Dumbbell Pullover On Floor. 2. Position yourself on the floor for Dumbbell Pullover On Floor. 3. With arms slightly bent, lower the weight behind your head in an arc. 4. Pull the weight back over your chest, squeezing your lats and chest. 5. Continue for your target rep count, maintaining good form throughout.', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 2, NULL, 7, 8, NULL, 5, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 8, 12, NULL, 6, NULL, TRUE, NULL, 'Strength', 57, 7, 8, TRUE, TRUE, 'pullover', 'Pullover On Floor', 'bicep_curl, face_pull, lat_pulldown', TRUE, 'dumbbell', FALSE, 3, 90, 4, 92, 90, 92, 90),
('4f9ae140-5c65-4f83-b928-9d9acdc17aab', 'Front Plank (Against Wall)', 'Core', 'Wall', '{"Abs"}'::text[], '{"Shoulders","Lower Back"}'::text[], 'Strengthen your midsection with this stabilization movement that works your abs. You''ll also feel your shoulders, lower back working to support the movement. Core strength is foundational for athletic performance and injury prevention.', '74381201', '74381201-Front-Plank-against-Wall-(male)_Waist_.mp4', 'male', FALSE, '2025-12-03 23:26:23.288245+00', '1. Position yourself at the appropriate distance from a wall. 2. Hold your body in a straight line from head to heels. 3. Don''t let your hips sag or pike up—engage your core and glutes. 4. Breathe steadily while maintaining the position. 5. Repeat for the prescribed number of repetitions. Ensure full range of motion on each rep.', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 2, NULL, 7, 7, NULL, 5, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 8, 12, NULL, 6, NULL, TRUE, NULL, 'Strength', 62, 7, 8, TRUE, TRUE, 'plank', 'Front Plank Against Wall', 'side_plank, dead_bug, hollow_hold', TRUE, 'bodyweight', TRUE, 3, 90, 4, 70, 88, 95, 65),
('4fa98b25-4a1b-4a0b-ac54-8d153ec47353', 'Lying Lower Back Stretch', 'Back', 'Bodyweight', '{"Lats"}'::text[], '{"Lower Back"}'::text[], 'Target your back with this stretching stretch that helps restore range of motion. The lying position provides back support and helps isolate the target muscles. Include this in your routine for better mobility and reduced muscle tension.', '32431201', '32431201-Lying-Lower-Back-Stretch-(female)_Back.mp4', 'female', FALSE, '2025-12-03 23:26:35.250398+00', '1. Lie down in the appropriate position for Lying Lower Back Stretch. 2. Move into the stretch position for Lying Lower Back Stretch. 3. Ease into the stretch until you feel gentle tension (not pain). 4. Hold for 20-30 seconds, breathing deeply and relaxing into the stretch. Control the movement—avoid using momentum.', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 1, NULL, 1, 1, NULL, 3, 'Lying', NULL, NULL, NULL, 1, 1, NULL, 1, NULL, TRUE, NULL, 'Stretch', 40, 2, 6, FALSE, TRUE, 'back_stretch', 'Lying Lower Back Stretch', 'stretch_hip, stretch_hamstring, stretch_shoulder', FALSE, 'bodyweight', TRUE, 1, 30, 2, 70, 88, 95, 65),
('4fb53cf0-700d-4047-a245-df47dc0efe3f', 'Standing Triple Yin Yang Circle', 'Shoulders', 'Bodyweight', '{"Shoulders"}'::text[], '{"Traps"}'::text[], 'The Standing Triple Yin Yang Circle is a movement exercise that targets your delts for shoulder development. The standing position engages your core for stability. A versatile bodyweight movement perfect for home or gym training. Strong shoulders improve overhead strength and support nearly all upper body movements.', '94321201', '94321201-Standing-Triple-Yin-Yang-Circle-(female)_Shoulders.mp4', 'female', FALSE, '2025-12-03 23:26:38.992671+00', '1. Stand with feet about shoulder-width apart. 2. Set up in the starting position for Standing Triple Yin Yang Circle. 3. Execute the movement with proper form, focusing on your delts. 4. Control both the lifting and lowering phases of the movement. 5. Repeat for the prescribed number of repetitions.', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 2, NULL, 7, 7, NULL, 5, 'Standing', NULL, NULL, NULL, 8, 12, NULL, 6, NULL, TRUE, NULL, 'Strength', 52, 7, 8, TRUE, TRUE, 'general_exercise', 'Standing Triple Yin Yang Circle', 'squat, bench_press, deadlift', FALSE, 'bodyweight', FALSE, 3, 90, 4, 70, 88, 95, 65),
('4fb62a4a-df75-496d-8ec1-0263f29f20a2', 'Seated Single Leg Hamstring Stretch (Gymnastic Rings)', 'Legs', 'Gymnastic Rings', '{"Hamstrings"}'::text[], '{"Glutes"}'::text[], 'This stretching movement works your hamstrings for balanced leg development. The seated position helps isolate the target muscles by removing momentum. Leg training boosts metabolism and builds functional, real-world strength.', '6921201', '06921201-Seated-Single-Leg-Hamstring-Stretch_Thighs-(female).mp4', 'female', FALSE, '2025-12-03 23:26:36.848698+00', '1. Sit with your back supported, core engaged, feet flat on the floor. 2. Complete all reps on one side, then switch to the other side. 3. Complete all reps with control before resting. Maintain a neutral spine throughout.', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 1, NULL, 1, 1, NULL, 3, 'Seated', NULL, NULL, NULL, 1, 1, NULL, 1, NULL, TRUE, NULL, 'Stretch', 25, 2, 6, FALSE, TRUE, 'hamstring_stretch', 'Seated Single Leg Hamstring Stretch', 'stretch_hip, stretch_calf, stretch_back', FALSE, 'gymnastic_rings', TRUE, 1, 30, 2, 68, 85, 85, 70),
('4fbb010b-82f1-4399-bb60-7cd87963e60a', 'Seated Knee Raise (Chair) - Alternating', 'Core', 'Chair', '{"Lower Abs"}'::text[], '{"Hip Flexors"}'::text[], 'Build a stronger core with the Seated Alternate Knee Raises On A Chair, focusing on your abs. The hip flexors assist throughout the movement, making this a well-rounded exercise. The seated position helps isolate the target muscles by removing momentum. Core strength is foundational for athletic performance and injury prevention.', '83001201', '83001201-Seated-Alternate-Knee-Raises-on-a-Chair-(male)_Wai.mp4', 'male', FALSE, '2025-12-03 23:26:23.79417+00', '1. Position yourself with a sturdy chair for support or as part of the movement. 2. Sit with your back supported, core engaged, feet flat on the floor. 3. Raise the weight in the prescribed direction for Seated Alternate Knee Raises On A Chair. 4. Lower with control, maintaining tension throughout. 5. Alternate between sides/arms/legs with each repetition. 6. Continue for your target rep count, maintaining good form throughout.', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 2, NULL, 5, 7, NULL, 6, 'Seated', NULL, NULL, NULL, 10, 15, NULL, 4, NULL, TRUE, NULL, 'Strength', 57, 5, 7, FALSE, TRUE, 'leg_raise', 'Seated Knee Raise On A Chair - Alternating', 'crunch, plank, v_up', FALSE, 'bodyweight', FALSE, 3, 60, 2, 70, 88, 95, 65),
('4fc6482e-2813-42d6-93b3-da0589d40da5', 'Seated Pulldown (Chair)', 'Back', 'Chair', '{"Lats"}'::text[], '{"Biceps","Upper Back"}'::text[], 'Build lat width and pulling strength with this pulling movement. The biceps, upper back assist throughout the movement, making this a well-rounded exercise. Being seated provides stability, allowing you to focus on the working muscles. A strong back improves posture, prevents injury, and balances pressing movements.', '104871201', '104871201-Seated-Pulldown-on-Chair-(male)_Back_.mp4', 'male', FALSE, '2025-12-03 23:26:21.890719+00', '1. Position yourself with a sturdy chair for support or as part of the movement. 2. Sit with your back supported, core engaged, feet flat on the floor. 3. Pull the bar/handle down toward your upper chest. 4. Drive your elbows down and back, squeezing your lats. 5. Control the weight back up without letting it yank your arms. 6. Continue for your target rep count, maintaining good form throughout. Don''t rush—quality over quantity.', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 2, NULL, 7, 7, NULL, 5, 'Seated', NULL, NULL, NULL, 8, 12, NULL, 6, NULL, TRUE, NULL, 'Strength', 37, 7, 8, TRUE, TRUE, 'lat_pulldown', 'Seated Pulldown On Chair', 'pull_up, bent_over_row, cable_row, face_pull', FALSE, 'bodyweight', FALSE, 3, 90, 4, 70, 88, 95, 65),
('4fc9c37e-3705-444e-882c-77724d7cc84f', 'Standing Triceps Stretch (Against Wall)', 'Arms', 'Wall', '{"Triceps"}'::text[], '{"Chest","Shoulders"}'::text[], 'Target your triceps with this stretching stretch that helps restore range of motion. Secondary activation of your shoulders provides additional muscle engagement. Performing this standing challenges your balance and core engagement. Flexibility work like this enhances performance and prevents stiffness.', '82421201', '82421201-Standing-Triceps-Stretch-against-Wall-(female)_Str.mp4', 'female', FALSE, '2025-12-03 23:26:38.992671+00', '1. Position yourself at the appropriate distance from a wall. 2. Begin in a standing position with good posture. 3. Move into the stretch position for Standing Triceps Stretch Against Wall. 4. Ease into the stretch until you feel gentle tension (not pain). 5. Hold for 20-30 seconds, breathing deeply and relaxing into the stretch.', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 1, NULL, 1, 1, NULL, 3, 'Standing', NULL, NULL, NULL, 1, 1, NULL, 1, NULL, TRUE, NULL, 'Stretch', 34, 2, 6, FALSE, TRUE, 'stretch_general', 'Standing Triceps Stretch Against Wall', 'bicep_curl, dip', FALSE, 'bodyweight', TRUE, 1, 30, 2, 70, 88, 95, 65),
('4fc9c782-015c-48da-821c-98aebea503cc', 'Sumo Squat Side Lunge', 'Legs', 'Bodyweight', '{"Quads"}'::text[], '{"Glutes","Inner Thighs","Hamstrings"}'::text[], 'The Sumo Squat Side Lunge is a squatting exercise that primarily loads your quadriceps. You''ll also feel your glutes, hamstrings working to support the movement. A versatile bodyweight movement perfect for home or gym training. Strong legs are the foundation for athletic performance and functional fitness.', '52111201', '52111201-Sumo-Squat-Side-Lunge_Hips_.mp4', 'female', FALSE, '2025-12-03 23:26:39.340041+00', '1. Push your hips back and bend your knees to lower your body. 2. Keep your chest up and knees tracking over your toes. 3. Drive through your heels to stand back up, squeezing your glutes at the top. 4. Complete all reps with control before resting. Engage your stabilizer muscles for better control. Beneficial for overall legs development.', 'Squat', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 2, NULL, 7, 7, NULL, 5, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 8, 12, NULL, 6, NULL, TRUE, NULL, 'Strength', 85, 7, 8, TRUE, TRUE, 'squat', 'Sumo Squat Side Lunge', 'leg_press, front_squat, goblet_squat, lunge, leg_extension', FALSE, 'bodyweight', FALSE, 3, 90, 4, 70, 88, 95, 65),
('4fcd06bd-eb7a-4cde-abc8-869122012aaa', 'Seated Raised Arms Inhale', 'Full Body', 'Bodyweight', '{"Full Body"}'::text[], '{}'::text[], 'Use this stretch to open up your full body area and enhance overall flexibility. Being seated provides stability, allowing you to focus on the working muscles. Include this in your routine for better mobility and reduced muscle tension.', '82161201', '82161201-Seated-Raised-Arms-Inhale-(female)_Stretching_.mp4', 'female', FALSE, '2025-12-03 23:26:36.848698+00', '1. Sit with your back supported, core engaged, feet flat on the floor. 2. Raise the weight in the prescribed direction for Seated Raised Arms Inhale. 3. Lower with control, maintaining tension throughout.', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 2, NULL, 5, 7, NULL, 6, 'Seated', NULL, NULL, NULL, 10, 15, NULL, 4, NULL, TRUE, NULL, 'Strength', 72, 5, 7, FALSE, TRUE, 'arm_exercise', 'Seated Raised Arms Inhale', 'bicep_curl, tricep_extension, hammer_curl', FALSE, 'bodyweight', FALSE, 3, 60, 2, 70, 88, 95, 65),
('4fd0aaef-c1e5-40b8-9ff1-b1b4cb239f15', 'Side Hip Abduction', 'Legs', 'Bodyweight', '{"Glutes"}'::text[], '{"Hip Abductors"}'::text[], 'The Side Hip Abduction is a lower body movement exercise that targets your glute med/abductors. You''ll also feel your glutes working to support the movement. This bodyweight exercise requires no equipment and can be done anywhere. Leg training boosts metabolism and builds functional, real-world strength.', '57281201', '57281201-Side-Hip-Abduction-(female)_Hips_.mp4', 'female', FALSE, '2025-12-03 23:26:36.985772+00', '1. Set up in the starting position for Side Hip Abduction. 2. Execute the movement with proper form, focusing on your glute med/abductors. 3. Control both the lifting and lowering phases of the movement. 4. Repeat for the prescribed number of repetitions.', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 2, NULL, 7, 7, NULL, 5, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 8, 12, NULL, 6, NULL, TRUE, NULL, 'Strength', 50, 7, 8, TRUE, TRUE, 'hip_abduction', 'Side Hip Abduction', 'hip_adduction, glute_bridge, clamshell', FALSE, 'bodyweight', FALSE, 3, 90, 4, 70, 88, 95, 65),
('4fd4cdf3-9da1-4b9b-ae89-3067669c67b8', 'Couch Hip Flexor Stretch', 'Legs', 'Bodyweight', '{"Hips"}'::text[], '{"Glutes","Hip Flexors"}'::text[], 'The Couch Hip Flexor Stretch provides a deep stretch for your hip flexors, ideal for recovery and mobility work. Secondary activation of your quads provides additional muscle engagement. Flexibility work like this enhances performance and prevents stiffness.', '82591201', '82591201-Couch-Hip-Flexor-Stretch-(female)_Stretching_.mp4', 'female', FALSE, '2025-12-03 23:26:32.374165+00', '1. Move into the stretch position for Couch Hip Flexor Stretch. 2. Ease into the stretch until you feel gentle tension (not pain). 3. Hold for 20-30 seconds, breathing deeply and relaxing into the stretch.', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 1, NULL, 1, 1, NULL, 3, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 1, 1, NULL, 1, NULL, TRUE, NULL, 'Stretch', 10, 2, 6, FALSE, TRUE, 'hip_stretch', 'Couch Hip Flexor Stretch', 'stretch_hamstring, stretch_glute, stretch_back', FALSE, 'bodyweight', TRUE, 1, 30, 2, 70, 88, 95, 65),
('4fe4d0f3-cc1e-4f80-9e2c-d5f85c9d5622', 'Slight Bend Top Crossover And Prayer Push', 'Chest', 'Bodyweight', '{"Chest"}'::text[], '{"Front Delts"}'::text[], 'This pushing exercise focuses on your pectorals for improved chest strength and development. Secondary activation of your front delts provides additional muscle engagement. No equipment needed—your body provides all the resistance. Chest strength improves pushing power for sports, daily tasks, and other lifts.', '94801201', '94801201-Slight-Bend-Top-Crossover-And-Prayer-Push-(female).mp4', 'female', FALSE, '2025-12-03 23:26:37.99429+00', '1. Set up in the starting position for Slight Bend Top Crossover And Prayer Push. 2. Execute the movement with proper form, focusing on your chest. 3. Control both the lifting and lowering phases of the movement. 4. Complete all reps with control before resting.', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 2, NULL, 7, 7, NULL, 5, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 8, 12, NULL, 6, NULL, TRUE, NULL, 'Strength', 35, 7, 8, TRUE, TRUE, 'boxing', 'Slight Bend Top Crossover And Prayer Push', 'squat, bench_press, deadlift', FALSE, 'bodyweight', FALSE, 3, 90, 4, 70, 88, 95, 65),
('4fecf096-53a8-452f-8baf-1bd2b117e9cd', 'Downward Dog To Chaturanga Pose', 'Core', 'Bodyweight', '{"Core"}'::text[], '{}'::text[], 'The Downward Dog To Chaturanga Pose provides a deep stretch for your full body, ideal for recovery and mobility work. You''ll also feel your hamstrings, calves, shoulders working to support the movement. Regular stretching improves flexibility, reduces injury risk, and aids recovery.', '79731201', '79731201-Downward-Dog-to-Chaturanga-Pose-(female)_Stretchin.mp4', 'female', FALSE, '2025-12-03 23:26:32.624497+00', '1. Move into the stretch position for Downward Dog To Chaturanga Pose. 2. Ease into the stretch until you feel gentle tension (not pain). 3. Hold for 20-30 seconds, breathing deeply and relaxing into the stretch.', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 1, NULL, 1, 1, NULL, 3, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 1, 1, NULL, 1, NULL, TRUE, NULL, 'Stretch', 15, 2, 6, FALSE, TRUE, 'yoga', 'Downward Dog To Chaturanga Pose', 'stretch_hip, stretch_back, plank', FALSE, 'bodyweight', TRUE, 1, 30, 2, 70, 88, 95, 65),
('4ff84d86-effd-47c9-99b1-077583656415', 'Kneeling Finger Press', 'Core', 'Bodyweight', '{"Abs"}'::text[], '{"Hip Flexors"}'::text[], 'The Kneeling Finger Press is an arm pressing exercise targeting your core. Kneeling helps eliminate lower body momentum from the movement. A versatile bodyweight movement perfect for home or gym training. Arm strength supports grip, pulling, and pushing in compound movements.', '73241201', '73241201-Kneeling-Finger-Press-(male)_Forearms_.mp4', 'male', FALSE, '2025-12-03 23:26:25.233728+00', '1. Kneel on the floor (use a pad for comfort if needed). 2. Execute the pressing motion for Kneeling Finger Press, extending through the target muscles. 3. Repeat for the prescribed number of repetitions.', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 1, NULL, 7, 7, NULL, 5, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 8, 12, NULL, 6, NULL, TRUE, NULL, 'Strength', 70, 7, 8, TRUE, TRUE, 'general_exercise', 'Kneeling Finger Press', 'squat, leg_extension, lunge', FALSE, 'bodyweight', FALSE, 3, 90, 4, 70, 88, 95, 65),
('4ff994f7-b725-4de8-9474-ce4d73319fe3', 'Standing Reverse Palm Prayer Push And Side Raise', 'Shoulders', 'Bodyweight', '{"Side Delts"}'::text[], '{"Traps"}'::text[], 'The Standing Reverse Palm Prayer Push And Side Raise ( is a pushing exercise that targets your lateral delts for shoulder development. The standing position engages your core for stability. A versatile bodyweight movement perfect for home or gym training. Shoulder development enhances both performance and upper body aesthetics.', '96211201', '96211201-Standing-Reverse-Palm-Prayer-Push-and-Side-Raise-(.mp4', 'female', FALSE, '2025-12-03 23:26:38.870314+00', '1. Begin in a standing position with good posture. 2. Raise your arms out to the sides until parallel to the floor. 3. Lower with control, maintaining tension throughout. 4. Complete all reps with control before resting.', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 2, NULL, 5, 7, NULL, 6, 'Standing', NULL, NULL, NULL, 10, 15, NULL, 4, NULL, TRUE, NULL, 'Strength', 57, 5, 7, FALSE, TRUE, 'boxing', 'Standing Reverse Palm Prayer Push And Side Raise (', 'shoulder_press, front_raise, rear_delt_fly, upright_row', FALSE, 'bodyweight', FALSE, 3, 60, 2, 70, 88, 95, 65),
('50047b4b-e3cc-4c27-bb1b-065da7a326e5', 'Assisted Nordic Hamstring Curl (Resistance Band)', 'Legs', 'Resistance Band, Gymnastic Rings', '{"Hamstrings"}'::text[], '{"Glutes"}'::text[], 'Strengthen the back of your thighs with this curling exercise. Secondary activation of your forearms provides additional muscle engagement. Resistance bands provide accommodating resistance that increases through the range of motion. Lower body strength improves everything from walking to heavy compound lifts.', '42041201', '42041201-Resistance-Band-Assisted-Nordic-Hamstring-Curl_Thi.mp4', 'male', FALSE, '2025-12-03 23:26:26.146796+00', '1. Secure the resistance band appropriately for Resistance Band Assisted Nordic Hamstring Curl. 2. Keep your elbows in a fixed position throughout the movement. 3. Curl the weight up by contracting your biceps, squeezing at the top. 4. Lower with control, resisting the weight on the way down. 5. Continue for your target rep count, maintaining good form throughout.', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 4, NULL, 5, 7, NULL, 6, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 10, 15, NULL, 4, NULL, TRUE, NULL, 'Strength', 63, 5, 7, FALSE, TRUE, 'leg_curl', 'Assisted Nordic Hamstring Curl', 'romanian_deadlift, hip_thrust', FALSE, 'band', FALSE, 3, 60, 2, 60, 85, 90, 50),
('500cad80-a3b4-4c1c-8372-6a8888a86bd8', 'Side To Side Leg Swing', 'Full Body', 'Bodyweight', '{"Full Body"}'::text[], '{}'::text[], 'The Side To Side Leg Swings is a flexibility exercise that targets your full body, helping to release tension and improve range of motion. Include this in your routine for better mobility and reduced muscle tension.', '25741201', '25741201-Side-to-Side-Leg-Swings-(female)_Hips.mp4', 'female', FALSE, '2025-12-03 23:26:37.429219+00', '1. Hinge at your hips, letting the weight swing back between your legs. 2. Explosively drive hips forward, propelling the weight forward/up. 3. Let gravity bring it back as you hinge for the next rep. Maintain a neutral spine throughout.', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 2, NULL, 7, 7, NULL, 5, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 8, 12, NULL, 6, NULL, TRUE, NULL, 'Strength', 50, 7, 8, TRUE, TRUE, 'leg_exercise', 'Side To Side Leg Swing', 'high_knees, butt_kicks, jumping_jack', FALSE, 'bodyweight', FALSE, 3, 90, 4, 70, 88, 95, 65),
('500de1ab-a909-4e68-81af-7a4ac926a708', 'Standing Obliques Pulse Twist - Alternating', 'Core', 'Bodyweight', '{"Obliques"}'::text[], '{"Abs"}'::text[], 'Build rotational power and define your waistline with the Alternate Obliques Pulse Twist Side Reach. Your abs work as secondary movers, adding to the training stimulus. This bodyweight exercise requires no equipment and can be done anywhere. Building core stability helps with everything from heavy deadlifts to daily activities.', '89241201', '89241201-Alternate-Obliques-Pulse-Twist-Side-Reach-(female).mp4', 'female', FALSE, '2025-12-03 23:26:30.412523+00', '1. Rotate your torso through the movement pattern for Alternate Obliques Pulse Twist Side Reach. 2. Control the rotation in both directions—avoid using momentum. 3. At the bottom or top, pulse up and down in small movements before completing the rep. 4. Alternate between sides/arms/legs with each repetition. 5. Complete all reps with control before resting. Keep your shoulders relaxed and away from your ears.', NULL, 'Pull', 'Compound', 'Bilateral (Alternating)', NULL, 2, NULL, 5, 7, NULL, 6, 'Standing', NULL, NULL, NULL, 10, 15, NULL, 4, NULL, TRUE, NULL, 'Strength', 52, 5, 7, FALSE, TRUE, 'russian_twist', 'Standing Obliques Pulse Twist - Alternating', 'squat, bench_press, deadlift', FALSE, 'bodyweight', FALSE, 3, 60, 2, 70, 88, 95, 65),
('50348264-aab8-4e04-a8b4-e114ae410a29', 'Twist Turn Slam (Medicine Ball)', 'Full Body', 'Medicine Ball', '{"Full Body"}'::text[], '{"Abs"}'::text[], 'Build power and athleticism with this high-intensity twisting exercise that challenges your entire body. The abs assist throughout the movement, making this a well-rounded exercise. Develops fast-twitch muscle fibers for quicker, more powerful movements.', '76101201', '76101201-Medicine-Ball-Twist-Turn-Slam_Plyometrics_.mp4', 'male', FALSE, '2025-12-03 23:26:28.260518+00', '1. Hold a medicine ball at the appropriate position for Medicine Ball Twist Turn Slam. 2. Rotate your torso through the movement pattern for Medicine Ball Twist Turn Slam. 3. Control the rotation in both directions—avoid using momentum. 4. Repeat for the prescribed number of repetitions.', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 2, NULL, 5, 7, NULL, 6, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 10, 15, NULL, 4, NULL, TRUE, NULL, 'Strength', 50, 5, 7, FALSE, TRUE, 'russian_twist', 'Medicine Ball Twist Turn Slam', 'squat, bench_press, deadlift', FALSE, 'medicine_ball', FALSE, 3, 60, 2, 70, 88, 95, 65),
('5037d817-da22-4b9b-a786-34c296d24b74', 'Seated Kickback (Chair)', 'Legs', 'Chair', '{"Glutes"}'::text[], '{"Rear Delts"}'::text[], 'The Seated Kickback On A Chair is a kicking exercise that develops back strength and muscle. The hamstrings assist throughout the movement, making this a well-rounded exercise. The seated position helps isolate the target muscles by removing momentum. A strong back improves posture, prevents injury, and balances pressing movements.', '90911201', '90911201-Sitting-Kickback-on-a-Chair-(female)_Upper-Arms_.mp4', 'female', FALSE, '2025-12-03 23:26:37.756436+00', '1. Position yourself with a sturdy chair for support or as part of the movement. 2. Sit with your back supported, core engaged, feet flat on the floor. 3. Keep your upper arm stationary and extend your forearm back. 4. Squeeze at full extension, then return with control. 5. Repeat for the prescribed number of repetitions.', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 2, NULL, 5, 7, NULL, 6, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 10, 15, NULL, 4, NULL, TRUE, NULL, 'Strength', 35, 5, 7, FALSE, TRUE, 'tricep_kickback', 'Seated Kickback On A Chair', 'lat_pulldown, bent_over_row, pull_up', FALSE, 'bodyweight', FALSE, 3, 60, 2, 70, 88, 95, 65),
('5037dafd-0909-4cb3-9406-c97fc39407ac', 'Bar Lateral Pulldown (Cable)', 'Back', 'Cables', '{"Lats"}'::text[], '{"Biceps","Upper Back"}'::text[], 'This pulling exercise emphasizes your lats for improved back development. Your biceps, upper back work as secondary movers, adding to the training stimulus. The cable setup allows you to adjust the angle of resistance. Back development is crucial for pulling strength and overall upper body function.', '1501201', '01501201-Cable-Bar-Lateral-Pulldown_Back.mp4', 'male', FALSE, '2025-12-03 23:26:28.397686+00', '1. Adjust the cable machine to the correct height and attachment for Cable Bar Lateral Pulldown. 2. Pull the bar/handle down toward your upper chest. 3. Drive your elbows down and back, squeezing your lats. 4. Control the weight back up without letting it yank your arms. 5. Complete all reps with control before resting. Keep your core engaged for stability.', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 2, NULL, 7, 8, NULL, 5, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 8, 12, NULL, 6, NULL, FALSE, NULL, 'Strength', 60, 7, 8, TRUE, TRUE, 'lat_pulldown', 'Bar Lateral Pulldown', 'pull_up, bent_over_row, cable_row, face_pull', TRUE, 'cable', FALSE, 3, 90, 4, 85, 88, 30, 92),
('50435172-dda6-4552-8b3a-fa7ee80ad705', 'Incline Push Up (TRX)', 'Chest', 'TRX', '{"Chest"}'::text[], '{"Front Delts","Triceps"}'::text[], 'Build a stronger chest with this pushing movement that develops pressing power. The triceps, front delts assist throughout the movement, making this a well-rounded exercise. Using an incline changes the angle of resistance for varied muscle recruitment. The TRX allows you to adjust difficulty by changing your body angle. A well-developed chest contributes to upper body strength and aesthetics.', '11161201', '11161201-Suspender-Incline-Push-up-(female)_Chest_.mp4', 'female', FALSE, '2025-12-03 23:26:39.472701+00', '1. Adjust the TRX/suspension straps to the appropriate length for Suspender Incline Push Up. 2. Keep your body in a straight line from head to heels throughout. 3. Lower your chest toward the floor by bending your elbows. 4. Push through your palms to return to the starting position. 5. Repeat for the prescribed number of repetitions.', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 1, NULL, 7, 7, NULL, 5, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 8, 12, NULL, 6, NULL, TRUE, NULL, 'Strength', 63, 7, 8, TRUE, TRUE, 'push_up', 'Suspender Incline Push Up', 'bench_press, chest_fly, dip', TRUE, 'trx', FALSE, 3, 90, 4, 68, 85, 85, 70),
('5053beac-280e-41c5-8eec-6e7d9ce1dbfe', 'Lying Ab Press', 'Core', 'Bodyweight', '{"Abs"}'::text[], '{"Hip Flexors"}'::text[], 'The Lying Ab Press is a core pressing exercise that primarily targets your abs. Performing this lying down removes momentum for stricter form. No equipment needed—your body provides all the resistance. Building core stability helps with everything from heavy deadlifts to daily activities.', '44591201', '44591201-Lying-Ab-Press-(male)_Waist_.mp4', 'male', FALSE, '2025-12-03 23:26:26.507873+00', '1. Lie down in the appropriate position for Lying Ab Press. 2. Execute the pressing motion for Lying Ab Press, extending through the target muscles. 3. Complete all reps with control before resting.', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 2, NULL, 7, 7, NULL, 5, 'Lying', NULL, NULL, NULL, 8, 12, NULL, 6, NULL, TRUE, NULL, 'Strength', 70, 7, 8, TRUE, TRUE, 'core_exercise', 'Lying Ab Press', 'plank, crunch, leg_raise', FALSE, 'bodyweight', FALSE, 3, 90, 4, 70, 88, 95, 65),
('50632f12-7ef4-4495-9838-008cd85efa30', 'Pushdown (Cable)', 'Arms', 'Cables', '{"Triceps"}'::text[], '{"Chest","Shoulders"}'::text[], 'The Cable Pushdown targets your triceps through a pushing motion. Cables provide constant tension throughout the full range of motion. Arm strength supports grip, pulling, and pushing in compound movements.', '97391201', '97391201-Cable-Pushdown-(female)_Upper-Arms_.mp4', 'female', FALSE, '2025-12-03 23:26:32.054831+00', '1. Adjust the cable machine to the correct height and attachment for Cable Pushdown. 2. Set up in the starting position for Cable Pushdown. 3. Execute the movement with proper form, focusing on your triceps. 4. Control both the lifting and lowering phases of the movement. 5. Repeat for the prescribed number of repetitions. Keep the movement smooth and controlled.', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 2, NULL, 5, 7, NULL, 6, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 12, 20, NULL, 4, NULL, FALSE, NULL, 'Strength', 60, 5, 7, FALSE, TRUE, 'tricep_pushdown', 'Pushdown', 'tricep_extension, close_grip_bench, dip', FALSE, 'cable', FALSE, 3, 60, 2, 85, 88, 30, 92),
('50667697-bae1-4d97-9966-80beffa28373', 'Single Arm Lat Stretch (Against Wall)', 'Back', 'Wall', '{"Lats"}'::text[], '{"Lower Back"}'::text[], 'The Single Arm Lat Stretch Against Wall is a flexibility exercise that targets your lats, helping to release tension and improve range of motion. The shoulders assist throughout the movement, making this a well-rounded exercise. Include this in your routine for better mobility and reduced muscle tension.', '76231201', '76231201-Single-Arm-Lat-Stretch-against-Wall-(male)_Stretch.mp4', 'male', FALSE, '2025-12-03 23:26:27.263406+00', '1. Position yourself at the appropriate distance from a wall. 2. Move into the stretch position for Single Arm Lat Stretch Against Wall. 3. Ease into the stretch until you feel gentle tension (not pain). 4. Hold for 20-30 seconds, breathing deeply and relaxing into the stretch. 5. Switch sides and repeat for equal time. 6. Complete all reps on one side, then switch to the other side.', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 1, NULL, 1, 1, NULL, 3, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 1, 1, NULL, 1, NULL, TRUE, NULL, 'Stretch', 27, 2, 6, FALSE, TRUE, 'lat_stretch', 'Single Arm Lat Stretch Against Wall', 'stretch_hip, stretch_back', FALSE, 'bodyweight', TRUE, 1, 30, 2, 70, 88, 95, 65),
('508da1b1-2eeb-47c7-aa3f-437a06914a28', 'Standing Bicep Curl - Twisting (Dumbbell)', 'Arms', 'Dumbbells', '{"Biceps"}'::text[], '{"Forearms"}'::text[], 'The Dumbbell Standing Biceps Curl is a curling exercise that isolates your biceps. The forearms assist throughout the movement, making this a well-rounded exercise. The standing position engages your core for stability. Using dumbbells requires more stabilization than barbell variations. Arm strength supports grip, pulling, and pushing in compound movements.', '4161201a', '04161201a-Dumbbell-Standing-Biceps-Curl_Upper-Arms-FIX_.mp4', 'male', FALSE, '2025-12-03 23:26:24.698781+00', '1. Select a pair of dumbbells at an appropriate weight for Dumbbell Standing Biceps Curl. 2. Stand with feet about shoulder-width apart. 3. Keep your elbows in a fixed position throughout the movement. 4. Curl the weight up by contracting your biceps, squeezing at the top. 5. Lower with control, resisting the weight on the way down. 6. Repeat for the prescribed number of repetitions.', 'Curl', 'Pull', NULL, NULL, NULL, 2, NULL, 5, 7, NULL, 6, 'Standing', NULL, NULL, NULL, 10, 15, NULL, 4, NULL, TRUE, NULL, 'Strength', 78, 5, 7, FALSE, TRUE, 'bicep_curl', 'Standing Biceps Curl', 'hammer_curl, preacher_curl, cable_curl', TRUE, 'dumbbell', FALSE, 3, 60, 2, 92, 90, 92, 90),
('5090baaa-16cc-45bd-acfc-fde2c6203c50', 'Front Plank Toe Tap', 'Core', 'Bodyweight', '{"Abs"}'::text[], '{"Shoulders","Lower Back"}'::text[], 'The Front Plank Toe Tap is a core stabilization exercise that primarily targets your abs. The shoulders, lower back assist throughout the movement, making this a well-rounded exercise. This bodyweight exercise requires no equipment and can be done anywhere. Building core stability helps with everything from heavy deadlifts to daily activities.', '33461201', '33461201-Front-Plank-Toe-Tap-(female)_Waist.mp4', 'female', FALSE, '2025-12-03 23:26:33.640031+00', '1. Hold your body in a straight line from head to heels. 2. Don''t let your hips sag or pike up—engage your core and glutes. 3. Breathe steadily while maintaining the position. 4. Repeat for the prescribed number of repetitions. Start with lighter weight to perfect your form. Include this in your core training.', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 2, NULL, 7, 7, NULL, 5, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 8, 12, NULL, 6, NULL, TRUE, NULL, 'Strength', 70, 7, 8, TRUE, TRUE, 'plank', 'Front Plank Toe Tap', 'side_plank, dead_bug, hollow_hold', FALSE, 'bodyweight', FALSE, 3, 90, 4, 70, 88, 95, 65),
('509af9fd-6e7b-4499-935d-dc1e3060172f', 'Seated Tibialis Press (Kettlebell)', 'Legs', 'Kettlebell', '{"Quads"}'::text[], '{"Glutes","Hamstrings"}'::text[], 'This pressing movement focuses on your gastrocnemius and soleus. The seated position helps isolate the target muscles by removing momentum. Kettlebells are excellent for building functional, real-world strength. Leg training boosts metabolism and builds functional, real-world strength.', '103671201', '103671201-Kettlebell-Sitting-Tibialis-Press_Calves_.mp4', 'male', FALSE, '2025-12-03 23:26:24.698781+00', '1. Select an appropriately weighted kettlebell for Kettlebell Seated Tibialis Press. 2. Sit with your back supported, core engaged, feet flat on the floor. 3. Execute the pressing motion for Kettlebell Seated Tibialis Press, extending through the target muscles. 4. Complete all reps with control before resting.', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 3, NULL, 7, 7, NULL, 5, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 8, 12, NULL, 6, NULL, TRUE, NULL, 'Strength', 78, 7, 8, TRUE, TRUE, 'general_exercise', 'Seated Tibialis Press', 'squat, bench_press, deadlift', FALSE, 'kettlebell', FALSE, 3, 90, 4, 75, 88, 88, 78),
('509e81ed-a024-4f0b-88fe-69868be9d641', 'Lying Single Arm Pronated Triceps Extension (Dumbbell)', 'Arms', 'Dumbbells, Flat Bench', '{"Triceps"}'::text[], '{"Chest","Shoulders"}'::text[], 'This extension movement isolates your triceps for improved arm development. The lying position provides back support and helps isolate the target muscles. Using dumbbells requires more stabilization than barbell variations. Dedicated arm training builds both strength and muscular definition.', '69951201', '69951201-Dumbbell-Lying-One-Arm-Pronated-Triceps-Extension-.mp4', 'female', FALSE, '2025-12-03 23:26:32.914483+00', '1. Select an appropriate weight dumbbell and hold it in one hand. 2. Lie down in the appropriate position for Dumbbell Lying One Arm Pronated Triceps Extension. 3. Use an overhand (pronated) grip with palms facing down/away. 4. Extend at the elbow until your arm is straight, squeezing the tricep. 5. Lower with control, keeping your upper arm stationary. 6. Complete all reps on one side, then switch to the other side. 7. Complete all reps with control before resting.', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 4, NULL, 5, 7, NULL, 6, 'Lying', NULL, NULL, NULL, 10, 15, NULL, 4, NULL, TRUE, NULL, 'Strength', 77, 5, 7, FALSE, TRUE, 'tricep_extension', 'Lying Single Arm Pronated Triceps Extension', 'tricep_pushdown, close_grip_bench', FALSE, 'dumbbell', FALSE, 3, 60, 2, 92, 90, 92, 90),
('50b6b6c1-66a2-4b7a-ba25-c22f5c8b9220', 'Standing Calf Raise (Cable)', 'Legs', 'Cables', '{"Calves"}'::text[], '{}'::text[], 'This raising movement focuses on your gastrocnemius and soleus. Performing this standing challenges your balance and core engagement. Cable resistance creates smooth, continuous muscle engagement. Lower body strength improves everything from walking to heavy compound lifts.', '13751201', '13751201-Cable-Standing-Calf-Raise_Calves_.mp4', 'male', FALSE, '2025-12-03 23:26:23.288245+00', '1. Adjust the cable machine to the correct height and attachment for Cable Standing Calf Raise. 2. Begin in a standing position with good posture. 3. Lower your heels below the platform to get a full stretch. 4. Rise up onto your toes as high as possible, squeezing your calves. 5. Lower with control and repeat. 6. Complete all reps with control before resting.', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 2, NULL, 5, 7, NULL, 6, 'Standing', NULL, NULL, NULL, 12, 20, NULL, 4, NULL, FALSE, NULL, 'Strength', 92, 5, 7, FALSE, TRUE, 'calf_raise', 'Standing Calf Raise', 'calf_raise, seated_calf_raise', FALSE, 'cable', FALSE, 3, 60, 2, 85, 88, 30, 92),
('50be3e05-900f-4f9e-86fc-cf2186e8431f', 'Rear Lunge (TRX)', 'Legs', 'TRX', '{"Quads"}'::text[], '{"Glutes","Hamstrings"}'::text[], 'This lunging movement emphasizes your quadriceps for stronger, more powerful legs. The glutes, hamstrings assist throughout the movement, making this a well-rounded exercise. The TRX allows you to adjust difficulty by changing your body angle. Lower body strength improves everything from walking to heavy compound lifts.', '11291201', '11291201-Suspender-Rear-Lunge-(female)_Thighs_.mp4', 'female', FALSE, '2025-12-03 23:26:39.472701+00', '1. Adjust the TRX/suspension straps to the appropriate length for Suspender Rear Lunge. 2. Step forward into a lunge until both knees are at about 90 degrees. 3. Push through your front/working leg to return to the starting position. 4. Complete all reps with control before resting.', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 3, NULL, 7, 7, NULL, 5, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 8, 12, NULL, 6, NULL, TRUE, NULL, 'Strength', 60, 7, 8, TRUE, TRUE, 'lunge', 'Suspender Rear Lunge', 'split_squat, step_up, squat', FALSE, 'trx', FALSE, 3, 90, 4, 68, 85, 85, 70),
('50d9ecc2-8550-4a2f-bfd8-592866849303', 'Landmine Squat Jump (Landmine)', 'Legs', 'Landmine Attachment, Barbell', '{"Quads"}'::text[], '{"Glutes","Hamstrings"}'::text[], 'This dynamic squatting movement gets your heart rate up while developing explosive strength. Secondary activation of your glutes, hamstrings provides additional muscle engagement. Plyometric training builds explosive power that transfers to sports and daily activities.', '106751201', '106751201-Landmine-Squat-Jump-(male)_Plyometrics_.mp4', 'male', FALSE, '2025-12-03 23:26:22.417605+00', '1. Push your hips back and bend your knees to lower your body. 2. Keep your chest up and knees tracking over your toes. 3. Explode upward from the bottom, jumping as high as possible. 4. Land softly with bent knees and immediately descend into the next rep. 5. Continue for your target rep count, maintaining good form throughout. Focus on the mind-muscle connection.', 'Squat', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 4, NULL, 5, 4, NULL, 8, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 8, 12, NULL, 7, NULL, TRUE, NULL, 'Plyometrics', 85, 9, 8, TRUE, TRUE, 'squat_jump', 'Landmine Squat Jump', 'squat, lunge, leg_press', FALSE, 'barbell', FALSE, 3, 60, 4, 95, 80, 65, 95),
('50e796dc-9fdc-4413-abb6-326d736886cd', 'Standing Raise (Dumbbell) - Alternating', 'Shoulders', 'Dumbbells', '{"Shoulders"}'::text[], '{"Traps"}'::text[], 'Build stronger shoulders with this raising movement focusing on your delts. Performing this standing challenges your balance and core engagement. The dumbbell variation provides freedom of movement and greater range of motion. Strong shoulders improve overhead strength and support nearly all upper body movements.', '4151201', '04151201-Dumbbell-Standing-Alternate-Raise_Shoulders.mp4', 'male', FALSE, '2025-12-03 23:26:22.644637+00', '1. Select a pair of dumbbells at an appropriate weight for Dumbbell Standing Alternate Raise. 2. Stand with feet about shoulder-width apart. 3. Raise the weight in the prescribed direction for Dumbbell Standing Alternate Raise. 4. Lower with control, maintaining tension throughout. 5. Alternate between sides/arms/legs with each repetition. 6. Complete all reps with control before resting.', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 2, NULL, 5, 7, NULL, 6, 'Standing', NULL, NULL, NULL, 10, 15, NULL, 4, NULL, TRUE, NULL, 'Strength', 84, 5, 7, FALSE, TRUE, 'general_exercise', 'Standing Raise - Alternating', 'squat, bench_press, deadlift', TRUE, 'dumbbell', FALSE, 3, 60, 2, 92, 90, 92, 90),
('50f3d7df-21cb-4495-b511-34d1560f8f9d', 'Double Rack Pistol Squat (Kettlebell)', 'Legs', 'Kettlebell', '{"Quads"}'::text[], '{"Glutes","Hamstrings"}'::text[], 'The Kettlebell Double Rack Pistol Squat is a squatting exercise that primarily loads your quadriceps. Your glutes work as secondary movers, adding to the training stimulus. The kettlebell''s offset center of mass increases the stability challenge. Strong legs are the foundation for athletic performance and functional fitness.', '98441201', '98441201-Kettlebell-Double-Rack-Pistol-Squat-(male)_Thighs_.mp4', 'male', FALSE, '2025-12-03 23:26:20.982555+00', '1. Position two kettlebells for Kettlebell Double Rack Pistol Squat. 2. Push your hips back and bend your knees to lower your body. 3. Keep your chest up and knees tracking over your toes. 4. Drive through your heels to stand back up, squeezing your glutes at the top. 5. Repeat for the prescribed number of repetitions.', 'Squat', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 4, NULL, 7, 7, NULL, 5, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 8, 12, NULL, 6, NULL, TRUE, NULL, 'Strength', 93, 7, 8, TRUE, TRUE, 'pistol_squat', 'Double Rack Pistol Squat', 'squat, bench_press, deadlift', FALSE, 'kettlebell', FALSE, 3, 90, 4, 75, 88, 88, 78),
('50fd0115-cb0f-4711-81c9-52c0b2fd6563', 'Lying Tip Toe', 'Legs', 'Bodyweight', '{"Quads"}'::text[], '{"Glutes","Hamstrings"}'::text[], 'The Lying Tip Toe isolates your calf muscles through a movement motion. Performing this lying down removes momentum for stricter form. A versatile bodyweight movement perfect for home or gym training. Strong legs are the foundation for athletic performance and functional fitness.', '71261201', '71261201-Lying-Tip-Toe-(female)_Calves.mp4', 'female', FALSE, '2025-12-03 23:26:35.38119+00', '1. Lie down in the appropriate position for Lying Tip Toe. 2. Set up in the starting position for Lying Tip Toe. 3. Execute the movement with proper form, focusing on your calves. 4. Control both the lifting and lowering phases of the movement. 5. Repeat for the prescribed number of repetitions.', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 2, NULL, 7, 7, NULL, 5, 'Lying', NULL, NULL, NULL, 8, 12, NULL, 6, NULL, TRUE, NULL, 'Strength', 50, 7, 8, TRUE, TRUE, 'calf_raise', 'Lying Tip Toe', 'squat, bench_press, deadlift', FALSE, 'bodyweight', FALSE, 3, 90, 4, 70, 88, 95, 65),
('5107bff7-8f33-4612-ad7d-a0e9e82dfcd4', 'Straight Leg Opposite Sit Up', 'Core', 'Bodyweight', '{"Abs"}'::text[], '{"Hip Flexors"}'::text[], 'Strengthen your midsection with this movement movement that works your abs. Your hip flexors work as secondary movers, adding to the training stimulus. No equipment needed—your body provides all the resistance. Core strength is foundational for athletic performance and injury prevention.', '85091201', '85091201-Straight-Leg-Opposite-Sit-up-(male)_Waist_.mp4', 'male', FALSE, '2025-12-03 23:26:28.968567+00', '1. Set up in the starting position for Straight Leg Opposite Sit Up. 2. Execute the movement with proper form, focusing on your abs. 3. Control both the lifting and lowering phases of the movement. 4. Complete all reps with control before resting.', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 2, NULL, 5, 7, NULL, 6, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 10, 15, NULL, 4, NULL, TRUE, NULL, 'Strength', 70, 5, 7, FALSE, TRUE, 'romanian_deadlift', 'Straight Leg Opposite Sit Up', 'deadlift, leg_curl, hip_thrust', FALSE, 'bodyweight', FALSE, 3, 60, 2, 70, 88, 95, 65);
